nt-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Decentralized</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-left:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-right:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-bottom:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-top:dashed #000000 0.75pt;vertical-align:middle;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Hardly decentralized</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-left:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-right:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-bottom:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-top:dashed #000000 0.75pt;vertical-align:middle;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Only partially decentralized</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height:13.75pt\"><td style=\"border-left:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-right:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-bottom:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-top:dashed #000000 0.75pt;vertical-align:middle;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Network value</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-left:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-right:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-bottom:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-top:dashed #000000 0.75pt;vertical-align:middle;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Network\'s own coin</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-left:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-right:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-bottom:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-top:dashed #000000 0.75pt;vertical-align:middle;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Any asset</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-left:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-right:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-bottom:dashed #000000 0.75pt;border-top:dashed #000000 0.75pt;vertical-align:middle;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Any asset</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">An important differentiator concerns access. Anyone can participate in a public blockchain, and the use of it is permissionless. Anyone can also operate a network node and participate in finding consensus. This does not apply to a private blockchain. Only those who are authorized by the operator of the private blockchain have access. Consensus-building also takes place only among approved instances. With a private blockchain, the transaction data is private, and participants only see the data that is unlocked for them. In contrast, the data of public blockchains can be viewed by anyone. Ultimately, the types of blockchain differ in their decentralization. While a public blockchain is distributed as widely as possible over many different network nodes, the other blockchain concepts usually run on one, two, six, or a dozen network nodes. The lower the decentralization among the network participants, the lower the redundancy and thus the resilience of the blockchain. The characteristic of potential immutability is also greatly weakened. Since such a blockchain has far fewer full nodes, it is much more likely that they will be manipulated or colluded with. Furthermore, public blockchains such as Bitcoin have their own blockchain-owned coin. Only thanks to its own unit of value can the peer-to-peer exchange of value within the network take place digitally and, above all, with minimized trust. With a private blockchain, on the other hand, a network\'s own coin is not mandatory. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This is also because no mechanism such as proof-of-work is needed to find consensus. The full nodes responsible for finding consensus on a private blockchain network are all known. Since they are required by the private blockchain operator to participate in consensus-building, they do not have to be incentivized with the help of a blockchain\'s own unit of value, as is the case with a decentralized, public blockchain. This doesn\'t have to mean that a private or permissioned blockchain solution can\'t also have value involved. It can even be different assets that are mapped via such a blockchain but are not its own. The biggest advantage of non-public blockchains is their speed and efficiency. Because consensus-building is spread over far fewer full nodes, private blockchains are considered more scalable, making them more suitable for the corporate context. A company itself can thus operate the full nodes, which together form the internal network. The corresponding blockchain and its underlying protocol are owned by the company. This has sole control over the private blockchain. Such a private blockchain can be useful if, for example, a company needs to maintain confidentiality or access restrictions but at the same time still wants to interact with a public blockchain and participate in its ecosystem. This is hardly possible with an ordinary database. A private blockchain solution can also be useful if a company wants to rely on the programmability of actions and activities within an ecosystem for its services. A simple, distributed database is often not enough here. A consortium blockchain in particular can be suitable here, as there can be a trust vacuum between individual companies. A consortium consists of independent actors that jointly control a network. As a body, they jointly decide who is allowed to join the network as a full node and view the transaction history. Like an internal blockchain, it is not permissionless, and the number of full nodes depends on the number of committee members.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><font face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/18.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 13: A public blockchain is permissionless, open, and accessible to everyone. Consortial and private blockchains represent closed networks. The former consist of different companies; the latter are defined by a single company.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Pascal Hügli (author’s presentation))</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What a blockchain ultimately is is not set in stone. Thus, in all three variants, there are a wide variety of manifestations of the basic principles. The fact is, however, that private blockchains make compromises in various features such as decentralization, redundancy, permissionless access, and access. However, it is precisely these characteristics that make a public blockchain what is commonly understood as a blockchain in the first place. One would do well to put any blockchain rhetoric through its paces. A blockchain that is not very transparent, requires approval, and is only distributed on a few network nodes is under completely different auspices than a public-permissionless blockchain, whose network consists of thousands of independent full nodes. It is questionable whether private and consortium blockchains will survive in the long term in isolated form. We know from the history of the Internet that in the beginning it was mainly intranets that were used. Over time, these have been replaced by the ever better and more secure Internet solutions. The open Internet, as we know it today, prevailed. Intranets have not disappeared today, but they only play a marginal role. It is quite possible that a similar fate could befall private and federated blockchains, as they are made obsolete by successfully scaling public blockchains. Or they survive as extended arms of public blockchains. Their niche space could be used by companies for specific applications.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span class=\"Apple-tab-span\" style=\"white-space:pre;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">	</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.27; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.2.2.2 Permissionless and open-source</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Now that we have analyzed the term \"blockchain\" and distinguished it according to its various variants, let\'s focus again on the public blockchain. Their relevant characteristics are:</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Concatenation (or hashing) of data: block-chain or time-chain</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Incentivization of miners by means of proof-of-work</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Decentralized database distributed across a variety of computers: Distributed Ledger</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Digital signatures of asymmetric public/private key cryptography</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Constant exchange of information via a peer-to-peer network</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Validation and enforcement of consensus rules by full nodes</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">One last characteristic we have not yet explained in detail: its permissionless, open-source character. The permission-free property means that no permission is required to become part of the network. The software is open to everyone and can be used by anyone. The Bitcoin program code is freely available on the Internet and can be downloaded by anyone. As a user, you only need wallet software, which you can get from the Internet. The permission-free use thus makes a public blockchain socially scalable, far more so than other networks designed for value exchange. A public blockchain like Bitcoin is globally distributed. Consequently, different parties that are in opposite places on this earth can exchange values without anyone being able to forbid them to do so. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This feature makes public blockchain particularly beneficial for the 1.7 trillion people who are still unbanked and thus excluded from financial applications. (Cash Matters, 2020) With public blockchains such as Bitcoin, the unbanked have access to a global financial infrastructure for the first time. In contrast to the existing system, the use of public blockchains does not require a bank account but only an internet connection. Not only is the network itself open, but the Bitcoin source code is also visible to everyone. This is located in a so-called repository at GitHub (n.d.), an internet hosting provider for software developers. Since Bitcoin is an open-source project, anyone can propose changes that can be implemented as long as a majority within the Bitcoin community agrees. As an open-source project, the source code of Bitcoin is always in the focus of a wide variety of people, which is why quick fixes at the level of development are de facto impossible. Bitcoin also follows the unwritten law of a rough consensus: changes are proposed as software updates, after which they are debated within the entire ecosystem. Only when an overwhelming consensus seems to emerge will a concrete implementation in the Bitcoin code be considered.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Good to know: Core developers are only the administrators</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Do Bitcoin core developers—also known as maintainers—have too much power over the Bitcoin protocol? After all, they have so-called commit access keys, i.e., the possibility to change the Bitcoin source code. But they do not have a free ride by any means. As a global phenomenon, Bitcoin is under the constant supervision of many people who know no less about software and programming than the core developers. Again and again, therefore, it happened that suggestions for changes by the core developers were not heard and were rejected by the community. So Bitcoin\'s core developers are not gatekeepers. Like language, Bitcoin is a social, emergent phenomenon. Although there are repeated attempts to influence a language through spelling reforms, the consensus on the meaning of words ultimately happens organically. The same applies to Bitcoin.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The fact that the Bitcoin code is open and transparent ultimately creates trust. Anyone who can read programming code and wants to be convinced of Bitcoin\'s performance characteristics and its promises can study the Bitcoin source code and verify what is promised with their own hands. The public character of the Bitcoin ledger also has another important advantage: transaction history, Bitcoin distribution, and thus the total number of all Bitcoin units in circulation can be fully verified at any time. This strengthens the auditability of the network and makes Bitcoin\'s fixed money supply of 21 million auditable around the clock. This puts Bitcoin in stark contrast to the traditional financial system, whose exact base money supply is difficult for a layman to audit exactly. In terms of innovation, Bitcoin\'s open-source character ultimately creates a real pull. As an open standard, the source code itself, but also peripheral application software, is interoperable and cumulative. This means that existing software merges with new innovation, which in turn creates the breeding ground for innovation.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.27; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.2.2.3 Forks: The Power of Forking</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">An advantageous feature of permissionless innovation in the field of software is the possibility of copying and adapting it at will at a vanishingly small marginal cost. In technical jargon, this is called forking. In contrast to so-called proprietary, i.e., copyrighted software, developers do not have to develop completely new products but can copy and modify the existing program code and publish a new version of the program. Each new version is a descendant of the previously developed code but is independent and unique from it. This \"forking\" is a constant occurrence in the field of open-source software. Since public blockchains are ultimately software, they can also go through forks. Blockchain forks are typically divided into the categories of soft fork and hard fork. The soft fork refers to any change to the source code that is backwards compatible. If, for example, a blockchain whose blocks were previously one megabyte in size switches to block sizes of 500 kilobytes, it is a soft fork. The new rule does not conflict with the old one, since 500 kilobytes is less than one megabyte. Old blocks still accept the new ones. In contrast, a hard fork refers to a protocol change that is not backwards compatible. For example, if the block size is increased from one to 2 megabytes. The hard fork expands the rules in a way that cannot be fulfilled by the old blocks—a fork occurs.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for Nerds: The Blockchain Restaurant Comparison</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Imagine a blockchain as a large, collectively run restaurant. There is no single central authority to enforce decisions. Initially, the restaurant only served vegetarian dishes. If the chefs decide to serve only meat-based recipes from now on, this would be equivalent to a \"hard fork\" in blockchain terms. Existing customers would have to either accept the new menu with meat dishes or find a new restaurant.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In contrast, a \"soft fork\" would occur if the chefs chose to make the menu entirely vegan. In this case, vegetarians could still dine at the restaurant.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin has already gone through several soft and hard forks. At first glance, forks seem quite suspicious. After all, they seem to offer the possibility of creating value out of thin air, as after a fork, two different units of value (coins) suddenly exist on two different blockchains. If you pay a little more attention to the phenomenon, you can see that forks are a socio-evolutionary mechanism of public blockchain networks that make it possible to try out new ideas and resolve conflicts. The possibility of forking also creates system competition, as different versions compete with each other. The possibility of a fork also serves as a tool to keep developers in check. For example, a group can split off at any time if it no longer likes the course of the further development of a blockchain. Developers must therefore always be innovative and receptive to feedback and can hardly program past the needs of the users. Like a sword of Damocles, the possibility of a fork hangs over the heads of the programmers. However, an excess of forks is not conducive to a public blockchain network. With each split, there is a split of the hashrate provided by miners. The more this is diluted and spread over individual forks, the more insecure the different blockchain versions become. It therefore makes sense for as many miners as possible to come together on one version and do their mining work there. So for a fork to be successful, it has to convince exponents of the old community. Only if enough users, developers, and miners turn to this fork can it exist in the long run. Since it exists as a new project independent of the old one after the spin-off, there has been no inflation of assets within the old network. There are two independent networks, with two different coins, each associated with a network.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Good to know: A decisive battle over the future of Bitcoin</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In August 2017, there was a major fork in Bitcoin, in which Bitcoin Cash forked as a new independent public blockchain. The split was preceded by a long debate, the so-called Blocksize War. This dispute was about a seemingly technical detail: How big should the blocks be in Bitcoin? Two groups faced each other. The \"big blockers\" wanted Bitcoin\'s block size to be adjusted upwards so that Bitcoin could process more transactions via the blockchain and thus scale better. The \"small blockers\" countered that if the block size were increased, the decentralization of the network would be jeopardized, as the larger data requirements would overwhelm many full nodes. Whether a majority of miners and companies were already in favor of an upward adjustment, the users prevailed. A split took place, and the \"big blockers\" implemented their visions in alternative forks such as Bitcoin Cash or Bitcoin SV.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.27; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.2.2.4 Different Ways of Reaching Consensus</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#2f5496;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-3562cf1e-7fff-36d1-370f-be9ed9ce6db7\"></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Public blockchains have two levels of consensus building. In social consensus-building, it is the community that ultimately determines what the programming code and thus the protocol of a public blockchain should look like. The rules are determined. In the case of Bitcoin, Satoshi Nakamoto has provided a framework. While certain things have since been implemented as improvements, other changes have never been able to reach consensus.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/19.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 14: In public blockchain projects such as Bitcoin, there are always two levels, the social and the technical. The former happens off-chain, and that\'s where the rules are set. The latter is protocol-based and ensures the enforcement of the rules.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Robert Breedlove)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In addition to the social level, public blockchains also have a technological level of consensus-building. This ensures the enforcement of the rules agreed on at the social level on a protocol basis. Most public blockchains currently use one or at least a modified form of the following consensus mechanisms:</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Proof-of-Work (PoW)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Proof-of-Stake (PoS)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Delegated Proof-of-Stake (DPoS)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Proof-of-Authority (PoA)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">We have already explained the proof-of-work mechanism in detail at the beginning of this chapter. Consequently, we want to dedicate ourselves here to the idea and mode of action of proof-of-stake. This consensus mechanism is mainly considered a much less energy-intensive alternative to PoW. In the meantime, a large number of public blockchain protocols are therefore based on PoS. With the proof-of-stake approach, energy in the form of electricity is no longer used to reach consensus. It will be replaced by the blockchain\'s own coin. Instead of spending labor in the form of energy, the blockchain\'s native coins must be put at risk. This process is called staking, and the coins must be staked. Whoever stakes his coins becomes a validator. The latter are the ones who vote with their staked coins for the block they want to add to the blockchain and thus contribute to the maintenance and consensus of a PoS blockchain. In doing so, they take on the same task that miners do in the proof-of-work approach. Consensus is thus not reached using an extrinsic component in the form of computing power but on the basis of a capital investment in the form of the blockchain-intrinsic coin. To motivate validators to stake their coins for the validation of new blocks, they are promised coins as a reward proportional to the amount staked. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">At the same time, the PoS consensus mechanism also provides for a punishment of those validators who validate false blocks and thus manipulate the transaction history. This process is called slashing and is intended to ensure that the validators of a PoS blockchain behave honestly and only attach correct blocks to the blockchain. As a validator, you are randomly selected by an algorithm. The amount of staked coins is relevant for the probability of being selected. The higher your stake, the greater the chance of being a validator of the next block. Delegated Proof-of-Stake, or DPoS for short, is another variant among the staking consensus mechanisms. DPoS entitles every coin holder to choose validators. The rule is one coin, one vote. For example, those with the largest stake are not entitled to confirm transactions. Rather, the entirety of all coin owners elects delegates to take on this task. The advantage here is a higher speed in the verification of transactions compared to the usual PoS mechanism. The consensus is spread over a smaller set of validators. This is comparable to the concepts of direct and indirect democracy. The latter is generally considered to be more efficient in decision-making because it is distributed over less representation. Proof-of-authority is a consensus mechanism in which blocks are added to the blockchain only by approved, known network participants. Since the identity of the validator is known, they have the incentive to maintain the transaction process and only add correct blocks to the blockchain. Otherwise, validators could suffer reputational damage.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.27; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.2.2.5 The challenge of scaling</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#2f5496;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-c5511546-7fff-7044-9430-a3b1084ffb93\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Opinions differ as to which consensus mechanism is the best. In favor of the proof-of-stake algorithm, its energy efficiency is invoked. Consensus-building takes place completely internally. The production of new blocks and thus the verification of new transactions costs capital but not computing power in the form of external energy. At this stage, it is unclear how secure the proof-of-stake consensus mechanism is. Whether such an implementation will provide the same collateral and guarantees as proof-of-work in the long term and on the scale of the Bitcoin network is still unclear due to reality, as there is no proof-of-stake blockchain of the size and market capitalization of Bitcoin. Nevertheless, proof-of-stake is seen as a desirable consensus mechanism, as it is supposed to allow for better basic scaling. In this context, scalability is mainly understood as the effort to increase transaction throughput and speed of public blockchain protocols. At present, these do not even come close to the transaction capacity of the dominant payment systems. The reason for this can be found in the so-called blockchain trilemma. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">At this point in time, a public, permissionless blockchain can only satisfactorily fulfill two of the following three characteristics at a time: decentralization, security, and scalability. Services such as Google, Facebook, or Visa, which are often compared to public blockchain protocols, only achieve their high transaction capacity because they neglect scalability and security at the expense of decentralization. In contrast, public blockchains prioritize decentralization and security, while scalability is not prioritized. The Bitcoin blockchain makes it possible to operate a full node without reservation. Because each full node validates and records every single transaction, it has the entire transaction history of the blockchain, ensuring that it is kept in sync at all times. But a network built in this way is only as strong as its weakest link. Scalability, and therefore transaction throughput and speed, depend on the computing capacity of the lowest-performing full nodes. Although these could be discarded to make the system faster, a public blockchain would clearly miss its goal of being as public and permissionless as possible. To scale a public blockchain like Bitcoin, the path of modular scaling is generally the most suitable. In this way, it makes it possible to increase the capacity of the overall system without giving up the fundamental properties of security and decentralization.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/20.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 15: The blockchain trilemma goes back to the thoughts of Ethereum founder Vitalik Buterin and points out that there are unavoidable trade-offs between decentralization, security, and scalability. A blockchain can only satisfactorily fulfill two of these three properties at the same time on its base layer.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f6ab95da-7fff-a176-13b0-0c70c32be054\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: SEBA BANK AG)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/21.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 16: Modular scaling is to take place via additional protocols such as off-chain payment channels. An alternative to this is the so-called sidechain, which runs parallel to a base-layer blockchain as an independent blockchain.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Pascal Hügli (author’s proprietary work))</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the modular scaling method, protocol level by protocol level is built. In this way, a multi-layered, integrative protocol complex is formed, the individual levels of which enable specialization. Modular systems of this type are more flexible, resistant, and versatile. The American systems theorist John Gall already recognized this when he put forward the following theorem: \"A complex system that works has invariably developed from a simple system that in turn has worked. A complex system developed from scratch never works and cannot be patched together to make it work. You have to start over with a functioning, simple system.\" Modular scaling can be divided into different approaches:</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Additional protocols (off-chain)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Sidechains (other-chain)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Roll-ups</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-2bec9381-7fff-e9c6-62b3-4d22c648327d\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The scaling of a public blockchain is to take place over different levels, also known as layers. Layer 1 embodies the base layer and is often called the mainchain. Additional protocols or sidechains build as layer 2 on the mainchain. By outsourcing transactions from the base layer to other levels, the number of possible transactions and the speed of the overall system should be massively increased. The finalization and final settlement of all transactions of the additional protocols or sidechains takes place on-chain on Layer 1. In addition to increasing transaction capacity, these modular scaling methods can also extend the functionality of a public blockchain. A well-known manifestation of additional protocols is the so-called payment or state channels. In payment channels, for example, transactions are executed outside the blockchain and only written to the base blockchain when settled. Theoretically, several different additional protocols can build on a basic blockchain and relieve it of transactions via off-chain processing. \"Off-chain\" means that the transactions are not written directly to the main chain but are only sporadically finalized on the base layer.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If implemented correctly, such additional protocols can scale a public blockchain without having to compromise on decentralization and security. Sidechains are another option for modular scaling. Blockchain activity can thus be outsourced from the mainchain to sidechains without losing the connection and thus the security and guarantees of the base layer blockchain. The difficulty of sidechains is that a reliable connection (pegging) between the sidechain and the base layer should be guaranteed. The more trust-minimizing the connection can be ensured, the more credible and authentic the sidechain is in its quest to be a true extension of the underlying base layer. A third variant is roll-ups. As mini-blockchains, they are used in particular when scaling smart contract platforms. In roll-ups, the data-intensive computation is separated from the base layer blockchain and thus outsourced. In concrete terms, this means that the transaction data stored in a roll-up is bundled and compressed outside the blockchain before it is processed, verified, and thus anchored on the base layer blockchain. However, it is not the entire transaction history that is written to the base layer blockchain, but a kind of fingerprint of it, which is far more efficient in terms of computer technology. In this sense, roll-ups can be considered a kind of combination of additional protocols such as payment channels and sidechains. While the transactions are carried out outside the blockchain, they are written directly to the base layer blockchain for settlement rather than a sidechain. The modular scaling of public blockchains is still in full swing, and a wide variety of approaches are being promoted in the form of different additional protocols, sidechains, and roll-ups. Since a technology like the public blockchain can never scale sufficiently, the scaling project and the innovation that comes with it will never be exhausted. Only effective modular scaling will make mass adoption and widespread adoption of public blockchains a fact. (Hügli &amp; Lanni, 2022)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><font color=\"#000000\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br><font face=\"__Montserrat_069ab3, __Montserrat_Fallback_069ab3, Montserrat, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><font face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"></span></font></font>\n</div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-09 09:42:08','2025-12-10 09:05:18'),(24,13,'Money, gold, or even a guarantor of time?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-1f94476f-7fff-f512-dd9b-1563065b4dbb\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What money is and what is not has always been debated by economists and monetary theorists. Various traditional economists argue that money can only be what is recognized as such by a state. On the other hand, there are monetary theorists who do not define money so narrowly. For example, gold and silver are considered by some experts to be real money—money that has ultimately organically crystallized into one in the market.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.3.1.1 Is Bitcoin money?</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Due to the digital scarcity discussed in the last chapter, Bitcoin can also be understood as a unit of value from an economic point of view. Each and every one of the 21 million Bitcoin units that will be available, all of which are divisible to the eighth decimal place, acts as an asset inherent in the Bitcoin system. Within the Bitcoin network, Bitcoin takes the money function. There is no definitive answer to the question of whether Bitcoin, as a unit of value of the Bitcoin network, can also be understood as money outside of it. Money is ultimately a subjective matter. The fact that Bitcoin is considered money by some is due to the fact that the crypto asset is used as such in certain specific contexts. The Austrian polymath Friedrich August von Hayek already pointed out this important circumstance when he described money not as a noun, but as an adjective. According to Hayek, money is less a rigid name word and can be reduced to a single thing but rather an adjective that applies to different things in different contexts to varying degrees. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Thus, in connection with goods, he did not write about money as such, but about more monetary and less monetary goods. (Hayek, 2011) The more expensive a good is, the better and faster it can be sold. In this context, one also speaks of the marketability of a good. With increasing money, the marketability of the corresponding good grows, and thus the possibility of finding a market and exchange partner for this good. Whether a thing can achieve a high level of sales or market—that is, whether the thing can be monetized and thus function as suitable money—can be traced back to various characteristics. The sooner a thing combines these qualities, the more likely it is that this thing is monetary. A high monetary value of an object ultimately turns it into money. As money, this thing can ultimately fulfill two functions above all: the medium of exchange and the store of value function. In the general understanding, money fulfills its function as a medium of exchange if it is as stable as possible in the price of other goods in the short term.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> In this context, we can also speak of short-term price stability. The store of value function of money seems to be given when the corresponding money can keep its price constant in relation to other goods even in the long term. If you can still buy the same number of goods or more with money after several years, it is considered stable in value. What about Bitcoin\'s money? Does Bitcoin have properties that make the crypto value monetary? A monetary analysis of Bitcoin suggests that the crypto asset excellently combines various properties of money. These are:</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Transportability</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Divisibility</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Durability</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Uniformity (or fungibility)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Verifiability</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Stable purchasing power</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Scarcity</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Particular attention should be paid to the last two points, as these are where Bitcoin\'s biggest weaknesses in terms of its </span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">monetariness</span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> can be located. Due to the high volatility, purchasing power fluctuates greatly, which is unfavorable for its function as a means of payment. This volatility stems from Bitcoin\'s scarcity and the disinflationary trend that comes with it. Before we address these two related points in detail, we will first briefly address the five less controversial characteristics. Transportability: Bitcoin is digital information and can therefore be transferred around the world at the speed of light within the Bitcoin network. No matter how high the value transferred to Bitcoin, in a few minutes (and via the Lightning Network in a few seconds), it is transferred to a new owner. As a crypto asset, Bitcoin is extremely portable. In practice, the private keys are Bitcoin. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If you have the access keys, you can move the Bitcoin linked to it without any effort. The fact that private keys can be held on a mobile phone or on a USB stick, written on paper, or even just memorized and thus stored in one\'s own memory makes Bitcoin highly transportable. Divisible: Bitcoins are divisible to the eighth decimal place. The smallest unit of Bitcoin is called Satoshi (Sats). A single Bitcoin is thus equivalent to one hundred millionth of a Satoshi. In off-chain payment channels, Bitcoin is even divisible to 13 decimal places, so-called \"milisatoshi.\" Durability: Bitcoin as an asset exists as long as the Bitcoin network lasts. Asset value and network are inextricably linked. Since Bitcoin has only existed for a little more than a decade, no definitive conclusions can yet be drawn about its permanence. However, due to its redundancy, Bitcoin is hardly destructible. To wipe out Bitcoin, every single copy of the Bitcoin Ledger would have to be destroyed. Bitcoin is ultimately nothing more than information. And information is hardly destructible. Uniformity: Within the Bitcoin network, every Bitcoin is the same as another. In technical jargon, this is called fungibility. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This means that Bitcoin transmitted in the network is treated equally by the code. Since Bitcoin units are traceable on the blockchain, certain Bitcoin can be flagged and rejected by third parties—for example, if they are deemed suspicious or unclean by financial institutions. Such Bitcoins are called tainted coins and are less fungible. The so-called virgin coins are considered immaculate coins. These are newly created Bitcoins that come directly from miners and are therefore supposed to be clean. In reality, the usefulness of these coins is questioned, as it can never be guaranteed that these newly created bitcoins are actually clean. This is because transaction fees in the form of Bitcoin units that are already circulating in the market are also included in this Bitcoin. If these units are stained, this rubs onto the new Bitcoin. In general, however, the market has so far rated Bitcoin as fungible. Protocol updates such as Taproot will also increase fungibility.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Verifiability: With appropriate software, Bitcoins can be easily checked for authenticity. The public transaction history and the associated transparency ensure that the total number of all Bitcoin units in circulation is fully verifiable at all times. This creates trust in the network and in Bitcoin\'s guarantees, according to which its money supply cannot be inflated beyond the intended fixed amount. If the transactions on the Bitcoin blockchain were obfuscated, the risk of so-called inflation errors (Dashjr, 2019)—an uncontrolled creation of new Bitcoin beyond the 21 million mark—would be much greater.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Table talk: No unsullied history</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the still young history of Bitcoin, two so-called inflation bugs have already occurred. These are previously undiscovered errors in the Bitcoin program code, the exploitation of which makes it possible to inflate the Bitcoin supply beyond the 21 million units specified in the code. The first of these two inflation mistakes happened in 2010. At that time, Satoshi Nakamoto was still active and corrected the mistake. In 2018, another of these bugs was discovered. Fortunately, it could be fixed before an attacker could exploit it. However, these events show that Bitcoin is software and therefore not infallible. Although a few so-called inflation bugs have already occurred in the history of Bitcoin, these in turn could be discovered and thus fixed due to the publicity of the program code.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/22.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span></p><div><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-ae5cc13b-7fff-2a2b-c81d-990af66a9b58\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 1: This table shows how well the numerous properties of money apply to Bitcoin, gold or government currencies.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Medium)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.27; text-align: justify; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.3.1.2 Bitcoin: A volatile affair</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Compared to most traditional assets, Bitcoin’s historical volatility, measured in sovereign currencies, remains high. Although the asset has now existed for more than fifteen years, this is still a short lifespan compared to gold, equities, or fiat currencies. Its relatively young age, coupled with ongoing uncertainty about its regulatory path and role in the global financial system, leaves ample room for speculation and thus price swings.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin’s volatility continues to shape its monetary identity. While it is increasingly recognized as a store of value, its acceptance as a medium of exchange is limited. Retail adoption remains small, and most merchants that “accept” Bitcoin do so through payment processors that instantly convert it into national currencies. The reason is simple: with realized daily volatility in the range of 1.5–3% on average in 2025, and occasional spikes far higher, few businesses can afford to take on the risk of holding Bitcoin directly. Traders operate on thin margins and calculate their expenses in relatively stable fiat currencies; adding Bitcoin exposure complicates accounting and increases financial risk.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In 2025 an important factor is the behavior of users themselves. Most Bitcoin holders prefer to keep their coins rather than spend them. If Bitcoin can appreciate by several percentage points in a matter of days, spending it on everyday goods feels counterintuitive. This “hodl” mentality slows its adoption as a transactional currency, even though payment channels like the Lightning Network have technically made small, fast Bitcoin payments possible.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The same volatility deters borrowing in Bitcoin. An asset capable of appreciating significantly within weeks is not attractive to hold on the liability side of a balance sheet. Businesses and individuals are understandably reluctant to take on debt that may become more expensive to repay if the underlying asset rises against fiat currencies.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The key question remains: will Bitcoin ever become less volatile against national currencies and thus more attractive as money for the masses? While some observers argue volatility will diminish as adoption deepens and liquidity grows, others consider it unlikely. Unlike state currencies, Bitcoin’s money supply is fixed, so only the demand side can adjust. This rigidity means that demand shocks—whether driven by speculation, macroeconomic shifts, or regulatory developments—translate directly into price volatility.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In practice, Bitcoin’s volatility has moderated compared to its early years, but it remains well above that of traditional currencies. Its role today is less about everyday payments and more about being a speculative store of value, a hedge against monetary policy, and a macro-sensitive digital asset. Whether this status will eventually stabilize its price dynamics or keep it locked in cycles of speculative surges and corrections remains an open debate.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.27; text-align: justify; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.3.1.3 Price stability: a question of liquidity</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The supply restriction actually ensures that sudden changes in demand cannot be reacted to and instead have to be balanced out by price fluctuations. At the same time, price volatility should decrease as liquidity grows in the Bitcoin market. For example, liquidity for assets is defined by the following parameters:</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 4.5pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Order book/market depth: How much does the price of an asset move relative to the amount you want to buy or sell of that asset? The larger the order book, the greater the market depth. Thanks to greater market depth, price movements can be better absorbed.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 4.5pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bid and ask prices: What is the trading spread, also known as the spread, between the best buy and sell price? The tighter the spreads, the smaller the scatter loss when buying and selling an asset.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 4.5pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Size of the quotes: The stock market prices (bid and ask) are set by the market participants. The larger the odds, the more liquid the market is.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Trading volume: The higher the trading volume, i.e., the turnover of an asset, the higher the sales volume and thus the trading liquidity.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Turnover frequency: In most cases, this is also referred to as the turnover ratio. What is meant is how often and in what number is an asset traded per day, relative and absolute to its total supply?</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Trading pair size: An asset will always trade against a different value. The more trading pairs there are, the more opportunities there are to be able to trade a corresponding asset. The level of liquidity of an asset depends on these parameters. As a general rule, the deeper the order book, the greater the market depth; the tighter the bid and ask prices; the larger the quotes, the trading volume, and the turnover frequency; and the more trading pairs there are, the more liquid an asset is. An analogy illustrates this point: The liquidity of an asset can be compared to a tub filled with water (Bitcoin market). A colored, water-soluble substance (demand shock) discolors the water-filled tub more the less water the tub holds. If liquidity increases many times over, i.e., there is much more water in the tub, a new substance addition has a much smaller discoloring effect (price volatility) on the increased total amount of water.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font face=\"__Montserrat_069ab3, __Montserrat_Fallback_069ab3, Montserrat, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/23.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-4b22241f-7fff-551b-6dfc-ca76beb46d38\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 2: The higher the basic liquidity, the less much additional admixture will fall further </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: transparent;\">liquidity. The example of differently sized tubs illustrates this aptly.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Pascal Hügli (self-presentation))</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Table talk: What does the data show so far?</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin\'s volatility mainly manifests itself in the form of extreme swings. These have become much rarer over the past few years. Measured as a median, however, volatility has hardly decreased. Thus, even twelve years after the birth of Bitcoin, volatility still increases sharply if, for example, it enters a bull market. With the transition to a subsequent bear market, volatility remains high for the time being, only to decrease over time and stabilize.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This fact also applies to an asset like Bitcoin. The increased market depth of recent years has made the crypto asset much easier, faster, and cheaper to trade in cash, thus attracting more and more buyers and sellers. This, in turn, increases liquidity. A self-reinforcing effect, then. Steadily growing liquidity stems from the fact that more and more market participants are willing to trade Bitcoin at certain price levels. As liquidity increases, Bitcoin is suddenly attracting investors for whom Bitcoin was previously considered too illiquid. Bitcoin\'s market capitalization is crucial in that a higher market capitalization arouses the interest of certain investors in the first place, and they ultimately provide more liquidity with an investment.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Companies such as Tesla (Ostroff &amp; Elliott, 2021) have already proven that the Bitcoin market allows for a US dollar investment in billions and that the liquidity is available for the purchase and sale of millions of euros. (Van der Heyden, 2021) Greater liquidity also creates the basis for greater market penetration. More and more liquid trading options for Bitcoin mean that more market participants have the opportunity to invest in Bitcoin. According to estimates, around 100 million people worldwide currently own Bitcoin. Extrapolated to the world\'s population, this is between 1 and 2%, indicating that Bitcoin\'s market penetration is still in its infancy. (Woo, 2021) The proportion of those who are likely to hold Bitcoin one day could still rise considerably. Once Bitcoin has reached the upper end of its S-shape-like acceptance curve, its monetization phase is likely to come to an end, which in turn would smooth out price volatility.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/24.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9ee43a48-7fff-a492-1442-51e4a805a15f\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 3: Bitcoin follows a classic S-curve in terms of mass adoption. It is difficult to determine which phase we are in at the beginning of 2022, probably in the late phase of \"Early Majority.\"</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: 21 Shares)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Currently, this monetization phase is far from complete. The market is still in a discovery process and is trying to find out where the long-term fair value of Bitcoin could lie. Bitcoin\'s price volatility is therefore a compelling expression of this discovery process that is currently taking place and will continue due to the ongoing monetization phase. Because without volatility, there is no growth.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">\n\n\n</span></span></span>\n\n\n</div></span></span></div></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-09 09:45:48','2026-01-01 06:46:31'),(25,13,'On Bitcoin\'s Scarcity','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-2d0dcaea-7fff-7b82-b551-7bb03a0c9bf2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As mentioned, the all-important concept of </span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">monetarity</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> goes back to the economist von Hayek. Another important economist who contributed to monetary theory is William Stanley Jevons. According to his analysis, a thing always goes through several phases in its monetization. Gold is one of them. He believed that historically, gold had first served as a valuable commodity for ornamental purposes, then as a commodity, then as a medium of exchange, and finally as a measure of value. (Jevons, 1885) A similar trajectory is also emerging for Bitcoin: Bitcoin started as a kind of digital collectible without any price. However, its first holders had already recognized a possible value, as they understood that Bitcoin fulfills a wide variety of monetary properties excellently. With this conviction and the willingness to speculate on a first acceptance of Bitcoin as a proto-unit of value (A Short History of Money), these holders finally gave the cryptoasset an actual price when they began to trade with it rudimentarily. </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">To date, the discovery process around Bitcoin has intensified to such an extent that even companies have added Bitcoin to their balance sheets as a reserve asset and thus as a reliable store of value. This consolidation and convergence of more and more beliefs about Bitcoin\'s suitability as a store of value represents another key moment in Bitcoin\'s monetization journey. This provides a basis for further network effects and thus more liquidity. Over the next few years, it will become clear whether Bitcoin can grow into the functions of a generally accepted means of payment as well as a widely recognized unit of account. A necessary prerequisite for people to even perceive Bitcoin as a possible store of value in its early days was its digital scarcity. Because in general, we humans associate scarcity or rarity with intrinsic value. We consider gemstones, diamonds, or pearls to be valuable because they are rare and considered scarce. In the wild, you don\'t find them just like that. The search for them requires work. </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The same applies to gold, the epitome of scarcity and intrinsic value. When asked why a kilogram of gold is valuable and therefore expensive, the answer is usually as follows:The precious metal is a scarce resource, and its extraction requires great effort. However, scarcity alone is not enough to justify the high value of an item. Suppose the author of this textbook were to draw a stick figure on a piece of paper and create only one copy. This drawing of the stick figure would be very brief, as it only exists once. Nevertheless, this drawing is unlikely to have any value, let alone a price. Only when other people subjectively consider what is drawn to be worth owning could a price for this drawing gradually emerge. The subjective desire for a thing is just as decisive. If, for whatever reason, it were to happen that more and more people would be willing to pay for this stick figure drawing, the price of it would probably rise. But the author of this textbook should quickly come up with the idea of making copies of it. This would allow him to sell the same drawing several times. As a result, the price of a stick figure drawing would fall. The vast majority of things do not become more expensive if many people want them. As soon as a thing is in high demand, its production is worthwhile, and this usually follows economies of scale. The larger the production volume, the lower the unit price. This connection does not apply to a few exceptional goods. Ultimately, these are precisely those goods that are commonly described as scarce. And these behave just the other way around, they show rising marginal costs in production. This means that the more of it you want to produce, the more cost-intensive the additional production becomes. Bitcoin belongs to this category. </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">We remember the mechanism of difficulty adjustment described in the previous chapter. If the Bitcoin price rises, more players sense the opportunity to mine Bitcoin profitably. This increases the number of miners and, as a result, the hashrate within the Bitcoin network, which is why the difficulty level adjusts upwards. After the adjustment, it is more difficult to mine new Bitcoin. This means that the additional production of Bitcoin has become more cost-intensive, which means higher marginal costs for miners in production. This reality just described is condensed in the concept of scarcity. Things like Bitcoin, which have rising marginal costs in production, are usually perceived as scarce and rare because more of it can only be produced with more effort and higher marginal costs. Compared to other goods that do not have rising but falling marginal costs and are easier to produce, Bitcoin is considered scarce. To complicate matters with this approach, individual Bitcoins, provided that the Bitcoin network remains, are indestructible. Or to put it another way: Bitcoin cannot be consumed. So all Bitcoin ever created still exists. It is true that the private keys that provide access to the corresponding Bitcoin units may be lost. These Bitcoins then still exist but are inaccessible and therefore no longer spendable. If the access keys are still available, they represent a potential Bitcoin offer. Due to this fact, we should always understand scarcity as a relative quantity. Also, when talking about scarcity, not only the supply side but also the demand side should be considered.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.3.2.1 A model for measuring scarcity?</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">An economic concept that can help us in this regard is the so-called </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">stock-to-flow</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> ratio (S2F ratio). This measures the scarcity, or rather the hardship, of a thing. We can think of this monetary hardship as the cost it takes to produce another unit of a thing. This refers to the marginal costs in production. But what is this S2F ratio calculated from? Stock could be translated as stock, while flow stands for new creation or inflows. Thus, the stock-to-flow benchmark measures the relationship between the existing stock of any commodity—gold, silver, platinum, or Bitcoin—and its annual creation or production.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/25.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b6809f42-7fff-9dfb-427b-a3996b3d19e6\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 4: Stock-to-flow comparison of different assets.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: Pascal Hügli (author’s own presentation/work))</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A high stock-to-flow value is an indication of the </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">hardship</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> of a corresponding good. The higher the stock compared to the new creation (flow), the less the supply of a good can be influenced by the flow component. If the stocks of the commodity in question are hoarded, which is encouraged by a good with a high stock-to-flow ratio, there is a clear shortage in the market as demand increases. If there is scarcity, supply and demand are not in balance. A shortage occurs when demand is higher than supply at any given time. If the flow component is difficult to influence, hardly any new flow will come onto the market via new creation to counteract the shortage. The result is a high stock-to-flow ratio, which is expressed in a high price for the commodity in question. (Hard) Money is conceptually inherent in the sense that demand is always greater than supply, precisely because the latter is difficult to influence and consequently results in a high stock-to-flow ratio over time. Unlike other commodities, such as gold, Bitcoin\'s stock-to-flow ratio can be accurately predicted. The reason for this is the new creation of Bitcoin, which is algorithmically determined and therefore transparently predictable.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span><div style=\"\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/26.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"><br></span><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-297d0d89-7fff-cc04-efc4-1b80483469ba\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 5: Approximately every four years, the amount of Bitcoin distributed per ten minutes halves. These events are called halvings.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: CMC Markets)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Bitcoin\'s suitability as a store of value is thus expressed in a high stock-to-flow ratio, as large quantities of it are hoarded and relatively few new units come into circulation. A high stock-to-flow ratio is a necessary, but not sufficient, condition for money. Also, a high stock-to-flow ratio is a required feature of hard money. At the same time, the key figure says nothing about how market participants value the commodity in question. It is merely an economic concept that helps to distinguish between monetary and non-monetary goods. However, in order for a good with a high stock-to-flow ratio to actually be perceived as money, the monetary properties explained at the beginning of the chapter must also be present. Applied to Bitcoin, the writing can be summarized: The steadily increasing stock-to-flow ratio makes the crypto asset excellently hoardable and is in turn an indication of its hardness as money. As we have seen, Bitcoin also has those properties due to its high divisibility, uniformity, durability, and transportability that also make it suitable money. The discussion about the volatility of Bitcoin can be supplemented by a few thoughts at this point. </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">For example, the stock-to-flow model as an economic model allows assumptions to be made about the volatility of Bitcoin, especially if you use the example of gold. Along with Bitcoin, gold has one of the highest stock-to-flow ratios. As we know from history, this has grown over the past 5000 years, and gold is considered relatively stable in price today. It can therefore be concluded that, in monetary theory, a high stock-to-flow ratio could gradually translate into low volatility. Theoretically, at least, it is the case that high stocks (stock) increase the probability ceteris paribus (Latin for: all other things being equal) that negative supply shocks or positive demand shocks can be absorbed in the price. Potential supply in the form of stocks can leave the hoards at any time and have a stabilizing effect on the price. The counterplay and example are provided by raw materials from the physical world: oil and gold. (Krüger, 2021) The stock-to-flow ratio of crude oil is very low, which explains the large price fluctuations when there are supply-side distortions. In the case of gold, on the other hand, the high stock-to-flow ratio has a price-dampening effect. For Bitcoin, this could mean that once its monetization phase, which follows an S-shaped curve, is completed, the Bitcoin price should become less volatile due to the steadily growing stock-to-flow ratio.&nbsp;This conclusion is contradicted by the fact that Bitcoin\'s stock-to-flow ratio has been increasing by leaps and bounds every four years due to its halving since the cryptoasset\'s creation. As a result, Bitcoin has an ever-increasing stock-to-flow ratio, but it is not stable precisely because it needs both a high stock and a steady, stable flow for stable money. If one of the two is not given, (high) volatility and a decrease in the character of money are the logical consequences.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><b>Good to know: Predict the Bitcoin price?</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The stock-to-flow model gained notoriety in the Bitcoin world after a financial analyst named PlanB tried to model the future Bitcoin price with it. He did this by orienting himself on other goods (especially precious metals) and applying the phases they had gone through in reaching their respective stock-to-flow ratios to Bitcoin. This led him to postulate impressive to improbable figures in his article \"Modeling Bitcoin with Scarcity\": In 2045, according to the model, one Bitcoin should be worth 235,000,000,000 US dollars. If the model were further calculated, the Bitcoin price would eventually converge towards infinity. In addition to enthusiasm, PlanB also received a lot of criticism. So the pseudonymous financial analyst doubled down and published an adjusted version of his stock-to-flow forecast. With \"price predictions\" of up to 288,000 US dollars by the end of 2024, he made music to the ears of Bitcoiners. The fact that the stock-to-flow model would correctly predict future price development based on past data points is by definition impossible. Past results can never be converted into future returns with absolute certainty. Also, the model only takes into account the supply side, but not the demand side. The model is most likely to be partially confirmed in the sense of a self-fulfilling prophecy, as the past correlation shows. For a long time, the model seemed to accurately predict the Bitcoin price before it collapsed at the end of 2021.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">It seems that Bitcoin is currently to be considered proto-money. For example, it will take a few more decades and thus halvings for Bitcoin before the monetization phase comes to an end. With each additional halving, the halving of supply decreases in its absolute significance until the flow is finally close to zero and thus de facto stable.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.27; text-align: justify; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.3.2.2 Insurance against currency devaluation</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The digital scarcity is of great importance for Bitcoin and its general perception. As an absolutely scarce commodity, Bitcoin is not only optimally transferable in time, but due to its digitality, Bitcoin can also be transferred globally as bits and bytes, which is why the cryptoasset is designed in synthesis from a monetary theory point of view for optimal transfer over space and time. We have already addressed the justified criticism of Bitcoin and its price instability, which makes it an unsuitable everyday medium of exchange, further in this chapter. We would like to address the argument that volatility makes Bitcoin unsuitable as an optimal store of value at this point. Again and again, it is complained that the recurring price fluctuations of Bitcoin are proof that the crypto value cannot store its value well. How can Bitcoin be considered an excellent means of storing value when the cryptoasset corrects by up to 70% in just a few months after any all-time high? The answer to this question lies in perspective.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; text-align: justify; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In the short term, Bitcoin is indeed volatile. However, this should not obscure the fact that the cryptoasset should live up to its role as a predestined store of value in the long term due to the digital scarcity and other monetary properties. Until then, Bitcoin is therefore seen as a new kind of life insurance against the rampant increase in the money supply. The protection that Bitcoin offers is particularly evident when other investments are compared to the expansion of the money supply. In general, Swiss investors live in the belief that they have done extremely well if they have invested in the Swiss Market Index (SMI) over the past few years. Its exchange rate has risen sharply measured in Swiss francs. However, if one compares the Swiss benchmark index not with its CHF valuation But with the Swiss monetary aggregate M2—a rough indicator of how much money is being created in Switzerland—then a different picture emerges: Until the financial crisis of 2008, Swiss equities were still able to keep pace with the expansion of the money supply. After that, a decoupling set in, and the shares fell behind the increase in money. As the following chart illustrates: If you choose the right denominator, i.e., the expansion of the money supply, the exchange rate of the SMI has remained flat since 2008. In other words, the increase in the money supply undermines the productivity gains of the Swiss economy, and the price gains of SMI investors are nominal but not real. Bitcoin was launched in January 2009. If you know about the decoupling just described, then the launch of Bitcoin at this exact time seems like a divine act with perfect timing. Thus, Bitcoin was able to defy the expansion of the money supply from day one. Its performance since its inception has been impressive, making it one of the few global assets that has provided investors with a real return rather than a nominal one.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/27.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: center; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-7b9f73b7-7fff-ecdc-27cb-a27c70a72fee\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Figure 6: Until the financial crisis of 2008, Swiss equities were still able to keep pace with the expansion of the money supply. After that, a decoupling set in, and the shares fell behind the increase in money.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">(Source: SNB &amp; Yahoo Finance)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The chart below impressively shows that even if the expansion of the money supply is included in the Bitcoin price, it is able to reflect the Bitcoin price in Swiss francs quite accurately.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/28.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f50e3dc9-7fff-2530-20fc-ec2192650f45\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 7: Approximately every four years, the amount of Bitcoin distributed per ten minutes halves. These events are called halvings.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: SNB&amp; 21Shares)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Whether as a store of value or insurance against money accumulation, Bitcoin represents a new type of asset that stands in stark contrast to the various current forms of government money. It is this otherness that makes Bitcoin a serious payment or savings alternative despite price volatility—measured in government currencies.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.3.2.3 Caesura in Monetary Theory: Bitcoin as Monetized Time</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As explained in the course of this chapter, the answer to the question of whether Bitcoin represents money depends on which definition of money is assumed. For example, Bitcoin fulfills some properties of money better than any money before. Bitcoin has not yet been able to establish itself as a generally accepted means of payment. Its price instability is too strong compared to the various means of payment prescribed by the state. Whether Bitcoin can ever be stable in price is currently an open question. Its scarcity (more precisely, supply restriction) makes Bitcoin inflexible and prevents quantitative adjustment to demand shocks. The relevance of any demand shocks could be reduced by a deeper, more liquid market for Bitcoin. The higher the liquidity and the greater the market depth, the more effectively the market can absorb even demand shocks. But why should the liquidity of the Bitcoin market increase over time and a steadily growing number of players hold Bitcoin when the crypto asset is not stable in price and is therefore not suitable as a means of payment? Paradoxically, the key lies in the supply constraint, which means that Bitcoin is generally perceived as a scarce commodity. </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">This scarcity makes people discover Bitcoin as stable in value and therefore as a suitable store of value. But not for the short term, but for the long term. The reason why Bitcoin is an excellent store of value in the long term is its absolute scarcity and the fact that Bitcoin\'s rising marginal costs in production are dictated by the Bitcoin protocol code and are in principle infinitely high. No matter how great the effort, miners can never mine more Bitcoin than is provided by the algorithm at any given time. One could therefore conclude: Bitcoin is exponentially potentiated gold. The implication of this is groundbreaking: Bitcoin is not fundamentally tied to energy expenditure but actually to time expenditure or, better, to an unchanging timeline. The difficulty adjustment ensures that Bitcoin\'s predefined issuance schedule of new Bitcoin units released by the Bitcoin protocol is constant and cannot be shaken by any amount of energy. In other words, Bitcoin is the first money that is immune to technological progress. A money like gold, whose marginal costs in production are increasing but never infinite, is theoretically infinitely scalable in its production. After all, every technological innovation that leads to more efficient energy conversion makes it possible to produce more money. Due to the presence of infinitely high marginal costs in production, Bitcoin ensures that for the first time there is a monetary resource that is not subject to technological improvements in energy conversion.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/29.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-ba24d6f4-7fff-6271-b17a-66b225525f3f\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 8: For every good on this earth, a higher price leads to increased production of the same good, because production is more profitable due to the higher price. Bitcoin\'s supply curve is completely inelastic. As the price rises, no more Bitcoin can be produced than the protocol code releases.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: Unchained Capital https://unchained.com/blog/all-21-million-bitcoin-already-exist/)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Time is the only resource of which we humans have never been able to create more so far and which is therefore absolutely scarce. As described by the American professor Julian Simon, it can therefore be considered the ultimate resource. This resource perfectly replicates Bitcoin. The crypto asset is monetized time. Bitcoin cannot be created faster by more energy, nor by more power or violence, but only by more time. However, since humanity has not yet been able to speed up or slow down time, the release of new Bitcoin cannot be influenced by any conceivable kind of effort. This makes the crypto asset the ultimate store of value.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.3.2.4 Answer to the Money Question: Bitcoin as the New Base Money</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In this respect, Bitcoin actually represents a monetary revolution. Never before has humanity had a monetary resource of global renown, which is absolutely scarce and infinite in its marginal production costs. For this uniqueness and monetary innovation, Bitcoin is also in demand. The theoretical question of if Bitcoin is money is receding into the background because of this fact. More and more people seem to answer this question for themselves with yes. This is shown in the following graphic.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/30.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-24b1be64-7fff-b783-586c-5e2b48de83fa\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 9: This chart shows the realized market capitalization, which only increases when a Bitcoin unit is revalued. The fact that this key figure is rising can be seen as an indication of new capital inflows, which in turn can be read as an increase in acceptance on the part of users.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><a href=\"https://twitter.com/WuBlockchain/status/1462783508514967555/photo/1\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; color: rgb(5, 99, 193); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">https://twitter.com/WuBlockchain/status/1462783508514967555/photo/1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></a><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A nuance that does not seem very clear at this point in time: Assuming we consider Bitcoin to be money, then it is fundamentally a new digital base money. As such, it serves as the basis for other monetary financial instruments based on it. The latter also includes currencies, the actual economic term for the thing that is (mis)understood by the general public today as money. But money is not just money but, in its existence, multi-layered and multifaceted. In order to better understand Bitcoin, money, and financial systems, this differentiation between base money and its higher-order forms of money is indispensable. Probably the best-known base money is gold. This has served as an anchor of value for other money based on it for centuries, including paper currencies. It was only when these were finally detached from gold that state money became so-called fiat money and currencies became the most widely used type of money as money surrogates. From then on, state currencies were considered fiat money, as they were no longer backed by an underlying asset often referred to as an intrinsic value—like gold—but could now be created without gold backing. Today, the dominant base money is money created by central banks. With digitalization, money has become increasingly dependent on intermediaries. As end users, we now operate mainly with money surrogates, the use of which is orchestrated by intermediaries (institutionalized counterparties). This means that at present, the use of money is generally database-based.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><b>Good to know: Fiat money is not unbacked money</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The term \"fiat\" comes from Latin and can be translated as \"to arise.\" In the creation story of the Bible, there is talk of \"Fiat Lux,\" which can be translated in English as \"Let there be light\" and symbolically describes a creation out of nothing. In the analogy, this terminology has therefore been established for unbacked paper money. But it is actually wrong. Although basic government money is unbacked today, it is issued in exchange for an equivalent value—usually government bonds. This means that fiat money can only be created by the central bank today against equivalent values that it has on the asset side in its books.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Even the base money issued by the central bank is ultimately database-based money, as it exists on the basis of a ledger or register and is issued through a balance sheet. The continued existence of such a database (ledger) must be ensured by human intervention. The reason for this irrefutable fact lies in the nature of the digital. By its very nature, the digital is virtual and thus always and everywhere an abstraction of the real (Sebag, 2022)—an abstraction that must be maintained and cannot exist by itself. Gold, on the other hand, is a non-database-based base money. There is no ledger in which the gold holdings must be kept in order for them to exist. The precious metal exists by laws of nature and out of itself. Only the historical money surrogates, such as bills of exchange or banknotes, which were denominated in gold, were in turn database-based and were issued via the balance sheet of an issuer (Hügli, 2021). </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Bitcoin is also an unprecedented special case in this respect. While the cryptoasset is also database-based, Bitcoin is unlike any other </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">database-based (base) money. As the first functioning implementation, the crypto asset is database-based base money that replicates the properties of non-database-based base money and therefore holds it. This is another manifestation of Bitcoin\'s monetary breakthrough: Although it is actually a database-based base money, Bitcoin feels more like a non-database-based base money in its concrete and practical use. The cryptocurrency can be described as a </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">digital bearer instrument, also known as a coin, which can be held independently and without the help of third parties. In the same way, Bitcoin can be transferred directly from person to person, also known as peer-to-peer. What distinguishes non-database-based money as base money is the fact that it does not require any trust. Thus, physical gold has always eluded any convention in its existence as a material asset—matter remains matter and, as such, depends neither on human faith nor human action. This is why gold is commonly described as trustless. The same is currently being said about Bitcoin, although the cryptoasset is also a database-based base money. As a digital base money with gold properties, higher types of money can be launched on Bitcoin, which hardly have to make do with compromises in terms of these properties. Thus, Bitcoin is the first base money that is not issued by an institutionalized counterparty and at the same time enables Bitcoin money surrogates that are also issued by a protocol and not by an institutionalized counterparty in the traditional sense. Given this novelty and the monetary revolution triggered by Bitcoin, it seems obvious that the textbooks on monetary theory need to be rewritten. This work provides a first contribution (Hügli &amp; Lanni, 2022).</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">\n</span></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></div></span></span></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-09 09:49:33','2026-01-01 06:57:32'),(28,14,'The Internet of Money','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f51ebaec-7fff-df10-f80a-1e5f02db926a\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In the previous chapter, we explained the reasons why Bitcoin is a new, digital base money. As an independent, independently based money, the crypto asset exists and functions within the Bitcoin network, which exists independently of state currencies and the traditional financial infrastructure. As we argue in this chapter, Bitcoin as a base money forms a solid foundation for a new financial order. In order to understand Bitcoin in its entirety, it is important to shed light on its numerous facets. In its most basic form, Bitcoin represents pure information. Although more and more people consider it to be a unit of value, Bitcoin does not exist physically but as virtual entries in a decentralized database. It is only human action, the interaction between miners, full nodes, and users, that ultimately brings Bitcoin to life. Like everything virtual, Bitcoin seems to follow the 3rd law of the British science fiction writer and physicist Arthur C. Clark: \"Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.\" (Clarke, n.d.)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.4.1.1 A protocol creates Internet-specific values</span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If we move away from this abstract level, we can classify Bitcoin somewhat more approachably as a technical implementation of software and hardware. As a new Internet protocol (IP), Bitcoin can be compared to other network protocols in the entire Internet protocol family. These include, for example, TCP, SMTP, or HTTP. BTC (Bitcoin) is to be seen as a new addition to this and establishes the monetary level of the Internet.</span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-d4fbe211-7fff-0815-774a-890c5e0fb09c\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/31.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 1: Bitcoin is considered another addition to the internet\'s family of basic protocols.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: Pantera Capital)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The comparison with other Internet protocols underlines the significance of Bitcoin and also points to its potential as an open-source protocol for the transmission of Internet values. The Internet and Bitcoin are complementary technologies. This is how Bitcoin lives on the internet, which gives it its global, cross-border character. In this respect, Bitcoin is to be seen as a complementary complement that expands the Internet of global communication to include the Internet of global value exchange.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for nerds: Using Bitcoin offline</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Since Bitcoin is pure information, Bitcoin can be transmitted not only over the Internet but also over other telecommunication media. Although the Internet is the most intuitive way of transmission, Bitcoin can also be transferred by means of any other telecommunications technology. For example, by sending an SMS or through the use of radio waves.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.4.1.2 The Value of Institutions</span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If we switch from a technical perspective to a socio-economic one, we can see Bitcoin and the public blockchain technology on which Bitcoin is based as a new type of institution (Allen et al., 2020) populating the internet. As a new institutional technology (Berg et al., 2019), it creates a new institutional framework that allows people to cooperate and interact with each other globally in a new and expanded way. Institutions shape all of our lives like hardly anything else. They are so close to us and yet so far away. Although confronted with them every day, most of the time we no longer notice them at all. Nevertheless, they are indispensable; they are the glue that holds societies together. By analogy, we can think of institutions as the social brain. Society as a whole forms a living, complex organism, and institutions are its brain, which enables the smoothest possible interaction between the individual parts of the body (actors within society). There is a reason why we hardly notice the institutions around us, and it is a good thing. As the social brain, the institutions function as an autonomic nervous system that allows us humans to function in this complex social organism without having to put every single action with other people through its paces. The act of institutionalization is ultimately the unconscious and therefore scalable creation of trust structures. Institutions of all kinds help us humans to scale human interaction. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Thus, the individual person is more successful and better off when he interacts and works together with other people. The history of mankind could therefore also be interpreted simplistically as a never-ending attempt to establish institutionalized trust structures for mutual cooperation. Mutual trust is a prerequisite for cooperation, and cooperation is the prerequisite for division of labor. This, in turn, is the foundation of our prosperity. Our current economic and social system, with its numerous institutions, is the product of a development process that has lasted thousands of years. It is characterized by the desire to create mutual trust and thus reduce transaction costs in interaction with other people. This has also been achieved with the help of formal and informal institutions. The former include, for example, constitutions, laws, treaties, various organizations, and regulators, while the latter include social norms, customs, and traditions. Above all, institutions have enabled us humans to protect property. The most relevant institution in this regard is the nation-state, which holds the monopoly on the rule of law and force and ensures institutionalized law and social order.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.4.1.3 Basic building blocks of trust</span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Today, the nation/state is the most important institution in social affairs. This has not always been the case over human history. Institutions, and with them their importance, have always changed over time. But the basic building blocks that make up an institution have always remained the same: technology, incentives, and the human element. It is a combination of these three components that breeds trust. As a historical analysis shows, institutions, in their general evolution, have always tended to ignore the human element in favor of the other two elements. The progressive evolution of institutions should therefore be described as a process in which the influence and thus the importance of human trust as a prerequisite for social interaction steadily diminishes with each evolutionary step of development. This is how the first attempts at coordination between people in the clan took place. The archetype of an institution was represented by shamans or chiefs. It was up to them to set rules for social interaction and to enforce these rules. In the course of history, these proto-institutions were formalized and thus cast in a framework that allowed for a reduction of the human element of trust. Monarchies with kings at the top followed and dominated the institutional picture for a long time. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Their trump card consisted primarily in political efficiency and less in the reduction of human trust elements. A new push, which further reduced the weight of the human element, occurred with the advent of the nation-state based on the separation of powers. The clever splitting of positions of power reduced the likelihood of human abuse of power. To paraphrase Lord Acton, the effort since time immemorial has been to reduce the power of the human element in institutions in order to curb the possibility of human abuse of power. With the advent of Bitcoin and public blockchain technology, the proportion of the human element in building trust can once again be greatly reduced. To an unprecedented extent, this new type of institution manages to prioritize the \"incentives\" and \"technology\" components over the human element. Areas that required the human element in conventional institutions are replaced by a clever combination of incentive structures, mathematics, and cryptography in Bitcoin and public blockchain technology. This reduces the requirements for the human element in the creation of social trust by a few powers. As this observation shows, public blockchain technology is more than just a new optimization technology for internal company processes. Certainly, public blockchains will one day be used by organizations and companies to increase the efficiency of their own actions. However, the real relevance of this new technology lies in being a new institutional enabling technology that creates a new trust infrastructure away from nation-states in the form of public blockchains for economic interaction of people. As a consequence, this new institutional technology will unleash new forms of human organization and interaction and enable productive economic activity, especially where property rights are insufficiently enforced today.</span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/32.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-183a6855-7fff-3461-04f9-93a98d7e360e\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 2: The three building blocks of institutionalized trust: an illustration of how the new crypto networks (public blockchains) weigh these building blocks differently compared to their predecessor institutions.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: a16z: Crypto, the Future of Trust)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\">1.4.1.4 An institution with unparalleled guarantees</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As a new socio-economic institution, Bitcoin and its public blockchain have a number of economic guarantees that no other institution guarantees to this extent. These are:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Censorship resistance &amp; availability: Values can be exchanged globally by anyone in a censorship-resistant way.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Property security: Property can be managed independently (self-sovereign) and is therefore protected from arbitrary access.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Reliability: Rules are enforced reliably and predictably.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Non-inflation: Shares in the network in the form of units of value owned cannot be diluted.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Transparency &amp; verifiability: The integrity of the system can be fully verified at all times. In addition to Bitcoin, the goal of other public blockchains is also to be able to guarantee most of these economic guarantees. Bitcoin is generally considered the most secure of all public blockchains. That is why Bitcoin\'s economic guarantees are among the most reliable and strongest.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Table talk: Safest of all</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">No other public blockchain has a larger hashrate, as the figures show. This also means that no other blockchain is as secure. This fact results from the following logic: The higher the hashrate, the more computing power and thus energy the Bitcoin network secures. As the hashrate increases, trust in Bitcoin\'s security ultimately increases. Bitcoin\'s proof-of-work algorithm is also its defense mechanism. Bitcoin \"consumes\" energy in the form of electricity and converts it into a kind of \"digital wall\" to protect the network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The fact that other public blockchains currently do not have the same security as Bitcoin is not necessarily due to a design flaw but to the fact that the Bitcoin blockchain has more cumulative work and thus effort for a successful attack per unit of time. Due to this fact, we want to take a closer look at these economic guarantees in the light of Bitcoin: Censorship resistance &amp; availability: Bitcoin is permissionless, and anyone can participate in the network without restrictions. There is no central control body that would have to authorize access to Bitcoin or transactions with it. Users of Bitcoin are not identified by their personal names or IP addresses but by means of a cryptographic key pair, consisting of a public and private key. To receive Bitcoin, all you need is a Bitcoin address. Transactions are sent by propagating them into the Bitcoin network. The spread of a Bitcoin transaction in the network and thus the execution of the same cannot be censored, as there is no central point of contact through which a transaction would have to enter the Bitcoin network. The dissemination of the transaction takes place in a decentralized manner on the basis of the peer-to-peer principle. Once a Bitcoin transaction has made it into the Bitcoin blockchain, the transaction is also increasingly secured over time, which also makes a possible reversal increasingly difficult. Bitcoin\'s censorship resistance is superior to many other value processing systems from the traditional world, as these can often be corrupted more easily than Bitcoin by political will.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Table Talk: The Financial System as a Political Weapon</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It is an undisputed, even deliberate fact that today\'s dollar-dominated financial system is used as a political weapon, and its resistance to censorship is not unlimited. For example, the United States maintains an Office for the Control of Foreign Assets (OFAC), whose task is to enforce economic and financial sanctions. Especially since the Second World War, financial sanctions have become more and more common. They are enforced via payment systems and their global settlement networks, such as Fedwire or CHIPS.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Property security: Bitcoin has an inherent, independent ownership system. In contrast to the conventional financial system, in which legal structures and local authorities create a legal system for property and, if necessary, enforce it, it is the decentralized network and cryptography that enforce property security in Bitcoin. Bitcoin can be held by means of independent control of a private key that is in the name of the corresponding Bitcoin. Thus, Bitcoin is to be understood as a non-counterparty asset that can be held without a third party and thus counterparty risk. Because access is only possible via the private access key, Bitcoin\'s ownership system, which is independent of traditional structures, has a high resistance to confiscation by third parties. Especially in regions of the world where citizens have to reckon with arbitrary confiscations due to weak state property rights, the Bitcoin ownership system provides great added value.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/33.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-df353a81-7fff-603d-048a-0d0358819f4b\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 3: Degree of sound asset protection for different assets.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Ark Invest: A Novel Economic Institution)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Reliability: Rules are enforced in the Bitcoin system on a protocol basis in a reliable and predictable manner. It is Bitcoin\'s software that formalizes the rules that apply within the network. These are enforced by the globally distributed full nodes. Anyone who tries to go against the rules will be rejected by the majority of full nodes. Software changes remain meaningless unless they are accepted by a significant majority of Null nodes. Non-inflation: Bitcoin\'s monetary policy is clearly defined and set in stone. There will never be more than 21 million Bitcoin units within the Bitcoin system. A Bitcoin always remains a Bitcoin. As a Bitcoin holder, you don\'t have to fear dilution. The proportion of Bitcoin you own always remains the same relative to the rest of the total. Since Bitcoin is nobody\'s obligation, it is not issued as a debt relationship by a traditional counterparty at the base money level. This means that the creation of new Bitcoin is not preceded by debt by a third party. At the same time, there is no single issuer that could independently override the 21 million upper limit. In this capacity, Bitcoin is very different from our current financial system, in which the base money supply is hardly limited. Central banks have an explicit mandate to guarantee price stability. This obligation requires a flexible monetary policy on the part of the central bank, which allows it to expand or decrease the base money supply. In reality, there is above all an inflation of the base money supply, which results in a continuous devaluation of the corresponding monetary unit. Transparency &amp; verifiability: While accurate verification of the (base) money supply is difficult for traditional financial institutions such as central banks and commercial banks, the rules implemented by Bitcoin can be checked for integrity by anyone at any time and around the clock with the help of dedicated Bitcoin-native software instruments. In this way, Bitcoin holders—their full nodes—can always ensure that they are protected from verifiability: unwanted rule changes or dilution of the Bitcoin base money supply. These economic guarantees are relentlessly and uncompromisingly enforced on the Bitcoin blockchain and create the basis for a new financial order under alternative auspices. Bitcoin provides these guarantees to an extent that no other institution on a global scale has been able to provide to date.</span></span></span></span></p><div>\n</div></span></span></div></span></span></div></div></div></div></span></span></div></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-09 09:57:38','2026-01-01 07:01:44'),(29,14,'Public blockchains as the basis for a financial order','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f52b14e3-7fff-5273-457e-25215910eef7\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Blockchain technology establishes the possibility of creating new financial orders, each of which exists natively on a corresponding public blockchain as an independent financial order. The development of these new financial orders is in full swing right now, as illustrated by the emergence of different public blockchains and their ecosystems. True to the previous focus of this textbook, we want to look at the schematic-prototypical structure of such a new financial order using the example of Bitcoin. However, before we take a closer look at Bitcoin\'s new financial order, let\'s first take a look at the current financial system.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\">1.4.2.1 The hierarchy of the financial system</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The current financial system is inherently hierarchical and multi-layered. The financial system itself is subject to the hierarchy of money, in which basic money forms the basis for further money surrogates. This hierarchy and multi-layeredness is what makes the current financial system what it is in the first place. Without this multi-tiered structure, in which specific settlement facilities form the foundation for a multitude of other layers and institutions that build on each other, the financial system as a whole would hardly be scalable and would be unable to handle the vast volume of transactions and financial operations. As an end user of fintech applications, you trigger settlement processes distributed across numerous levels. Fintechs often operate on the basis of Visa or Mastercard. Credit card companies like these, on the other hand, have traditional banking relationships. These traditional banks rely on a network of international correspondent banks that are one level above the local central banks and eventually above their settlement systems. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It is only this layer-like structure of our current financial system that enables the efficiency that we know from everyday transactions using credit or debit cards or mobile payments. While the former are instantaneous, the payments are only finally processed via the underlying levels in the following days. So what comes in real time only learns the so-called final settlement days later. In the following, we want to look at this multi-layered structure in detail. The focus is to be primarily on the payment infrastructure. In English, this infrastructure is also referred to as the \"payment stack.\" This multi-layered entity is an essential part of the current financial system. For explanation purposes, the payment infrastructure is to be divided into six different, interdependent layers in descending order of precedence:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Application level</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Processing level</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Payment account level</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Connection level</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Message layer</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Settlement level</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Each of these layers fulfills an essential function within the multi-tiered payment infrastructure. One should not forget: In reality, the demarcations between the individual classes are not always clear. Application level: At this level, a payment via an application is initiated by an end user. Either by means of a physical payment card (credit, debit, or prepaid card) or by means of mobile payment solutions. The latter is linked to a payment card. Examples of application service providers are Apple Pay, PayPal, and Revolut. Traditional or retail banks can also take on this function. Processing level: The application service providers forward the payment details of a payment to the processing service providers. These are primarily technology providers that bring banks and card networks together and help merchants and end-users accept and process credit, debit, and prepaid payments. Processing service providers ensure communication with the application level. They also check transaction details, ensure that funds are available, and enforce anti-fraud measures. Examples of processing service providers are individual banks themselves, but above all lesser-known companies such as First Data or Vantiv. Payment account level: Payment account service providers are located at the third level. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">These allow merchants and end users to execute or receive payments. While end-users usually access their account via a top-level application service provider, merchants rely on the processing service providers. Examples of payment account providers are SIX Payments, Payrexx, and PayPal. Connection level: The various payment account providers in turn use entities at the connection level. Here, it is connection service providers such as banks that provide access to messaging and settlement services. They ensure that end-users and merchants have access to funds and lines of credit and that they are connected to the underlying layers. In many cases, connection service providers are the only ones who have access to these underlying layers. Non-banks that provide payment account services to end-users or merchants must maintain accounts with banks in order to process payments through them through these accounts. Examples of connection service providers are banks or non-banks such as PayPal. Message layer: Messaging service providers enable communication between payment senders and payees. They are responsible for the flow of money orders that runs between the banks involved in payment transactions. The payment information sent through messaging services enables the authorization and clearing of payment transactions. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">At this level, only settlement instructions are transmitted. The final settlement takes place one level below. Examples include payment card networks such as Visa or the SWIFT system. Settlement level: Up to this level, no payment has been finally settled. Only the settlement service providers bring about the actual payment processing between the sender and recipient of the payment. The settlement can be done on a gross basis so that each transaction is processed individually. The situation is different if payments are offset on a net basis. Credits and debits are periodically offset against each other, after which the outstanding net amount is settled in one transaction. Examples of settlement services include Fedwire, CHIPS, ACH, Target2, or SIC. In order to smoothly execute the high number of payment transactions that today\'s financial system handles on a daily basis, the multi-layered financial system must function around the clock. The different levels are mutually dependent; each level has specific service providers who perform tasks and thus complete the overall picture as individual puzzle pieces. It is only the interaction of all levels and components that makes the financial system what it is today. The whole is more than the sum of its parts. Without this complex order, it would not be possible to scale financial transactions, i.e., to efficiently carry out as many transactions as possible as quickly as possible, and to serve a broad mass.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\">1.4.2.2 Bitcoin as a multi-layered financial order</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin scales no differently than the traditional financial system. Its modular scaling method creates a multi-layered financial order. This development was not clear from the beginning. Bitcoin was introduced by Satoshi Nakamoto as a peer-to-peer electronic cash system, which led many early Bitcoin pioneers to view the Bitcoin network as a decentralized competitor to PayPal. Over time, the idea of what Bitcoin actually is. The longer it went on, the more the focus was no longer on the network but on the unit of value associated with the asset gold. Not a payment network, but censorship-resistant, scarce digital gold would represent Bitcoin. Thus, the narratives and perspectives on what Bitcoin actually is. A little more than twelve years after Bitcoin\'s creation, it seems increasingly clear: Bitcoin is money and a payment network at the same time. Both have incredible potential and are mutually reinforcing. The latter inevitably follows the former. This important nuance was already clear to Satoshi Nakamoto, which is why he chose the terms in his white paper carefully. By describing Bitcoin as an electronic cash system rather than an electronic payment system, the anonymous founder of Bitcoin pointed out between the lines a subtlety that is commonly overlooked. Cash has a very important feature: a cash payment is always immediately final, i.e., processed immediately. Cash is base money and typically refers to a base monetary value of a settlement infrastructure. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Against this background, it seems obvious that Satoshi Nakamoto must have intended to introduce the Bitcoin blockchain as a new basic settlement infrastructure for a blockchain-owned base money. Bitcoin was probably intended from the beginning as a base money, which would be supplemented by a PayPal- or Visa-like payment network as development progressed. The innovation over traditional systems is that while gold is base money, it does not have an inherent payment network. Payment systems such as PayPal and Visa, on the other hand, do not have an inherent base money and therefore rely on fiat currencies such as the US dollar. Bitcoin offers a synthesis here that combines the best of both worlds. A base money on which a seamless payment network that exists for the purpose of scaling Bitcoin thrives. This is one of the reasons why Bitcoin is also to be seen as super gold, moving within the trajectories of an unstoppable PayPal network. Before we dedicate ourselves to the higher layers within Bitcoin\'s financial order and their protocols and solutions, such as the Lightning Network, let\'s first take a slightly deeper look at Bitcoin, the settlement infrastructure, and the base money.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.4.2.3 Blockchain Base Layer: A Global Settlement Infrastructure</span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin, which is transferred directly on the Bitcoin blockchain and thus at the settlement level, is called \"on-chain Bitcoin.\" For the settlement infrastructure, on the other hand, the general term \"base layer\" or \"mainchain\" is used. Transactions of on-chain Bitcoin, also known as on-chain transactions, are limited in quantity, which means that Bitcoin\'s settlement infrastructure can only process a limited number of on-chain transactions due to the limited block space. This circumstance is due to the limited data capacity of Bitcoin blocks. A block holds a maximum of 1 megabyte of data. Although this block size limit can be extended somewhat thanks to technical implementations such as SegWit, the block size remains limited. The minimum data size required for a Bitcoin transaction is 61 bytes. (Georgiadis, 2019) Consequently, a Bitcoin block can theoretically hold a maximum of about 16,393 transactions (1,000,000 bytes divided by 61 bytes). Blocks are produced every ten minutes on average. This means that 144 Bitcoin blocks are added to the blockchain in a single day. If we multiply this number by the theoretical maximum number of transactions, the result is a total of 2,360,592 transactions that Bitcoin can process per day via its base layer. This equates to a maximum transaction throughput of 27 transactions per second (tps).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for nerds: A kind of purification for the blockchain</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">SegWit can be used to increase the block size of a blockchain by storing signature data removed from transactions. When certain parts of a transaction are removed, space or capacity is freed up to add further transactions to the chain. Since most of the space in a transaction consists of a signature, a considerable amount of \"block space\" can be freed up by making it more efficient. In 2017, SegWit was added to Bitcoin.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In reality, Bitcoin transactions are many times larger than just 61 bytes. As a result, the number of transactions per day is much lower. For 2021, the 200-day moving average is just over 300 000 transactions per day. (COINMETRICS, n.d.) The Bitcoin base layer recorded the most transactions ever recorded in one day with 498,142 transactions on December 14, 2017. It therefore has a similar function to that performed in the traditional system at the settlement level by the Fedwire system or CHIPS: final settlement of higher-ranking transactions. In the first quarter of 2021, Fedwire processed 796,733 transactions per day, more than twice as many as the Bitcoin mainchain, whose 315,290 Bitcoin transactions were processed in the same period. The Fedwire system is also limited in its transaction throughput to a maximum transaction throughput due to conflicting technological goals. Just like Fedwire, Bitcoin scales with the size and revenue value of its transactions, not their frequency. This means that it is not the number of transactions that should be maximized at the lowest level, but rather the value of each transaction, i.e., the total transaction value.</span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/34.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b41da8c5-7fff-7569-0f46-3ce710306880\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 4: Bitcoin finally settled around $45 trillion via its settlement infrastructure in 2021. That is twice as much as in all previous years combined.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: Ark Invest: A Novel Economic Institution)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The higher the total transaction value of on-chain transactions, the higher the economic density of the Bitcoin blockchain. It results from the value of all transactions implemented via the base layer, divided by the data throughput provided by Bitcoin. Total transaction value divided by the bytes, because in the end it is bytes that Bitcoin handles. As a historical perspective shows, Bitcoin\'s economic density is increasing because more and more transaction value per byte is being processed via the Bitcoin blockchain. As this perspective inevitably makes us understand, Bitcoin\'s underlying blockchain represents a new global settlement infrastructure. Due to its infrastructural independence from the current financial system, the Bitcoin blockchain forms the foundation for a new censorship-resistant financial and transaction system. Final settlement forms the foundation of any financial order, as all financial transactions are built on top of it. The final settlement draws a line under the transactions carried out at the higher levels and enables an overall balance: Did a trade take place at all? To whom was a loan granted or a transaction made? Who ultimately owns what? What conditions have been agreed upon? Is the reported financial activity trustworthy and consistent? All of this was ensured by companies, governments, and central banks before the arrival of public blockchains. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The paradigm shift around public blockchains such as Bitcoin has made a new institutional technology possible today. (Berg et al., 2017) The Bitcoin base layer forms the foundation for the final settlement of transactions in a Bitcoin economy. By analogy, the base layer is to be understood as a container ship whose blocks are the individual containers. The individual containers all have a fixed size. In order for more and more goods to be transferred by means of this container freighter, an attempt must be made to pack more and more economic activity and thus transaction value into the individual containers. This is made possible by modular scaling, the goal of which is to scale the Bitcoin ecosystem layer by layer, thus packing more and more economic activity and transaction value into different individual containers.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\">1.4.2.4 The Lightning Network and Other Scaling Ventures</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin\'s multi-layered construction is currently in full swing. Second-layer protocols are built on the base layer, while sidechains are built in parallel. Bitcoin transactions on second-layer protocols are off-chain transactions; those on the sidechains can be called other-chain transactions. Both types of transactions have a well-defined connection to the Bitcoin blockchain, but they take place outside of it. The most popular off-chain variant is the Lightning Network. This is built directly on the Bitcoin base layer and acts as an additional protocol that allows the management of off-chain payment channels. So we can think of the Lightning Network as a superordinate network of payment channels. In order to open such a payment channel, a transaction must be initiated on the Bitcoin blockchain, which transfers the desired number of Bitcoin to the off-chain payment channel. Two Lightning users can be part of such a payment channel; at least one party must replenish it with Bitcoin units. If the parties have agreed to the establishment of the payment channel, it is open. Both players involved in the payment channel can then execute as many Bitcoin transactions as they want among themselves. After each payment, the overall balance is updated so that users in the respective payment channel can see at all times who is entitled to how many Bitcoins. Thanks to cryptography, smart contracts, and a sophisticated incentive structure, the protocol ensures that no Lightning user can scam another. In theory, payment channels can stay open indefinitely and serve any purpose. If the channel is to be closed again, another transaction is triggered on the Bitcoin blockchain. Each user receives as much Bitcoin as they are entitled to according to the current balance of the payment channel. The Bitcoin units are then back on the base layer.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Good to know: Lightning makes it possible</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Lightning Network makes it possible for Bitcoin to act as a means of payment without having to be a means of payment. How is that supposed to work? The Lightning Network can be used to process payments in all kinds of national currencies without being exposed to Bitcoin\'s price volatility. A state currency can be exchanged for Bitcoin. As a blockchain-owned asset, these Bitcoin can be sent directly around the world via the Lightning Network to a recipient address in seconds and exchanged back into dollars, euros, yen, or another national currency at the recipient\'s location. Due to the immediacy of the Lightning Network, Bitcoin\'s volatility against state currencies hardly plays a role in this case. As an open, permissionless monetary network, Bitcoin is already distributed worldwide today, not least because of its minimal infrastructure requirements for users. Also, the global liquidity of Bitcoin as an asset is increasing as the number of Bitcoin trading exchanges and Bitcoin ATMs continues to grow.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A frequently used analogy is that of the bar credit tabs. For example, there are bars that allow their customers to consume an entire evening without having to pay the same for each drink every time. Rather, the bartender keeps a record of how much a customer consumes. At the end of the evening, the customer has to pay his total balance of drinks consumed. Bitcoin, which is transferred off-chain in payment channels via the Lightning Network, is written to by the network. When they are written down to the public blockchain, they are finally settled. The base layer thus acts as the final authority and final arbiter for the Lightning Network.</span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/35.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9a730bbc-7fff-9daa-c016-523ac2ea79c9\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 5: The Lightning Network enables fast Bitcoin transactions according to the principle of the cover letter. Transactions are executed immediately but are only finally settled with a final transaction on the Bitcoin blockchain.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: Coinshares)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">By expanding Bitcoin\'s transaction throughput, the Lightning Network allows for huge scaling of Bitcoin transactions. Since the transactions take place directly between the parties involved, they do not need immediate confirmation from the entire Bitcoin network (only when they are finally settled). As a result, transaction throughput is ultimately hardly limited, and theoretically, several million transactions can be carried out per second. Whenever Lightning transactions are to be finally settled on the Bitcoin mainchain, an on-chain transaction takes place, which is used to settle as well as settle all transactions previously made in the Lightning payment channel against each other. The Lightning Network serves as a second-layer protocol for higher layers. For example, the RGB project. The Lightning Network wants to use this to offer Bitcoin more functionality by enabling a platform for the issuance and tokenization of digital assets, such as stocks, bonds, and other securities, as well as digital collectibles (NFTs). Other scaling projects that also operate on the second level are Liquid, Rootstock (RSK), Sequentia, and Stacks. While Liquid acts as a Bitcoin sidechain and enables trading platforms and market makers to make faster and confidential transactions, the other two projects aim to realize more complex financial logic via smart contracts and thus numerous transactions as they are known from the traditional financial world. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This includes financial activities such as credit transactions of all kinds, but also derivative trading platforms. On a third level, so-called financial operating systems are located, which aggregate and use the various off-chain and other-chain solutions to realize concrete services and applications. The most well-known implementation of this is Sovryn. This aggregator can be used to use stablecoins, trade derivatives, borrow credit, and more. Access to these financial operating systems of the Bitcoin ecosystem is provided by various wallets. They serve as digital user interfaces to interact with sidechains or second-layer protocols. Well-known wallets for using sidechains are MetaMask and Liquality. Various wallets, such as Breez Wallet or BlueWallet, however, offer the possibility to use the Lightning Network. This Bitcoin-based multi-layered financial order is still under construction. The higher levels benefit from Bitcoin\'s economic guarantees. But it is in the nature of things that you never have exactly the same security and certainty about the transactions at higher levels. However, modular scaling is and remains the most effective way to make this financial order based on Bitcoin a reality. The better and more reliably the higher levels are tied to the Bitcoin base layer, the better and more reliable the guarantees that one has at these higher levels. The Bitcoin mainchain thus provides a robust foundation for numerous higher layers, with which the efficiency and speed of today\'s financial system can be achieved, if not exceeded by far.</span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/36.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e546241b-7fff-d562-aaf1-ca4b05a49e78\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 6: The multi-layered Bitcoin ecosystem is already taking shape.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Veriphi)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\">1.4.2.5 Comparing like with like</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Understanding that Bitcoin scales in different layers and divides different core functionalities across multiple, interacting protocols allows one to make meaningful and meaningful comparisons with the traditional financial system. The Bitcoin base layer should be compared with the settlement infrastructures of central banks such as Fedwire in the USA or the European Target system.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Table Talk: Fiat-Based Money Settlement System</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Central banks around the world now have their own settlement systems. These payment systems operated by them are those that ensure absolute finality in the settlement of payments in basic money. These systems are also known as large-value payment systems (LVPS). Among the best known are Fedwire (USA), TARGET (European Union), CHAPS (England), BOJ-Net (Japan), and SIC (Switzerland).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In various media, Bitcoin is still far too often compared to payment network providers such as Visa. Anyone who does this commits a category comparison error and compares apples with oranges. Thus, Visa is only one piece of the puzzle of a traditional payment system, which in turn is ultimately part of the traditional financial system. As a higher tier in this financial system, the Visa network scales and functions because the underlying layers allow it. The following example illustrates how complex this network of underlying levels is: If a person wants to pay for something with a Visa card, a Visa transaction is initiated. At the beginning of the payment file, the data of this person reaches a processing service provider. On behalf of the merchant, the counterparty to this transaction, the processing service provider processes the payment information. The latter get from there to Visa. The company then locates the bank that issued the Visa card for the payer. At this bank, a payment processor finally checks whether the information about the person in question is correct and that he or she has the necessary funds. If everything is correct, the payment processor informs the credit card company Visa, which in turn informs the processing service provider so that the Visa transaction can be carried out effectively. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">For Visa to work, the relevant information must pass through multiple databases from different actors. Visa itself is only one part of this entire transaction chain. Once the transaction has been completed, the final settlement is still to come. As we know from everyday life, credit card transactions are billed and processed with a time delay. Only at the level of the banking system and finally at the lowest level of the settlement infrastructure of central banks are transactions such as those of Visa finally settled afterwards. Compared to transactions on the Bitcoin base layer, Visa transactions are therefore not final. And the scalability of the Visa network is so high because it is based on a multi-layered structure that allows the higher-level payment network to scale. If Visa had to take over all the necessary functions and tasks itself, the company and thus the network would be overwhelmed. It could never achieve the transaction throughput that it actually guarantees today. Visa is an abstraction layer of our financial system and should therefore be correctly compared to a second-layer additional protocol such as the Lightning Network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\">1.4.2.6 For a single financial regulation</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin scales using an interplay of different, decentralized, censorship-resistant protocol solutions that rely on Bitcoin\'s base layer for security and resilience. This creates the prerequisite for a new financial order that represents a real alternative to the traditional financial system at various levels. The most fundamental difference can be found at the base money level. The base money supply in the Bitcoin system is limited to 21 million. The same cannot be said of the traditional monetary system. Its monetary base is continuously expanded by the central banks. Herein lies the fundamental difference: While a financial order based on Bitcoin is limited to an absolute amount in the base money supply, the conventional financial system knows no such limitation. This fundamental difference gives the two systems a fundamentally different appearance, as the systems operate under fundamentally different auspices, so to speak. Or to put it in concrete terms: Bitcoin\'s financial order does not allow any room for intervention at the level of the base money, while the current financial system deliberately has base money interventionist levers. The new Bitcoin financial order is characterized by other differences from the traditional financial system. Due to the public transaction history, there is greater transparency. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The base money supply can be reliably checked and audited at any time. Also, any economic activity that happens on the Bitcoin blockchain can be traced via real-time data using so-called on-chain analysis. Volumes, transaction volumes, and payment flows are public and clearly visible. Counterparties in the form of protocols are not only identifiable and their condition or solvency fully verifiable, but the counterparty risks are also different and less numerous. Today\'s financial structures are divided into fragmented individual solutions that must be kept synchronized via so-called deferred net settlement. By definition, the balance sheets and books within such a system cannot be in perfect harmony with each other. A financial order that is uniformly based on a basic layer is more interoperable in this respect. Reliability, transparency, and faster final settlement reduce the cost overhang and also result in lower transaction costs and thus fees. However, the Bitcoin base layer is not only interacted with by decentralized, non-counterparty additional protocols. Various centralized entities, above all crypto exchanges and, in the future, probably increasingly banks, offer services that are directly related to Bitcoin\'s public blockchain: for example, Bitcoin bank deposits, custody, Bitcoin-based lending transactions, and payment services. Of course, these companies maintain an internal ledger, which, unlike the Bitcoin ledger, is not publicly visible and therefore does not have to be in line with it. Anyone who uses such a central unit when using Bitcoin is confronted with classic counterparty risk and other challenges familiar from the traditional financial system. Centralized nodes will not disappear in the new Bitcoin financial order either. This does not mean that the advantageous properties of Bitcoins are lost because of this. What\'s more, they could even be used by companies to create trust. Cryptographic tools make it possible to prove directly via the public blockchain that the assets in custody actually exist. This, in turn, increases transparency and creates trust in the central counterparty.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for Nerds: Prove What You\'ve Got</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin enables cryptographic proof of custodial Bitcoin reserves. \"Proof of Reserve\" is a specific procedure in which a Bitcoin bank transparently can prove the existence of on-chain reserves in Bitcoin. In addition, it is important to cryptographically prove that the outstanding liabilities are the Bitcoin reserves on the asset side (Proof of Reliability). The latter can—thanks to cryptographic advances using so-called zero-knowledge proofs—be anonymous so that the privacy of depositors and other creditors is maintained. If \"Proof of Reserve\" and \"Proof of Liability\" match, the \"Proof of Solvency\" is proven and can be obtained.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter1/37.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0dfdca23-7fff-045c-717b-17e1f9e0ec79\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 7: The Bitcoin public blockchain is at the heart of a vibrant Bitcoin economy. In this way, it forms the settlement infrastructure that different actors use for their financial applications.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: Castle Island Ventures)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.4.2.7 Unmatched Social Scalability</span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A financial order based on a public blockchain, such as that of Bitcoin, is characterized by its social scalability (Szabo, 2017), which surpasses that of the existing financial system. Due to its openness and permission-free architecture, more people can be reached easier and served with financial services. The current financial system and its financial operations are global. The division of labor and economic trade have long since reached an international dimension. However, the traditional financial system is more like a patchwork quilt than a Persian carpet. From an end-user\'s perspective, financial transactions across borders are bumpy and never seamless. The processes and transaction channels are also not very transparent, and because of this, they are costly. In addition to technical incompatibilities, regulatory hurdles are also the problem. But the problem is a fundamental one: the current financial system requires international money and capital flows but must overcome the boundaries of individual economic and currency areas. Nation-states have their own national currency. In the case of the euro, a common currency has emerged through a supranational union of several nation-states. Whether national or supranational currencies, both are tied to an economic area and prescribed as legal tender within its territory. In the past, the main national currencies were pegged to gold. There was an obligation to redeem it, and the paper money could be redeemed for gold at the issuing central bank. Since the U.S. finally abolished the gold standard in 1971, the world has transitioned to a system of floating exchange rates. </span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The exchange rate of most currencies today is flexibly determined by the supply and demand behavior on the foreign exchange markets. From a bird\'s eye view, the current financial system is based on a kind of international barter of fictional currencies (fiat currencies). Due to the existing fragmentation into different national or supranational currencies, foreign currency markets have emerged worldwide, which document the different exchange relationships and make the exchange of individual currencies possible. However, this barter character takes its toll on international financial transactions: the exchange rate risks lead to increased transaction costs. To counteract the latter, the US dollar, as the currency of the world\'s strongest post-war economy, has developed into the reserve currency. It has thus become an internationally accepted means of payment, and in this way it counteracts the fragmented national currency market to some extent. Market participants in the US economic area in particular benefit from this prominent position (</span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">exorbitant</span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> privilege) of the US dollar. A public blockchain, for its part, provides uniform base money for other compatible money surrogates that can make a variety of financial applications possible. Even more crucial: The basic money of a public blockchain like Bitcoin is global because the blockchain itself is designed for globality. This protects such a financial order from media disruptions, unless these are enforced by regulation. However, even legal restrictions cannot necessarily stop a public blockchain, as the transaction flow occurs through decentralized nodes, which are difficult to censor. It\'s undisputed: Bitcoin and other public blockchains form the basis for the most socially scalable financial networks currently possible. (Hügli &amp; Lanni, 2022)</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></span></span></span>\n</div></div></span></span></div></div></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-09 09:59:23','2026-01-01 07:06:37'),(33,15,'Switzerland\'s success story','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a0353c6a-7fff-463f-c3c7-1491c5bb941f\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">From the \"poor man\" of Europe to the economic miracle</span></span></span></span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">More than ten years ago, a respected journalist from the Financial Times wrote, \"For nations, small is beautiful.\" If we take a look at almost every ranking of national wealth, the small countries clearly dominate it.\" His remark is particularly apt for Switzerland. In many categories, Switzerland is a comparatively small country. In terms of area, it ranks 135th out of 220 countries worldwide. It is also only slightly higher in terms of population at 99th place, but if we refer to the size of its economic performance, Switzerland is above average. In terms of gross domestic product (GDP), it is one of the 20 largest economies in the world. For a small country with a correspondingly small population, Switzerland is disproportionately wealthy. For direct comparison: Switzerland has only nine million inhabitants, but its GDP in 2018 was equivalent to that of Peru, Portugal, and Vietnam combined, which have a total of 140 million inhabitants. This combination of a relatively small country and considerable economic power means that the Swiss population is extremely wealthy. Measured by purchasing power parity (PPP), per capita income averages USD 70,000 per year. A value that is higher in only eight countries in the world. In terms of average per capita wealth, Switzerland is even at the top with USD 230,000. The Human Development Index, which takes a broader approach to measuring wealth and includes life expectancy, education, and income, places Switzerland in second place (data as of 2018).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b>1.5.1.1 A capitalist paradise</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland has a high level of prosperity and a largely equal distribution of wealth.&nbsp; With the highest per capita income of all OECD countries and few disparities in the distribution of net income. The majority of the 34 OECD countries (Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development) are industrialized nations that have committed themselves to the principles of democracy and the market economy. But how does it achieve this? A key factor is the relatively balanced distribution of gross income. Switzerland\'s dual education system and high-performing labor market ensure high employment rates and good wages for many people, with lower wages regulated by sectoral collective agreements negotiated by employers and trade unions. Since the labor market ensures equal pay, Switzerland has less need to redistribute income. In this way, it can achieve more equal distribution of net income compared to Austria, France, Germany, and Sweden, with significantly less redistribution. In this way, the country can keep its social security network small and minimize market intervention and taxes. This, in turn, ensures that the country is and remains attractive to global companies. In an article in the New York Times last year, author and economist Ruchir Sharma pointed out that Switzerland is a much better role model than the Scandinavian countries, which are so often praised by the US presidential candidates. He points to higher per capita wealth and lower inequality, noting in particular that Switzerland has achieved this position without high taxes or cumbersome bureaucracy. Switzerland, the article concludes, is a less socialist but more successful \"capitalist paradise.\"</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">1.5.1.2 Switzerland, the \"poor man\"</span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">But Switzerland has not always been an economic model of success. Towards the end of the Middle Ages, it was anything but a paradise; it was even considered the \"poor man of Europe,\" as the authors James Breiding and Gerhard Schwarz explain in a much-quoted book on the economic history of Switzerland. Just 200 years ago, they argue, Switzerland was still far from its current position as one of the richest countries in Europe when it came to the three key indicators of GDP, wages, and migration. Historical data from the Maddison Project show that the prosperity of the Swiss population in the mid-19th century, measured by GDP per capita, was lower than in today\'s G7 countries and significantly lower than in the US. Until the beginning of the 20th century, the gap between Switzerland and the USA continued to widen and only narrowed in the 1950s and 1960s. In the early 2000s, Switzerland overtook the USA. As a study by the University of Oxford shows, Switzerland performed particularly poorly in terms of wage payments. For example, between 1800 and 1913, the real wages of construction workers in the city of Zurich were about half the wage level of comparable other European cities studied. In the decades that followed, Zurich was able to catch up somewhat, but in 1910 the city was still below the level of comparable cities. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Today, as a UBS study shows, this situation has been reversed. Construction workers in Zurich earn twice as much as their colleagues in most other cities. Migration is the third indicator of a country\'s prosperity. A proven rule of thumb is that poor countries tend to have a high churn rate, while rich countries have a lot of immigration. Net migration (immigration minus emigration) was negative for many years. In the 19th century, tens of thousands of workers left Switzerland, mostly for North America or neighboring countries. In addition to the desire to settle in another country, this was mainly a consequence of poverty and the poor economic situation in a predominantly agricultural country. From the middle of the 20th century, however, the picture changed significantly. Strong immigration reversed the situation and led to a positive migration balance, where immigration was higher than emigration.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b>1.5.1.3 A varied recipe for success</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How did a small, poor country with little or no natural resources manage to become so prosperous? Or to put it another way: What are the factors that make up Switzerland\'s economic success? It is obvious that the recipe for success is diverse and complex and involves a number of factors. The country\'s political institutions have undoubtedly played an important role. In their book Why Nations Fail, economists Daron Acemoglu and James Robinson have explained in detail how important political institutions are to a country\'s prosperity. They argue that long-term economic prosperity is the result of inclusive institutions. A broad democratic distribution of power creates the conditions for a market economy and competition. Switzerland scores particularly well in this respect. It is a strongly federal country with a bottom-up structure and operates on the principle of subsidiarity. This limits the power of the state and keeps interference and the tax burden low. Federalism and the principle of broad citizen participation in public life help Swiss citizens to identify with their state, while semi-direct and consensus-oriented democracy results in a broad distribution of power between politicians, the people, and political parties. There is no other country in the world where the government has consisted of a coalition of four parties for decades. Another element is the long-standing social partnership that characterizes the relationship between employers and employees. These features combine to provide a very high level of stability, which has also been demonstrated during the COVID-19 crisis.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In addition to the advantages of political institutions, especially the federal structure, Switzerland has long had a business-friendly framework that has contributed to the country\'s economic success. The free market economy and unrestricted entrepreneurship have played a crucial role for many decades and are reflected in the country\'s liberal labor market. There is no state industrial policy, as well as low corporate taxation. Swiss companies have long had access to qualified workers because politics and business have placed particular emphasis on the quality of education and training institutions. In the 19th century, Switzerland was a pioneer in the field of national and technical education. The Federal Institutes of Technology (ETH), then called the \"Polytechnic,\" date back to this period, as does the model of vocational education and training, which is institutionally anchored in the so-called \"Federal Decree.\" The well-developed infrastructure, especially the rail and road network, is another factor in Switzerland\'s economic success. Another essential aspect that contributes to the country\'s prosperity is its international openness, not only to goods and services but also to the free movement of labor. The early focus on exports kept innovation and productivity high, but Switzerland also attracted innovators. In the 16th century, the Huguenots, expelled from France, brought their know-how in the watch industry to French-speaking Switzerland. In the 19th century, British visitors laid the foundation for the tourism industry. In the same century, immigrants founded some of the largest companies in the world today, such as ABB and Nestlé. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This open-mindedness has been an important factor in the diversification of the Swiss economy, a decisive advantage in difficult economic times. Switzerland has also benefited from the fact that it has virtually no natural resources. Countries with a significant extractive sector often find it difficult to cope with structural change. In addition, Switzerland has undoubtedly benefited from its geographical location, its size, and its cultural diversity. Since the domestic market is small, Swiss companies have had to export to neighboring countries for a long time. The linguistic similarities to large domestic markets such as Germany, France, and Italy have made this easier. Conversely, Switzerland\'s linguistic diversity has facilitated the integration of workers from neighboring countries. Throughout the 20th century, Switzerland was largely spared the devastating consequences of war. Their neutrality may have been decisive, but luck and diplomatic skills also played a role. During the Second World War, politics and business in Switzerland took a pragmatic approach and, in most cases, preferred economic interests to ideological engagement. Around 50 years after the end of the war, the country and its banks came under enormous international pressure, which damaged Switzerland\'s reputation and forced it to come to terms with its history. Swiss banking secrecy and illegal financial flows are repeatedly discussed in public but have hardly affected the country\'s overall economic success. Even in its heyday, untaxed income never exceeded 1 to 3% of Swiss GDP (Grampp et al., 2020).</span></span></span></span></p></span>\n\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-09 10:12:26','2026-01-01 07:08:23'),(52,15,'Doing business in Switzerland','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-5a834b80-7fff-e678-8ee2-936eadd1f376\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">1.5.2.1 Country Profile</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland is an ideal example of a successful multicultural and multilingual society that lives together in a peaceful way. The Swiss Confederation is a small landlocked country with an area of 41,290 km² and a population of 8.9 million. It is strategically located in the heart of Europe and shares borders with Germany, France, Italy, Austria, and Liechtenstein. The linguistic geography of Switzerland is very broad and consists of the four languages German, French, Italian, and Romansh (based on Latin and spoken by a small minority in the canton of Graubünden). English is widely spoken, especially among professionals.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">1.5.2.2 Domestic policy</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland has a stable, consensus-based system of government designed to promote direct democracy. The 26 cantons are the constituent states of the federal state of Switzerland. As a highly decentralized, genuine confederation of states, political and administrative responsibilities are divided between the federal government, the cantons, and the communes. Each canton has its own constitution, its own code of civil procedure, and its own chamber of parliament. The constitution provides for the separation of the three state powers: the Federal Assembly, the Federal Council, and the Federal Supreme Court. As Switzerland is located at the heart of the European Economic Area (EEA), there are well-established relations between Switzerland and the EU, which mainly cover trade, labor, and transport issues.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">1.5.2.3 Economic Overview</span></b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\"></b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div></div></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland is a peaceful, prosperous, and modern market economy with a GDP per capita that is among the highest in the world. The economic downturn in Switzerland was not as deep as in most other OECD countries. Due to the relatively low imbalance and the low debt burden, the Swiss economy is likely to return to pre-crisis levels faster than its Western European competitors.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">GDP: GDP is stable with positive indicators. The average annual gross domestic product fluctuates between 450 and 500 billion (US$).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Inflation: Inflation is low with constant values between 0.5 and 2%.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Unemployment: Switzerland has one of the most stable and proactive labor markets with world-class occupational pension solutions. It has the lowest unemployment figures in Europe.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Private consumption: As it is closely correlated with the development of GDP, interest rates, and the monetary environment, private consumption in Switzerland is extremely strong, which is due to a generally positive consumer sentiment.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Industrial production: Swiss industrial production focuses on high-value-added products such as pharmaceuticals, electronic devices, precision tools, and industrial machinery.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Imports/exports: Traditionally, Switzerland\'s exports far exceed imports. The reason for this is that Switzerland processes several imported goods and resells them to its trading partners at a profitable margin.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.2.4 Education system</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland claims to have one of the best education systems in the world and pays great attention to the importance of human labor. The level of education largely determines employment prospects and plays a key role in international competitiveness. Almost the entire Swiss population is able to read and write. Local education processes differ from canton to canton, but the basic structure is based on a common dual system for all cantons.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.5 Telecommunications/IT</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The state plays a leading role in the development and implementation of forward-looking, innovative, and sustainable Information and Communication Technology (ICT) solutions. The Swiss government and the private sector are important for the development and dissemination of ICT for infrastructure, content, and applications. According to the Economist Intelligence Unit, per capita spending on information and communication technology in Switzerland is among the highest in the world and well above the Western European average. IT-intensive industries such as financial services account for a large part of the economy.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.6 Transport systems</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Swiss transport system is known as one of the best in the world. The dense network of railway, bus, and tram lines and well-thought-out timetables make it possible to reach any point of the country in the shortest possible time. Every year, a lot of money is invested in transport infrastructure and road construction. Expressways and motorways connect France, Germany, Italy, Liechtenstein, and Austria. The international airports of Zurich, Geneva, Basel, and Lugano are served from all over the world and have their own train and bus stations with direct connections to all major cities in Switzerland and neighboring countries.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.7 Quality of life</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland is one of the countries with the highest quality of life, which is due to the stable political situation, the sustainable social system, and the strong economic factors. With one of the highest GDPs per capita, Switzerland has one of the lowest crime rates in the world. In addition, the quality of food and other goods and services is very high and of great importance to the population. Switzerland also offers a wide range of opportunities for leisure, recreation, culture, and sports. The country is visited by many tourists who appreciate experiencing a diverse landscape of unique beauty.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.8 Competitive Tax Environment</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland is internationally known for its favorable tax environment. For companies, most cantons in Switzerland offer special tax regulations that can reduce the already moderate tax burden to an extremely attractive level. In addition, both individuals and legal entities can benefit from double taxation treaties and bilateral agreements.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.9 State support</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland offers support at various levels to entrepreneurs who want to set up or start a business in the country. New companies, especially those operating in the field of innovative technologies, are supported by a variety of incentives and subsidies at both the federal and cantonal levels.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.10 Swiss population</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland\'s diversity is also reflected in the demographic characteristics of its population. Officially, more than one-fifth of the country\'s total population is made up of resident foreigners and temporary foreign workers. This gives Switzerland one of the most favorable competitive positions on the international market. Above all, the qualification of the workforce and human resources are decisive. The proportion of foreigners in Switzerland is the second highest in the entire country and contributes to three-quarters of total population growth.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.11 Working in Switzerland</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Foreign nationals who want to immigrate to Switzerland must comply with the entry and customs regulations. In any case, a valid and accepted travel document is required, as well as, in certain cases, a visa, confirmation of sufficient funds, and suitable accommodation. The validity period of the ID and visa requirements varies depending on nationality. For more information on entry requirements, please visit:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Swiss Embassies and Consulates: www.eda.admin.ch &gt; Travel Advice &amp; Representations</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">ID and visa requirements: www.sem.admin.ch/sem/de/home.html&gt; Topics&gt;Entry, Residence &amp; Work &gt; Entry</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"__Montserrat_069ab3, __Montserrat_Fallback_069ab3, Montserrat, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Employed foreigners are an important part of the Swiss economy, with a particular interest in highly qualified personnel. In recent years, great efforts have been made to facilitate the entry process for this particular group of immigrants. When it comes to accepting foreign workers and their family members, Switzerland can be described as a country with a dual admission system. Immigrants from EU/EFTA countries are generally treated on an equal footing with Swiss nationals in terms of residence regulations and access to the labor market. They have the free right to enter and reside in Switzerland, provided they receive a work and residence permit. Further information can be found under www.sem.admin.ch/sem/de/home.html &gt; Entry, residence &amp; work &gt; Entry &gt; EU/EFTA nationals (State Secretariat for Migration SEM, n.d.) in Switzerland. For the other third-country nationals and some EU citizens who want to live and work in Switzerland, the entry procedure is much more complex. Visas are limited and must be applied for before entry.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland is known for its good working conditions and attaches great importance to maintaining and improving them. The employment contract is generally governed by the Swiss Code of Obligations and can be concluded for a definite or indefinite period of time, on a full-time or part-time basis. The wage can be calculated according to time periods (time wage) or according to the work done (piece wage). From a legal point of view, there is no minimum wage unless it is stipulated in a collective agreement. The regular notice periods are between one and three months, depending on the duration of the employment relationship. In the event of termination, both parties to the contract are protected by law against unfair terminations. The maximum working hours are between 45 and 50 hours per week and depend on the respective industry. For example, industrial workers and office workers have a maximum working time of 45 hours. The legal standard for working leave is four weeks. However, the holiday entitlement depends on the employer, the employment contract, and the age of the employee.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.12 Residence permits</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Anyone planning to stay or take up employment in Switzerland for more than three months must register with their municipality within eight to fourteen days of arrival. Essentially, there are four different permits.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Short-term residence and internship permit (L): The type L permit is issued upon presentation of an employment contract with the same period of validity for up to 12 months. The residence permit can be extended to up to 18 months for trainees between the ages of 18 and 30 who wish to improve their qualifications.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Long-term residence permit (B): This is usually issued for one year upon presentation of an employment contract and can be renewed annually.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cross-border commuter permit (G): The cross-border commuter permit is issued to foreign employees who reside abroad, provided that they return to their home country at least weekly.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Settlement Permit (C): This can be applied for by persons from the EU-10 and EU-15 countries after a regular and uninterrupted residence in Switzerland of five or ten years.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.13 Accommodation and Cost of Living</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">According to the Swiss Immigration Office, the average cost of accommodation in larger cities is over 20% of the average salary. The generally high housing costs and mandatory health insurance contribute to the high cost of living. On the other hand, there are the advantages of extremely low crime, a functioning social security network, a high quality of life, and a well-developed and efficient public transport network. (Livingston Mark et al., n.d.), (Homegate, n.d.), (Immoscout24, n.d.).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.14 The social security system</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Swiss social security system is based on the so-called three-pillar system. This is a three-tier system of public, occupational, and private insurance. These are intended to enable the maintenance of the previous standard of living at the time of retirement in the event of disability or death for the individual or the surviving dependents. Pillars I and II are aimed at mandatory benefits, while Pillar III includes private social security.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Pillar I</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This pillar consists of old-age and survivors\' insurance (AHV) and disability insurance (IV). The AHV/IV is mandatory for all persons who are residents in Switzerland or have a paid professional activity in Switzerland. The AHV protects insured persons from loss of income in the event of retirement or disability and aims to secure their livelihoods and provide financial benefits in the event of disability. The minimum annual contribution is CHF 460. For those in employment, the AHV/IV contribution amounts to 10.3% of gross salary and is borne equally, half by the employer and half by the employee.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Pillar II</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This pillar includes occupational social insurance, which enables old, surviving dependents and disabled people with an AHV/IV pension to maintain their previous standard of living. All employed professionals in Switzerland with an annual income of at least CHF 20,880 are subject to compulsory insurance. The contributions are based on the age of the insured person and are usually borne half by the employer and half by the employee.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Pillar III</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The third pillar is a voluntary personal insurance scheme that further increases benefits upon retirement. Third-pillar insurance is often seen as a form of savings and offers certain tax advantages.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.15 Health insurance</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It covers medical costs and guarantees access to good medical care. This insurance is usually individually tailored to the needs of the individual. This insurance is mandatory for all Swiss nationals and residents. In Switzerland, health insurance is paid more monthly and is considered one of the most expensive in the world. However, exemptions and premium reductions are possible. For more information, visit the www.bsv.admin.ch website. (Federal Social Insurance Office FSIO, n.d.)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.16 Taxation</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In recent years, Switzerland has been working hard to develop new ideas for its tax system and improve an already favorable tax climate. The Swiss tax system reflects the country\'s federal structure and is based on the constitution, according to which all 26 cantons have the full right to levy taxes, except for those reserved exclusively for the federal government. The Swiss tax structure can be divided into two tax levels—the federal and the cantonal level.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Taxes on income and wealth: All natural persons with permanent or temporary residence in Switzerland are subject to taxation, both at the federal and cantonal levels. Taxes are collected by the cantonal tax authorities. These are assessed on the basis of a tax return to be submitted by the taxpayer for a period of one year.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Personal income tax: Income tax is paid by resident individuals on their worldwide income, subject to certain allowable deductions at both the cantonal and federal level. Exceptions to foreign investments are possible to a limited extent. The total income is calculated from employed or self-employed gainful employment, from compensatory or supplementary benefits, and from income from movable and immovable property. Individual tax rates are usually progressive, with a maximum tax rate of 11.5% at the federal level. However, each canton can set its own tax rates up to a maximum rate of around 30%. The typical total income tax burden in Switzerland is between 10% and 35%. It is important to point out that capital gains are usually exempt from tax in Switzerland.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Wealth tax: Natural persons in Switzerland are subject to taxation of their net assets. Wealth tax is levied only at the cantonal level in accordance with the respective cantonal tax laws. The tax is based on the balance of the combined gross assets of immovable and movable assets such as bank deposits, securities, real estate, and the like. Taxes are also levied on assets that do not yield any income. The wealth tax is progressive, ranging from 0.5% to about 5% of net wealth.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Exceptions: Expats are foreign executives and certain specialists who are temporarily posted to Switzerland for a period of up to five years. Eligible professionals can apply for tax relief for expenses they incur as a result of their stay, such as moving and travel expenses to and from Switzerland, part of the accommodation costs, and costs for school-age children. A cross-border commuter is a person who lives in the selected countries, such as Austria, France, Germany, Italy, and Liechtenstein, and works in Switzerland. The Swiss taxation of these people varies and can lead to partial taxation depending on where they work and where they live.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Lump-sum taxation (LSt): Persons with temporary or permanent residence in Switzerland who enter Switzerland for the first time or have been absent for at least ten years and are not gainfully employed are eligible. Swiss citizens can only benefit from lump-sum taxation for one year anyway. Lump-sum taxation is a form of special tax regime provided for in both federal tax and cantonal tax legislation, which can lead to subsequent contractual relief for income from foreign sources. The main features of the LSt are no wealth tax and the assessment basis for income tax must be agreed upon with the tax authorities. The minimum taxable income is CHF 200,000 per year, i.e., approx. CHF 30,000 to 40,000 in taxes. The tax base must correspond to the taxpayer\'s actual annual expenses. The tax base must not be less than five times the rental value or rent of Swiss real estate of the taxpayer. The tax base may not be less than any income from Swiss sources. The taxpayer can choose whether or not to declare foreign income or assets. In addition, there is no exit taxation and an ordinary gift and inheritance tax.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Conditions for claiming LSt: As an EU citizen, you must not have been gainfully employed in Switzerland after registering your main residence there. In addition, no gainful employment must have been carried out in Switzerland for at least 10 years. As a non-EU citizen, the same conditions initially apply as those listed above for EU citizens. In addition, the person must be at least 55 years old and have special connections or relationships that are of considerable interest to the canton for the issuance of the residence permit. Exceptions to the age limit are possible, but very rare.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\">1.5.2.17 Real Estate for Residential Use</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If you want to purchase a property in Switzerland, you must note that the legal situation may vary depending on the origin and legal status of the foreign buyer. The location of the property can also change the legal situation, depending on whether it is located in a tourist area or not. For foreign nationals, the federal law provides for purchase conditions and legal framework conditions in the form of the Lex Furgler-Koller-Friedrichi [SD1] or LFAIE. The LFAIE regulates sales to non-Swiss nationals on the basis of annual quotas per tourism region and has the following conditions. Foreigners who do not reside in Switzerland are only allowed to own one property per family in Switzerland. The owner must use the property as a holiday home. There may be restrictions on the size of the living space. The property can be rented out for up to 11 months per year. The restrictions on reselling real estate vary depending on the location. EU citizens/EFTA nationals are only treated in the same way as Swiss citizens when acquiring residential property as a residence or as a holiday home if they have their main residence in Switzerland or have a type \"B\" permit. All non-EU foreigners are subject to restrictions when acquiring a main residence in Switzerland, unless they are in possession of a Swiss residence or a type \"B\" permit. When buying a holiday home, on the other hand, there are no restrictions only for people with Swiss residence. In all other cases, a permit is required and LFAIE regulations apply.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Financing the mortgage: The common mortgage offered by Swiss banks for purchases in which only the property serves as collateral is 50 to 70% of the total purchase price, depending on income. In some cantons, fire insurance is mandatory for the building and its furnishings. The acquisition of the property becomes legally binding with the entry of the buyer or buyers in the land register. The estimated average cost of maintaining a building is usually between 0.9% and 1.1% of the purchase price. The tax value of the property, which usually corresponds to 2/3 of the market value, is used to determine the taxable assets and the rental value. This in turn forms the basis for income tax. In most cases, both are collected at the owner\'s residence.</span></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 06:05:03','2026-01-01 07:12:23'),(53,15,'Banking and finance business in Switzerland','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-3393ddd1-7fff-bc6e-3164-7042db0e7c69\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.1 The Swiss banking system at a glance</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Swiss banking sector is considered a key sector of the Swiss economy and enjoys an international reputation for its competence and professionalism. Banks are active in all sectors, both private and commercial. Switzerland is a world leader in private banking. The role of the country\'s central bank is played by the Swiss National Bank (SNB). Along with Union Bank of Switzerland (UBS) and Credit Suisse (CS), these are the key banks in Switzerland. (Swiss Banking, n.d.)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">1.5.3.2 Legal system</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Switzerland is not bound by European legislation, as it is neither a member state of the European Union (EU) nor the European Economic Area (EEA). This gives Switzerland the autonomy to regulate its financial services sector as it sees fit.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><b>1.5.3.3 Legal forms of banking regulation</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Banking regulation can take different legal forms. In Switzerland, the basic principles are regulated in federal legislation, for example, in the Banking Act, the Stock Exchange Act, or the Financial Market Supervision Act. The details are laid down in government ordinances, such as the Banking Ordinance or the Stock Exchange Ordinance. In addition, there are ordinances and circulars issued by the Financial Market Supervisory Authority (FINMA) as well as self-regulatory instructions, guidelines, and recommendations issued by the financial sector itself, but under the supervision of FINMA, in particular by the Swiss Bankers Association (SBA). (Swiss Banking, n.d.).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.4 Swiss Financial Market Supervisory Authority (FINMA)</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The main person responsible for regulating banks and financial markets is FINMA, which operates as an independent federal supervisory authority. As part of a dual supervisory system, FINMA supervises and controls both the audit firms that carry out the audits and the special audits commissioned by FINMA (Swiss Financial Market Supervisory Authority FINMA, n.d.).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.5 The SIX Swiss Exchange and the Swiss Bankers Association</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Certain aspects of securities brokerage, such as the organization of trading, are subject to self-regulation by SIX and by the Swiss Bankers Association under the overarching supervision of FINMA. SIX also ensures compliance with the regulatory framework for securities insurance and trading, as well as monitoring and enforcing compliance with these regulations (SIX, n.d.).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.6 Monitoring of UBS&nbsp;</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:12pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">UBS AG is by far the largest bank in Switzerland, holding more than half of all domestic banking assets following its acquisition of Credit Suisse Group AG in 2023. The collapse of Credit Suisse and its emergency takeover by UBS marked the end of Switzerland’s “two-pillar” banking system, leaving UBS as the sole Swiss global systemically important bank (G-SIB).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Due to its size, complexity, and interconnectedness, UBS is subject to strict regulatory oversight by FINMA, the Swiss Financial Market Supervisory Authority, as well as international bodies such as the Financial Stability Board. UBS is required to maintain higher capital buffers, prepare recovery and resolution plans (“too big to fail” regulations), and undergo intensive supervision to mitigate systemic risks.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.7 Swiss National Bank</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In contrast to FINMA, the SNB has the task of monitoring compliance with liquidity regulations. It also acts as a supervisory authority for payment and securities settlement systems (Swiss National Bank, n.d.).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.8 Supervision of other banks and securities dealers</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In its supervisory activities, FINMA relies heavily on the work of recognized audit firms, which are entrusted with the regular conduct of sectoral audits of financial institutions and thus ensure direct supervision. Within FINMA, the Supervision of Asset Management Banks and Securities Dealers divisions and the Supervision of Retail, Commercial, and Commercial Banks are responsible for the supervision of banks, securities dealers, and Pfandbrief banks. Institutions that form an economic unit with other entities in the financial sector are also audited on a consolidated basis as part of the supervision of financial services groups.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.9 Relationships with customers</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Its main competence is the provision of first-class banking services to private and corporate clients as well as to high-net-worth individuals. Data protection and legal certainty, legal protection, and discretion are guaranteed by federal laws and ordinances for the customers of Swiss banks. Efficient and effective management of private and corporate assets through state-of-the-art information processing techniques, socio-political and financial stability, and consistency of banking principles are important points in dealing with clients. Multilingual staff, who are constantly trained to meet the requirements of the comprehensive and demanding system of the Swiss banking sector, also contribute to this.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><b>1.5.3.10 Opening a Swiss bank account</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><h5 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.10.1 Private</b></span></span></span></span></h5><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Regular Name Account</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Any person of legal age can open an account in Switzerland, provided that they are able to provide the bank with official and valid identification documents and prove that they are the beneficial owner in case the assets have another or an additional beneficial owner. The legal origin of the assets must be proven.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Numbered Accounts</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The requirements for opening an account are identical to those for a regular account. The numbered accounts are intended to provide a higher level of internal security and confidentiality. The account address is replaced by a number or password. This type of account does not enjoy any additional legal protection in terms of confidentiality and should not be used for international transfers. For international payment services, the identity of the numbered account must be disclosed.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Restrictions</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The provision of financial services can be denied to so-called politically exposed persons if they may pose a reputational risk or if there are doubts about the origin of the funds.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h5 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.10.2 Company</b></span></span></span></span></h5><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A company can open a Swiss bank account, whether its registered office is in Switzerland or not. Legal entities registered in Switzerland that carry out trade, service, and production business and are therefore registered in the Swiss Commercial Register (SCR) should submit the relevant extract from the SCR to the bank. Legal entities registered abroad and those not registered in the SCR should provide the bank with an extract from the commercial register or equivalent documents that allow the bank to identify the company, establish its existence, and designate its representatives. This also applies to companies operating in a country that does not maintain an official commercial register. These documents should not be older than 12 months.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h5 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.10.3 Domiciliary companies</b></span></span></span></span></h5><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">These are domestic and foreign companies that do not carry out any operational activities and therefore do not have their own staff or business premises. In addition, they must declare the identity of the beneficial owners of their assets using a special form (Form A).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.27;text-align: justify;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>1.5.3.11 Monetary policy and interest rate stability</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:12pt;padding:12pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Swiss National Bank’s (SNB) monetary policy strategy consists of three elements. First, the SNB defines price stability as an annual increase in the Swiss consumer price index of less than 2%. Second, it bases its monetary policy decisions on a medium-term inflation forecast, which serves as the main indicator for assessing future price developments. Third, the SNB sets an operational target for the SNB policy rate, which guides short-term interest rates in Switzerland. The policy rate is implemented through the Swiss Average Rate Overnight (SARON), which replaced the discontinued Libor benchmark in 2021.</span></span></span></span></p></span>\n\n\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-10 06:06:12','2026-01-01 13:11:19'),(54,19,'Different types of blockchain','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-2d8e8e4a-7fff-cb72-486c-65ef585696fb\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Blockchain is considered the next great technological achievement after the invention of the internet. That\'s why many companies are involved in the development of other applications based on blockchains, and many start-ups have been founded. Blockchain technology has been an integral part of business and IT for several years now. It plays a key role in digital transformation. The development of decentralized networks has led to the development of various types of blockchain technologies, which we will explore below. These have different properties and functions. This also means that each type has its advantages and disadvantages and therefore also specific applications and potentials.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Overview of blockchain types:</b></span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Public Blockchain (öffentliche Blockchain)</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Private Blockchain</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Consortium Blockchain or Federated Blockchain</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Hybrid Blockchain</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 06:16:17','2026-01-09 11:20:05'),(55,19,'Why do we need different types of blockchain?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0db443a5-7fff-2941-ea4a-600a7fa912a8\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The different types of blockchains arose due to the need to adapt them to different needs. The different types enable companies of all sizes active in several industries to significantly improve process flows. There are now simple and complex blockchains that are either open-source or can be used via licenses. One of the biggest unique features of this technology is that it is adaptable and can be integrated into any industry to adapt to the specific business model, whatever industry you are in. In many cases, starting with an application is enough to familiarize yourself with the possibilities of blockchain. Many companies also rely on cloud solutions here, as they make it easier to connect other partners. Companies such as Amazon, Microsoft, Google, IBM, and Oracle offer various features on their cloud platforms to build a blockchain. There are also several blockchain protocols that allow you to develop your own decentralized applications, so-called dApps. This includes, for example, Ethereum. The requirements of a supply chain network are different from those of real estate and other businesses. This required the further development of different blockchain types.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/1.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-28e937fd-7fff-5596-d283-247bf2d7b934\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 1: The Four Basic Types of Blockchain Networks</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: iMi Blockchain, 2021)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The individual goals influence the decision on the blockchain type. If, for example, cryptocurrencies need to be introduced, a public blockchain can be useful. If the ultimate goal is to keep some of the data open while another part remains private, then a hybrid blockchain is ideal.</span></span></span></span></p><div>\n</div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 06:17:30','2026-01-09 11:20:47'),(56,19,' Public blockchains','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-d0f2f7a9-7fff-81dd-40d5-15df99595d78\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/2.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 2: Type Public Blockchain</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: iMi Blockchain, 2021)</span></span></span></span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Public blockchains are freely accessible to the public, so any user can join the network. That\'s why every user keeps the network running by making transactions and joining the group of validators.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Within public blockchains, however, governance rules may prevail that limit or expand the powers of individual participants. Public blockchains are one of the most popular and form the basis for digital currencies such as Bitcoin, Ethereum, Litecoin, and many other altcoins. By using the internet or an internet connection, anyone from anywhere can contribute to the management of the network. In a public blockchain, any participant can be a node operator and keep a copy of the transactions that take place on the network. Due to the large number of users, public blockchains have a high level of general network security, as there are a large number of network nodes.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A public blockchain can be, but does not necessarily have to be, open source. If a provider decides to make the blockchain publicly available, they can use open-source code or their own or a combination of both for programming. To use and participate in a public blockchain, it is necessary to download the corresponding software. The participant then operates its own node and verifies information, validates transactions, and can also add new blocks to the blockchain if necessary. All nodes in a blockchain make up the blockchain network and have a complete copy of the database. When the application is launched, the locally stored copy of the blockchain database is updated and continuously updated on the fly.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is off-chaining?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">On the blockchain, transactions are considered valid if they are stored on the blockchain in the public ledger. This requires authentication and validation by a defined number of participants. In off-chain transactions, an app uses the functions of the public blockchain but stores \"secret\" data in an area outside the public blockchain. The transactions take place \"outside\" the actual blockchain and are processed in different ways.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">On the one hand, this can be done by a temporary \"third party\" or via the definition of smart contracts. PayPal works according to these principles, technically speaking. Off-chain transactions are executed in real time, so they don\'t have to go through a lengthy process like traditional transactions on the blockchain. In a public blockchain, unlike the private blockchain, not all participants are known. Via proof-of-stake or other consensus methods, participants anonymously participate in governance decisions, can join DAOs, or receive rewards for staking the tokens. The consensus process checks whether each participant behaves according to the underlying protocol and adheres to the rules of the blockchain.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Popular public blockchains include Ethereum, Bitcoin, Litecoin, and Tezos. The active cooperation and networking of thousands of nodes creates the high security of the network. If the global decentralized network is connected to a developer community via open source, they are constantly developing the blockchain.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Consensus in public blockchains</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">No person or group is responsible for controlling the public blockchain. Therefore, decision-making and verification of transactions are achieved through various consensus mechanisms, such as proof-of-work or proof-of-stake. Consensus plays an essential role in blockchains. The mechanism ensures within the blockchain that all transactions are valid and that all participants in a blockchain have access to all data. Only valid transactions are stored in the blockchain. Validity is determined by consensus.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The proof-of-work algorithm (PoW) is used, for example, in the Bitcoin blockchain. Blockchains such as Ethereum also rely on PoW but now also use other technologies. PoW works with solving a computational problem when creating a consensus, i.e., confirming a transaction in the blockchain. This approach requires high computing and resource power from the nodes, which increases power and hardware costs. Proof-of-Stake (PoS) consensus is used in Ethereum 2.0, among other things. In contrast to PoW, PoS is said to cause significantly lower power and resource costs because the nodes do not require high performance. When using PoS, it is not the performance of a node that determines who calculates the consensus, but a random selection in conjunction with a weighting decides who is allowed to solve the arithmetic puzzle. In order for certain nodes in the blockchain to be allowed to validate a transaction, they must have a certain number of tokens or coins. In the next chapter, we will cover PoW and PoS in a little more detail.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b>2.1.3.1 Advantages of a Public Blockchain</b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b><br></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A public blockchain network has no restrictive access and can be used by anyone for free. While there may be hardware requirements for subscribers, there are absolutely no other defined restrictions on who can contribute to network growth. With all participants on the network and to ensure the optimal functionality of public blockchains, trust is becoming the standard. No one can manipulate the entire network. The incentive model, which is based on the consensus protocol highlighted earlier, prompts network participants to give their all to contribute to the blockchain. This increases the efficiency of the system. Overall, public blockchain networks are very secure because a single point of attack cannot lead to the collapse of the entire system.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b>2.1.3.2 Disadvantages of a Public Blockchain</b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Slower transaction speed and lack of scalability top the list of drawbacks that the public blockchain network suffers from. The presence of numerous participants, many of whom must follow the consensus process to validate transactions, usually leads to delays. Since there are no restrictions on the number of participants who can join the network, the blockchain may reach a saturation point where the number of participants may start working against the platform.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The energy consumption of the PoW blockchain model makes the entire innovation a problem for environmentalists and climate activists as well.</span></span></span></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 06:39:19','2026-01-09 11:23:26'),(57,19,'Private blockchains','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0b7c438e-7fff-4fe3-852c-acf6b05b0c65\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:2.4;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/3.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 2.4; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 3: Type Private Blockchain</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 2.4; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: iMi Blockchain, 2021)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Private blockchains are those that are designed for more limited or closed operation. In contrast to public blockchains, there is one or more responsible persons who take care of the maintenance of the blockchain. For example, they determine who is allowed to perform which actions and who has access to certain data on the blockchain. The consensus is reached on the coordination of the central controllers, i.e., authorized nodes, who grant or revoke mining rights to users within the network. This makes the private blockchain more centralized but still cryptographically secured. Private blockchains are ideal for businesses that want to use the technology to streamline their internal operations. The organization defines the accessibility requirements for the network that can perform transactions and validate the transactions that take place on-chain. Private blockchains are also ideal for a group of companies that share similar data in their daily activities. They are also used for IoT (Internet of Things) applications.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The aspect of centralization makes it generally debatable whether this variant can actually be called a blockchain, as it contradicts the basic idea of Bitcoin, a distributed ledger without a central authority. Well-known private blockchains include R3, Hyperledger, and Ripple. Legitimate blockchain networks, like others, are encrypted and have a high level of data cryptography, making them less vulnerable to attack compared to traditional distributed ledger technologies or digital databases. When different entities with different permissions access a network of information and data, private blockchains offer appropriate methods such as authentication through identity management systems that control entry into the private environment. Private blockchains are also often referred to as permissioned blockchains, as access is not possible for everyone but requires approval.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is zero-knowledge?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">\"Zero-knowledge\" refers to the zero-knowledge proof, which is a knowledge-free protocol where the data remains in the hands of the users, thus ensuring the security of this content. The zero-knowledge proof is based on complex procedures, such as the Phase-Fiat-Shamir-Protocol.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Simply put, cryptography ensures that a \"verifier\" of a secret does not know the secret but can confirm with a high degree of probability that the content of the secret shown to him by the \"prover\" is correct. There are approaches that can conduct private transactions on a public blockchain. The zero-knowledge approach is used for this purpose. In this case, the public nodes confirm a transaction whose complete content they do not know. This is only possible with high security requirements. The great benefit speaks in favor of using ZK in the cloud, but the effort is relatively high, and therefore zero-knowledge proofs have not been used much so far. In addition, it is problematic with this procedure that the proof is always valid for only one person. Furthermore, it should be remembered that if the key is lost, access to the data in the cloud is no longer possible.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.1.4.1 Advantages of Private Blockchains</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">On a private blockchain platform, the verification of transactions is very fast; the fewer people manage the system. When using a private blockchain, companies and organizations benefit from the efficiency of transactions and maintain control over the insight of their internal company activities. A public blockchain would be unsuitable for a company, as the competition could theoretically also gain insight into the private transactions. In addition, the company\'s management can better select which employees within the network are authorized to perform a specific task. Scalability on a private blockchain network is also hassle-free, as there is no need to increase the number of validators. This means that the network speed remains the same, while the number of validators can remain constant. As an operator of a private blockchain, it must be clear that this is not a decentralized approach. At least initially, the network participants must agree that one participant is in control. If the network is large enough, it can be agreed that the rules of the game, so-called governance, will be decentralized. The drudgery of decision-making per ecosystem development, which always follows a defined process in a public blockchain, is eliminated in private blockchains. All of this contributes to increasing the efficiency of the system.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.1.4.2 Disadvantages of Private Blockchains</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Decentralization is one of the hallmarks of any distributed ledger technology, and the fact that a central authority makes the final decision on a private blockchain contradicts this fundamental principle. On this basis, private blockchains are neither more trustworthy than their public alternatives, nor are they as transparent. A bad decision by the controlling authority can have a detrimental effect on the entire system. This makes the security regulations of private blockchains not as strong as other types of blockchain networks. The same applies to applications from service providers such as IBM. Offering blockchain as a service completely contradicts the open-source initiative that blockchain is all about.</span></span></span></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 06:42:35','2026-01-09 11:25:02'),(58,19,'Consortium Blockchain or Federated Blockchains','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e2f9143a-7fff-7ec2-d525-d9d2dedaee82\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/4.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 4: Type Federated Blockchains</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: iMi Blockchain, 2021)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Consortium or Federated Blockchains</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This type of blockchain is an extension of private blockchains. It seeks to remove the sole autonomy of the private blockchain. Here, more than one person or company is responsible for the network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There is a group of companies or representative people who work together and make decisions for the best benefit of the entire network. Such groups are also called consortia or federations, from which the name can be derived. Because of this composition, we can say that a consortium blockchain is a semi-decentralized network that includes both public and private blockchain functions. In this way, certain data is public to all participating members, while others are restricted. The functionality of a federated blockchain can be explained using the following example. A consortium consists of 20 financial institutions. These have stipulated in a code that a transaction, a block, or a decision within the network may only be assumed to be true if more than 15 of the participating institutions confirm it. In this way, a consensus is reached within a consortium.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This type of blockchain allows transactions to be processed quickly without having to rely on the decision of an individual, as is the case with private blockchain. Voting within the consortium also prevents wrong decisions or fraudulent activities by individual participants, as a defined majority decision must be available. Consortium blockchains are mainly applied through Hyperledger Fabric, Corda, and Quorum, among others.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Public-Permissionless Blockchains</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Depending on the visibility of the data, a distinction is still made between public and private variants of the different blockchain types. Public-permissionless blockchains have open entries, while the participants remain anonymous or pseudonymous. Examples of public permissionless blockchains are Bitcoin and Ethereum.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Private-Permissioned Blockchains</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">When using private-permissioned blockchains, only specified persons are allowed to access the blockchain, and only defined participants are allowed to validate transactions. Here the group of participants is clear. The technology controls the access of the participants, as in the case of Sovrin from the company Evernym, where the end users are subject to the predetermined framework conditions of the system. A well-known example is the R3 consortium with its solution \"Corda,\" in which all participants are known and even often know each other. This simplifies the procedure and ensures extremely fast block creation.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.1.5.1 Advantages of the Consortium Blockchain</span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Consortium blockchains offer a number of benefits for companies that work with them. Blockchain achieves greater efficiency by combining the functions of private and connected blockchain. The private parts of the network can easily be used to introduce some unique features tailored to all participants. Just like private blockchains, federated blockchains are highly scalable and well-secured, taking into account the benefits of their decentralized nature. According to the latter point, consortium blockchains use the combined hash power provided by each public node. Access control is improved because the network can thrive and work for everyone with a defined consensus or governance model.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.1.5.2 Disadvantages of the Consortium Blockchain</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The risk of involving different participants can predispose the network. This is concerning because at least one of the key nodes can be the subject of an attack or malicious action that compromises the entire network. Using blockchains in the consortium can also mean working on a pivotal point, as government regulations or any form of inconsistency on the part of one of the participating members can offset the system. Sharing the features of public blockchains doesn\'t mean they\'re just as secure. Federated blockchain networks still have some vulnerabilities for security breaches, but these can be fixed.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 06:43:46','2026-01-09 11:26:11'),(59,19,'Hybrid Blockchain','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-ba5b13b8-7fff-3e08-ec0d-58a17cabdd18\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/5.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 5: Type Hybrid Blockchain</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: iMi Blockchain)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A hybrid blockchain also uses the combined functions of private and public blockchain networks. At first glance, hybrid blockchains bear a close resemblance to consortium blockchains, but the difference between the two is huge. Unlike consortium blockchains with multiple participants who work together to maintain the network, a hybrid blockchain can have a network administrator with a single entity.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Hybrid blockchains work best when a company needs some of its data accessible and others to remain private for internal use. The multi-chain model of the hybrid blockchain can offer many advantages, as defined by the owner of the system. Transparency can be open or closed, depending on how the rules are set. The decentralization model in hybrid blockchains is partial, as opposed to that of a consortium blockchain, where all participants take full control of the network. Hybrid blockchains give companies the opportunity to distribute their cakes and own them at the same time. This gives you the visibility you need while protecting your most important data. Distributing incentives is also another important decision that any blockchain project that wants to use the hybrid model must decide on. The decision to introduce incentives depends on the business model and whether these benefits contribute to the growth of the system. The main platforms for hybrid blockchain systems include DragonChain and XinFin\'s Hybrid Blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\">2.1.6.1 Advantages of Hybrid Blockchain</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In addition to the hybrid blockchain benefits described in the features above, these blockchain networks can withstand the popular 51% attack model emanating from their decentralized component. The consensus in hybrid blockchains can be easily modified or even changed depending on your needs. The ease of scaling a hybrid blockchain is also one of the main advantages.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.1.6.2 Disadvantages of a hybrid blockchain</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The trust score is low because control is usually taken by a central authority. Adopting or switching to a hybrid blockchain system by an organization with some sort of distributed ledger system can be tedious. In the absence of incentives for system operation, external contributors may not be motivated to participate in maintaining the operating system (Godfrey, 2021; Herrnberger, 2022).</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-10 06:45:45','2026-01-09 11:27:19'),(60,20,'Staking','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e1bc9563-7fff-947d-430d-7fb23c529ed1\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.1.1 Explanation</span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Staking is a crucial process in cryptocurrency networks that allows participants to actively participate in the network and ensure its security. In this process, participants store their cryptocurrencies in a special wallet and stake a certain amount for a predefined period of time. Those who engage in staking will have the opportunity to be selected as validators for transactions and adding new blocks to the blockchain. As a reward, transaction fees and, if necessary, new units of the cryptocurrency beckon.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Staking is used in particular in the context of Proof-of-Stake (PoS) consensus mechanisms as an efficient alternative to resource-intensive Proof-of-Work (PoW) mining. This process not only promotes the active participation of participants in the network but also strengthens security. In addition, staking acts as a source of income for those who allocate their cryptocurrencies for this purpose.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A basic idea of staking can be gained by considering Proof of Stake (PoS). This consensus mechanism allows blockchains to operate more efficiently while maintaining decentralization. Staking thus means holding back cryptocurrencies in order to receive rewards. Whether in one\'s own crypto wallet or through staking services from exchanges like Binance, this process offers a straightforward way to generate revenue while supporting the smooth functioning of the blockchain network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.1.2 How it works</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As we discussed earlier, proof-of-work blockchains rely on mining to add new blocks to the blockchain. In contrast, proof-of-stake blockchains generate and validate new blocks through the process of staking. When staking, validators freeze their coins so that they can be randomly selected by the protocol at certain intervals to create a block. Usually, participants who stake larger amounts have a higher chance of being selected as the next block validator.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This allows blocks to be produced without relying on special mining hardware, such as ASICs. While ASIC mining requires a significant investment in hardware, staking requires a direct investment in the cryptocurrency itself. So, instead of competing for the next block with computational work, PoS validators are selected based on the number of coins they stake. The \"stake\" (the stake in coins that is held) is the incentive for validators to maintain network security. If they don\'t, their entire stake could be at risk.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">While each proof-of-stake blockchain has its own currency for staking, some networks apply a two-token system where rewards are paid out in a second token.</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\">On a very practical level, staking simply means that the money is stored in a suitable wallet. This essentially allows anyone to perform various network functions in exchange for staking rewards. This can include adding coins to a staking pool, which we\'ll cover shortly.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How are staking rewards calculated?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There is no short answer here. Each blockchain network may use a different way of calculating staking rewards.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Some are adjusted block by block, taking into account many different factors. These may include:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">how many coins the validator staked</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">how long the validator has been actively staking</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">how many coins are staked in total on the network</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">the inflation rate</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Other factors</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">For some other networks, staking rewards are set as a fixed percentage. These rewards are distributed to validators as a kind of compensation for inflation. Inflation encourages users to spend their coins instead of keeping them, which can increase their use as a cryptocurrency. So, with this model, validators can calculate exactly what staking rewards they can expect.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A predictable reward schedule rather than a probability-based chance of receiving a block reward may seem more attractive to some. And since this is public information, it could encourage more participants to participate in staking.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.1.3 Staking Pools</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A staking pool is a group of coin owners who pool their resources to increase their chances of validating blocks and earning rewards. They pool their influence in staking and divide the rewards proportionally to their contributions in the pool.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Setting up and maintaining a staking pool often requires a lot of time and expertise. Staking pools are usually most effective in networks where the barrier to entry (technical or financial) is relatively high. Therefore, many pool providers charge a fee from the staking rewards that are distributed to participants.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In addition, pools can provide additional flexibility for individual staking participants. Typically, the staking must be locked for a certain period of time and usually has a payout or \"unbinding\" or exit time specified in the protocol. In addition, a significant minimum amount of staking is almost certainly required to discourage malicious behavior.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Most staking pools only require a small minimum balance and do not add any additional withdrawal times. Therefore, participating in a staking pool instead of participating in staking on your own could be ideal for newcomers.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.1.4 Cold Staking</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cold staking refers to the process of staking in a wallet that is not connected to the internet. This can be done with a hardware wallet, but it can also be done with an isolated software wallet (offline).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Networks that support cold staking allow users to stake while keeping their funds safely offline. It is worth noting that when the stakeholder retrieves their coins from cold storage, they will no longer receive rewards.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cold staking is especially useful for large stakeholders who want to ensure maximum protection of their funds while supporting the network. (Binance Academy, 2019)</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 06:48:06','2026-01-09 11:29:06'),(61,20,'Proof of Stake','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-365c0dd5-7fff-e438-ea1c-ae4777d9ff0b\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b>2.2.2.1 Explanation</b></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b><br></b></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If you know how Bitcoin works, you\'re probably familiar with Proof of Work (PoW). It is the mechanism that makes it possible to collect transactions in blocks. These blocks are then linked together to form the blockchain. More specifically, miners compete to solve a complex mathematical puzzle, and whoever solves it first gets the right to add the next block to the blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Work has proven to be a very robust mechanism to facilitate consensus in a decentralized way. The problem is that it involves a lot of arbitrary calculations. The puzzle that miners are vying to solve serves no other purpose than to keep the network secure. One could argue that this in itself justifies this excess of calculations. At this point, you may be wondering: Are there other ways to maintain a decentralized consensus without the heavy computational overhead?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Welcome to Proof of Stake. The main idea is that participants can lock coins (their \"stake\"), and at certain intervals, the protocol randomly assigns one of them the right to validate the next block. Usually, the probability of being selected is proportional to the number of coins – the more coins deposited and locked, the higher the chances.The key difference, of course, is how PoW and PoS determine which participant validates new transactions. For a better understanding, let\'s take a look at the table below:</span></span></span></span></p><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"margin-left:4.8pt;\" align=\"left\"><table style=\"text-align: justify; border-width: initial; border-style: none; border-color: initial;\"><colgroup><col width=\"200\"><col width=\"200\"><col width=\"200\"></colgroup><tbody><tr style=\"height:15.9pt\"><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Work (PoW)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Stake (PoS)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height:74.9pt\"><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Who can mine/validate blocks?</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The higher the computing power, the higher the probability that a block will be mined.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The more coins are staked, the more likely it is that a new block will be validated.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height:65.9pt\"><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How is a block mined/validated?</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Miners compete against each other to solve complex mathematical puzzles with their computing resources.</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As a rule, the algorithm determines the winner at random, taking into account the amount of coins staked.</span></span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height:25.9pt\"><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Mining Equipment</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Professional mining hardware, such as ASIC, CPU, and GPU</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Any computer or mobile device with an internet connection</span></span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height:52.4pt\"><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How are the rewards distributed?</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The first person to mine the block will receive a block reward.</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Validators can receive a share of the transaction fees collected by the block they validate.</span></span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height:52.4pt\"><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How is the network secured?</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The larger the hash value, the more secure the network is</span></span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"border-width: 1pt; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); vertical-align: top; padding: 0pt 5.4pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Staking locks the cryptocurrency on the blockchain to secure the network.</span></span></span></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Stake (PoS) and Proof of Work (PoW) are two different consensus mechanisms used in the crypto world, and there are opposing opinions about which one is better. Proponents of Proof of Stake argue that PoS has some clear advantages over PoW. In particular, they emphasize that PoS networks are often superior in terms of scalability and transaction speed. PoS allows participants to validate blocks and confirm transactions based on cryptocurrency ownership, rather than using expensive mining hardware and energy. This results in lower operating costs and enables faster transaction settlements. In addition, PoS is often considered more environmentally friendly because it consumes less energy compared to PoW and is therefore less harmful to the environment. In contrast, many PoW proponents argue that proof of work still holds an important place in the crypto ecosystem. PoW has proven to be an extremely secure mechanism over the years and is especially popular with large and established cryptocurrencies.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-80032daa-7fff-6160-a4f9-8c8ad9d831d4\" style=\"\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.2.2 Who Developed Proof of Stake?</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The first mention of the proof-of-stake concept can be attributed to Sunny King and Scott Nadal in their article published for Peercoin in 2012. They describe it as a \"peer-to-peer cryptocurrency design derived from Satoshi Nakamoto\'s Bitcoin.\" The Peercoin network was launched with a hybrid PoW/PoS mechanism, where PoW was mainly used to mine the initial stock. However, it was not necessary for the long term. sustainability of the network, and its importance was gradually reduced. In fact, the network\'s security relied largely on PoS.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.2.3 Risks</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Centralization risk</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the proof-of-work blockchains, mining involves the use of computing power to hack the block\'s data until a valid solution is found. However, with today\'s leading cryptocurrencies, finding these solutions is becoming increasingly challenging, and the process of generating numerous hashes is proving costly in terms of hardware and energy. As a result, some miners prefer to pool their mining resources in so-called mining pools to increase their chances of receiving block rewards. As of December 2021, the four largest mining pools collectively controlled about 50% of the total Bitcoin hashing power. The predominance of these mining pools makes it difficult for individual crypto enthusiasts to earn mining rewards on their own. But how decentralized is mining now? There is still no single entity that can control acknowledgments on the network. In this case, a 51% attack would be possible, and the network would lose its value. Some might argue that while mining is still decentralized, it is no longer highly decentralized. Certain areas, mining equipment manufacturers, and energy producers continue to dominate mining, reducing overall decentralization for proof-of-work blockchains.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The proof-of-stake consensus mechanism takes a different approach, replacing mining power with staking. This mechanism lowers the barriers to entry for an individual to confirm transactions and reduces the importance of location, equipment, and other factors. Your stake is simply determined by the amount of tokens you own. However, most PoS networks require you to run a validator node to start confirming transactions. This node can be expensive to run, but not as expensive as multiple mining rigs. Users then stake their tokens behind specific validators, which gives us a similar model to mining pools. Even though proof of stake is easier to handle for the average user, it is still prone to the same centralization problem as mining pools.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Vulnerabilities</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In addition to the risk of centralization, the fact that the four largest mining pools own the majority of the hashing power of the Bitcoin network could increase the risk of a 51% attack. A 51% attack refers to a potential attack on the security of a blockchain system by a malicious actor or organization that manages to control more than 50% of the total network hashing power. The attacker could override the blockchain consensus algorithm and commit malicious acts for their own benefit, such as double-spending, rejecting or modifying transaction records, or preventing others from mining. However, due to the size of the Bitcoin network, this is unlikely to happen with Bitcoin.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In contrast, anyone who wants to attack a PoS blockchain would need to own more than 50% of the coins on the network. This would drive up demand in the market and the price of coins, which could cost tens of billions of dollars. Even if they carry out a 51% attack, the value of their staked coins would drop drastically as the network is compromised. Therefore, it is not very likely that a 51% attack will occur on a cryptocurrency that uses the PoS consensus, especially if it is a cryptocurrency with a large market cap.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Work and Proof of Stake both have their place in the crypto ecosystem, and it\'s hard to say for sure which consensus protocol works better. PoW may be criticized for producing high carbon emissions when mining, but it has proven to be a secure algorithm for protecting blockchain networks. However, as Ethereum moves from PoW to PoS, the proof-of-stake system could be preferred by new projects in the future.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.2.4 Disadvantages of Proof of Stake</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Many see proof of stake as a better alternative to proof of work, but it\'s worth noting that the PoS algorithm also has flaws. Due to the mechanism used to distribute the rewards, validators with a higher stake can increase their chances of validating the next block. The more coins a validator accumulates, the more coins they can stake and earn, which is criticized by some as \"making the rich even richer.\" These \"richer\" validators can also influence voting on the network, as PoS blockchains often grant governance rights to validators. Another issue is the security risks for cryptocurrencies with smaller market capitalizations that use PoS. As mentioned earlier, it is not very likely that a 51% attack would occur on the more popular cryptocurrencies such as ETH or BNB. However, smaller digital assets with a lower value are more vulnerable to attacks. The attackers could potentially acquire enough coins to gain an advantage over other validators. They could take advantage of the PoS system by frequently being selected as validators. The rewards earned can then be used for further bets and increase their chance of being selected in the next round. (Binance Academy, 2018)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.2.5 Delegated Proof of Stake (DPoS)</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">An alternative version of this mechanism was developed by Daniel Larimer in 2014 and is called Delegated Proof of Stake (DPoS). It was initially used as part of the BitShares blockchain, but soon after, other networks adopted the model. These include Steem and EOS, which were also launched by Larimer.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">DPoS allows users to set their coin balances as votes, with voting rights proportional to the number of coins held. These votes are then used to elect a number of delegates who manage the blockchain on behalf of their constituents, ensuring security and consensus. Typically, staking rewards are distributed to these elected delegates, who then distribute a portion of the rewards to their constituents in proportion to their individual contributions.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The DPoS model makes it possible to achieve consensus with a smaller number of validating nodes. As such, it tends to improve network performance. On the other hand, it can also lead to a lower degree of decentralization, as the network relies on a small, select group of validating nodes. These nodes handle the operation and overall governance of the blockchain. They participate in the processes of consensus-building and the definition of the most important governance parameters. Simply put, DPoS allows its users to signal their influence through other participants in the network. (Binance Academy, 2019)</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div>\n\n</div></span></span></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 06:51:20','2026-01-09 11:32:34');
INSERT INTO `subsections` VALUES (62,20,'Proof of Work (PoW)','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-1a7002f0-7fff-49dd-6518-92784250d857\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.3.1 PoW Statement</span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>What is a proof of work?</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the world of cryptocurrencies, Proof of Work (PoW) is a consensus mechanism used in Bitcoin and other blockchains. Through a process called mining, PoW is used to create new blocks, creating a continuous transaction history that prevents double spending. Its main purpose is to ensure the integrity and security of the cryptocurrency\'s network.</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Technically, proof of work is a \"cryptographic proof\" in which a node (prover) proves to the other network participants (verifiers) that a certain computing power has been provided.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Contrary to popular belief, Bitcoin did not invent proof of work. He has merely put the concept in the spotlight and innovatively turned it into a competitive task (mining) supported by a financial incentive in the form of a coin reward. However, we can\'t fully understand proof of work without knowing its origins.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.3.2 History</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The concept of proof of work dates back to 1992, when Moni Naor and Cynthia Dwork began tackling the problem of email spamming. They published a scientific journal entitled \"Pricing via Processing or Combatting Junk Mail.\" The concept aimed to curb spamming by requiring the senders of emails to perform some calculations before sending an email.</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In 1997, Adam Back developed a protocol called Hashcash, a more advanced concept for preventing email spamming. Hashcash itself already included some kind of double-spending (a peculiarity of blockchain technology) by incorporating the so-called \"double-spending protection\" concept. Interestingly, these original concepts themselves were not called proof of work.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Hal Finney, Proof Of Work, and Bitcoin</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In 1999, two years after Adam Back\'s Hashcash concept was developed, an academic essay by Ari Juels and Markus Jakobsson titled \"Proofs of Work and Bread Pudding Protocols\" was published. This was the first time that the term \"proof of work\" actually appeared. The essay describes the proof of work concept as \"a protocol in which a prover shows a verifier that it has done a certain amount of computational effort in a given time interval.\" This version is already similar to the proof-of-work concept used in Bitcoin. However, the main difference is that this earlier version is not based on an economic incentive.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">So the innovation in proof of work did not stand still. In 2004, Hal Finney developed the concept of \"Reusable Proof of Work (RPOW),\" which was based on Adam Back\'s Hashcash concept. This concept is still considered an important piece of the puzzle in the development of digital money and was a significant precursor to Bitcoin.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">On October 13, 2008, Satoshi Nakamoto published Bitcoin\'s whitepaper titled </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">\"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System.\" </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the paper, Satoshi made it clear that proof of work plays an important role in Bitcoin\'s success. Proof of work is used to process and timestamp transactions, creating a chronological transaction history commonly referred to as blockchain. He directly referred to Adam Back\'s Hashcash concept and compared it to the proof of work in Bitcoin\'s whitepaper.</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The above excerpt shows how the concept of proof of work has evolved over the years.</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> It turned out to be the first consensus mechanism in cryptocurrency; that\'s why some people believe that Satoshi actually created proof of work with the creation of Bitcoin. However, proof of work existed long before the creation of the first cryptocurrency (Bitcoin) and was incorporated by Satoshi as one of the essential aspects that make Bitcoin work.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.3.3 Function &amp; Applications of Proof of Work</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As explained above, proof of work became popular due to the success of Bitcoin and the blockchain technology behind it. Therefore, it is almost impossible to intellectually separate Proof of Work from Bitcoin and its blockchain technology these days. Ultimately, proof of work is a consensus mechanism for securing a blockchain like Bitcoin\'s, which makes it possible to create a decentralized transaction history that every network participant agrees to.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is a blockchain? Blockchain is a digital ledger that stores data records without a central server or a single storage point. The data is stored in blocks on each node connected to the network, and the nodes are spread all over the world.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">To get the decentralized transaction history, transactions need to be added to the blockchain. This task is performed by miners who follow the proof-of-work algorithm. They compete against each other to solve a cryptographic problem by finding a valid hash (nonce) that meets the system\'s protocol criteria. Each miner who solves the problem first is given the authority to attach the new data (block full of transactions) to the existing blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Before new blocks can be added to the blockchain by providing the necessary proof of work, miners need to hack three important things:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The batch of transactions to be added to the block</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A hash of the previous block</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A nonce that represents a random number generated specifically for the purpose of making mining computationally intensive</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If one of the three entries is missing, an invalid hash is determined.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The concept of the nonce can be explained in more detail by mentioning the so-called \"level of difficulty.\" This feature, which is part of Bitcoin\'s design, describes how easy or hard it is for miners to find a valid hash. The protocol sets the difficulty level and automatically adjusts to the speed needed to find a nonce. In other words, the higher the difficulty, the harder it is to find a valid hash and vice versa. This also means that creating proof of work becomes more difficult as more miners join a proof-of-work blockchain. If miners leave the network instead, mining becomes easier. So, adjusting the difficulty level ensures that mining doesn\'t get easier the more computing power is used by all miners on the network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">One last question is: Why would miners go through a computational effort to add blocks to the blockchain? Because they are rewarded for it. Any miner who finds a nonce and is thus able to add their transaction block to the blockchain will be rewarded with new coins from the Proof of Work blockchain system. In this way, miners are incentivized to mine.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">To make a long story short: Proof of Work works through guesswork. Miners collect a stack of transactions into a block. To add this block to the blockchain, they have to put in a computational effort by looking for a valid nonce. Once such a hash is found, the solution is presented to the network. If it is valid, the transaction block is added to the blockchain, and the puzzle work begins again.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Where is proof of work used?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The most popular use case of proof of work as a blockchain consensus mechanism is Bitcoin. The total share of all cryptocurrencies that work with the proof of work protocol is estimated to be 64% of the global crypto market.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The numbers don\'t lie. Proof of Work still dominates the crypto space, even after the recent announcement of Ethereum\'s migration from Proof of Work to the Proof of Stake consensus mechanism. Ethereum Classic, Monero, Dash, Zcash, Bitcoin Cash, Dogecoin, and other crypto projects are still actively working with proof of work.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.3.4 Benefits of Proof of Work</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of work is the backbone of Bitcoin. It helps the cryptocurrency maintain and secure its distributed transaction ledger in a decentralized manner. The consensus mechanism has a good track record of securing a distributed ledger, and Bitcoin is living proof of this. After all, the mother of all cryptocurrencies has never been hacked, nor has a fake currency been issued on its blockchain</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Since Bitcoin is based on the proof-of-work method, its security depends on how much computing power is used to secure the Bitcoin network. This number can be expressed using the concept of hash rate. The higher the hash rate, the more computing power and therefore energy is used to secure Bitcoin. While it can be said that the more hash rate a proof-of-work network like Bitcoin compiles, the more secure it becomes, it is also important that the hash rate is distributed and not controlled by just a few players.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">One of the benefits of proof of work is that it only gets better over time. The more it grows, the more secure and expensive the system becomes for hacker attacks. The puzzle that is solved during the mining process becomes more and more difficult to solve as the number of miners increases. And the more miners there are, the more computing power is needed to successfully participate in mining, which is why the security level of proof-of-work blockchains increases.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.3.5 Disadvantages of Proof of Work</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; padding: 12pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Work (PoW) remains a foundational consensus mechanism in blockchain technology, but it has several notable disadvantages:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">High Energy Consumption</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">: Bitcoin\'s annual energy consumption reached approximately 173 terawatt-hours (TWh) in 2025, surpassing the energy usage of entire nations like Ukraine. This equates to about 0.5% of global electricity demand.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Environmental Impact</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">: Each Bitcoin transaction emits around 633 kg of CO₂, comparable to the carbon footprint of over 1.4 million Visa transactions.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Hardware Dependency</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">: PoW requires specialized mining equipment, leading to significant electronic waste. In 2025, Bitcoin mining produced approximately 21.3 kilotonnes of electronic waste, akin to the small IT equipment waste of the Netherlands.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Scalability Issues</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">: The energy-intensive nature of PoW limits its scalability, resulting in lower transaction throughput compared to alternative consensus mechanisms.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Centralization Risks</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">: The high costs associated with PoW mining can lead to centralization, as only large entities can afford the necessary infrastructure, potentially undermining the decentralized ethos of blockchain.</span></span></span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><br></font></div></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In contrast, Ethereum\'s transition from PoW to Proof of Stake (PoS) in 2022 significantly reduced its energy consumption by over 99.9%, highlighting the potential for more sustainable consensus mechanisms.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Pros</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Work provides blockchain networks with a high level of security because it uniquely achieves consensus through mining.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It upholds the principles of blockchain technology by providing a truly decentralized process of attaching transactions to a distributed ledger.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Economic incentives support this; miners are paid for mining.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.3.6 Further background</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Work (PoW) is a form of cryptographic proof in which one party (the prover) proves to others (the verifiers) that a certain amount of a certain computational effort has been expended. The verifiers can then confirm this effort with minimal effort.</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The concept was developed in 1993 by Moni Naor and Cynthia Dwork to prevent denial-of-service attacks and other misuse of services such as spam, on a network by requiring a certain amount of work from a rservices,r of services, which usually means processing time for a computer.</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Proof of Work was later used by Bitcoin as the basis for consensus in a permissionless decentralized network where miners compete with each other to attach blocks and mine new currency, with the probability of success for each miner being proportional to the computational effort. PoW and PoS are still the two most well-known mechanisms for deterring Sybils.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A key feature of proof of work procedures is their asymmetry: the work—the calculation—must be moderately difficult (but doable) for the prover or requester but easy to verify for the verifier or service provider. This idea is also known as the CPU cost function, customer puzzle, calculation puzzle, or CPU price function. Another common feature is built-in incentive structures that reward the allocation of computing power to the network with value in the form of cryptocurrency. The purpose of proof-of-work algorithms is not to prove that certain work has been done or that a computational puzzle has been solved, but to discourage the manipulation of data by imposing high energy and hardware control requirements to be able to do so.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.3.7 Protocols</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There are two classes of proof-of-work protocols:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Challenge-response protocols</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> assume a direct interactive connection between the requestor (client) and the provider (server). The provider selects a task, such as an item in a quantity with a property; the requester finds the corresponding response in the quantity, which is returned and reviewed by the provider. Since the provider selects the task on site, the difficulty of the task can be adjusted to the current load. The effort on the part of the requester may be limited if the Challenge Response protocol has a known solution (chosen by the provider) or exists in a limited search space.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Solution review protocols</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> do not assume such a connection: consequently, the problem itself must be posed before the requester looks for a solution, and the vendor must review both the choice of problem and the solution found. Most of these methods are unrestricted probabilistic iterative methods such as Hashcash.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Protocols with a known solution tend to have a slightly lower variance than protocols with unlimited probability, because the variance of a rectangular distribution is less than the variance of a Poisson distribution (with the same mean).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Variance is the use of several independent ranges; the average of several samples has a lower variance. There are also features with a fixed cost, such as the time lock puzzle. In addition, the underlying functions used by these systems can be</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• CPU-bound, where the calculation is done at the speed of the processor, which varies greatly over time, as well as from high-end servers to low-end portable devices.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Memory-bound, where compute speed is limited by main memory accesses (either latency or bandwidth), whose performance is expected to be less sensitive to hardware development.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">• Network-bound, when the client needs to do only a few calculations but needs to fetch some tokens from remote servers before requesting the final service provider. In this sense, the work is not really done by the requester, but there are still delays due to the latency of obtaining the required tokens.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Finally, some PoW systems offer abbreviation calculations that allow participants who know a secret, usually a private key, to generate cheap PoWs. The reason for this is that mailing list holders can create stamps for each recipient without incurring high costs. Whether such a function is desirable depends on the respective usage scenario</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 07:20:42','2026-01-09 11:39:25'),(63,20,'Mining','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-ddd99626-7fff-b6ad-ee21-c7115e1fdcca\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.482; background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.4.1 Explanation</span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There are three main ways to get Bitcoin and other cryptocurrencies. You can “buy” them on an exchange like Coinbase, “receive” them as payment for goods or services, or “mine” them virtually. We explain the third category here using Bitcoin as an example.</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Mining refers to a process in which networks formed by special computers generate and circulate new Bitcoin and verify new transactions. Mining is the process that Bitcoin and various other cryptocurrencies use to generate new coins and verify new transactions. It involves huge, decentralized computer networks around the world that verify and secure blockchains, the virtual ledgers that document cryptocurrency transactions. In return for providing their computing power, the computers in the network are rewarded with new coins. It\'s a virtuous circle: the miners maintain and secure the blockchain, the blockchain awards the coins, and the coins incentivize the miners to maintain the blockchain.</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.482; background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.4.2 How it works</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>How does cryptocurrency mining work?</b></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Mining cryptocurrencies is a process in which miners use computing power to process transactions and earn rewards in cryptocurrencies. This involves adding new blocks of transactions to the system. It is important to agree on the price and duration of the block cup within the mining network. Mining requires special software to solve mathematical problems and confirm legal transactions. The reward depends on the amount of energy needed to mine it, and the stability of the power grid plays a crucial role. To mine cryptocurrencies, you need the right equipment, be it an ASIC microprocessor or a powerful GPU (graphics processing unit). The choice of hardware depends on the coin to be mined. Stability is more important than speed, and a cost-effective power supply is crucial. Mining consists of validating transactions, creating blocks, and inserting them into the blockchain. Rewards consist of the transaction fees and the newly created currency.</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Mining and Bitcoin circulation</b></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In addition, mining serves another important purpose: it is the only way to put new cryptocurrencies into circulation. In other words, mining is basically the \"mining\" of currencies. Aside from the coins minted via the genesis block (the very first block created by founder Satoshi Nakamoto), every single one of these bitcoins was created by miners. In the world of miners, Bitcoin is a new currency, but there will be no new currency, Bitcoin. There will be a time when Bitcoin mining ends; according to Bitcoin protocol, the number of Bitcoins will be 21 million. However, as the number of \"millions\" of Bitcoins decreases by thousands, the number of Bitcoins will not be reached until around 2140. However, this does not mean that transactions can no longer be verified. Miners will continue to verify transactions and receive fees to maintain the integrity of the Bitcoin network. Aside from the short-term Bitcoin payout, miners can get \"voting rights\" when changes are made to the Bitcoin network protocol. In other words, miners have some influence on the decision-making process on topics like forking (Coinbase, n.d.).</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Types of mining</b></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As explained in the previous sections, there are two types of mining:</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.482;background-color:#f8fafc;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\" id=\"docs-internal-guid-5dab7b8c-7fff-3e7c-a43a-d3df0834e4c9\"><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Work (PoW)</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 7pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">PoW, which is most commonly used in currencies such as Bitcoin, Ethereum, Litecoin, and Monero, requires complex puzzles to be solved before new blocks can be added</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.482;background-color:#f8fafc;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\"><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proof of Stake (PoS)</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">PoS is based on the participation and reward of owners of large amounts of cryptocurrency. Many companies use PoS to increase their market value. (Binance Academy, 2018)</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.482; background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.4.3 Is mining still worth it?</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You may have thought about mining Bitcoin yourself. A decade ago, anyone with a decent computer at home could participate. But as blockchain has grown, so has the computing power required to maintain it (many times more: in October 2019, 12 trillion times more computing power was required to mine a Bitcoin than when the first blocks were mined in January 2009). Therefore, Bitcoin mining is probably no longer profitable for hobby miners these days. Virtually all mining is now done by specialized companies or groups of people pooling their resources.</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Basically, Bitcoin mining is still a way to make money without direct financial investment, but no longer for everyone. Bitcoin mining is comparable to running a large data center. Companies buy the mining hardware and pay for the electricity needed to keep it running (and cool). For this to be profitable, the value of the coins earned must be higher than the cost of mining those coins (Coinbase, n.d.).</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin miners are rewarded with rewards for completing \"blocks\" of verified transactions that are added to the blockchain. Those who find the solution to a hash puzzle first receive the rewards. Mining requires a graphics processing unit (GPU) or an application-specific computing core (ASIC). Miners receive a reward for monitoring Bitcoin transactions and ensuring their validity. Because responsibilities are distributed among many users around the world, Bitcoin is a \"decentralized\" system, or a system that does not rely on an institution such as a bank or financial institution to make all decisions. Although the Bitcoin reward for miners decreases and is capped at 21 million, mining continues as miners also receive transaction fees. However, mining requires special equipment and significant electrical energy. The probability of finding the right hash number is low, and mining is not as profitable as it used to be. Mining pools combine their computing power to increase the chances of rewards. The reward for mining was originally 50 BTC, but it was halved to control inflation. As of 2025, the Bitcoin block reward is 3.125 BTC per block, following the halving on April 20, 2024, plus transaction fees, which currently account for roughly 1% of total miner revenue. Mining returns are strongly influenced by the Bitcoin price, network hash rate, and energy costs, making efficiency and access to low-cost electricity critical for profitability.</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What motivates the miners? The network organizes a lottery. Every computer on the network competes to be the first to guess a 64-digit hexadecimal number, called a \"hash.\" The faster a computer can guess the number, the more likely it is to receive the reward. The winner updates the blockchain ledger with all newly verified transactions and adds a newly verified \"block\" to the chain that contains all these transactions and receives a predetermined amount of newly minted Bitcoin. As the difficulty of mining increases, the reward will continue to decrease until there are no more Bitcoins to mine.</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There are alternatives to mining, such as buying Bitcoin directly on exchanges or investing in companies that make equipment for mining. The legality of Bitcoin mining varies depending on the geographical location. However, mining comes with risks, including the need for expensive equipment, high energy costs, and low probabilities of success. Overall, it is important to consider current market factors and personal resources before deciding to mine Bitcoin. (Financial Flow, 2021)</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.482; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></h4><div><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/Crieteria.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.482; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><br></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.482; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 1: Criteria that influence the profitability of mines</span></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Source: Financial flow, Bitcoin mining: Is it still worth it? How does cryptocurrency mining work?</span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.482; background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.4.4 How to mine?</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">So they are paid for their work as \"auditors.\" They are tasked with verifying the legitimacy of Bitcoin transactions. By reviewing the data stored in the database, they can help solve the \"dual use problem.\" With physical coins, it\'s not a problem: if you pick up a 20 CHF bill to buy a bottle of wine, you won\'t have it anymore, and there\'s no risk of using the same 20 CHF bill to buy wine the next day. There is a possibility, but the probability is small. With a cryptocurrency, on the other hand, there is a possibility that the holder withdraws some of the money and sends it to another location while maintaining the value of the money. (\"Problem of dual use\"). Let\'s say you had a real $20 bill and a copy of it that\'s worth $20. If you take the trouble to check both serial numbers of the bills, you would find that they are the same number, so one of them would have to be wrong. In his case, a Bitcoin miner checks the transactions to make sure that users don\'t spend the same money twice.</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">To get Bitcoins, you need to meet two conditions. One is a minimum of security; the other is a question of luck.</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.482;background-color:#f8fafc;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\"><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You need to check ~1MB of data. This is the most important task.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You have to be the first miner to give the right answer to a number. This answer is also known as \"work performance.\"</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.44;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:7pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: inherit;\">The 1MB limit was set by Satoshi Nakamoto and is the subject of controversy, as some miners believe that the block size should be increased to hold more data. This would allow the network to process more data and process more transactions. 1 MB of transactions can be as small as one transaction (although this is not very common) or several thousand, depending on how much money you want to spend on the purchase. It\'s time to take a closer look at the cryptocurrency process and understand how it works.</span></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: inherit;\"><br></span></div></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Nodes: Check transactions for legitimacy</b></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Transactions: Form the basis for building a market economy. So, let\'s look at the entire process to understand how it all fits together:</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Example</b>:</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Let\'s say you\'re a cryptominer, and your friend Andy borrows $5,000 from another friend named Jake to buy a fancy new high-end gaming setup. This is a device with the best gaming characteristics, from the LED mouse to the multi-456 screen display to the killer combo headset with microphone. To calm him down, Andy sends him a letter. He has to go through a lengthy process to complete the verification (more on that in a moment).</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Individual tasks are added to a list of other tasks to form a block. The next step is to bundle all operations into a list that is added to a new, incomplete record. The payment of Andy\'s Bitcoin to Jake would be considered a transaction. By adding the transaction to the blockchain (once verification is complete), spending cryptocurrencies can be interrupted by a permanent record. The record is immutable, which means that it cannot be manipulated or altered. A hash and other types of data are added to the unconfirmed list. If multiple transactions are added, the hash of the previous block and a new hash for the new block will also be added. The header of the last block and a new hash value are combined to produce the new hash value. This hash value is added to the incomplete protocol and then has to be verified by a miner. Suppose you are so happy that you are the one who is most pleased. You should call all the other miners on the network to tell them that you have done something great and have them confirm it. Miners check the hash of the block to confirm that the block is legitimate.</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In this procedural step, the other members verify the authenticity of the incomplete document by checking the hash value. But how to encrypt a hash file? Imagine applying a SHA-256 hash value to the plain text \"I live nearby.\" This means that the hash valuan SHA-256\"6a0aa6e5058089f590f9562b3a299326ea54dfad1add8f0a141b731580f558a7\"Well, I don\'t know about you, but I certainly won\'t be able to read what that long line in the text says. Once the block is confirmed, the block is published on the blockchain.</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the job market, proof-of-work (PoW) is the most important component of work. PoW is the time-consuming task of finding the hash and proving to others that you did it legitimately, in a way that they can verify. For the user, this means that Andy\'s transfer of a Bitcoin block to Jake is now confirmed and added to the block\'s blockchain. As the most recent blockchain, the new blockchain was only added at the end of the blockchain period. This is because blockchain ledgers are chronological and build on previously published entries.</span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.2.4.5 Why is crypto mining done?</span></span></b></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">People like to use money for payments—whether it\'s with credit cards, PayPal, or Venmo—to buy money and send it to friends or acquaintances. However, in a world where many people want to avoid the \"hassle\" of cash and coins, the question arises as to how to do crypto mining. There is no clear answer to this question, because after all, we all have different needs, interests, and goals. We would now like to present some of these reasons.</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">People want more privacy and control over their finances. Not everyone is as honest as others on this matter. Many want more security and peace of mind, especially when it comes to the security of their assets. This means that Uncle Sam shouldn\'t know when you bought your new surround system and how much you spent on it. To bypass some of traditional centralized banking, some people keep their money under the mattress or in an old safe deposit box. However, there is also another way to remove money from the traditional, centralized banking system: the use of cryptocurrencies.</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin, Dash, Ethereum, and Monero offer users a certain level of anonymity. Why? Because the process of key encryption and hashing that we talked about increases anonymity.</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It\'s about the Benjamin Franklins. According to Coherent Marketing, the fiber optic cable market will be worth $38 billion by 2025. For many people, using the internet is extremely profitable and is considered a good investment. However, this is not always the case, as mining is often expensive and does not always bring a high profit. However, some cryptocurrencies, such as Bitcoin, have significant value, mainly due to their limited total supply of 21 million BTC, of which 18,512,200 BTC are already in circulation. People have the opportunity to buy and sell Bitcoins, with 100,000,000 Satoshis per BTC existing. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: inherit;\">Crypto is still new, exciting, and shiny. One reason for this is that there are people who want to use the new technology to participate in the market. Essentially, they want to be part of the next big trend. But how many people are involved in crypto mining? On June 23, 2020, PR Newswire issued a press release stating that \"there are now more than 1,000,000 Bitcoin miners.\" This number only applies to those who have specifically chosen Bitcoin! </span></h4><div><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: inherit;\"><br></span></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.44; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What does this mean for the environment? Proof-of-work mining requires significant computing power and energy, leading to concerns about environmental impact. Mining without your own hardware, as is the case with cloud mining, allows anyone to get started without high costs. The return on investment (ROI) for mining is currently high, but the time it takes to achieve ROI is long. The scope of the equipment depends on the technology and the number of video devices. (PTGR, n.d.)</span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.482; background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></h4><div><div><div><div><div>\n\n\n\n</div></div></div></div></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-10 07:22:14','2026-01-09 11:43:15'),(64,21,'What are cryptocurrencies?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e03a3c73-7fff-44a5-563a-8b49f2675b81\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">With Bitcoin, Ethereum, and other cryptocurrencies, we are breaking new ground in investing, banking, and using money.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies are basically decentralized, digital money created for use on the internet. The first cryptocurrency, Bitcoin, was launched in 2008, and it remains by far the largest, most influential, and most well-known cryptocurrency. Over the past decade, Bitcoin and other cryptocurrencies such as Ethereum have evolved into digital alternatives to money issued by government agencies.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/7.gif\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-65bb3b26-7fff-c3ba-47b1-f410646fdf3e\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 1: Bitcoin transfer since 2009</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: CoinMetrics.io)</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">From a market cap perspective, Bitcoin, Ethereum, Bitcoin Cash, and Litecoin are some of the most popular cryptocurrencies. Other well-known cryptocurrencies include Tezos, EOS, and ZCash. Some of these are comparable to Bitcoin. Others rely on different technologies or can do more than just transfer assets thanks to new functions.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies allow assets to be transferred online without resorting to an intermediary such as a bank or payment system. In this way, assets can be transferred worldwide, practically in real time, around the clock, and at low fees.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies are not usually issued or controlled by governments or other central authorities. They are managed by peer-to-peer computer networks that use free, open-source software. In principle, anyone who wants to participate can get involved.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Who or what guarantees the security of cryptocurrencies if there are no banks or government agencies behind them? Cryptocurrencies are secure because all transactions are verified using a technology called blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The blockchain of a cryptocurrency is comparable to the balance sheet or ledger of a bank. Each currency has its own blockchain. It is an ongoing, constantly rechecked register that records every single transaction that has been carried out with that currency.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Unlike a bank\'s ledger, the blockchain of cryptocurrencies is distributed among all participants in the digital currency network</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">No company, country, or third-party provider has control over this network, and anyone can become a participant. A blockchain is a groundbreaking technology that has only recently become available and is the result of decades of innovation in computer science and mathematics.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Basic concepts</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Transferability</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Thanks to cryptocurrencies, financial transactions with people on the other side of the globe are just as easy as paying with money in your local grocery store.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-4f5da887-7fff-2651-0e0d-3026c326b7c2\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/8.gif\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 2: Transfer Bitcoin inexpensively and extremely quickly</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Bank of America, JPM CHase, Coinmetrics.io)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Privacy</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">When you pay with cryptocurrencies, you do not have to disclose any superfluous personal data to the merchant. This ensures that your financial data is not shared with third parties such as banks, payment providers, advertisers, and credit reference agencies. And because there is no need to send sensitive data over the internet, there is extremely little risk of your financial data falling into the wrong hands or your identity being stolen.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Safety</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Almost all cryptocurrencies, including Bitcoin, Ethereum, Tezos, and Bitcoin Cash, are secured via a technology called blockchain. The blockchain is continuously checked and verified using enormous computing power.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/9.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-34639a3f-7fff-b8d4-acb6-602bfc746b99\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 3: Hardware cost to achieve majority hashrate in billions of dollars</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Bitmain.com and Blockchain.info)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Mobility</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Since your holdings of cryptocurrencies are not tied to a financial institution or government entity, they are available to you regardless of location and also regardless of what happens to the major global financial intermediaries.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Transparency</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Every transaction on the Bitcoin, Ethereum, Tezos, and Bitcoin Cash networks can be viewed publicly without exception. This means that neither the transactions nor the money supply nor the regulations can be changed retrospectively.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Irreversibility</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Unlike credit card payments, cryptocurrency payments cannot be reversed. This greatly reduces the risk of fraud for merchants. As far as customers are concerned, this could reduce the cost of purchase transactions, as it removes one of the main arguments used by credit card providers to justify their high processing fees.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Protection</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The network that underpins Bitcoin has never been hacked. And the basic concepts that form the foundation of cryptocurrencies contribute to their security: they are permissionless systems, and the core software is open source. This means that countless computer scientists and cryptography experts have been able to examine all aspects of networks and their security.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.1.1 Why are cryptocurrencies the future of finance?</span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies are the first alternative to traditional banking, and they have huge advantages over previous payment methods and traditional asset classes. Think of cryptocurrencies as a kind of Money 2.0—a new type of money born on the internet, which has the potential to become the fastest, easiest, cheapest, safest, and most universal method of exchanging assets ever.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies can be used to purchase goods and services or held as part of an investment strategy. However, they cannot be manipulated by a central authority, as there is simply no such authority. Your cryptocurrency is and will remain safe—no matter what happens at the government level.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/10.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 4: Bitcoin has outperformed the world\'s stock indices</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Tradingview)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Digital currencies enable equal opportunities, regardless of where you were born or lived. As long as you have a smartphone or other device with an internet connection, you have the same access to cryptocurrencies as everyone else.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 8pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">At Coinbase, we believe diverse opinions, backgrounds, and experiences are essential in creating an open financial system that\'s equitable and accessible to all. In our survey, 48% of Black Americans indicated they have been negatively impacted by the current financial system (banking, currencies, stock markets, lending/borrowing, etc.) because of their race or gender.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies create unique opportunities to expand the economic freedom of people worldwide. The fact that digital currencies in principle know no borders promotes free trade, even in countries that rigorously control the finances of their citizens. In places where the main problem is inflation, cryptocurrencies can offer an alternative to failed fiat currencies for savings and payments.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As part of a broader investment strategy, there are a wide variety of ways to add cryptocurrencies. One approach is to buy and hold a cryptocurrency, such as Bitcoin, which was virtually worthless in 2008 and is now worth thousands of dollars per coin. Another option would be a more active strategy, i.e., buying and selling cryptocurrencies that go through volatile periods.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">One option for investors who are interested in cryptocurrencies but don\'t want to take too much risk is the USD Coin currency, which is pegged 1:1 to the value of the US dollar. It combines the benefits of cryptocurrencies, including the ability to make international transfers in a fast and cheap way, with the stability of a traditional currency. Coinbase customers who hold USDC receive rewards, making the currency an attractive alternative to a traditional savings account.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Why invest in cryptocurrencies?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Online exchanges like Coinbase have made buying and selling cryptocurrencies easy, secure, and financially interesting.</span></span></span></span></p></li><ul style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It only takes a few minutes to create a secure account, and then you can buy cryptocurrencies by debit card or bank account.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You can buy any amount of cryptocurrencies, as fractions of coins can also be purchased. For example, you can buy $25 worth of Bitcoin.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Many digital currencies, including USD Coin and Tezos, offer currency holders rewards purely for holding.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">On Coinbase, you can earn an annual interest rate of up to 1%, which is quite a bit higher than the interest on most traditional savings accounts.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You can also earn an APR of up to 5% when you stake Tezos on Coinbase. Learn more about the rewards for staking Tezos.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Unlike stocks or bonds, you can easily transfer your cryptocurrencies to other people or use them to buy goods or services.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#2f5496;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#2f5496;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Millions of people hold Bitcoin and other digital currencies as an admixture in their investment portfolios.</span></span></div><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/11+a.gif\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 5: Buying Bitcoin would have generated 595% profit over the past 4 years</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: dcabtc.com)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is a stablecoin?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">USD Coin is an example of a cryptocurrency called a stablecoin. You could call these currencies crypto-dollars—they are designed for minimal volatility and maximum usability. Stablecoins combine some of the best features of cryptocurrencies (seamless global transactions, security, and privacy) with the valuation stability of fiat currencies.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Stablecoins achieve this by pegging their value to an external factor, usually a fiat currency like the U.S. dollar or a commodity like gold.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As a result, their valuations are less likely to fluctuate drastically from one day to the next. This stability can increase its suitability as everyday money, as both buyers and merchants can trust that the value of their transaction will hardly change over a longer period of time.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">They can also serve as a safe and stable tool to invest savings, like with a traditional savings account.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Crucial question</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What does the future of cryptocurrencies look like?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Experts often highlight that cryptocurrencies can address the shortcomings of our current financial system. High fees, identity theft, and extreme economic inequality are unfortunately part of our current financial system, and cryptocurrencies can offer potential solutions to these problems. The technology that underpins digital currencies also has far-reaching potential beyond the financial industry, from radically reshaping supply chains to building a new, decentralized internet.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.1.2 How do cryptocurrencies work?</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is the first and most well-known cryptocurrency, but it\'s not the only one; there are thousands of different cryptocurrencies. Many of these, such as Litecoin and Bitcoin Cash, have adopted the essential properties of Bitcoin but are exploring new ways to process transactions. Others offer a wider range of features. Ethereum, for example, can be used to run applications and create contracts. However, all four are based on a concept called blockchain, which is crucial if you want to understand how cryptocurrencies work.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Basically, a blockchain is a list of transactions that anyone can view and verify. For example, the Bitcoin blockchain is a register that records when someone sends or receives Bitcoin. This transaction list is fundamental for most cryptocurrencies because it allows secure payments between people who don\'t know each other without the use of an external verification agency, such as a bank.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Blockchain technology is also exciting because it offers many possible applications beyond cryptocurrencies. Blockchains are used in medical research, to improve the sharing of patient data, to streamline supply chains, to strengthen privacy on the internet, and in many other areas of application.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The basic principles behind Bitcoin, as well as the Bitcoin blockchain, were first published in a white paper published in late 2007 by a person or group named Satoshi Nakamoto.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The blockchain ledger, a kind of account book, is distributed across all computers in the network, which continuously check whether the blockchain is correct. This means that there is no central vault, company, or database that is vulnerable to hacking, theft, or tampering.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Concept</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies rely on an asymmetric encryption method that uses public and private keys to transfer ownership of coins within a secure and distributed ledger. A private key (Coinbase, n.d.) is an extremely secure password. It must never be shared with others. This key can be used to transfer assets on the network. A matching public key can be easily shared with other people to preserve assets on the network. No one can draw conclusions about your private key based on the public key.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What does cryptocurrency mining mean?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The units of most cryptocurrencies are generated through a decentralized (also known as peer-to-peer) computer network as part of a process called \"mining.\" But mining doesn\'t just create more Bitcoin or Ethereum units. It is also a mechanism that updates and secures the network by continuously reviewing the public blockchain ledger and adding new transactions.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In principle, anyone with a computer and an internet connection can act as a miner. But don\'t get too excited; it\'s important to remember that mining isn\'t always lucrative. Depending on what cryptocurrency you mine, how fast your computer is, and how much electricity costs in your area, your bottom line mining expenses could exceed your cryptocurrency earnings.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">For this reason, cryptocurrency mining is nowadays largely carried out by specialized companies or by individuals who provide their computing power in large groups.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How does the network motivate miners to participate in the maintenance of the blockchain? In the case of Bitcoin, for example, the network uses a lottery procedure in which all mining rigs worldwide compete with each other. Here, the first thing they try to do is solve a mathematical problem that simultaneously checks the blockchain and adds new transactions to it. Each winner receives new Bitcoins, which then find their way into the broader market.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Crucial question</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What determines the value of a cryptocurrency?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The economic value of cryptocurrencies, as with all other goods and services, is determined by supply and demand.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The supply refers to the amount available; for example, how many Bitcoin are available for purchase at any given time. Demand refers to the desire to possess, i.e., how many people want to buy Bitcoin and how strong their desire to do so is. The value of a cryptocurrency is always determined by the ratio of these two factors.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">But cryptocurrency can also be very valuable in other ways. For example, you get a benefit from using a cryptocurrency. Many people enjoy spending or giving away cryptocurrencies. In other words, they are proud to support an exciting new financial system. Similarly, some people like to shop with Bitcoin because they find the low fees attractive and want to achieve greater acceptance of Bitcoin among companies.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.1.3 How to buy Bitcoin and other cryptocurrencies</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The easiest way to acquire cryptocurrencies is through an online exchange such as Coinbase.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">On Coinbase you buy the most popular cryptocurrencies, including Bitcoin (BTC), Litecoin (LTC), Ethereum (ETH), Bitcoin Cash (BCH), and Ethereum Classic (ETC). Or you can invest in emerging coins like Stellar Lumens or EOS.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The best thing to do is to ask yourself what you want to do with a cryptocurrency and then choose the currency that best achieves your goals. For example, if you want to buy a laptop with a cryptocurrency, Bitcoin would probably be a good choice because it is the cryptocurrency with the most adoption. However, if you want to play a digital card game, Ethereum is more likely to do so.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Note that you don\'t have to buy a whole coin. On Coinbase, you can also buy parts of coins in increments from as little as $2, euros, pounds, or in your local currency.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How are cryptocurrencies stored?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Storing cryptocurrencies is similar to storing money, which means you need to protect them from theft and loss. There are many ways to store cryptocurrencies both online and offline, but the simplest solution is a trusted, secure exchange like Coinbase.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Customers can securely store, send, receive, and exchange cryptocurrencies by logging into their account via computer, tablet, or phone.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Want to transfer money from your wallet to a bank account? With the Coinbase app, this process is as easy as transferring money from one bank to another. (Similar to traditional bank transfers or ATM withdrawals, exchanges </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:#d4d4d4;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">like</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> Coinbase set a daily limit, and it can take anywhere from a few days to a week for the transaction to complete.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What can you do with cryptocurrencies?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There is a wide range of applications for cryptocurrencies, and new ones are being added over time. Here are some ideas to help you get started, from everyday activities to exploring new technological frontiers:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Shopping: Several thousand merchants already accept cryptocurrencies worldwide.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Donate for a good cause: There are benefits to donating and accepting cryptocurrencies, and many nonprofits accept Bitcoin donations. (Company, 2019)</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Gifting: Cryptocurrencies are an excellent gift for friends and family who are interested in new technologies.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Tip: Authors, musicians, and other online content creators sometimes leave their Bitcoin address or a QR code at the bottom of their articles. If you like their content, you can say thank you with a small amount of crypto.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Discover new and unique connections between money and technology: Orchid is a VPN that protects you online while also serving as a digital currency. Orchid is basically divided into two parts: there\'s the Orchid VPN app and the OXT cryptocurrency, and both parts are built on top of the Ethereum network. Mesmerized? Find out more here.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Travel worldwide: Since cryptocurrencies are not tied to a specific country, traveling with cryptocurrencies can reduce the costs associated with currency exchange operations. There is already a small but steadily growing community of self-proclaimed \"crypto nomads\" who pay primarily or in some cases exclusively with cryptocurrencies when traveling.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Buy possessions in a virtual game world: Decentraland, which is also built on the Ethereum blockchain, is the first virtual world to be fully owned by its users. Users can buy and sell land, avatar clothing, and various other items while partying in virtual nightclubs or mingling in virtual art galleries.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Discover decentralized finance, also known as DeFi: A wide range of new companies aim to replicate the entire global financial system, from investing in structures similar to mutual funds to mechanisms for issuing/borrowing and far beyond, without any central authorities. (Coinbase, n.d.)</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p></li></ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre;\"><br></span></font></li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-984d5462-7fff-3700-1acd-a7f5ca8e7124\"></span></span></p></ul></span></span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"></span></font>\n\n</div></span></span></div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 07:32:22','2026-01-09 11:47:10'),(65,21,'What is Bitcoin?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-d4c87cc2-7fff-e2eb-9d86-03f9d7abd3be\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The world\'s first widely used cryptocurrency. With Bitcoin, people can send digital money securely and directly to each other on the Internet.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin was created by Satoshi Nakamoto, a pseudonymous person or team who summarized the technology in a white paper (Nakamoto, n.d.) in 2008. It is an appealingly simple concept: Bitcoin is digital money that enables secure peer-to-peer transactions on the Internet.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Unlike services like Venmo and PayPal, which rely on the traditional financial system of money and existing debit/credit accounts for permission to transfer, Bitcoin is decentralized: two people, no matter where they are in the world, can send Bitcoin to each other without the need for a bank, government agency, or other institution.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Every transaction regarding Bitcoin is registered in the blockchain. A blockchain is similar to a bank\'s ledger or the directory of customer funds that are deposited and withdrawn from a bank. Simply put, it is the record of all transactions that have ever been made with Bitcoin.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Unlike a bank\'s ledger, the Bitcoin blockchain is spread across the entire network. No company, country, or third-party provider has control over this network, and anyone can become a part of it.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There will only ever be 21 million Bitcoin. This is digital money that cannot be affected by inflation or manipulation in any way.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You don\'t necessarily have to buy a whole Bitcoin: you can only buy a fraction of a coin if that\'s all you want or need.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"__Montserrat_069ab3, __Montserrat_Fallback_069ab3, Montserrat, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Crucial questions:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is BTC?</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">BTC is the abbreviation for Bitcoin.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Is Bitcoin a cryptocurrency?</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Yes, Bitcoin is the first widely used cryptocurrency, which is just another name for digital money.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Is there a simple Bitcoin definition?</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is digital money that enables secure and seamless peer-to-peer transactions on the internet.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is the price of Bitcoin?</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The current price of Bitcoin can be found on the Coinbase website.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Is Bitcoin an investment opportunity?</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As with any other asset, you can make money by buying BTC at a low price and selling it at a high price. However, you can also lose money in the reverse scenario.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What was Bitcoin\'s starting price?</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">At the beginning of 2010, a BTC had a value of a fraction of a US penny. In the first quarter of 2011, the value was already over one dollar. At the end of 2017, its value skyrocketed and stood at almost $20,000. You can track the price of Bitcoin here.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/13.gif\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b0c94aa7-7fff-2ee2-8bb0-0f9fc6780d84\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 6: Buying Bitcoin would have generated 595% profit over the past 4 years</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: dcabtc.com)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.2.1 Bitcoin Basics</span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Since Bitcoin\'s inception, thousands of new cryptocurrencies have been introduced, but Bitcoin (abbreviated BTC) is still the most successful in terms of market capitalization and trading volume.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/14.gif\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-2fba1422-7fff-a37f-3ac5-ba7c57ee3ef5\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 7: Bitcoin transfer since 2009</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: CoinMetrics.io)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Depending on your goals, Bitcoin can be used as</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Investment Vehicle</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Store of value, comparable to gold</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ability to transfer funds worldwide</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">just a way to explore a new technology</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is a currency native to the Internet. Unlike government-issued currencies such as the dollar or the euro, Bitcoin allows online transfers without intermediaries such as a bank or payment system. The removal of these coordinators creates a whole host of new opportunities, including the potential to move money around the world on the internet faster and more cost-effectively, and allows individuals to have maximum control over their own assets.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It\'s legal to use, hold, and trade Bitcoin, and it can be spent on anything from travel to charity donations. It is accepted as a form of payment by companies such as Microsoft and Expedia.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Is Bitcoin money? It is used as a medium of exchange, store of value, and unit of account—all of which are properties of money. Meanwhile, it only exists digitally, and there is no physical version of it.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.2.2 Who Launched Bitcoin?</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">To really understand how Bitcoin works, it\'s helpful to start at the beginning. The question of who actually launched Bitcoin is fascinating, because even a decade after the technology was invented and despite a lot of research by journalists and members of the crypto community, its creator remains anonymous.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin was launched via whitepaper Oct 31, 2008, by Satoshi Nakamoto</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This white paper is not the first time that the idea of digital money that makes use of the fields of cryptography and computer science has been considered. Indeed, the publication refers to previous concepts, but it was a uniquely elegant solution to the problem of building trust between the various online entities, where people (like Bitcoin\'s own creator) often hide behind pseudonyms or are physically on the other side of the planet.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Nakamoto developed a pair of intertwined concepts: the Bitcoin private key and the blockchain ledger. If you own Bitcoins, you control them via a private key—a sequence of randomly selected numbers and letters that unlocks a virtual vault when you make a purchase. Each private key is tracked on the virtual ledger, which is called the blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"__Montserrat_069ab3, __Montserrat_Fallback_069ab3, Montserrat, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">When Bitcoin first appeared, it was a great advance in computer science, as it solved a fundamental problem of trading on the Internet: how to transfer funds between two people without a trusted intermediary (like a bank)? By solving this problem, Bitcoin\'s invention had far-reaching implications: as a currency for the internet, it enables cross-border and global financial transactions without the involvement of banks, credit card companies, lenders, or even governments. If two people wherever they live can and payments to each other without encountering these coordinators, this creates the potential for an open financial system that is more efficient, freer, and innovative. In short, this is Bitcoin.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/15.gif\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 8: Annual global interest in Bitcoin</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Trends)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.2.3 How Bitcoin Works</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Unlike credit card networks like Visa and payment systems like PayPal, Bitcoin doesn\'t belong to any individual or company. Bitcoin is the world\'s first freely accessible payment network that anyone with an internet connection can participate in. Bitcoin was designed for use on the internet and does not rely on banks or private companies to process transactions.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">One of the most important elements of Bitcoin is its blockchain, which tracks who owns what, similar to how a bank tracks assets. What distinguishes the Bitcoin blockchain from a bank\'s ledger is its decentralization. This means that anyone can view the blockchain, and no single entity has control over it.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Here are a few details on how it all works:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-5da0bb8e-7fff-4def-246a-dfefd3c55e30\"></span></span></p><ul style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration-line: none; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Specialized computers, called \"mining rigs,\" perform the equations needed to verify and record a new transaction. In the early days, a typical desktop PC was powerful enough to participate in mining, so pretty much anyone who was interested could try their hand at it. Today, the computers needed are massive, specialized, and often belong to companies or a large number of individuals pooling their resources. (In October 2019, it took 12 trillion times more computing power to mine a Bitcoin than it did when Nakamoto mined the first blocks in January 2009.)</span></span></div><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; background-color: transparent; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p></li></ul><div style=\"\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/16.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-cdaa013a-7fff-ff16-ae66-229c0171b604\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 9: Hardware Cost to Achieve Majority Hashrate in Billions of Dollars</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Bitmain.com, Blockchain.info)</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 12px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The combined computing power of the miners is used to ensure the accuracy of the ever-growing ledger. Bitcoin is inextricably linked to the blockchain. Every new Bitcoin is recorded on this, as well as every subsequent transaction with all existing coins.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How does the network motivate miners to participate in the constant, essential work of maintaining the blockchain and verifying transactions? You can think of the Bitcoin network as a constant lottery, where all miners around the world want to solve a mathematical problem first. About every 10 minutes, a winner is found, and the winner updates the Bitcoin ledger with new valid transactions. The prize changes over time, but since the beginning of 2020, each winner of this raffle has received 12.5 Bitcoins.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the beginning, a Bitcoin was basically worthless. At the end of 2019, trading was around $7,500. As the value of Bitcoin has increased, its easy divisibility (the ability to buy a small fraction of a Bitcoin) has become a key attribute. One Bitcoin is currently divisible into eight decimal places (100 millionths of a Bitcoin). The Bitcoin community refers to the smallest unit as a \"Satoshi.\"</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Nakamoto has set up the network in such a way that the amount of Bitcoins never exceeds 21 million, which ensures their scarcity. Currently, around three million Bitcoin are still available for mining, a process that will happen more and more slowly. The last blocks will theoretically be mined in 2140.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/17.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 10: Overview of differences between cryptocurrencies and other currencies</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Coinbase.com)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cryptocurrencies and traditional currencies have some features in common, such as how you can use them to buy things or transfer them electronically. However, they also differ in interesting ways. Here are some highlights.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 2.4; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is the world\'s first freely accessible payment network that anyone with an internet connection can participate in.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Crucial question:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How do Bitcoins get their value?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-73d272de-7fff-9fda-044e-d6d8e1fbb492\"></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Essentially the same as a traditional currency because they have proven to be a viable and convenient way to store value, meaning they can be easily exchanged for goods, services, or other assets. They are rare (compared to gold, for example), secure, portable, and also easily shareable, allowing transactions of all sizes.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/18.gif\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 11: Bitcoin transfer since 2009</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: CoinMetrics.io)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.2.4 How to get Bitcoin</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The easiest way to buy Bitcoins is through any online exchange. There, you can easily buy, sell, send, receive, and store Bitcoins without having to hold them yourself using so-called public and private keys.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">However, if you choose to buy and store Bitcoins outside of an online exchange, here\'s how it works.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Each person who joins the Bitcoin network receives a public key, a long string of letters and numbers that you can think of as an email address, and a private key that corresponds to a password.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">When you buy or send/receive bitcoins, you receive a public key, which you can think of as a key that unlocks a virtual vault and gives you access to your funds.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Anyone can send you bitcoins using your public key, but only the private key holder can access the bitcoins in the \"virtual vault\" once they have been sent.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There are many ways to store Bitcoins, both online and offline. The simplest solution is a virtual wallet.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If you want to transfer money from your wallet to a bank account after selling your bitcoins, the Coinbase app makes it as easy as transferring funds from one bank to another. Similar to traditional bank transfers or ATM withdrawals, exchanges like Coinbase set a daily limit, and it can take anywhere from a few days to a week for the transaction to complete.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Crucial question:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is the difference between Bitcoin and blockchain?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">All Bitcoin transactions and public keys are recorded in a virtual ledger called a blockchain. The ledger is, in a sense, a chronological list of transactions. This ledger is copied in exactly the same form to every computer connected to the Bitcoin network, and it is constantly checked and backed up with an enormous amount of computing power around the world. The blockchain concept has proven to be powerful and adaptable, and there are now a variety of blockchains that are not related to cryptocurrencies and are used for supply chain management, for example. The \"Bitcoin blockchain\" refers specifically to the virtual ledger where Bitcoin transactions and private keys are recorded.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.2.5 How Bitcoin is used</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In 2013, a Bitcoin enthusiast named Laszlo Hanyecz created a post on a forum where he offered 10,000 BTC to someone who delivered two pizzas to his home in Jacksonville, Florida, which was worth around $25 at the time. As the legend goes, these two pizzas, which another early Bitcoin user bought at a local Papa John\'s, went down in history as the first successful purchase of non-virtual goods using Bitcoins. Luckily, it\'s much easier to use Bitcoins these days!</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It\'s simple: transactions with BTC are not much different from transactions with a credit or debit card. However, instead of being asked to enter card information, simply enter the payment amount and the service provider\'s public key (similar to an email address) via a wallet app. (For in-person transactions using smartphones or tablets, a QR code is often displayed to make the process easier. When you scan the code, your wallet app will automatically fill in the relevant information.)</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It\'s private: One of the benefits of paying with bitcoins is that it limits the amount of personal information you need to provide. You only need to provide your name and address if you are purchasing physical goods that need to be shipped.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It\'s flexible: what you should do with your Bitcoins depends entirely on your personal interests. Here are a few ideas:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You can sell it for money on an exchange or at a Bitcoin ATM.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You can spend it with a Bitcoin debit card like any other currency online or in brick-and-mortar stores.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You can keep some or all of it as part of your investment and savings strategy.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You can donate to a charitable cause that is important to you.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">And if you have a big budget and dream of an unfulfilling astronaut career? Richard Branson\'s Virgin Galactic is happy to accept BTC in exchange for the opportunity to embark on one of its upcoming space tourism missions.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 72pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 2.4; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Due to the cryptographic nature of the Bitcoin network, Bitcoin payments are inherently more secure than standard debit/credit card transactions.</span></span></span></span></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b>2.3.2.6 What Makes Bitcoin a New Type of Money?</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is global. You can send the Bitcoins across the entire planet as easily as you can pay with cash in the physical world. With Bitcoin, there is no closure on weekends, no fee is charged to access your own money, and no arbitrary restrictions are imposed.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is irreversible. Bitcoin behaves like cash in the sense that transactions cannot be reversed by the sender. In comparison, credit cards, traditional online payment systems, and bank transactions can be canceled after payment is made, sometimes months after the initial transaction—due to the central intermediary making the transactions. This leads to a higher risk of fraud for merchants, which in turn can lead to higher fees for using credit cards.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is private. When you pay with Bitcoins, there are no bank statements or the need to provide unnecessary personal information to the merchant. Bitcoin transactions do not contain any identifying information other than the Bitcoin addresses and amounts involved.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is safe. Due to the cryptographic nature of the Bitcoin network, Bitcoin payments are inherently more secure than standard debit/credit card transactions. When making a Bitcoin payment, there is no need to send confidential information over the internet. There is a very low risk of your financial information being compromised or your identity being stolen.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is open. Every transaction on the Bitcoin network is made public without exception. This means that there is no room for manipulation of transactions (apart from a highly unlikely 51% attack scenario) or for a change in the Bitcoin supply. The software that forms the core of Bitcoin is free and open-source, so anyone can review the code.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is protected. In more than ten years, the Bitcoin network has never been successfully hacked. And because the system offers free access and is open source, countless computer scientists and cryptographers have been able to examine all aspects of the network and its security.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.2.7 Where does Bitcoin come from?</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin is effectively \"mined\" by a huge, decentralized (also known as \"peer-to-peer\") computer network that constantly checks and secures the accuracy of the blockchain. Every single Bitcoin transaction is reflected in this ledger, with new information periodically aggregated into a \"block\" that is added to all previous blocks. (Coinbase, n.d</span>.)</span></span></span></p></li></ul><div><br></div><div style=\"\"><font style=\"\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"></span></font></font>\n</div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 07:40:27','2026-01-09 11:52:51'),(66,21,'What is Ethereum?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-5b8afccd-7fff-fb5b-2d07-ead81923619a\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum is the second-largest cryptocurrency in terms of market capitalization after Bitcoin. It is also a decentralized computing platform on which a large number of different applications can be carried out, including the entire DeFi universe.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum, launched in 2015, is the second-largest cryptocurrency in terms of market capitalization after Bitcoin. Unlike Bitcoin, however, it was not originally designed as a digital currency. Instead, Ethereum\'s founders wanted to develop a new type of global, decentralized computing platform that had the security and openness of blockchains (Coinbase, n.d.) and extended these characteristics to a variety of applications.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">From financial instruments to games to complex databases, everything is already being done on the Ethereum blockchain, and its future potential is limited only by the imagination of developers. The non-profit Ethereum Foundation says, \"With Ethereum, pretty much everything can be codified, decentralized, secured, and traded.\"</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum has become a popular investment vehicle and repository of assets (and, like Bitcoin, can be used to send or receive value without intermediaries).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Through the Ethereum blockchain, developers can develop and run a huge number of applications, including everything from games and modern databases to complex decentralized financial instruments, meaning they don\'t require a bank or other intermediary institutions.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Ethereum-based applications are developed using \"smart contracts.\" Smart Contracts (Coinbase, n.d.) work like traditional paper contracts. They set out the terms of an agreement between the parties. But unlike an old-fashioned contract, smart contracts are executed automatically when the conditions are met, without the participating parties knowing who is the counterparty to the transaction and without the need for an intermediary.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum, like Bitcoin, is an open-source project that is not owned or operated by an individual. Anyone with an internet connection can create an Ethereum node or interact with the network.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Just like the decentralized Bitcoin blockchain allows two unknowns anywhere in the world to send or receive money without the intermediary of a bank, the smart contracts conducted on Ethereum\'s decentralized blockchain allow developers to create complex applications that run exactly as programmed, without being affected by interruptions, censorship, fraud, or interference from external parties.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Popular Ethereum-based innovations include stablecoins (Coinbase, n.d.) (such as the DAI, whose value is pegged to the US dollar through a smart contract), decentralized finance applications (called DeFi), and other decentralized apps (also called dApps).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is the difference between Ethereum, Ether, and ETH?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum is the name of the network. \"Ether\" is the native cryptocurrency token used by the Ethereum network. However, in everyday parlance, the token is most often referred to as \"ETH\" (or simply \"Ethereum\"). As a way to send, receive, or store value, ETH works almost the same way as Bitcoin, but it also has a special role in the Ethereum network. Because users pay the fees to execute the smart contracts in ETH, it could be seen as the fuel that keeps the whole thing going (hence, these fees are also known as \"gas\").</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If you compare Bitcoin to \"digital gold,\" then you could compare ETH to \"digital oil.\"</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.3.1 Is Ethereum safe?</span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">ETH is currently secured by the Ethereum blockchain in the same way that Bitcoin is secured by its blockchain. A large proportion of the computing power contributed by all the computers on the network verifies and secures all transactions, making third-party intervention virtually impossible.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/19.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-3cbe2f63-7fff-8463-2613-600c4d4271e4\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 12: Ethereum logo</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Coinbase.com)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The basic concepts that form the basis of cryptocurrencies contribute to their security: they are permissionless systems, and the core software is open source. This means that countless computer scientists and cryptography experts have been able to examine all aspects of networks and their security.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">However, applications that run on the Ethereum blockchain are only as secure as designed by their developers. For example, a code can sometimes be error-ridden, and this could lead to the loss of funds. So while the source code is visible to everyone, the user bases of the individual applications are much smaller than Ethereum as a whole and are therefore scrutinized by fewer eyes. It is therefore important to be aware of any decentralized application you want to use.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Ethereum protocol is currently being updated in a way that is designed to make it faster and even more secure. Details of this can be found in the Ethereum 2.0 section below.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\">2.3.3.2 How does Ethereum work?</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><b style=\"\"><br></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">You may already know that the Bitcoin blockchain is very similar to a bankbook or even a checkbook. It\'s a continuous list of all transactions that have ever been made on the network, all the way back to the first transaction, and all the computers on the network contribute their computing power to ensure that this list is accurate and secure.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Ethereum blockchain, on the other hand, is more like a computer: it also takes care of documenting and securing transactions but is significantly more flexible than the Bitcoin blockchain. Developers can use the Ethereum blockchain to develop a wide range of tools, from logistics management software to games and the full range of DeFi applications (which include everything from lending and borrowing to stock trading, etc.).</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum uses a \"virtual machine\" to provide these services. Such a machine is comparable to a huge, global computer made up of many individual computers running the Ethereum software. To keep these computers running, participants must invest in both hardware and electricity. To cover these costs, the network employs its own Bitcoin-like cryptocurrency called Ether (or ETH).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">ETH keeps everything running. You interact with the Ethereum network by paying the network to run the smart contracts with ETH. For this reason, fees paid in ETH are referred to as \"gas\" (i.e., fuel).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Gas prices fluctuate depending on how busy the network is. A new version of the Ethereum blockchain, called Ethereum 2.0, aims to increase efficiency. Its introduction began in December 2020. (The transition to the new blockchain is expected to take place over the next two years.)</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.3.3 What is Ethereum 2.0?</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum 2.0 (often referred to as ETH2) represents a major upgrade to the Ethereum network, designed to increase security, scalability, and energy efficiency while allowing the network to continue growing.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The transition from Ethereum 1.0 to Ethereum 2.0 was completed with the Merge on September 15, 2022, which replaced Ethereum’s energy-intensive Proof of Work (PoW) mechanism with Proof of Stake (PoS). Existing ETH holders did not need to take any action; their assets on Ethereum 1.0 automatically transitioned to the PoS Ethereum network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Subsequent upgrades have further enhanced network functionality:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Shapella Upgrade – April 12, 2023:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> Enabled withdrawals of staked ETH, unlocking liquidity for validators.</span></span></span></span></div></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proto-Danksharding / EIP-4844 – March 2024:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> Introduced a transaction data sharding mechanism to significantly reduce gas fees for rollups, paving the way for greater layer-2 scalability.</span></span></span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><br></font></div></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum 2.0 is now fully operational, with PoS securing the network and scaling improvements underway. These upgrades mark a fundamental shift in Ethereum’s architecture, making it more sustainable and capable of supporting broader decentralized applications and DeFi activity.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What made Ethereum 2.0 necessary?&nbsp;Moving a popular crypto asset to a new platform is a complex undertaking. However, it is necessary for Ethereum to scale and evolve. The reason for this is that the \"proof-of-work\" process used by the ETH 1.0 blockchain to verify transactions causes congestion and higher fees, as well as requiring the use of large resources (especially electricity).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is the proof-of-work process? How do cryptocurrency networks without intermediary central oversight, such as Visa or PayPal, ensure that no one spends the same money twice? They use a consensus method. When ETH 1.0 was launched, it applied the consensus process introduced by Bitcoin: the very aptly named proof-of-work process.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The proof-of-work process requires a high level of processing, which is mainly carried out by virtual \"miners\" (Coinbase, n.d.) that compete with each other worldwide to solve a time-consuming mathematical puzzle.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The winner gets to update the blockchain with the last verified transactions and is rewarded with a predetermined amount of ETH.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This process takes place every 30 seconds (as opposed to Bitcoin\'s 10-minute cycle). As traffic on the network has increased, the limitations of the proof-of-work process have become apparent in the form of congestion, with charges increasing unpredictably during these congestions.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">What is staking?</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Ethereum founders were aware of the limitations of the proof-of-work process. Therefore, a completely different solution was developed for Ethereum 2.0, a solution that will ultimately allow the network to process thousands of Ethereum transactions in a matter of seconds.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ethereum 2.0 uses a consensus process called Proof of Stake, which is faster, less resource-intensive, and (at least in theory) more secure. The end result is similar to the proof-of-work procedure in that a network participant is selected to verify recent transactions, update the blockchain, and earn some ETH.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">However, the proof-of-stake process does not require a network of competing miners to solve a puzzle as quickly as possible but a robust network of participants who are actually invested in the success of the company.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">These stakeholders are called validators. Instead of contributing to processing power, as miners do, validators contribute ETH to a \"staking pool.\"</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This process, in which ETH is contributed to the pool, is called staking. If you choose to stake some of your ETH, you will receive a reward equal to your stake.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The network selects a winner based on the amount of ETH each validator has in the pool, as well as the amount of time that amount of ETH is in the pool—so the most invested participants are rewarded.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Once the winner has validated the last block of transactions, other validators can confirm the correctness of the block. When the number of these confirmations reaches a threshold, the network updates the blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">All participating validators will receive a reward in ETH, which will be awarded by the network in proportion to the stake of each individual validator.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Anyone can participate in staking.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Introduction to Smart Contracts</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Smart contracts are based on a proposal first made in the 1990s by computer scientist and lawyer Nick Szabo. (Szabo, 1997) Szabo famously compared a smart contract to a coin-operated machine. Imagine a vending machine that dispenses a drink after inserting 25 cents. If you put a dollar in the vending machine and select a drink, then it is configured to either give you the drink and 75 cents change or (if the drink of your choice is sold out) ask you to choose something else or give you your dollar back. This is an example of a simple smart contract. Just as the vending machine does not require a human intermediary in the sales transaction, smart contracts can automate virtually any type of barter.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.3.4 A Brief History of Ethereum</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2013</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Vitalik Buterin, a 19-year-old programmer (and co-founder of Bitcoin Magazine), publishes a white paper proposing a highly flexible blockchain that could support virtually any type of transaction.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2014</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Toronto-based teenager is running a crowdfunding campaign with a team of co-founders, including Gavin Wood, where they are selling $18 million worth of tokens before launch to fund the development of the Ethereum protocol.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2015</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In July, the first public version of the Ethereum blockchain will be launched. The smart contract functionality will be introduced on the Ethereum blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2016</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Hackers steal approximately $50 million from a smart contract-driven venture capital fund called DAO (Decentralized Autonomous Organization) by exploiting a software bug.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In a controversial vote, the Ethereum community decides to change the protocol to recover the lost money. The Ethereum blockchain will be split (via a hard fork (Coinbase, n.d.)) into two separate blockchains, each with its own active community: Ethereum and Ethereum Classic.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2017</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The ERC-20 standard is created. This standard makes it easier for developers to develop compatible applications. ERC-20 defines a way to store a value (or token) (Coinbase, n.d.) on the Ethereum blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The first, widely popular Ethereum-based app is introduced. It is a game called CryptoKitties in which users collect and trade digital cats. The game becomes extremely popular (Mala, 2018). At the height of their popularity, rare digital cats sell for over $200,000.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The non-profit organization Ethereum Enterprise Alliance is formed to develop practical applications for smart contract technology. Its members include JP Morgan, Samsung, Microsoft, and Mastercard.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">MakerDAO, the first decentralized finance protocol (also called DeFi) on the Ethereum blockchain, is launched. Maker is also introducing the first ETH-based stablecoin, the DAI.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">ETH exceeds the value of $100 for the first time.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2018</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">DeFi, which aims to transform the financial services industry by making transactions faster, cheaper, and more secure, is gaining momentum with the launch of lending protocol Compound and decentralized exchange Uniswap.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The USDC stablecoin is launched. In the first year, 1 billion USDC will be issued, supported by the CENTRE consortium (a partnership between Coinbase and Circle).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">ETH breaks through the $1,000 mark for the first time in January before falling back below $100.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2020</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In December, the upgrade to Ethereum 2.0 will begin. The complete transition from Ethereum 1.0 to Ethereum 2.0 is expected to take about two years.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The proof-of-stake process will be introduced as part of the first phase of Ethereum 2.0. ETH 1.0 continues to use proof-of-work as a consensus mechanism.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2021</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">ETH hits a new all-time high of over $1,700 in February</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The current prices can be viewed at https://www.coinbase.com/price/ethereum</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.3.5 How to buy Ethereum?</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Regardless of how you acquire your ETH, it\'s important to understand some basic concepts. Each address on the Ethereum network is assigned a public and private key, and you need a wallet to manage your crypto assets.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Public key:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> This is the crypto version of an email address. Your Ethereum public key is the address where other people can send you ETH and Ethereum-based tokens like USDC and Dai. You can easily share this key with other people.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Private key: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This acts like a password. You should never share this private key with anyone else. A private key is a long string of letters and numbers. (It can also take the form of a phrase called a seed phrase (Coinbase HELP, n.d.).) You must never lose your private keys. If you lose these, you lose your Ether forever.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Wallet:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> To store and secure your Ether, you need a wallet. If you\'re just getting started, the easiest way is to set up an account either through the Coinbase app or on </span></span></span></span><a href=\"http://coinbase.com\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">coinbase.com</span></span></span></span></a><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> in this case, you\'ll interact with a \"custodial wallet\" that stores and secures your private keys for you. You should gradually learn about other wallet options that allow you to interact with decentralized finance (or DeFi protocols), such as Compound (a lending and savings application) or Uniswap (a decentralized exchange where you can trade cryptocurrencies). (Coinbase, n.d.)</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.3.6 In What Ways Does Ethereum Have Value?</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There are a few ways to approach the answer to this question. At one level, as with any other asset, the value of Ethereum is determined by the markets. It is purchased around the clock and paid for with Bitcoin, dollars, euros, yen, or other currencies. The price can fluctuate daily depending on demand. (Ethereum\'s value tends to fluctuate compared to currencies like the U.S. dollar or stocks like Fortune 500 stocks because it\'s still a technology in development.) But why the price development in the market is the way it is is a much more complex question. For many investors, Ethereum\'s value stems from its flexibility as a platform for issuing stablecoins and conducting DeFi applications. This leads to a growing user base and rising transaction fees.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.3.3.7 What\'s Next for Ethereum?</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Since the early 2020s, Ethereum has remained the leading platform for decentralized applications, DeFi, and NFTs, benefiting from a strong network effect. Its market capitalization fluctuates in line with broader crypto cycles, and the majority of popular stablecoins, such as USDC and USDT, continue to operate primarily on Ethereum.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Looking ahead, Ethereum’s roadmap focuses on scalability, security, and composability:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Layer-2 Rollups:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> Rollups are now the primary mechanism for scaling Ethereum, processing most transactions off-chain while settling on Ethereum to maintain security. They dramatically reduce gas fees and enable faster throughput for dApps.</span></span></span></span></div></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Proto-Danksharding / EIP-4844:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Introduced in March 2024, this feature adds a data sharding mechanism optimized for rollups, further lowering transaction costs and paving the way for future full sharding.</span></span></span></span></div></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Long-Term Sharding:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> Full Ethereum sharding, expected in the coming years, will split the network into EIP-4844 chains (shards), increasing transaction throughput and storage capacity while maintaining decentralization.</span></span></span></span></div></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">EigenLayer Restaking:</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"> EigenLayer allows ETH stakers to “restake” their assets to secure additional protocols, creating new opportunities for network security and economic participation.</span></span></span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><br></font></div></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">While Ethereum remains the dominant smart contract platform, competition from emerging blockchains continues to grow. Its success will depend on the continued rollout of these upgrades and the ecosystem’s ability to leverage Ethereum’s security, decentralization, and growing layer-2 infrastructure.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div>\n\n</div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-10 07:42:49','2026-01-09 11:58:34'),(67,22,'Crypto: A New Investment Universe','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the previous part, we introduced the crypto world as a new asset class and embedded it in the portfolio context using Bitcoin as an example. However, as we explain below, the term \"asset class\" does not do justice to the world of cryptoassets. Analogous to gold, the crypto sector knows digital stores of value such as Bitcoin. There are also digital currencies such as stablecoins. There is also digital art and collectibles in the form of NFTs, as well as cash flow tokens that are similar in nature to stocks. Or bond-like products such as coins from proof-of-stake blockchains can be identified. In view of this fact, one should speak less of an asset class in the context of cryptoassets and more of an investment universe. This seems to cover all traditional asset classes. What is new about the crypto investment universe is that individual assets combine the aspects and characteristics of multiple asset classes. This fact makes the search for a suitable valuation model for these new assets difficult and points to the fact that new approaches and unconventional approaches are needed.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.1 Beyond cryptocurrencies</span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In general, cryptoassets are largely understood as an asset class in their own right, let alone as an entire investment universe. This is how the term \"cryptocurrencies\" is commonly used, regardless of whether the cryptoasset in question is actually a digital currency or not. As we explained in Chapter 3, this term is actually insufficient for Bitcoin alone, as Bitcoin primarily aims to be digital base money. The term \"cryptocurrency\" is even more problematic where a coin or token is not supposed to be a currency at all. Although every coin or token should reflect a value proposition in some way, it does not have to have anything to do with that of a classic currency. So what is currently summarized under the term \"cryptocurrencies\" does not necessarily have to have a currency character. In general, therefore, one should speak of crypto assets or cryptoassets in order to do justice to the diversity of the crypto world. This is because cryptocurrencies are ultimately to be seen as a subcategory of a large number of different cryptoassets. The fact that cryptoassets are repeatedly referred to as crypto is due to the importance of cryptography for them (Seth, 2020), which is applied to this new type of asset. Cryptography is used to securely encrypt crucial data within crypto networks. It is what enables the unfalsifiable proof of digital goods without having to disclose personal data. And without them, it would not be possible to do without central trust offices. If data were not securely encrypted using cryptography, this security would have to be ensured by an identified, central entity. As we saw in Chapter 1.2, cryptographic encryption is only one of the components that must work in harmony with other components in order for a cryptoasset to function as a cryptoasset.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Table Talk: Cryptoassets versus Digital Assets</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Instead of cryptoassets, one also reads the term \"digital assets\" again and again. In most cases, it means the same thing. But the term \"digital assets\" can also cause confusion. Namely, when the defining characteristics of a digital asset are not clear: Digital assets in the sense of cryptoassets are blockchain-based assets. As such, they are digital owner instruments. This means that they can be stored and held independently and without the assistance of a third party. This does not apply to the assets held digitized today, such as shares, bonds, or money. For the sake of the right distinction, one could also speak of electronic shares, bonds, or money in connection with these digitized assets. In English, there is a more appropriate clear distinction between the terms. For example, one can speak of \"digital money\" and \"digitized money.\" While the latter has only been cast in a digitized form, the former is digital money that exists as a blockchain-based asset.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.2 Cryptoassets: An Attempt at Categorization</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 10pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Given the large number of different cryptoassets, it is essential to work towards a defining categorization of each blockchain-based asset. The Swiss financial market regulator made the first attempt by an official body in 2018. For example, FINMA published guidelines that differentiated between payment, utility, and investment tokens. (FINMA, 2018) What amounted to a very progressive step on the part of a regulator was a first rough approximation. Gradually, the categorization was refined. Due to the fast pace of life, innovation, and the resulting continuous change, it has not yet been possible to work out a conclusive categorization. The following illustration is the attempt of this textbook to make as comprehensive a breakdown as possible of the various cryptoassets.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/20.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span><div style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-aad84408-7fff-e917-c337-d9f7f53bb18e\" style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 1: Cryptoassets can be divided into coins and tokens. Within the token category, a distinction must be made between fungible and non-fungible tokens. For each coin or token category, this illustration refers to a cryptoasset type that can be observed in reality.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Source: Pascal Hügli (self-presentation)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">At the beginning of any categorization there should be the distinction between coin and token already discussed in this textbook. These two categories can each be broken down into further subcategories. For the category of tokens, a distinction should also be made between fungible and non-fungible tokens. Coins and tokens can then be separated into their corresponding coin or token types. These represent different crypto asset classes within a crypto asset universe. In the best case, the various asset classes, or rather the investment values of them, can be compared with a counterpart from the traditional world. This can help to form possible mnemonics that can be helpful in evaluation and characterization. The goal of an attempt at categorization must be to gain an understanding of what type of asset you are dealing with. Only such an understanding makes it possible to potentially correctly value a given cryptoasset. For example, a cryptoasset can contain a payment coin but also elements of a utility coin, which is the case with Bitcoin or Ether, for example. There are also cryptoassets that have a cash flow component and at the same time have governance elements.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.3 Payment Coin/Cryptocurrency</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As described, \"cryptocurrencies\" is the most well-known and therefore most common term. Although the founder of Bitcoin, Satoshi Nakamoto, himself had never spoken of a cryptocurrency, this term was soon used in connection with Bitcoin. For example, the early discoverers and users of Bitcoin had no doubt that this novel, digital phenomenon would function like a currency—only decentralized and made functional by cryptographic tools. What is described as a cryptocurrency is to be understood in monetary theory correctly as the digital base money of an independent network. In the form of a native asset of a public blockchain, it acts as a settlement instrument within a blockchain system. This is an independent coin that exists as long as the associated public blockchain is maintained by its decentralized accountants and auditors. The term \"cryptocurrency\" was also popularized because the early understanding of a coin was that it should prevail as a currency—i.e., a means of payment—outside its own blockchain network. Bitcoin was perceived less as a base money and more as a new means of payment competing with national currencies. Examples that we can count among cryptocurrencies are Bitcoin (BTC), Bitcoin Cash (BCH), and Dash. The latter can also be counted among the so-called privacy coins. These are coins that guarantee not only pseudo-anonymity on their base layer but also anonymity. This anonymization can vary in severity. The best-known privacy coins besides Dash are Monero (XMR), Zcash (ZEC) or Horizon (HZN).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for nerds: Anonymous cryptocurrencies, and</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">While Bitcoin has a public ledger that keeps track of real-world transactions and ownership structures transparently comprehensible, these are included in the Privacy Coins are obfuscated. Privacy is anchored at the level of the basic protocol. Here-for so-called Ring Confidential Transactions (RingCT). About ring signatures, different transactions can be mixed together so that we cannot see exactly which coins have been spent. Only the sender and receiver of a transaction know how many coins have changed hands. Another variant is based on the concept of \"shielded addresses.\" These addresses are encrypted on the blockchain and therefore cannot be viewed. It\'s cryptography of so-called zero-knowledge proofs, which allows users to control the ownership and prove the validity of certain information without disclosing that information to third parties. This allows the sender, recipient, and amount to remain anonymous.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.4 Utility Coins</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As the name suggests, utility coins are also blockchain-native assets and therefore act as their settlement instrument. In this sense, they are also to be considered units of value that are used to process transactions on a blockchain. Within its own blockchain, a usage coin serves as a means of payment—namely, as a means of payment for block space on the corresponding public blockchain. The reason why the category of the utility coin has been created in addition to the term cryptocurrency—or payment coin—as follows:In blockchain circles, there is disagreement as to whether there can be coins in the long term that never function as a means of payment outside their own blockchain network. Their sole benefit would be to provide access to the blockchain network as a utility coin. Anyone who wants to use the blockchain network must have the corresponding usage coin. Why would you want to use the blockchain network of a utility coin and, consequently, the usage coin itself? The keyword in this regard is that of the so-called smart contract platform. This term is used for public blockchain networks that enable smart contract applications such as those around DeFi. In order to be able to use these smart contract applications, you must have the corresponding usage coin. This serves the purpose of being able to execute the smart contracts. The best-known example of a utility coin is Ether, which is needed to execute smart contracts on the Ethereum blockchain. Without Ether, the Ethereum smart contracts cannot be triggered, and therefore smart contract applications of all kinds cannot be used on Ethereum. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In addition to Ethereum, there are various other smart contract platforms that have their own usage coin. For example, Cardano, Polkadot, Algorand, Terra, or Icon. Each of these public blockchains has its own utility coin: ADA, DOT, ALGO, LUNA, or ICX. Ether must be used to pay for smart contracts to execute codes. The fact that payment and usage functions merge shows that the boundary between cryptocurrency (payment coin) and usage coin cannot be clearly drawn. For example, some argue that Ether is both a utility coin and a payment coin. Conversely, it can be said for Bitcoin: if you want to use the Bitcoin blockchain, you must have Bitcoin as the native coin of the Bitcoin network—from this perspective, Bitcoin would also be considered a utility coin. The reason why Ether was considered more of a utility coin and Bitcoin more of a payment coin from the beginning is due to their initial assessment:While Bitcoin was primarily considered a means of payment outside the blockchain, Ether was considered more of a unit of use for the Ethereum-based, decentralized world computer network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.5 Usage Tokens</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The utility token is a similar concept to the utility coin. The difference is that the usage coin acts as the native asset of a public blockchain, which is not the case for the usage token. The function of a utility token, however, is to simplify the use of a DeFi protocol on a smart contract platform. A frequently cited example of a usage token is the BAT token, the usage token of the Basic Attention protocol. Other prominent examples include LINK, the token of the Chainlink network, as well as the SNX token, which is required to use the Synthetix platform.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for nerds: A utility token</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The utility token is a similar concept to the utility coin. The difference is that the usage coin acts as the native asset of a public blockchain, which is not the case for the usage token. The function of a utility token, however, is to simplify the use of a DeFi protocol on a smart contract platform. A frequently cited example of a usage token is the BAT token, the usage token of the Basic Attention protocol. Other prominent examples include LINK, the token of the Chainlink network, as well as the SNX token, which is required to use the Synthetix platform.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for nerds: A utility token par excellence</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Chainlink is an Ethereum-based, decentralized trading platform for oracle services. In order to use Chainlink\'s services, its LINK usage token is essential. Smart contracts that obtain data from the Chainlink network must use LINK. This is used to pay the network accounts that provide relevant on- or off-chain data as oracle service providers. At the same time, LINK is required when acting as an Oracle service provider. The utilization token must be deposited on the Chainlink platform. This incentivizes the Oracle service provider/data provider to deliver correct data. If Oracle service providers deliver false, incorrect data, a portion of the deposited tokens is deducted as a penalty. In other words, LINK can be used to pay compliant Oracle service providers and penalize malicious Oracle service providers.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.6 Payment Tokens</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The payment tokens are cryptoassets that are intended to act as a means of payment. In this case, we are talking about the so-called stablecoins. In contrast to payment coins, however, they do not represent a native asset of a public blockchain but are based on one as tokens. According to this definition, the chosen term \"stablecoins\" is actually wrong, as stablecoins are payment tokens and not payment coins, as they run on multiple public blockchains.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></h4><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.7 Investment tokens</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Investment tokens are backed by real goods. The coverage of an investment token can be various: for example, precious metals, real estate, works of art, or other capital goods or securities. Even stablecoins are classified by some observers in the category of investment tokens, as in the most prominent cases, these tokens are backed by underlying, fiat-denominated reserves or directly by fiat money. An investment token is issued via a public blockchain. One also often speaks of a so-called security token or a tokenized security because the investment token has a kind of collateralization by the underlying value. This can be based on a contractual agreement, such as interest or cash flow payments. If an investment is even backed by a real good such as gold, there is a connection to something that exists outside the blockchain. In order to guarantee this connection to the underlying thing, investment tokens are at best bound by a redemption obligation. This means that the token can be redeemed for the underlying value. If the token is presented to the token issuer, it must exchange it for the underlying thing. Especially in the case of a stablecoin or a token backed by precious metals, such a redemption obligation should make sense. In reality, such obligations are hardly secured due to legal vagueness. </span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Exceptions are jurisdictions such as Switzerland, Liechtenstein, or other small states such as Malta. Due to the continuing regulatory ambiguity in many jurisdictions, examples of investment tokens are still few and far between. An investment token also comes with counterparty risk. For example, a counterparty must ensure that the real asset backing the investment token is reliably stored in Liechtenstein. Because without the underlying asset, the investment token lacks its value coverage. Two more well-known manifestations are Tether Gold (XAUT) and DixiDAO (DGD)—both of which are investment tokens backed by precious metals. In Switzerland, a Picasso painting was also tokenized as an investment token for the first time in July 2021. (SWI swissinfo.ch, 2021) The Curio-Invest project is also in the process of bringing luxury vehicles onto the blockchain. In a first step as an investment object, in a second step as tokenized rental cars that belong to the token holders.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Table Talk: The Promise of Tokenization</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">For some time now, financial circles have been talking about tokenization. This refers to the process of securitizing one or a variety of assets from the off-chain world on a blockchain and thus on-chain. With tokenization, objects in the real world are to receive a digital twin in the form of a token and thus be mapped in cyberspace via the blockchain. Basically, tokenization is no different from the securitization we know from the traditional financial world. In contrast to conventional securitization, however, real assets are not stored on isolated databases of individual banks but, in the best case, tokenized via a public blockchain. There are still various assets for which securitization is not worthwhile. Examples of this are luxury watches, classic cars, or a cattle farm. The main hope of tokenization is to make so-called unbankable assets more tradable.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.8 Equity Token</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the meantime, there are tokens that generate a kind of cash flow and pay it out to the token holders. The value of this token thus reflects any possible cash flow resulting from the token usage and use of the protocol. In concrete terms, this can mean that the users of a protocol pay network fees for use, which go to the protocol in the form of a cash flow and can thus be paid out to the token holders. These rights to cash flows are not codified in formal legal and contractual agreements, as is the case with conventional shares. In the case of equity tokens, these rights are programmed into the code of the underlying protocol as smart contracts and are thus inherently attached to the equity token. The cash flows from equity tokens thus come from the economic activity of the underlying network and its use. This can be compared to dividend-paying stocks, whose cash flows are also derived from the underlying corporate profits. In this respect, it is important to distinguish this type of cash flow from that which is achieved by inflating a token quantity in a protocol. The latter is commonly referred to as staking and requires token holders to park their tokens at the protocol itself and thus be rewarded by the protocol by issuing new tokens.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">People who don\'t stake their tokens experience a dilution of their token share, at the expense of those who deposit their tokens with the protocol. Such smart contract-based cash flow models are generally classified as high-risk. For example, the fear of developers and issuers is that a protocol token used to pay out network fees could be classified as a security token by regulators. This would not only bring more regulation for the specific project but would also not be legally compliant in many jurisdictions—especially the USA—at the end of 2021, as the necessary legal framework for such equity tokens does not exist. At the end of 2021, there are a large number of equity tokens, even though they still operate in a regulatory gray area in many jurisdictions. In order to counteract a possible regulatory risk, various protocols have decided to bring their equity token to investors by launching it as fairly as possible. In such a case, the tokens are not created by a pre-mine and released for investment. Rather, the protocol follows a clear issuance calendar that is programmed into the protocol via smart contracts and continuously issues the tokens to first-time users based on usage. (Massari &amp; Catalini, 2021) Well-known examples of these equity tokens include SushiSwap (SUSHI), Sovryn (SOV), and Balanced-DAO (BALN).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e371f404-7fff-9b32-a717-121ed9ea8e2f\" style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.9 Governance Token</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In addition to cash flows, some cryptoassets offer investors the opportunity to make decisions and have a say. While coins such as Bitcoin and Ether do not offer such rights, other coins as well as tokens have voting rights programmed directly into the smart contract. Governance tokens thus mimic voting stocks that are familiar from the traditional financial world. The co-exercise of governance is of great importance in traditional financial markets. Shareholders can vote on executive compensation, board seats, and company resolutions. Participation in such decisions is significant. as it can influence the company or the people who run the company. The main motivation of programmed voting rights is the creation of mechanisms for the efficient resolution of disputes about the future development of a blockchain or protocol. Coin or token holders will be able to vote on various protocol parameters such as inflation, coin/token distribution, or incentives. An important prerequisite for ensuring that this governance can be held as fairly as possible is so-called on-chain voting. Voting and exercising voting rights is done directly via the blockchain or via the underlying protocol itself.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for nerds: Code-driven governance</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Governance models come in different manifestations. There are governance systems in which governance decisions are made directly by the code itself. This means that after an on-chain vote, the code knows the result and executes potential changes itself. Individual developers have no way to change the code behind a system. An example of this is the governance system of Sovryn, also called Bitocracy.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the case of various protocols, it can and is also voted on whether network fees should be paid out to token holders in the form of dividends. Such compensation mechanisms are not always implemented from the beginning of governance tokens, but it is up to the token holders to activate this mechanism via on-chain voting. The governance function is also important because different protocols independently have financial resources that fall to the protocol due to fees. The entirety of these funds is not always distributed to the token holders. In order to be able to determine the use of these funds, the governance function is also required. Prominent governance examples of cryptoassets are provided by public blockchains such as Decred (DCR) or Tezos (XZT). DeFi protocols such as Uniswap (UNI), 1inch (1INCH), Sovryn (SOV), and Balanced (BALN) also have advanced governance functionalities.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.10 Synthetic Tokens</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Synthetic tokens are synthetic assets that are created on the basis of a debt. This means that a synthetic token is created as a debt relationship. The basis of this debt relationship is collateralization in the form of another cryptoasset. In order to obtain the underlying collateralization of a synthetic token, the debt relationship must be repaid. Synthetic tokens are complex financial derivatives on the blockchain. They can be used to reflect the price of other assets without the need to hold the assets depicted in real terms. For example, there are synthetic tokens on popular stocks of Tesla (TSLA), Amazon (AMZN), Google (GOOGL), or Apple (AAPL). Synthetic tokens are used to make crypto assets deposited in protocols liquid. For example, stablecoins can be placed in a liquidity pool of a decentralized trading exchange. A synthetic token is then deposited in the liquidity pool in the form of a liquidity pool token (LP token), representing the deposited tokens. These LP tokens, in turn, can be used as collateral on another protocol, making the stablecoins originally deposited in the liquidity pool reusable.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Something for nerds: Synthetic token on the blockchain</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">One of the best-known blockchain-based platforms for the issuance of synthetic tokens is Synthetix. The users of Synthetix, who hold so-called Synths on the protocol, do not own the real asset but can still participate in its price movements. The Synthetix utility token (SNX) must be used in order to be able to issue debt positions in the form of Synths and thus create synthetic tokens. So-called stakers of SNX receive inflation rewards as well as the fees incurred when creating synths.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-d3606dcc-7fff-3357-a668-32a241781600\" style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.235;\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.4.1.11 Non-Fungible Token (NFT)</span></span></span></span></span></span></h4><div><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">NFTs, also known as non-fungible tokens, are among the most prominent cryptoassets. It is important to understand that NFTs do not define their own token category besides usage, payment, or other tokens. Rather, it is a superordinate shell, especially since basically any type of token—whether utility, payment, or investment tokens—can be represented as a non-fungible token. In most cases, NFTs are denominated in a digital file, a digital artwork, or a digitized piece of music. If an NFT is based on something intangible, it is a digital NFT. If an NFT is for a material, tangible thing, it has already been referred to as a phygital NFT (Valenta, 2021). In this case, the NFT represents an investment token that represents a property or a physical work of art. In order to understand an NFT in its entirety, it is necessary to grasp its three main components: The obvious is the non-fungible token, which is programmed as a smart contract on a public blockchain. In addition, each NFT is provided with information that informs about the underlying asset. This type of information exists in the form of metadata. This is structured data that contains information about characteristics of other data. The third component is the represented asset itself.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/21.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-8503f0d4-7fff-a720-f7d1-c8d397ecc058\" style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 2: A smart contract, the metadata, and the underlying asset work together to define the overall anatomy of an NFT.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Source: Martin Valenta</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">If you look at this entire anatomy of an NFT, the following facts make sense:The non-fungible token itself is on the blockchain and connects to an underlying asset. The nature of this connection is defined by the metadata associated with the NFT. What is clear, however, is that while the metadata can theoretically also be stored directly on the blockchain—which is rarely done in practice—the underlying asset is outside the blockchain in the vast majority of cases. For example, storing the underlying asset on the blockchain is associated with high costs. This means that the non-fungible token can be owned exclusively by the owner. The same does not necessarily apply to the metadata or the underlying asset. In order to ensure the connection between the NFT, the metadata, and the underlying asset, mechanisms are needed that go beyond the guarantees of a public blockchain. At this point in time, the legitimate question in this regard is whether companies will succeed in establishing profitable business models that can guarantee this connection. Treaties and legal enforcement mechanisms, as we know them from the traditional world, are also likely to play an important role.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/22.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e6160ef5-7fff-8ae0-3608-06744eb46c09\" style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 3: An NFT defines and determines on the blockchain who the owner of it is. The use of the underlying value of the NFT is not guaranteed by the blockchain but is dependent on conventional institutions for enforcement.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Source: Martin Valenta</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The situation is different if a non-fungible token is designed as a utility token, for example. For example, an NFT could serve as an access token for a website or as a verification token to participate in a concert—physical or digital. (Digital, 2022) NFTs are likely to bring exciting innovations in this area in the near future. Prominent examples of NFT platforms are OpenSea and Rarible.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098);\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b>Good to know: Access thanks to NFT</b></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"border-color: rgb(226, 232, 240); outline-color: oklab(0.34196 -0.0223922 -0.0795719 / 0.15098); font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">NFTs can also be used as virtual access cards for physical and digital events and experiences. This is referred to as \"token-gated\" content. So there is no paywall. In order to see the content on a website, access must be unlocked with a specifically designated NFT. Content such as videos, podcasts, or music can only be made accessible to fans who can show a certain non-fungible token. The first projects are already offering such services.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div>\n\n</div></span></span></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></span></span></div></span></span></div></div></div>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-10 07:53:35','2026-01-09 12:10:30'),(68,23,'Life Sciences and Healthcare','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6d5284a0-7fff-6200-7572-3a818ac9493d\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain can significantly support digitization and global participation in drug development, which has been accelerated by the pandemic. Blockchain helps handle data and track operations between partners in the value chain, addressing concerns raised by social alienation and the virtualization of work.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The digitization of everything</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">When the pandemic hit, it became clear that the conduct of traditional clinical activities, from the simple delivery of medical supplies to hospitals to the complex operations of a large-scale clinical trial, could no longer be done in person. In response, organizations were forced to perform critical activities virtually, often using tedious and manual solutions to get the job done. Where digital solutions existed, companies accelerated their introduction and implementation. Organizations quickly realized the importance (and difficulty) of improving the way data is tracked and shared effectively. Although digitalization in life sciences was already trending before the pandemic (e.g., telemedicine in clinical trials), we believe that digitalization will continue as the dominant trend. In fact, 61% of life sciences executives say digital assets will be very important in the next three years. Also, blockchain can play an important role by serving as a data backbone to facilitate secure data exchange, connectivity, and auditability of all processes in the value chain. As life sciences recover from the pandemic, we expect new investments and cross-industry pilots where they are incorporating blockchain technology, along with other digital technologies such as cloud, IoT, and AI, will enable virtual clinical trials, touchless supply chains, and other innovative applications. The companies can make a convincing case that the problems that arose during the pandemic can be solved by digital technology and that virtualization in life sciences can help meet patient expectations in the future.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Educating the public</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The second crucial change triggered by the pandemic concerns educating the public about the industry and the process of delivering new medicines to patients. Specifically, it is about Operation Warp Speed, a federal program that aims to provide a vaccine against COVID-19 within a year. This has been discussed again and again in the media. For example, the public was sensitized to the importance of participating in clinical trials and sharing medical data in order to advance scientific research. For clinical researchers, obtaining data from patients and getting them to participate in trials is generally challenging. However, our clients point out that many people were more willing to share their medical data and participate in vaccine trials during the pandemic. As a result, many life scientists we spoke to are optimistic that people will be willing to participate in research even after the pandemic. If these predictions come true, life sciences companies should be prepared for privacy concerns. They should ensure that patients retain ownership of their data throughout the process. Blockchain could play an important role as a data backbone and serve as a trusted mechanism for granting consent to share data. In the past year, some small pilot projects have pushed the boundaries of the use of blockchain for exactly these purposes. Further activities in this area can help to give patients the opportunity to participate in medical research and play a greater role. However, it is still too early to say whether patients will withdraw more because of the experience with the pandemic.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain Challenges</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A look at virtualization and public education shows that we expect the situation for blockchain pilots to stabilize once the pandemic subsides. As a result, life sciences leaders must be prepared to remove the long-standing barriers to adoption (e.g., regulatory concerns, IP management, and executive prioritization). In fact, 50% of life scientists surveyed cited a lack of regulatory clarity as the biggest obstacle to blockchain adoption. We believe that something could happen quickly on the regulatory front. Since the US Food and Drug Administration experimented with blockchain in the supply chain before the pandemic. It is possible that it will take an innovative approach and promote blockchain (and other exponential technologies) to accelerate the delivery of medicines to the market. Nevertheless, we still need concrete evidence to verify the effectiveness and potential of new blockchain-based solutions. Even though life sciences leaders seem willing to experiment with blockchain pilots, the actual adoption will still take time. This is especially important when you consider how much internal and external coordination, financial investment, and technology is required for such a transformation. Ultimately, we still need to evaluate the most effective approaches to determine the value of blockchain, especially as life sciences companies push for digitalization.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Key Takeaways</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The trends that have emerged during the pandemic could have a significant impact on user adoption of blockchain in the future. Digitization and virtualization trends became necessary during the pandemic to carry out everyday activities and to support the development of a vaccine. We believe that these trends will evolve into a \"new normal\" and that blockchain can and will be used as a data backbone to drive activities from clinical trials to supply chain and commercialization. As the public becomes more familiar with the process of developing COVID-19 therapies, global cultural changes will encourage them to share their personal information and play a more active role in the drug development lifecycle. This, in turn, requires improved ways to share information, with blockchain playing a crucial role. The exchange of information is clearly changing and will continue to develop. With the potential to save time and money by improving how businesses, regulators, and individuals communicate with each other, now is the time to embrace these changes—the processes are already underway. (Kudumala &amp; Israel, 2020)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 07:56:48','2025-10-08 09:00:37'),(70,23,'Government Governance','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-cc64555a-7fff-9ae6-c754-12fa76850403\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The consortium model creates new paradigm for blockchain adoption</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The U.S. government faces unique challenges when it comes to researching blockchain, testing test cases, and implementing solutions. While the path to implementation may be clear for the private sector, the distributed peer-to-peer constructs that underpin blockchain are often hampered by the complex politics of interagency collaboration and information sharing. This requires a new approach. The importance of blockchain is obvious. According to Deloitte\'s 2020 Global Blockchain Survey, 68% of the authorities surveyed said that blockchain will be a strategic priority in the next two years. For the government to use blockchain effectively, change is needed. We believe that a new business model can help change the current thinking of authorities about blockchain policies and regulations. First, authorities must continue to acquire knowledge about emerging distributed ledger technologies (DLT) such as blockchain, their capabilities, and the value they can create. Second, the federal government needs a central hub to establish a new paradigm for this business model. This could take the form of an association of government representatives and stakeholders whose task is to help the authorities grow beyond their individual interests and focus on the big picture.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The state as a regulator, regulated, and consumer of blockchain technology&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The government is in a unique position as a regulator, the regulated, and a blockchain consumer. As regulators, government agencies regulate either digital assets or the processes that are migrated to blockchain-based solutions (e.g., food safety and cryptocurrencies). When the government is regulated, it too must comply with some regulations and mandates that the commercial industry is not subject to (e.g., FedRAMP and Section 508). As consumers, government agencies can use blockchain to increase their operational efficiency. Due to the numerous tasks that government agencies perform, they can give the impression that they cannot keep up with their business partners. Still, authorities generally move between three phases of blockchain adoption: exploring, experimenting, and implementing. In fact, most respondents believe that blockchain is scalable on a broad scale and will eventually catch on and achieve mainstream adoption. While some authorities are unwilling or unable to take the risk, others are starting testing. Some agencies are successfully experimenting with the underlying technologies, while others, such as the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS), have already adopted solutions. Despite the varying levels of blockchain adoption, authorities often struggle because it is not always easy to exchange with other authorities. Although there is a lot to be gained from data sharing, they lack the system interoperability necessary for potential operational efficiency. This is partly due to the way it is funded, the setting of policies, cultural differences, and the breakdown of agency departments. For example, it can take months to resolve legal issues (e.g., liability issues) when different authorities want to share information about a publicly available service (e.g., liability or IP ownership), often leading to unsuitable outcomes for all parties involved. Since blockchain and other DLTs are peer-to-peer systems, the value is achieved through network effects, which means that an ecosystem must be created in order to be successful. Trade and industry often have an association or form a joint venture or other legal entity that acts as a trusted, centralized authority and serves as a connecting element of the ecosystem. This is not an option for the government at the moment, which cannot simply decide to form a joint venture with other ministries, such as the Ministry of Finance, the Ministry of Health, and the Office of Housing and Urban Development (HUD). So how should the government begin to address the need for a new business model that requires collective decisions on governance, policy, mandates, standards, budgeting, and risk tolerance? Similar to industry, there must be a coalition that has the ability and authority to drive policies forward. The Digital Taxonomy Act and the American Compete Act, which emerged from the House Committee on Energy and Commerce, take a look at the Commerce Department\'s authorization to research blockchain solutions. We believe that this authority should expand the agency\'s mandate to establish a formal office that acts as a central body with the authority to oversee the adoption of blockchain in government. The Digital Taxonomy Act and the American Competition Act, which emerged from the House of Representatives Committee on Energy and Commerce, will authorize the Department of Commerce to explore blockchain solutions. We believe that this authority should expand the mission of the organization. An office is to be formally created to act as a central body with the authority to oversee the adoption of blockchain in government on a broader scale.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">One model that the new office could follow is the Joint Artificial Intelligence Center at the Department of Defense (DoD). It was set up to \"prepare\" the Department of Defense for artificial intelligence (AI) and its potential applications in government. The creation of a similar prototype for distributed ledger technology could help address some of the larger political, decision-making, and regulatory issues associated with the adoption of government policies, as well as address regulatory issues related to the government\'s adoption of blockchain-based solutions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Key takeaways</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The government\'s understanding of blockchain is evolving. Authorities should also continue to learn about the underlying capabilities and value that can be derived from the blockchain. This cannot be done overnight or in a vacuum. The government, especially at the federal level, must work towards creating a central center with well-defined government representatives to create a paradigm for a new peer-to-peer engagement model. This needs to go beyond simply evaluating and recommending blockchain use cases. Steady progress is already visible. About 60% of the authorities surveyed said that they have already put blockchain up and running. In addition, establishing a government office to support policy implementation and governance of agencies can help form or participate in consortia and test the feasibility of new DLT ecosystems. Expanding this office\'s mandate can help create a more robust and sustainable template for blockchain adoption in other agencies. This cannot be done through redistribution or new laws alone, but a centralized office is a positive sign of future commitment to blockchain. Ultimately, the high level of coordination that comes with a central office can provide a clear path forward for authorities with the right representatives and help the government take advantage of this new technology and develop sustainable governance. (Henry &amp; Ricky, 2020)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:30:04','2025-10-08 09:01:03'),(71,23,'Paradigm shift in distributed ledger technologies','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-d03e9533-7fff-69d0-84f4-7895488c5739\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The social impact of funding opportunities, risks and financial inclusion</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Where blockchain and digital currencies once served as speculative tools, they now enable small and medium-sized enterprise (SME) supply chain financing, supply chain financing, and global trade remittance. This development creates new market opportunities for secure transactions. In Deloitte\'s 2020 Global Blockchain Survey, banking and capital markets executives cited digital currencies as their most important blockchain use in 2020. In addition, 63% said that digital assets will play an important role in their businesses. Despite all the uncertainties in the financial world, blockchain and distributed ledger technology (DLT) are creating positive social impact for SMEs today. This is particularly evident in several areas: improving funding opportunities, reducing risk, and promoting financial inclusion.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Financing challenges and opportunities</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The collection and sharing of big data by ecosystem actors can help SMEs to obtain finance in particularly difficult times. For example, during the height of the first wave of the pandemic, we saw SMEs struggle to obtain financing. Many applicants were left without the urgently needed funds. According to the World Bank, SMEs account for about 90% of businesses and more than 50% of jobs worldwide. A problem with the human capital of SMEs could therefore have an impact on the entire market. For example, bankruptcies (or even short-term closures) can lead to high unemployment, which unfortunately occurred far too often this year (where? In Switzerland? The USA?. We believe that the adoption of digital ledger technology can be a long-term solution that goes beyond short-term or crisis-related government stimulus measures. DLT can help improve SMEs\' access to finance by leveraging the data collected in the ecosystem. In fact, we believe that loan approval rates could increase once DLT is introduced because the information used in credit decision models is of higher quality. In addition, the use of digital ledgers can help companies operating abroad to speed up payments, thus increasing the efficiency of transactions. Legitimate digital currencies such as stablecoins and central bank digital currencies (CBDCs)—digitized versions of central banks\' fiat currencies—help reduce settlement times. DLT can reduce turnaround times for cross-border transfers from overnight (and sometimes up to two weeks) to same-day and possibly even real-time settlement. The advantages are obvious. In particular, DLT can help reduce the time it takes to correct errors in transactions and allow companies to focus on their next business without worrying about liquidity, funding, or losing vendor rebates.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Reduce risk</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">DLT helps improve data transparency and reduce risk for financial institutions. This, in turn, reduces the costs for SMEs to obtain financing and insurance coverage. For example, fake orders and invoices would be detected if they do not match the invoices of logistics companies. In addition, double financing would be uncovered without sensitive customer data being disclosed. On the other hand, in addition to the benefits of unregulated digital currencies, there are other considerations, including a lack of compliance (e.g., KYC and AML2), which leads to uncertainties around financial legitimacy in high-volume cross-border and business-related transactions. Unregulated digital currencies often pose market and legal risks for banks and companies involved in these transactions. However, regulators are becoming increasingly vigilant and subjecting previously unregulated currencies to more defined rules by governments and central banks in order to reduce the risks involved.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">DLT and Financial Inclusion</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">DLT is increasingly promoting financial inclusion, both as a means of financing SMEs in more developed economies, where a lack of information or credit history can make it difficult for banks to finance, and in digital payments for populations that visit no or few banks. DLT helps non-bank populations to use digital payments offline, which is crucial where network access is inconsistent and expensive. Finally, DLT reduces payment processing costs for SMEs, which is beneficial for companies with low profit margins that would otherwise have to pay high settlement fees, which in turn can impact the company\'s new investment and growth.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Key takeaways</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As more companies adopt blockchain and DLT, the short- and long-term effects will become clearer. Market paradigms are evolving from competition to collaboration, which helps address the new realities of today\'s business environment. Against the backdrop of this change, DLT is an ideal platform for secure, real-time data synchronization that can reduce costs, risks, and hurdles in accessing working capital. In the medium term, DLT can serve as a platform for companies to mitigate risk and gain financial inclusion. And in the long term, cross-border payments, especially for SMEs and large enterprises, should become much faster and less error-prone, which could lead to a more efficient global trading ecosystem. Access to efficient markets and banking services could be one of the last pillars to fall. In other words, the reason why companies are created and work towards achieving a certain size is because of access to capital. In the past, a certain size was required to reduce the cost of participating in the banking system. DLT is changing these paradigms, and all SMEs, regardless of their size, can enjoy the same level of financial and banking services and the same low costs. (Sin &amp; Walker, 2020)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:42:38','2025-10-08 09:01:33'),(72,23,'The Manufacturing Industry and the New Blockchain Paradox','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-bfe8f367-7fff-32de-9451-157af0e149b9\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How Progressive Leaders Can Help Improve the Supply Chain Ecosystem</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The year 2020 has revealed a remarkable paradox regarding the blockchain investments that companies plan to make in their manufacturing and supply chains over the next 12 months. In Deloitte\'s 2020 Global Blockchain Survey, 42% of manufacturing executives said they are making significant investments in blockchain, but only 30% believe there is a compelling business case for using blockchain in their organization.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Why is there such a discrepancy?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">On the surface, manufacturing and supply chain use cases are often focused on efficiency at the operational level and generally do not require input from the higher levels of the organization. If you go a little deeper, use cases that are to reach the C-suite usually have to enable new business models that require more decision-making at the C-suite. We believe there is great business potential beyond operational efficiency that could transform the way the industry operates and how suppliers work together along the chain. This, in turn, can help create a new need for increased leadership engagement. Creating new business models by overhauling existing processes won\'t be easy and will likely require manufacturing leaders to accept the potential transparency and power of blockchain use cases—something they haven\'t necessarily embraced so far. Currently, executives in the manufacturing industry are more cautious and slower to adopt blockchain than their counterparts in other industries (e.g., banking and capital markets), who are more likely to accept blockchain in their operations. According to our data, positive sentiment in the manufacturing industry lags behind the survey as a whole when it comes to the question of what role digital assets will play and whether there is a compelling business case for blockchain. However, our experience shows that the manufacturing industry has indeed moved towards blockchain, albeit in a more deliberate and gradual way. Traditionally, manufacturing and supply chain leaders have embraced blockchain and other distributed ledger technologies (DLT) to increase efficiency while reducing risk. Now, however, traditions are changing, as the focus seems to be shifting to a more holistic view of how business should be conducted. As a result, companies are focusing less on using blockchain to solve specific problems and more on using blockchain to address potential problems before they occur. To move further and faster in this direction, we believe companies should adopt new governance models that support their business goals, especially in terms of transparency. This goal follows a precedent in shipping, for example, where blockchain initiatives are joining forces to create a new ecosystem that could modernize the entire industry. In short, companies seem to be changing their fundamental views on what blockchain can and can\'t do, and more importantly, they are rethinking their idea of how blockchain can provide effective redundancy and address shortcomings in their supply chains, as they have come to light during the COVID-19 pandemic. So what does it take to achieve this goal?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain in a changing world</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Recent global events have shown how fragile global supply chains can be and how costly their recovery can ultimately be. When parts aren\'t available when manufacturers need them, the delays impact both their profits and their reputation with customers. So, using blockchain to increase redundancy throughout the supply chain can save manufacturers time and money. In the event of a recall, an automaker that does not effectively track its components could have difficulty tracing certain parts. This could result in more vehicles than necessary having to be recalled, resulting in significantly higher costs and greater inconvenience for customers, who will have to change their schedules to avoid unexpected and potentially unnecessary repairs and dealer visits. Blockchain should be seen as a central enabler of process improvements, rather than a single, independent solution. In general, it can help streamline data to improve security, integrity, and efficiency, as well as increase customer satisfaction. In particular, blockchain can help optimize the supply chain by using multi-layered solutions, including digital twins, artificial intelligence (AI), and Internet of Things (IoT) trackers enabled by 5G to help filter, register, and transmit large amounts of data. Digital twins are the fastest-evolving part of the multi-layered solution, enabling truly groundbreaking active track-and-trace capabilities over traditional parts or products. Companies can use relevant data to track products or physical components through various actors in the value chain, from the supply chain to a digital representative to after-sales processes. This enables complete traceability of the components, their sources, and the end products. In addition, real-time communication with the goods within the supply chain can take place throughout the manufacturing process. In cross-border trade, the part can be \"self-explanatory\" and automatically handle VAT accounting and other item-related tax issues. The use cases in manufacturing go beyond efficiency and evolve into more holistic, strategic, and advanced applications. Germany, for example, has developed a federal strategy to explore dozens of areas where blockchain solutions can be used. The European Union is also focusing on blockchain service infrastructure to provide a unified view of market data, which can help standardize the tracking and tracing of products and goods flowing through Europe. China has also recently activated a regional version of Network Blockchain to create a blockchain infrastructure. These types of regional initiatives offer significant potential to influence infrastructure, the way business is conducted, future competitiveness, and other important functions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Key takeaways</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain can help create a single source of truth throughout the supply chain by increasing transparency, efficiency, and process speed for stakeholders in the network. Our data shows a paradox between the belief in an effective business case for leveraging blockchain and the way companies actually invest in the underlying technologies. However, this should not be the case. Leaders are well-positioned to bridge this gap by thinking beyond operational efficiencies and focusing on the broader benefits that blockchain can provide. Since the supply chain is inherently a collaborative ecosystem that brings people and organizations together for a common purpose, blockchain should be a natural solution to achieve the strategic goals of the supply chain. This is the main reason why, despite the ongoing \"show me\" sentiment among manufacturers regarding the technology, blockchain has emerged from a period of experimentation and abstraction and is now firmly on the radar of executives. Forward-thinking leaders should take a close look at how they can use blockchain solutions to increase customer satisfaction, improve value systems, create new billing methods, and enable suppliers to respond immediately to quality issues. All of these benefits are within reach today. The current climate in the supply chain should create a new need to drive blockchain-powered solutions to overcome everyday difficulties. The stakes are too high, and the opportunities are too diverse to overlook the opportunities for improvement. Adopting blockchain solutions can not only help create a new, advanced ecosystem, but also improve collaboration and governance across the&nbsp;ecosystem. Looking ahead, leading companies have found that such a mindset helps the industry improve today\'s supply chain ecosystem. Now is the time for other organizations to join the blockchain movement. (Mølbjerg &amp; Paulsen, 2020)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:43:42','2025-10-08 09:02:18'),(73,23,'The banking sector is being reshaped by blockchain technology','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-335193b9-7fff-f5cd-cd66-a719f98629e8\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain and banks are just the beginning. From a macro perspective, banks serve as critical repositories and transshipment points for value. As digitized, secure, and tamper-proof ledgers, blockchains could perform the same function, adding more accuracy and information sharing to the financial services ecosystem. JPMorgan Chase has entered the blockchain space with the JPM Coin, which aims to facilitate cross-border payments in real time between its business customers. Other banks, such as Goldman Sachs and Citigroup, have also experimented with blockchain. The incumbent banks conducted a stock swap in February 2020 based on Axoni\'s Axcore blockchain. More broadly, blockchain has the potential to transform the banking sector, which is worth more than $5 billion, by eliminating the need for banks\' most important services, from payments to settlement and settlement systems. Facilitating payments is extremely profitable for banks—cross-border B2B transactions alone will reach a total value of $35 trillion in 2022, according to Juniper Research. However, blockchain technology provides a secure and cost-effective way to transmit payments, eliminating the need for third-party verification and surpassing processing times for traditional bank transfers. Therefore, the number of cross-border B2B payments via blockchain will increase to almost 1.8 billion by 2025, compared to 122 million in 2020. Blockchain company Ripple has partnered with over 300 customers, including financial institutions such as Santander and Western Union, to improve the efficiency of cross-border payments. Its RippleNet payment network uses a decentralized infrastructure to reduce the time it takes to submit an international payment to 3 seconds, compared to up to 5 days for traditional international bank transfers. R3, another major player working on distributed ledger technology for banks, was able to observe how its technology was used by the Swiss central bank for a successful pilot project to settle large transactions between financial institutions using digital currencies.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Stock Trading and Hedge Funds</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">For years, companies have been working to make it easier to buy, sell, and trade stocks. New blockchain-focused startups are now trying to automate and secure the process more efficiently than any previous solution. TØ.com (standing for T-zero), a subsidiary of Overstock, aims to enable online stock trading using blockchain technology. The tT-ZERO platform integrates cryptographically secure distributed ledgers into existing trading processes to reduce settlement times and costs and increase transparency and auditability. Credit Suisse has also set itself the goal of shortening settlement times. In April 2021, it made history by settling two stock trades—one at 11 a.m. and one at 3 p.m.—in a same-day settlement cycle for the first time. The settlement took place at 4:30 p.m. via the Paxos Settlement Service. Partnerships—existing trading networks and exchanges—will help blockchain achieve a breakthrough in this area. Blockchain company Chain, which was acquired by Stellar in 2018, helped implement a live blockchain integration that successfully connected the Nasdaq exchange and Citi\'s banking infrastructure. Recently, Nasdaq partnered with the company R3 to develop a platform using R3\'s blockchain software solution, Corda, to enable financial institutions to create and manage their own digital asset marketplaces. Meanwhile, Numerai is adopting the hedge fund model—which employs a number of traders and quants—and decentralizing it. Numerai, backed by names like First Round Capital and Union Square Ventures, sends encrypted datasets to its thousands of quantum scientists and asks them to create predictive models, and the best participants are rewarded with the Numerai token called Numeraire. Then, Numerai takes the strategy and creates a metamodel to trade. In October 2020, Numerai announced a new project called Numerai Signals, which accepts signals from models trained on arbitrary datasets, not just its own. The company has made $50 million of its Numeraire tokens available as a reward for the \"most original signals.\" As of Q3 21, the platform had 3,398 models and tokens worth $28 million in use, with numeraire staking reportedly yielding a 3-month return of 15%. Blockchain technology is also making its way into impact investing. Impact tokens can incentivize activities that support the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals. These tokens are integrated into smart contracts and are provided as a reward for certain activities. The possible applications of impact tokens are manifold. Collaboration Impact Tokens are awarded to tourists who choose less popular attractions to reduce overcrowding in other destinations, and they are also awarded to governments to manage tourist flows. HARA tokens provide incentives for farmers to share and verify agricultural data.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:45:29','2025-10-08 09:02:58'),(75,23,'Crowdfunding','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a4a59069-7fff-8a44-d0a4-0c7533f8b060\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Crowdfunding is being transformed by blockchain technology</span></span></b></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The crowdfunding industry emerged to facilitate capital raising by giving funders (also known as \"pledgers\") or individual investors the ability to directly fund creators and entrepreneurs, which is a natural link to blockchain capabilities. For example, the movie BRAID became the first major feature film to be funded via a token \"crowdsale\" campaign on the Ethereum blockchain, through a $1.4 million campaign on Weifund. While the film was shot and even premiered at the Tribeca Film Festival to an overwhelmingly positive response, it\'s unclear whether or not the investors got their money back. Another example of blockchain-powered crowdfunding is Initial Coin Offerings (ICOs), where companies sell cryptocurrency tokens in their companies in the same way that a publicly traded company sells stocks. Companies like CoinList, which emerged from a collaboration between Protocol Labs and AngelList, are bringing digital assets into the mainstream by helping blockchain companies structure legal and compliant ICOs. Other startups popping up in the ICO ecosystem include Waves, a platform for storing, managing, and issuing digital assets, and Republic, which has launched a crypto initiative designed to help people invest in ICOs from as little as $10. Pledgecamp is a competitor to Kickstarter and Indiegogo that aims to increase transparency (via smart contracts) and offer \"backer insurance\" by decentralizing the process. When projects reach their funding goal, the money is transferred to a secure escrow exchange, which releases the money gradually. Funders can see how the money they invest is being spent, and they can help determine the direction of the project, for example, by voting on whether to launch a new phase of development.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:46:49','2025-10-08 09:04:04'),(76,23,'Crypto Exchanges','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-86019814-7fff-f242-4b95-98f9edf1f494\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Crypto exchanges are being fundamentally changed by blockchain technology</span></span></b></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">One way blockchain reduces traditional cybersecurity risks is by simply eliminating the need for human intermediaries, reducing the risk of hacking, corruption, or human error. Ironically, some of the most successful blockchain companies are fairly centralized middlemen. However, many new projects simplify the buying and selling of blockchain-based currencies by moving the entire exchange to a blockchain. A high-profile project in this area is Enigma, which lists MIT and Flybridge Capital as supporters. Enigma is the developer of Catalyst, a decentralized off-chain exchange and investment platform that operates as a clearinghouse without the need for a third party. Centralized exchanges such as Binance and Coinbase have taken steps in the decentralized exchange space by launching Binance DEX in 2019 and acquiring the peer-to-peer (P2P) trading platform Paradex in 2018.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:47:41','2025-10-08 09:04:28'),(77,23,'Wills and inheritances','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-8a0d85fa-7fff-b7b8-486a-869f83de168a\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Wills and inheritances are significantly changed by blockchain technology. Wills are a very special type of contract that is an ideal use case for a blockchain solution for smart contracts. In addition to the need to verify the actual death of the deceased, litigation related to wills often involves challenging the \"authenticity\" of a will—that is, whether the legal interpretation is consistent with the intentions of the deceased. While the application of blockchain technology would not completely eliminate these difficulties, it would make it easier to determine factual information, provide verifiable transaction data, and reject unfounded claims. Japanese startup Zweispace is developing a blockchain-based self-execution system that automatically distributes the assets of an inheritance trust to beneficiaries once the trustee\'s death is confirmed.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:48:53','2025-10-08 09:04:54'),(78,23,'Accounting','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-8cec5a97-7fff-bb31-d929-4abffc1ce70b\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As the banking sector continues to adapt to cryptocurrencies and blockchain technology, accountants are also starting to follow suit. Accountants work with a variety of documents—from tax forms to bank statements to spreadsheets—that contain extensive personal or organizational information. The incorporation of blockchain technology could make it easier to track this sensitive data as it is processed by accounting firms. The data tracking enabled by blockchain technology can also help automate certain accounting services using AI, which could reduce human error and fraud. The big four accounting firms have already jumped on the bandwagon:KPMG has invested in programs and projects to research and share information about blockchain; PwC has created an auditing service for cryptocurrency assets; Deloitte has developed blockchain-based software, while EY\'s Blockchain Analyzer can help auditors accurately audit digital assets.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:49:44','2025-10-08 09:05:19'),(79,23,'Loans and credits','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b3f35be7-7fff-a2f7-f0d7-7e7ef8822360\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Traditional banks and lenders issue loans based on a system of credit reports. Using a credit report prepared by one of the three major credit bureaus—Experian, TransUnion, and Equifax—banks assess the risk that you won\'t be able to repay your debt. This centralized system can be detrimental to consumers. The Federal Trade Commission (FTC) estimates that more than one-third of Americans have a \"potentially material error\" in their credit score that negatively impacts their ability to obtain a loan. In addition, the concentration of this sensitive information in 3 institutions creates a great vulnerability. The Equifax hack in September 2017 exposed the credit information of nearly 150 million Americans. Alternative lending using blockchain technology offers a cheaper, more efficient, and safer way to make personal loans accessible to a greater number of consumers. With a cryptographically secure, decentralized ledger of historical payments, consumers would be able to apply for loans based on a global credit score.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A number of companies are working in this area. Dharma Labs, for example, is a tokenized debt protocol. It aims to provide developers with the tools and standards needed to build online debt marketplaces. Bloom wants to transfer credit scoring to the blockchain and is developing a protocol for managing identity, risk, and creditworthiness scoring using blockchain technology.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Another alternative to traditional loans is P2P lending. Individuals and businesses can lend and lend to each other without having to deal with the rigid requirements of banks. These loans are usually issued through fintech platforms. The startups that operate these platforms conduct risk assessments, approve the applications, and hold the lenders\' funds and the amounts collected from the borrowers in trust funds. While these activities facilitate lending, they also make fintech firms the middleman.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">However, there is little room for third parties in decentralized finance (DeFi), where smart contracts eliminate the need for a trusted intermediary. DeFi lending allows for true P2P funding—lenders and borrowers trade directly with each other at their own risk using cryptocurrencies. In January 2022, the total value locked in DeFi was $92.36 billion, up from $34.69 billion the previous year.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">DeFi lending requires borrowers to provide collateral by depositing an amount of currency through a smart contract that is at least equal to the amount they want to borrow. To protect against fluctuations in the value of cryptocurrencies, some loan pools require borrowers to overcollateralize their loans. The catch for borrowers is that interest rates on DeFi loans tend to be higher than traditional financing, often reaching 10%. The lure, on the other hand, is that the value of the borrowed coin could skyrocket, meaning they can make a pretty profit.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">BankSocial is an Ethereum-based platform that claims to be the first blockchain-based P2P lending platform. It uses a social consensus lending pool and pays its members to own tokens that are used to fund loans. Members stake tokens in exchange for a portion of the interest they receive on each loan.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Lendoit has a similar claim but a different concept. The company focuses on microloans, dispenses with collateral, and has a marketplace for selling defaulted receivables. It collects a portion of each loan in a compensation fund, and that portion is immediately paid out to the lender in the event of default to mitigate the loss. Still, there is a way for traditional, regulated institutions to enter the DeFi space without having to increase their risk appetite. Lending platform Aave, for example, has set up an approved liquidity pool that only allows \"whitelist\" institutions—those that pass due diligence—to lend and borrow cryptocurrencies.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:50:38','2025-10-08 09:05:48'),(80,23,'Insurance','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-99f1fc67-7fff-526b-6607-a86963c70b60\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Most blockchain applications in the insurance industry today focus on improving operational efficiency. Instead of developing new products, insurance companies are looking for ways blockchain can reduce costs, speed time to market, and provide a better customer experience. For example, using a blockchain to create a single source of truth for transactions between parties has the potential to significantly reduce processing time and costs for insurance companies. Many blockchain initiatives in the insurance sector involve cross-border partnerships or deal with cross-border transactions, leveraging the immutability and version control aspects of blockchain technology.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Insurwave, a joint project of consulting firm EY and blockchain company Guardtime, offers a blockchain platform for marine insurance. The Insurwave solution is based on Corda\'s distributed ledger technology and creates an immutable database between shippers and insurers to enable better risk assessment and faster claims payouts.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">One sector that could benefit the most is reinsurance—the insurance for insurers—which PwC says could save up to $10 billion by using blockchain. Applications of blockchain in this sector include improving risk analysis, automating processes, and speeding up claims settlement.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">With B3i Re, insurers, reinsurers, and brokers can create and manage contracts on distributed ledgers. Any changes to the terms of the contract are recorded on the ledger, allowing different parties to compare the versions of the contract, making negotiations easier and ensuring contract certainty at all times. Using a distributed ledger also eliminates the risk of forgery that comes with manual processing.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:51:20','2025-10-08 09:06:31'),(81,23,'Charitable Causes','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9ca7bb3e-7fff-793b-acfa-e90b9893f546\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain technology is changing charity. For anyone who donates to charity, the blockchain provides the ability to track exactly where donations are going, when they are arriving, and into whose hands they are going. From there, the blockchain can provide the accountability and transparency to address the recurring complaints surrounding charitable giving including organizational inefficiencies (or even financial misconduct) that can prevent the money from reaching those for whom it\'s intended.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Bitcoin-based charities such as the BitGive Foundation use a secure and transparent distributed ledger to give donors greater insight into how the funds are received and used.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The company has also launched GiveTrack, a blockchain-based multidimensional donation platform that makes it possible to transfer, track, and permanently document financial transactions for charity worldwide. By using GiveTrack, charities can build donor trust.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:52:35','2025-10-08 09:07:01'),(82,23,'Mobility sector','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9ce504c2-7fff-1e96-ad7c-836edfe23d50\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Recording physical assets—such as car parts—on a blockchain is an excellent example of how useful the technology can be in tracking ownership with a tamper-proof, neutral, and resilient system. While paper records are susceptible to forgery and/or physical decay, and centralized databases can be hacked, damaged by human error, and/or tampered with, blockchains are immutable and do not have a single entity controlling the ledger. Blockchains could be used to track parts in a supply chain and sort out counterfeit parts. The technology also has a major impact on recalls in the automotive industry, which affected around 32 million vehicles in 2020. With a record of the whereabouts of parts, from suppliers to individual vehicles, blockchain could enable targeted recalls.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The Mobility Open Blockchain Initiative (MOBI), a consortium that includes automakers such as Ford, BMW, Honda, and GM, has been working on a vehicle and parts tracking initiative. The \"Vehicle Identity (VID) Standard\" initiative provides \"birth certificates\" for vehicles, which can be used to track maintenance history and vehicle registration in a common ledger, even across borders.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Another example: Daimler partnered with Ocean Protocol, a decentralized data exchange service based in Singapore, to explore how blockchain could be used to share supply chain data between its manufacturing centers and partners.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">As part of MOBI, other automakers such as GM and BMW have joined forces to share data from self-driving cars using blockchain technology.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:53:12','2025-10-08 09:07:44'),(83,23,'Car leasing and distribution','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-52856790-7fff-a266-2511-b7e45c27d50b\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Leasing, buying, or selling a vehicle is a notoriously patchy process for those involved on all sides of a transaction, but blockchain could change that.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">In 2015, Visa partnered with transaction management startup DocuSign to use blockchain to streamline car leasing and turn it into a \"click, sign, and go\" process. Using the Visa DocuSign tool, potential customers select the car they want to lease, and the transaction is entered into the blockchain\'s public ledger. Then, from the driver\'s seat, the customer signs a lease and insurance policy, and the blockchain is updated with this information.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Today, companies like Estonia-based carVertical are using blockchain technology to track car history more reliably for users looking to buy a used car. carVertical stores data about vehicles from various sources, including leasing and insurance history, in a single ledger. Using the data stored in the ledger, carVertical creates a more comprehensive report of a vehicle\'s history based on the VIN numbers entered by users.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:53:50','2025-10-08 09:08:49'),(84,23,'Carpooling','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-60609ec5-7fff-44cb-ced6-9f24c848272c\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Ride-sharing apps like Uber and Lyft represent the opposite of decentralization, as they essentially act as intermediary hubs, using algorithms to control their fleets of drivers (and dictate what they charge). Blockchain could bring new options to this dynamic: with a distributed ledger, drivers and passengers could create a more user-driven, value-driven marketplace.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Arcade City, for example, handles all transactions through a blockchain system. The startup operates similarly to other ride-sharing companies but allows drivers to set their fares (taking a percentage of drivers\' fares), with the blockchain logging all interactions. In this way, Arcade City can appeal to professional drivers who would rather set up their own transport company than be controlled by a corporate headquarters. In this scenario, drivers can build their own recurring customer base and offer additional services such as deliveries or roadside assistance. Arcade City announced in January 2021 that it would make its code available as open source to enable more peer-to-peer trading.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Another blockchain-based ridesharing app is Drife. The startup operates in Bangalore and plans to launch in other cities in India. The app works through a system of \"personalized smart contracts\" between drivers and passengers, where drivers stake Drife\'s DRF token to be selected for rides. Instead of paying a fee for each ride, Drife\'s drivers pay an annual fee to use the app.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:54:45','2025-10-08 09:09:48'),(85,23,'Public transport','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f44d6bef-7fff-0cb1-a0e6-3cae138f1439\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The growth of cities has also put pressure on many transport systems, which are often expensive and inefficient to operate. The use of blockchain technology could help cities better understand how their residents use public transport.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The UK-based company DOVU, for example, allows its users to share their commuter and traffic data—including the use of buses, trains, bike rental companies, and even pedestrian paths—through a blockchain-powered app, which then rewards them with crypto tokens. The company has entered into partnerships with car manufacturers and the local transport company Go-Ahead.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain could also contribute to a more functional and efficient system. For example, a public ledger can be used to store and share information about the efficiency or punctuality of vehicles—information that can help better optimize routes and schedules.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:55:21','2025-10-08 09:10:51'),(86,23,'Transport sector','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-ee5b217a-7fff-b6bf-96d6-4a3aaeb0def9\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The assets that can be tracked and recorded using blockchain are not only digital transactions but also physical items, such as transport vehicles. And while many of the other industries discussed work with public records, private blockchain networks offer their own opportunities.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Blockchain in Transport Alliance (BiTA) was founded to develop industry standards and train its network of members. It is the largest commercial blockchain alliance in existence, and its nearly 500 members are developing the frameworks that will transform the trucking and transportation industry.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain can improve transactions, shipment tracking, and fleet management, protect assets, and increase fleet efficiency. For example, it can facilitate the tracking of food contamination by tracking a truck transporting ingredients and determining whether or not safe storage conditions have been maintained in the event of delays. In addition, routes can be optimized by matching truck drivers and items to be delivered with trucks in a specific region.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">However, for a decentralized ledger to work in this industry, everyone involved needs to be on board: small and large businesses, last-mile shippers, and large trucking companies. Without extensive participation, the system will not be able to be fully optimized.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:56:43','2025-10-08 09:11:21'),(87,23,'Aviation','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-96463703-7fff-2c62-7dd4-640e275b2371\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Think about the data that goes into booking a flight: names, birthdays, credit card numbers, entry requirements, destinations, and sometimes even hotel or car rental information, depending on how flights are booked. Using blockchain technology to secure and reconcile this data can make the trip safer and more convenient for the traveler. Converting a physical ticket into a digital token provides a new layer of security. Using a smart contract as part of the ticket token can help airlines control the sale and use of tickets to provide verified experiences to customers. It can also be used to create more accurate aircraft maintenance logs, prevent overbookings, and more.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Russian airline S7 Airlines is deploying a private, Ethereum-based blockchain that uses smart contracts to reduce settlement times between the airline and its agents from 14 days to 15 seconds. In 2019, the airline announced that it was handling $1 million in ticket sales per month through its blockchain.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Other blockchain apps, such as Winding Tree\'s decentralized travel marketplace, eliminate the need for travel agencies. American Airlines uses the marketplace to allow employees of a large company to book leisure tickets at the corporate rate without having to contact a travel agent.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Another area where blockchain is already being used is airline loyalty. Singapore Airlines\' Kris+ lifestyle app has a digital wallet built on a blockchain that securely converts miles into cryptocurrency that can be used with trading partners. This program rewards frequent flyers instantly, allowing them to safely use their points for a variety of purchases, not just additional flights.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">There are also many problems behind the scenes that can be solved with blockchain—especially related to aircraft maintenance, repair, and operation (MRO). PwC estimates that the use of blockchain could reduce MRO costs by about $3.5 billion thanks to improved efficiency. Tracking aircraft spare parts is a manual process that often leads to delays, costs, and errors in maintenance. Blockchain solves these problems with accurate and traceable digital records that can provide an accurate maintenance history along with details on how to configure an aircraft. Detailed MRO data can be fed into algorithms to support predictive maintenance and reduce downtime. They can also be used to quickly track down parts and suppliers and increase the resale value of aircraft.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:58:17','2025-10-08 09:11:49'),(88,23,'Space and Defense','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-bb47d98f-7fff-4048-79e3-ff7636a97df6\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Sixty-one percent of aerospace and defense companies are working with blockchain or distributed ledger solutions, according to Accenture. Blockchain technology has the potential to streamline the inventory and authentication of parts, the tracking of personnel certifications, and much more.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">For example, GoDirect Trade (a unit of Honeywell Aerospace) is an aerospace parts marketplace that uses blockchain to list parts for resale. Its ledger stores the maintenance and manufacturing history for each of its 25,000 parts in one place. This data is then used to immediately list refurbished parts in accordance with Federal Aviation Administration requirements, avoiding the manual and paper-heavy processes that characterize the resale of parts for aviation.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">To comply with NATO standards, French aerospace and defense company Thales Group is using blockchain at one of its new manufacturing sites to trace naval equipment and other parts manufactured there.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Countries such as Russia and the US are also making progress on blockchain. In 2018, the Russian Ministry of Defense set up a blockchain research lab. In 2019, the U.S. The Department of Defense hired start-up SIMBA Chain to develop a blockchain solution that will enable government agencies to securely share and track R&amp;D data.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:58:49','2025-10-08 09:12:16'),(89,23,'Hospitality','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-3d4c1a19-7fff-c334-017a-b4bb7b94cea0\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Large hotel chains lose up to 30% of their total revenue to commissions on third-party booking services. Small chains and independent hotels give between 18% and 22% of their revenue to third-party sellers.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain technology makes the booking and sales process more efficient and allows hoteliers to keep a larger share of revenue.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">For example, Winding Tree is working with hotels, airlines, and tourism offices to create a decentralized B2B travel marketplace. Hotels upload their app\'s API to the marketplace to make it accessible to online travel agencies. The two companies can get in touch directly with each other so that the online travel agency can offer the hotel rooms online.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Decentralized platforms are also changing the area of shared apartments. Dtravel, for example, has positioned itself as an Airbnb competitor. As a community-managed platform, all participants—people who own the TRVL token—have a say in Dtravel\'s decisions, such as setting homesharing policies. Hosts don\'t pay any transaction fees; instead, they contribute 1% of all bookings to the Dtravel ecosystem\'s property protection pool. Guests pay transaction fees as low as 5% when paying for bookings via TRVL—which is much lower than the service fee of up to 14.2% of the booking total on Airbnb, excluding platform fees.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:59:26','2025-10-08 09:12:41'),(90,23,'Internet of Things (IoT) in Industry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e269b340-7fff-3dbf-79fb-6fbf26a363c7\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">IoT in industry is being disrupted by blockchain technology. A number of companies are using blockchain technology to give any device the ability to securely connect, interact, and transact independently of a central authority. A blockchain could serve as a public ledger for a large number of devices that no longer need a central node to mediate communication between them. The devices would be able to communicate autonomously with each other to manage software updates, bugs, or energy management. In 2017, South Korean logistics company Hyundai Merchant Marine (HMM) conducted test runs of a blockchain system developed jointly with Samsung SDS that uses IoT devices for real-time monitoring. The \"paperless operation\" was used for ship arrival/departure, bills of lading, and cargo tracking. More recently, companies such as Helium and NetObjex have introduced blockchain-based networks for IoT devices in internet infrastructure and smart city traffic, respectively.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Others deal with the security of IoT networks. As critical infrastructures such as power plants and transportation are equipped with connected sensors, privacy and security concerns have arisen. Companies like Xage use blockchain\'s tamper-proof ledgers to secure data in industrial device networks.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 08:59:53','2025-10-08 09:13:08'),(91,23,'3D Printing','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-87a9ac20-7fff-eb9e-1a37-c2f3c73c26f6\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">3D printing is also being disrupted by blockchain technology. 3D printing and \"additive manufacturing\" (i.e., the production of 3D objects by applying layers) are highly technology-driven processes in which the digital files can be easily transferred at the click of a mouse. As a result, parts and products are easier to share and track, leading to smarter digital supply networks and supply chains. Using blockchain to support these evolving infrastructures can eliminate security vulnerabilities, protect intellectual property from theft, and streamline project management, ultimately helping 3D printing and additive manufacturing grow and scale. The U.S. Air Force, for example, is collaborating with SIMBA Chain as part of its Blockchain Approach for Supply Chain Additive Manufacturing Parts (BASECAMP) project. The blockchain-based platform registers and tracks 3D printed parts for more secure and tamper-proof recording. Blockchain systems such as Vistory\'s MainChain and Data Gumbo\'s GumboNet also help protect the integrity of the 3D printing process by providing traceable, authenticated records of 3D designs.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:00:38','2025-09-10 09:00:38'),(92,23,'Construction, Architecture and Construction','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-c13e2866-7fff-91de-f27b-8d02eca44d30\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">How blockchain technology is changing construction, architecture, and construction. Construction is a highly regulated industry that employs a variety of tradespeople who often take on very complex projects. Verifying their identities, the quality of their work, and their reliability can be difficult and time-consuming. A blockchain-based ecosystem could help solve this challenge by making it easier for general contractors to verify identities and track progress across multiple teams. Blockchain technology could also help ensure that building materials are sourced from the right sources and are of adequate quality, while smart contracts could make it easier to make timely payments depending on project milestones. For example, Amsterdam-based construction company HerenBouw used blockchain to document transactions over the course of a major development project in the city, creating a more accurate, verifiable record of orders placed and disbursed.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:01:21','2025-09-10 09:01:21'),(93,23,'Real Estate','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0b8e1cde-7fff-2be0-17a3-ceb97ef87cf4\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Problematic aspects of real estate transactions are the lack of transparency during and after the transaction, the large amount of paperwork, possible fraud and errors in public records. Blockchain offers a way to reduce the need for paper-based records and speed up transactions—helping stakeholders increase efficiency and reduce transaction costs on all sides of the transaction. Blockchain applications for real estate can help record, track, and transfer land, title deeds, liens, and more, ensuring that all documents are accurate and verifiable. The entity Propy wants to offer a secure home purchase via a blockchain-based smart contract platform. All documents are signed online and stored securely, while deeds and other contracts are recorded not only on paper but also using blockchain technology. Tech startup Ubitquity offers a software-as-a-service (SaaS) blockchain platform for financing, real estate, and mortgage companies. The company is working with Washington-based Stewart Title, among others, to use blockchain technology to capture documents and create token-based property titles. Coupled with virtual reality and gaming, blockchain makes it possible to buy virtual land. On the metaverse gaming platform Decentraland, both individuals and companies have paid record sums for a piece of digital land. The Metaverse Group bought 116 plots of land worth $2.4 million in cryptocurrency in November 2020, while someone paid $450,000 to be the neighbor of musician Snoop Dogg in the metaverse The Sandbox.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:02:02','2025-09-10 09:02:02'),(94,23,'Energy Management','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-c3f53ce9-7fff-b855-be6d-19c9efc50fd1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The energy industry is another industry that has traditionally been highly centralized. In the U.S. and the U.K., energy deals require either contacting an established utility such as Duke Energy or National Grid or working with a middleman who buys from a major electric utility. As in other industries, distributed ledgers could minimize (or eliminate altogether) the need for middlemen. Companies like LO3 Energy are rethinking the traditional process of exchanging energy. LO3 Energy\'s Pando product, which runs on the open-source Energy Web Chain blockchain platform, allows customers of utilities to \"transact\" as part of \"distributed energy generation systems\" that allow people to generate, buy, and sell energy to their neighbors. Other companies have also used blockchain to provide access to renewable energy. For example, two major Spanish energy companies—Acciona Energy and Iberdrola—are using blockchain to certify the cleanliness of energy by tracing its origin.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:02:36','2025-09-10 09:02:36'),(95,23,'Waste Management','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-353854e1-7fff-2f3a-c78f-fc3f70af7efb\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blockchain technology can also contribute to improvement in waste management. Recycling is one of the best ways to reduce the amount of waste in the landfill—but it can be a confusing and tedious practice that isn\'t really worth it. A blockchain-based solution could help optimize existing recycling systems. There are many companies that want to create incentives for recycling. Plastic Bank offers money or digital tokens in exchange for used plastic and is working with IBM to spread its recycling solution worldwide. W2V Eco Solutions is a more locally focused platform that allows communities to reward people who properly sort their recycling with coins. RecycleGO\'s blockchain-based software can enable recycling companies to better track and thus optimize their recycling activities within their local supply chain. In addition to IBM, established companies such as the German chemical manufacturer BASF have also joined the movement. In August 2020, BASF launched a blockchain-based pilot project for plastics recycling called reciChain. As part of this project, plastics manufacturers are marking plastics with unique \"chemical barcode tags\" to better track them throughout their lifecycle and incentivize recycling. The consortium includes members such as NOVA Chemicals, Deloitte, and Save-On-Foods.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:03:06','2025-09-10 09:03:06'),(96,23,'Oil and Gas Industry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-83850f74-7fff-9e28-10c9-e70ea1d7c5a6\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">One of the key benefits of blockchain for the oil and gas industry is its ability to automate the validation and enforcement of contracts between multiple stakeholders in the supply chain. The Abu Dhabi National Oil Company, for example, uses a blockchain-based system to securely and automatically track production volumes and execute transactions at the various stages of oil and gas production, from the production side to the customer side. This reduces the time it takes to process transactions and also improves transparency. Meanwhile, the OOC Oil &amp; Gas Blockchain Consortium has created a platform for automating the processes involved in transporting production water. This includes triggering automated payments to suppliers and providing authenticated, immutable records to help resolve disputes.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:03:35','2025-09-10 09:03:35'),(97,23,'Healthcare','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-bfeda930-7fff-2546-c2ed-5db1b60ac4a9\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In particular, the exchange of information in the healthcare sector is optimized by blockchain technology. Healthcare organizations are unable to securely share data across platforms. Better data collaboration between care providers could ultimately mean more accurate diagnoses, more effective treatments, and more cost-effective care. The use of blockchain technology could allow hospitals, health insurance companies, and other parties in the healthcare value chain to share access to their networks without compromising the security and integrity of the data.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">HealthVerity is one of the players in this space, combining a health data exchange with a blockchain product to manage permissions and access rights. Others are working on better management of provider information using blockchain technology.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">One organization—Synaptic Health Alliance—has brought together Aetna, Cognizant, Humana, MultiPlan, Quest Diagnostics, UnitedHealth Group, and others to ensure their provider directories are up to date. By sharing this vendor information, these companies can reduce their work by storing and updating the data in a shared, accessible database.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Meanwhile, Hashed Health is developing a blockchain-based system for verifying medical credentials that will allow doctors to prove that they are licensed in certain areas.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:04:16','2025-09-10 09:04:16'),(98,23,'Distribution and monitoring of vaccines','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-10b841c5-7fff-eb99-8ef9-77a102611255\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Because blockchain provides real-time visibility into the supply chain, it can respond more quickly to supply disruptions, which is critical for vaccine distribution during a pandemic. Such transparency also helps identify vaccine batches that need to be recalled in the event of an adverse event. Governments in Malaysia and Singapore are already using blockchain to authenticate vaccine certificates and are using systems that can trace the exact batch of vaccine of the vial used for a person. The two countries want to make their systems interoperable so that certificates can be quickly verified when their residents cross each other\'s borders.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:05:04','2025-09-10 09:05:04'),(99,23,'Genome Research','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-3d871a71-7fff-7319-3244-b5f44759a46e\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Genome researchers perform calculations on huge data sets, usually stored in centralized, cloud-based databases. Like anything centralized, this type of storage carries the risk of a single vulnerability that puts sensitive information at risk in the event of a data breach. It also gives a single entity control over the personal genomic data of millions of people. As climate scientists learned after the 2016 U.S. election, such control can be detrimental, as political views and changing laws can jeopardize the availability of scientific data. To solve these problems, the genomics industry is taking inspiration from the concept of computing networks (grids) used for Bitcoin mining. The Ethereum-based Zenome system uses computing and storage nodes to perform bioinformatics analyses. The users of the system pay the nodes for their services. The Zenome system also aims to protect individuals\' ownership and control over their own genomic data. Users who upload their information to the blockchain can sell temporary or permanent access to their data to companies such as pharmaceutical companies. EncrypGen allows people to upload their raw DNA data and removes personal identifiers and sensitive information. People can sell these files on the GeneChain marketplace, which accepts various cryptocurrencies. GeneChain has its own token called DNA.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In May 2021, Nebula Genomics auctioned off the first genomic NFT. The NFT visually and artistically represented the DNA of Professor George Church, who developed the first direct genomic sequencing method in 1984. The project team pointed out that the genome of every human being is a non-falsifiable representation of basic, personal data. Although this project is a novel use case, it also has practical applications. Church\'s genomic NFT encodes the digital location of its complete genomic data, which is hosted on the Oasis Network, a distributed network created by Oasis Labs. The NFT also leverages Parcel, a privacy-friendly SDK from Oasis Labs that combines confidential data processing with blockchain.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:05:38','2025-09-10 09:05:38'),(100,23,'Claims Management','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-cf766685-7fff-34a3-816a-ef1c8f09d419\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The healthcare backend is slow, complex, and expensive. Blockchain, aligned with data standards, has the potential to speed up some of these processes and reduce costs. One area where this could be possible is receivables management, where multiple intermediaries focus on standardizing data, as these are complex and variable procedures. For this work, payers must collect complex data from different entities to determine what services a patient has received and to determine the patient\'s specific plan. Doctors need to know how much they can charge a patient. And everyone wants to know at what point in the process an application is at any given time. For example, Change Healthcare has developed a system called the Intelligent Healthcare Network that tracks the progress of a claim and tracks each of the above transactions (data submitted for review, the review itself, approval or rejection, etc.). The company has also improved the speed and scalability of processing transactions, which has been a bottleneck in many public blockchain projects. Change Healthcare says it carries out up to 50 million transactions per day via the network, an average of 550 transactions per second.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:06:24','2025-09-10 09:06:24'),(101,23,'Pharmaceutical Industry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-7a14f1d9-7fff-e504-06e6-55b868827844\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The pharmaceutical industry is not known for being fast-paced. Although the industry\'s focus is on innovation and problem-solving, there\'s a lot of bureaucracy surrounding clinical trials, regulatory approvals, and more. Using a blockchain ledger can create a more efficient system that opens the door to faster innovation, more regulated production, and smarter security of medical data.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blockchain can also enforce safer drug production. If mistakes are made, they can be detected and traced back to the source. This helps prevent recalls, or at least allows manufacturers to quickly contact retailers to reduce the impact of unsafe drugs on patients\' health and companies\' finances. Chronicled, for example, launched the MediLedger Network in 2017 along with several major drug manufacturers and drug supply chain giants. The project uses a blockchain-based system to track who has come into contact with which drug and when to verify drug returns. In July 2020, MediLedger announced plans to partner with Deloitte to expand its solution to track and combat counterfeit Covid-19 drugs.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:07:25','2025-09-10 09:07:25'),(102,23,'Research and Clinical Trials','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f5de4097-7fff-8203-c77a-c5d0f8827689\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In addition to better data sharing, blockchain offers the opportunity to improve healthcare even before the treatment phase—in research and clinical trials. Effective research and clinical trials require the coordination of multiple sites and stakeholders, as well as the careful management of large amounts of sensitive data from different sources. An important function that blockchain could perform is to link different data within a study, which often takes place in different research institutions and is managed by different researchers. This would prevent the need to reconcile separate databases to create a traceable record of what a participant has done. Once a study is complete, there would be an easily accessible audit trail that could be presented to regulators, investigators, or other researchers (a task typically done by electronic master files for trials).</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:08:13','2025-09-10 09:08:13'),(103,23,'State and public records','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a7e90e57-7fff-67b3-aa6c-ce2020b5ac28\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Public service management is another area where blockchain can help reduce paper-based processes, minimize fraud, and increase accountability between authorities and their citizens. Some governments have taken it upon themselves to take advantage of the blockchain. For example, the Swedish Land Registry has been exploring the use of blockchain for land registry registration to potentially prevent fraud and reduce ownership disputes. It has also tested the use of smart contracts to handle real estate sales. Illinois, Vermont, and other states in the USA have now announced similar initiatives. Start-ups are also helping with the effort—in Eastern Europe, BitFury Group has partnered with the Georgian government to secure and track government data.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:08:47','2025-09-10 09:08:47'),(104,23,'Elections','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9850ec27-7fff-e281-245e-c32b87164ac0\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Elections require voter identity authentication, secure records to track votes, and trusted counts to determine the election winner. In the future, blockchain tools could serve as the basic infrastructure for voting, tracking, and counting—potentially eliminating the need for recounts by preventing electoral fraud. By recording votes as transactions through a blockchain, governments and voters would have an auditable audit trail that ensures no votes are changed or removed and no illegitimate votes are added. A blockchain startup, Follow My Vote, has made its patent-pending end-to-end blockchain voting solution available to the public. Agora, another start-up company, is developing a blockchain-based method of voting. The technology aims to prevent election fraud by using a custom blockchain record. The platform was tested on a limited scale in the 2018 Sierra Leone elections and showed results close to those of the official counts.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:09:21','2025-09-10 09:09:21'),(105,23,'Tracking Weapons','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-75b8ced2-7fff-446c-0332-8226d29f6dd0\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The blockchain\'s ledger offers several options related to gun ownership and use. If gun possession-related information were logged and linked via the blockchain, it would be possible to trace where the weapons came from in the event of unlawful use. In the long term, there are other opportunities to create public-private partnerships related to such information, such as linking existing no-fly lists to blockchain transaction records, in order to more effectively prevent illicit arms purchases.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:09:55','2025-09-10 09:09:55'),(106,23,'Law Enforcement','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-8a6836f3-7fff-c1a1-29ae-e9ae334768bf\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In police investigations, maintaining the integrity of the chain of evidence is paramount. Therefore, a distributed, hard-to-forge record kept via blockchain could provide additional security for handling evidence. In addition, the blockchain can be used to flag certain types of transaction patterns, thus alerting the police if a person engages in suspicious financial activity. Start-ups are developing innovations to make these advantages usable for law enforcement. Chronicled develops sealable, tamper-proof containers with near-field communication chips that register the contents of the container via a blockchain system—an ideal solution for evidence management in law enforcement.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Elliptic, meanwhile, is developing a system to continuously review Bitcoin registries, uncover complex relationships within transactions, and flag suspicious transactions/histories to alert law enforcement.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:10:34','2025-09-10 09:10:34'),(107,23,'The postal system','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9f476be3-7fff-3d80-ad12-d7434c5ce440\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Even the US Postal Service (USPS) is looking into blockchain adoption to improve operations and service. Distributed ledger technology could help create a tracking system that reduces the cost of USPS and saves postal workers time. The Office of the Inspector General released a report in 2016 summarizing the opportunities for the agency to use blockchain, including simplifying financial services (e.g., money orders), building a better \"Internet of Postal Things,\" improving consumer identity validation, and simplifying supply chain management.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In August 2020, the USPS filed a patent for postal voting systems powered by blockchain technology. This includes methods such as sending \"token-linked QR codes\" to voters and storing voter signatures on a blockchain. The following year, CaseMail was certified, a service that uses the blockchain to generate ePost labels as non-forgeable tokens or NFTs. By using digitally stamped labels, Swiss Post can track the path of a parcel and securely record it on the blockchain.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:11:19','2025-09-10 09:11:19'),(108,23,'Humanitarian aid','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-530d60f4-7fff-0ba8-e099-c493c7d053e4\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The adoption of blockchain could help streamline the public aid system, which is often held up by bureaucracy. The United Nations World Food Programme (WFP), for example, uses blockchain to distribute humanitarian aid to refugees in a secure and private way. Since refugees are often unable to open bank accounts, WFP is able to send aid directly by using blockchain and biometric authentication technologies for transaction verification and registration. In Jordan, WFP has set up eye iris scanners in grocery stores in refugee camps, which reliably identify people in need of financial support for their purchases. All transactions are instantly recorded on a private blockchain, and the payment is automatically transferred from the individual\'s blockchain-enabled account.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:11:54','2025-09-10 09:11:54'),(109,23,'Retail and consumer goods industry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-90dbf5f8-7fff-85e6-4568-b1c13db8dcb1\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Currently, consumers\' trust in the retail system is mainly linked to their trust in the marketplace where they make their purchases. For example, trust is a key element of Amazon\'s success with customers. Blockchain could decentralize this trust and link it more to the sellers on the various marketplaces and platforms than to the websites themselves. Startups like Bleexy are developing decentralized blockchain utilities to connect manufacturers, brands, retailers, third-party sellers, content providers, and consumers without intermediaries. Similarly, Germany-based e-commerce software developer Gambio has launched GAMB (Global Alliance of Merchants on the Blockchain)—a decentralized marketplace designed to give retailers full control over their retail space. Any merchant who owns GMB tokens can participate in the alliance because this token gives merchants the ability to vote on marketplace issues. Meanwhile, Moët Hennessy Louis Vuitton (LVMH), together with Microsoft and blockchain startup ConsenSys, has created a platform for authenticating luxury goods using blockchain. The AURA platform allows customers to track their products from design to distribution. For the brand, AURA provides additional protection against counterfeit goods and fraud. Retailers will also soon be found in the metaverse. Walmart plans to launch its own cryptocurrency and NFTs and is also focusing on setting up stores in virtual countries.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:12:25','2025-09-10 09:12:25'),(110,23,'Online Trading','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-015859fd-7fff-fa08-e732-8e5e615cd370\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blockchain technology has the potential to transform e-commerce by reducing transaction costs and increasing transaction security. E-commerce giants such as Walmart, Amazon, and Alibaba have begun exploring blockchain technology. In March 2020, for example, Alibaba filed a patent for a blockchain-based transaction system in Brazil. In global trade, blockchain could play a helpful role in traceability by providing proof of delivery and secure tracking of contract details without the risk of data alteration. The Home Depot has partnered with IBM to use blockchain to manage its supplier relationships. By having a shared, time-stamped record of the flow of goods during shipment and receipt, the retailer was able to reduce its supplier disputes and the time it takes to resolve them.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:12:57','2025-09-10 09:12:57'),(111,23,'Food and beverage industry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6a389e77-7fff-8ec0-7998-676d237829fd\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">E. coli, salmonella, accidental horse meat—there have been a lot of disturbing incidents in the food and beverage industry. Blockchain technology could help manufacturers and retailers avoid such mishaps. As a decentralized ledger that records, stores, and tracks data, blockchain provides a way to monitor the food supply chain and trace contamination issues back to their origin. This benefits the food processor, who can avoid harmful products being delivered to retailers; the retailer, who can reduce recalls or respond to them faster and more effectively; and the consumer, who can trust that what they buy is safe to consume. Walmart and Sam\'s Club have joined IBM\'s Food Trust network, which uses a decentralized blockchain ledger. In 2018, retailers asked their suppliers, especially those of green leafy vegetables, to add their product data to the ledger by 2019. The system is intended to make it easier to quickly trace the origin of food—a decisive advantage when it comes to determining the source of contaminated products, for example. As long as both parties agree, the blockchain serves as an accountability platform that can help reduce food recalls, mislabeled products, and confusion about where a problem originated. Blockchain-based traceability, for example, can be easily applied as a QR code that, when scanned, shows the entire journey of a product to a customer\'s shopping cart. Building on their blockchain pilot project launched in 2018 with the IBM Food Trust, Nestlé and Carrefour are testing a similar service with customers for their Mousline mashed potatoes in France. Consumers can access the data stored in the project blockchain by scanning a QR code on the Mousline packaging, tracking the product\'s journey from the farmer to the Nestlé factory to the Carrefour store.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:13:33','2025-09-10 09:13:33'),(112,23,'Cannabis','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-8327d015-7fff-1a2e-18a7-0c45fb845ebd\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Due to the legalization of marijuana in Canada and growing support for legalization in the U.S., the cannabis industry is benefiting from major investments in technology and research. The legalized cannabis industry is likely to be tightly regulated and could benefit from a transparent and secure system for tracking production and distribution. Blockchain technology could enable a record of product movements from farm to dispensing point, helping to increase security and compliance. Mile High Labs, a manufacturer and supplier of CBD products, has partnered with Chain.io to create a blockchain-powered supply chain for the cannabis industry. Beyond supply chains, Mile High Labs is also interested in leveraging ledger technology for regulation and compliance. IBM has also proposed blockchain technology as a way for governments to control the origin and sale of cannabis.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:14:05','2025-09-10 09:14:05'),(113,23,'Gift Cards and Loyalty Programs','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0ea1fb73-7fff-7ee5-324a-b9990cddaf41\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blockchains can help retailers that offer gift cards and loyalty programs make these systems cheaper and more secure, as fewer middlemen are needed to process card issuance and sales transactions. Similarly, enhanced fraud prevention, enabled by the blockchain\'s unique verification feature, can save costs and help prevent illegitimate users from receiving stolen funds. An example of a company operating in this space is Loyyal, an innovative company that aims to make loyalty rewards more easily interchangeable across different sectors (e.g., rewards for multiple brands of airlines, retailers, and consumers) by using blockchain to support and verify their value.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:14:37','2025-09-10 09:14:37'),(114,23,'Agriculture and Natural Resources','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a994cbbb-7fff-20f3-880b-042b6a29be9b\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In addition to the security and traceability aspects discussed in the context of the food and beverage industry, blockchain has the potential to support the development of agriculture. A decentralized blockchain system could improve transactions, market expansion, and product-specific logistics throughout the agricultural supply chain. In agriculture, a blockchain record can create a level of trust between traders who might otherwise have no experience with each other. It can also help expand the market and promote healthy competition between sellers. One company, AgriDigital, is already using blockchain technology to digitize the buying, selling, and storage of grain and plans to add more raw materials. It makes the management of relationships between stakeholders—from farmers to stock traders—centralized and secure. In addition to efficiency gains, blockchain can also open up new revenue streams for farmers. A novel example is the carbon offset market, which incentivizes the cultivation of hemp, a carbon-negative crop. Farmers can tokenize each crop to sell carbon credits on the market.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:15:29','2025-09-10 09:15:29'),(115,23,'Animal husbandry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-83df3c02-7fff-c2f0-1b9a-723af02994f1\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Similar to agriculture, blockchain technology helps improve food safety, traceability, and sustainability in animal husbandry—the breeding and rearing of animals. Food safety company Neogen has partnered with food-focused blockchain platform Ripe Technology to use blockchain technology to bring together data about an animal\'s genomic profile, feed, and medical history. NSF Verify uses the blockchain to create \"a trusted record for farm animals from birth to consumer.\" Developed by NSF International and other industry leaders, the platform tags animals at birth with RFID markers and then tracks and registers their movements throughout their lifespan on a blockchain. Another startup, Breedr, allows farmers in the UK to track and store data about their cows through a mobile app. Breeder claims that the app can help farmers make better rearing decisions by giving them insights into each animal\'s performance and growth via blockchain—this can reduce the time it takes to get an animal to market. In the area of sustainability, the chemical manufacturer BASF and Arc-net entered into a partnership in 2018 to support the value chain of animal production. The pilot combines BASF\'s sustainability calculation tool, AgBalance Livestock, with arc-net\'s blockchain technology to create a traceable \"ecological footprint\" of meat, dairy, and egg products.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:15:59','2025-09-10 09:15:59'),(116,23,'Fisheries','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-341878bd-7fff-3b6b-4399-a6380e252c62\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Between 20 and 30% of the fish sold in the USA are caught illegally. According to the Wall Street Journal, fishing is also one of the largest industries in the world where forced labor is used. Blockchain-based systems could help make the industry more sustainable, environmentally friendly, and compliant. Registering the type and amount of fishing nets on a blockchain could allow authorities to track whether the boats return to port with the number of nets they left with. The blockchain can also be used to identify and track the fish themselves. The World Wildlife Fund has partnered with ConsenSys and SeaQuest Fiji to launch a blockchain system that proves where, when, and how the tuna was caught. Consumers can use their smartphones to scan a QR code to track the fish\'s journey \"from bait to plate\" and confirm that they are buying legally caught, sustainable tuna without slave labor or oppressive working conditions.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:16:31','2025-09-10 09:16:31'),(117,23,'Forestry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-3aa8d8d7-7fff-bab9-9cfd-03d9cb27345b\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Organizations such as the U.S. Endowment for Forestry and Communities are exploring how blockchain could help secure the global timber supply chain. In October 2020, the ForesTrust organization announced a collaboration with IBM to create the ForesTrust blockchain network, which will be used to \"track wood and wood fibers from the forest to the consumer.\" The initiative aims to promote trust in the international timber trade and to create transparency about the origin of imported timber. To protect natural resources such as forests, the start-up Veridium Labs is developing a \"blockchain-based marketplace for carbon credits and natural capital\" that aims to simplify the purchase of carbon credits to offset the individual or corporate carbon footprint. The company tokenizes carbon credits so that companies can acquire and exchange them more easily and transparently.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:17:01','2025-09-10 09:17:01'),(118,23,'Mining','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-7abd071b-7fff-308f-d920-74131ae68b7b\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blockchain could be a transformative force for the mining industry, requiring the coordination and collaboration of many different players with different incentives. In addition, the industry has been late in transitioning from paper-based processes, which has led to a lack of data transparency that has made it difficult to address issues such as fraud and unsafe working conditions. Blockchain could help track the path of metals and minerals from mine to manufacturer, improving collaboration and traceability in the supply chain.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Companies such as Ford and LG Chem are using IBM\'s blockchain platform to track the cobalt mined in the Democratic Republic of Congo that is used in lithium-ion batteries. Canada\'s MineHub Technologies is also partnering with IBM to develop a blockchain-based platform to digitize many of the paper-based processes that are part of the mining supply chain.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Meanwhile, diamond company De Beers is developing a blockchain-based traceability solution for the diamond industry, called Tracr, that can be used to mark and track diamonds from mine to buyer. Major diamond producers such as Alrosa have joined the pilot project. In December 2020, the World Economic Forum\'s Mining and Metals Blockchain Initiative released a proof of concept for its blockchain-based carbon tracing platform, which aims to ensure the \"traceability of emissions from mine to final product.\"</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The regulatory environment for mining also contributes to the promotion of responsible procurement. In January 2021, the EU Regulation on Conflict-Prone Minerals came into force. The regulation stipulates that EU importers of tin, tungsten, tantalum, and gold may only obtain them from responsible and conflict-free sources, as the trade in these raw materials has been linked to the financing of armed conflicts and forced labor. Blockchain solutions could be key to meeting the regulation\'s requirements for supply chain transparency.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">labor.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:17:39','2025-09-10 09:17:39'),(119,23,'Information and telecommunications sector','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-fd5299df-7fff-cc20-2e8c-38964c9e68ed\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">One service that telecommunications companies can offer well is identity management. Telecom companies have a huge amount of data about their customers\' habits, such as how much mobile data they use monthly, how many hours of video they watch per week, what type of phone they use, where they go, and so on. Customers trust telecom providers with their data more than Facebook (and in some regions even more than Google and Apple), according to a survey by Analysys Mason.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Telecom companies can take advantage of their position by offering blockchain-based identity management services, such as personal data management. This would allow customers to decide whether to allow telcos to share certain types of data with certain companies by using a tamper-proof mechanism such as an access token. In exchange for sharing their data, the customer may receive compensation or a discount for the services of the company in question. In this case, the history of data access would be permanently recorded on the blockchain.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Although telcos will find even more revenue opportunities in the 5G era, they will first need to build the necessary infrastructure—and that\'s expensive. Thanks to the transparency and immutability of blockchain records, telecommunications companies can more easily manage contracts to co-build 5G infrastructure or implement sharing models for leasing networks. China Unicom and China Telecom have agreed to jointly build 5G networks, using a decentralized, blockchain-based platform to manage resource tendering, brokerage, leasing, service valuation, and contract processing. The initiative will save both telcos an estimated $45.5 billion in infrastructure investment costs. Blockchain can also bring efficiency gains to improve the profits of telecommunications companies. For example, telcos can use smart contracts to automate the negotiation, billing, and implementation of service level agreements (SLAs) with roaming partners in multiple countries. These processes are currently complicated, as each country and service provider may have different regulations, network standards, and contract terms.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:18:14','2025-09-10 09:18:14'),(122,23,'Messaging Applications','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9ad6721a-7fff-7afa-6e08-8c3d7ffac6ba\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">A number of messaging platforms are integrating blockchain and crypto features into their apps to improve user security and privacy. Status describes itself as a \"privacy-first messenger.\" The open-source platform enables peer-to-peer messaging based on the Ethereum blockchain and eliminates \"monitoring third parties.\" Signal, a popular encrypted messaging service, is reportedly planning to expand to cryptocurrency payments. These apps operate in an unregulated environment. For example, the encrypted messaging app Telegram raised $1.7 billion from private investors before cancelling the public sale of its planned $1.2 billion Initial Coin Offering (ICO). About a year later, the company launched the test client for its blockchain-based TON (Telegram Open Network). However, in May 2020, Telegram announced that it would discontinue the project after unresolved negotiations with the SEC.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:30:16','2025-09-10 09:30:16'),(123,23,'Publishing','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-c02df6e2-7fff-53d7-f1fe-444637adeb0e\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blockchain could find a wide range of applications in the publishing industry, from entry into the industry to rights management and piracy. Currently, the industry is controlled by a small group of publishers, making it difficult for new and unknown authors to establish themselves. New platforms are emerging to improve the playing field for authors and to promote collaboration between authors, editors, translators, and publishers.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Bookchain, a project by Montreal-based start-up Scenarex, is an Ethereum-based e-book publishing platform. Authors and publishers can upload files to the platform and each configure a smart contract that regulates how the book can be accessed and determines the price. The platform allows authors to bypass third-party vendors and negotiate directly with readers, as well as track where each of their ebooks is in real time. Readers also get full rights to the books once they buy them.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Latvia-based Publica wants to take the process of book financing with the help of smart contracts through crowdfunding. The platform allows authors to sell tokens to fund their project before launching it—a \"book ICO,\" as Publica calls it. Once the book is completed and published on the company\'s blockchain-based platform, it will become available to supporters who own tokens.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Latvia-based company Publica wants to finance book financing with the help of smart contracts via crowdfunding. The platform allows authors to sell tokens to fund their project before launching it—a \"book ICO,\" as Publica calls it. Once the book is completed and published on the company\'s blockchain-based platform, it will become available to supporters who own tokens.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">With virtually forgery-proof records, blockchain offers the ability to maintain the integrity of messages and trace their origin. The New York Times\' (NYT) News Provenance Project will store contextual metadata on news photos on the blockchain to prevent them from being tampered with or shared out of context. The NYT is also working with Adobe and Twitter on the Content Authenticity Initiative, which will use the blockchain to record the editing history of news content.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">A decentralized publishing environment also helps counter censorship in the news media, as no entity is able to delete messages shared on a public blockchain—once a transaction has been added to the network and verified by it, it is added to a \"block\" of information. Since each block contains the digital signature of the previous block and contributes to the subsequent lock, it is virtually impossible to delete a block without breaking the entire chain.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">This property of the blockchain, which is described as censorship-resistant, was proven in 2018 when an open letter about an alleged harassment case at Peking University in China began circulating online. The government censored the letter on WeChat, the country\'s main app, and on other websites and platforms. As a result, an unidentified person posted the letter on the Ethereum blockchain—where it will exist for as long as the blockchain exists. However, the transaction was largely symbolic, as it will be difficult to find the message without knowing its hex code or transaction ID.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">However, governments can still censor the block explorers used to scan a blockchain, as China did in the case of the activist student\'s letter. The country has since banned public blockchains and instead plans to use customized blockchains from platforms that meet the country\'s strict rules and requirements.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:30:55','2025-09-10 09:30:55'),(124,23,'Education and Science','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-48227614-7fff-edb9-ba8e-93642b38a1ce\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Academic credentials must by their nature be universally accepted and verifiable. In both primary/secondary and higher education, the verification of academic transcripts remains a largely manual process, heavily reliant on paper paperwork and case-by-case checks. The use of blockchain solutions in education could streamline verification procedures, thereby reducing fraudulent claims for unearned education credits. Sony Global Education, for example, has partnered with IBM to develop an education platform that uses blockchain to secure and share student data.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In 2016, Learning Machine collaborated with the MIT Media Lab to launch the Blockcerts toolset, which provides an open infrastructure for academic credentials on the blockchain. In 2020, the company was acquired by Hyland Credentials, which offers a blockchain-based system for issuing and verifying digital credentials.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:31:26','2025-09-10 09:31:26'),(125,23,'Libraries','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f6d89999-7fff-d7ac-eb5c-ceced0ff06d4\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In December 2017, San José State University\'s School of Information received a $100,000 grant from the Institute of Museum and Library Services to fund a year-long project exploring the potential of blockchain technology for information services. Potential uses of blockchain in libraries so far include helping libraries expand their services by building an expanded metadata archive, developing a protocol to support community-based collections, and facilitating more effective digital rights management. Sandra Hirsh and Susan Alman\'s work at SJSU caught the attention of the American Library Association\'s Center for the Future of Libraries. They worked with the ALA on a book project with case studies on how blockchain affects libraries and what can be achieved in the future. The book was published in November 2019.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:32:27','2025-09-10 09:32:27'),(126,23,'Entertainment Industry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-07c7c5b9-7fff-53cc-08da-5cc56b644298\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Entrepreneurs from the entertainment industry are relying on blockchain technology to make the exchange of content more equitable for creators. It uses smart contracts that automatically distribute revenue from the purchase of creative works according to predetermined licensing agreements. Muzika, a blockchain-based music streaming platform, has partnered with Binance, a crypto exchange network, to help independent artists get money from their listeners. Muzika has stated that it plans to give artists 90% of the revenue they generate. In 2017, Spotify acquired blockchain startup Mediachain, which had developed a \"decentralized media library\" to better identify the rights holders of songs on Spotify\'s royalty payment platform. UK-based blockchain startup JAAK also plans to work with music rights holders and other players in the entertainment industry. JAAK, which offers an operating system for content, is developing a platform that will allow media owners to convert their inventory of media, metadata, and rights into \"smart content\" that can execute licensing transactions on the Ethereum blockchain itself.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:32:59','2025-09-10 09:32:59'),(127,23,'Streaming Service','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-5412b4fd-7fff-ced3-8cd3-33ec522865e1\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blockchain could help drastically reduce the cost of video traffic by decentralizing video encoding, storage, and distribution. This could disrupt Netflix, YouTube, and other players in the video distribution ecosystem. The VideoCoin network is already working to unlock this capital. The decentralized network provides cloud video infrastructure—encoding, storage, and distribution—in the form of an algorithmic peer-to-peer market. It runs on a new blockchain where customers spend VideoCoins to rent these services. Livepeer is another decentralized network built on the Ethereum blockchain that allows users to share live videos with like-minded people. Users can earn Livepeer tokens by performing video transcoding.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:33:28','2025-09-10 09:33:28'),(128,23,'Gaming','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-31879d52-7fff-77e9-d93c-ced100704a99\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Online gaming continues to experience expansive growth and is now considered a competitive sport with coveted titles to be won, big cash prizes, and even a black market. Blockchain technology allows players to level the playing field, rewards, and exchange value in digital universes. Through the blockchain, digital tokens can be securely exchanged for cryptocurrency without third-party investment. Through the decentralized ledger of a blockchain, players can use a perfected character or set of skills and items across all digital worlds. This means that they can earn rewards faster and exchange them through a decentralized source. These possibilities already exist. Launched in 2014 and delisted in 2019, Project Huntercoin was a gaming ecosystem where players earned internal cryptocurrency rewards (in this case, HUC coins). For eSports and sports betting, there was UnikoinGold until it was discontinued in 2020 due to regulatory restrictions. Enjin Coin, an Ethereum-based cryptocurrency, supports over a billion digital assets in games that are stored on a blockchain and can be traded and sold between users. With a decentralized blockchain base, gaming platforms can enable more secure and transparent money exchanges.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">NFTs and the metaverse will make the play-to-earn model even more profitable. In 2021, the NFT-based online video game Axie Infinity became popular, and sales rose from about $20,000 at the beginning of the year to a peak of $246.32 million in November. Players of the game can earn tokens that can be spent in the game as well as traded on a crypto exchange for real money.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blankos Block Party rose to fame with a similar NFT-driven gameplay: players can buy digital vinyl toy figures designed by artists and build their own games. Its manufacturer, Mythical Games, raised $75 million to launch both the game and the platform in mid-2021. In the virtual world of Decentraland, people can walk around and explore properties owned by users. You can pay to enter clubs, play games, participate in space adventures, and try other experiences dreamed up by the world\'s builders. In 2022, the platform hosted a virtual reality tennis tournament in partnership with the Australian Open, featuring a digital replica of Rod Laver Arena and virtual meetings with professional players.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:34:05','2025-09-10 09:34:05'),(129,23,'Social Media Content','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b39ab391-7fff-cd82-352b-25c9554822db\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Thanks to blockchain, content creators\' relatives have new ways to earn money on social media. Twitter now allows tipping writers in Bitcoin, while TikTok is partnering with NFT artists to create art for creators\' viral content on the platform. Chingari, an Indian short-form video platform, has launched an NFT marketplace for content creators on its platform. Early fans can even earn rewards for supporting budding creators. BitClout, a decentralized social network launched in 2021, lets users create their own coins that other members of the network can buy and sell. These \"Creator Coins\" make it easier to speculate on creators—for example, if you think an influencer will become very popular, buy their Creator Coins now in the hopes of being able to sell them later at a much higher price.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Other companies envision social media networks as platforms where people get paid for the content they produce and where users can maintain their anonymity. One idea is the Karma app, which incentivizes users to create positive content in exchange for tokens.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:34:36','2025-09-10 09:34:36'),(130,23,'Sports Industry','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-1a1375dd-7fff-8c84-e1ca-7ab275b5cca4\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Investing in athletes has traditionally been the job of sports management agencies and corporations, but blockchain could decentralize the process of funding athletes by democratizing fans\' ability to participate financially in the future of tomorrow\'s sports stars. The concept of using blockchain to invest in athletes (and earn returns) has not yet been tested on a larger scale. However, at least one organization, the Jetcoin Institute, has promoted the idea that fans use cryptocurrencies—in this case, \"Jetcoins\"—to invest in their favorite athletes and receive a small portion of the athlete\'s future earnings (as well as VIP events, seat upgrades, etc.). Jetcoin has developed this approach as part of a partnership with the Hellas Verona football club in Italy, among other things.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:35:24','2025-09-10 09:35:24'),(131,23,'Gambling','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-3c9231c4-7fff-0774-4a45-5e817c500209\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Online gambling has experienced significant growth in recent years. But some of the core problems—especially the large transparency gap—have not yet been solved. The adoption of blockchain technology can help create transparency and build trust between a company and its customers. The technology helps ensure fair gaming—records in the ledger cannot be tampered with, so there is no \"the house always wins.\" Sites like Wagerr embrace the idea of \"trustless betting,\" which means that the system is so decentralized that you don\'t need trust. Decentralization makes gambling more universally accessible and reliably balances the costs for online casinos. It also allows for a certain level of anonymity, which is important for many players. Websites that require too much documentation and verification prevent people from playing and could be considered good targets for hackers.</span></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:35:58','2025-09-10 09:35:58'),(132,23,'Art','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f71dce74-7fff-84c9-fbe3-7ef6197d4a6a\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The art industry has already started using blockchain and tokenization as a means to improve global access to the art market and reduce transaction costs. In July 2018, London-based gallery Dadiani Fine Art partnered with art investment blockchain platform Maecenas to sell fractional shares of Andy Warhol\'s \"14 Electric Chairs.\" The auction was conducted using a smart contract on the Ethereum network. Another example is blockchain company Artory, which offers a public ledger to track the history, provenance, and archival material of artworks. In April 2019, it raised $7.3 million in its Series A funding from 2020 Ventures and Hasso Plattner Capital. In the world of digital art, NFTs are used to certify ownership of individual works of art. Artist Beeple, for example, uses NFTs based on blockchain technology to create a unique signature for each artwork he sells, allowing him to track each work, earn royalties, and avoid counterfeiting. NFT sales volume increased in 2021, reaching $10.7 billion in the third quarter, compared to $30 million in the third quarter of 20. Some of the most popular NFT artworks of the year were profile pictures sold by the Bored Ape Yacht Club, which had sold more than $1 billion worth of NFTs as of January 2022. Much of the interest was triggered by prominent buyers and the perks offered by the club, as well as speculation on rising prices and high resale values.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">But like all disruptive developments, NFT investing has also led to controversy. An NFT collector has lost $2.2 million worth of Bored Ape artwork in a hack, and popular YouTubers have sold their channels as NFTs without their knowledge or consent. These incidents have led to criticism of the authentication and security of NFTs, raising doubts about how valuable a vulnerable asset can be. Critics have pointed to the paradox of investing in deregulated NFTs while demanding that a centralized platform step in to retrieve the stolen artworks.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:36:57','2025-09-10 09:36:57'),(133,23,'Photography','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a77f9844-7fff-9552-7c72-5c931fcd16a6\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In our digital world, where stealing images often requires only two clicks of the mouse, it\'s often difficult for photographers to earn royalties for their work. YouPic is developing a \"decentralized photo platform\" where photographers can securely register and license their images using smart contracts. Through the platform, photographers can be paid directly by customers, eliminating the need for brokers and their commissions.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Photochain uses blockchain technology to store licensing and copyright information for images from the medical and scientific fields. The company claims to charge photographers a lower commission than the rest of the industry while allowing content providers to have \"full control over the price, copyright, and licensing of their images\" for sale on the company\'s platform.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:37:42','2025-09-10 09:37:42'),(134,23,'Cloud Computing and Storage','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-27ead652-7fff-777e-a040-29eccfde08e5\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Cloud services require large computing resources and data storage capacities, which can be inefficient when adopting IoT products. Blockchain technology can help enable more decentralized cloud services and increase connectivity, security, and computing power. Salesforce, which offers cloud solutions for businesses, has launched Salesforce Blockchain, for example. The product is built on top of the CRM software Salesforce is known for and leverages smart contracts and blockchain-based data exchange. Companies that offer cloud storage often back up their customers\' data on a central server, which can mean increased vulnerability of the network to hacker attacks. Blockchain cloud storage solutions allow storage to be decentralized, making it less vulnerable to attacks that can cause systemic damage and widespread data loss. Filecoin, also known as the \"Airbnb for file storage,\" is a high-profile crypto project that rewards hosting files. This could help create a decentralized version of S3 of Amazon Web Services. The company behind it, Protocol Labs, has received investment from Union Square Ventures, Naval Ravikant, and the Winklevoss brothers, among a number of other prominent names. However, Filecoin is just one of many projects in this space—other token names in the storage space include Storj and Siacoin. Storj offers a blockchain-enabled cloud storage network to improve security and reduce transaction costs for storing information in the cloud. Storj users can also rent out their unused digital storage space on a peer-to-peer basis, potentially creating a new market for crowdsourced cloud storage capacity.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Blockchain allows cloud computing providers to overcome the limitations of cloud exchanges—networks that allow businesses to connect to multiple clouds and switch resources as their computing needs change. Cloud exchanges are controlled by a single company and are therefore vulnerable to fraud. Blockchain-based cloud exchanges are decentralized, making them less vulnerable to fraudulent transactions and cyberattacks. Different individuals and organizations can offer their computing resources, which stimulates competition and incentivizes fair pricing. iExec, a marketplace for computing resources, is built on the Ethereum blockchain. Organizations can rent compute resources, blockchain applications, and datasets using the marketplace\'s eRLC token through iExec.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:38:36','2025-09-10 09:38:36'),(135,23,'Internet identity','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-4124fb92-7fff-ed29-1ece-2d554b08c74e\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In today\'s web, it\'s hard to determine your true identity, and your personal information resides on the servers of the companies for the applications you use, which are hardly interactive (even using Facebook as a login will only get you so far). Platforms like Serto (formerly uPort) believe in a future where you can simply carry your identity around with you on the internet.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">IBM offers a blockchain-powered identity management tool called IBM Verify Credentials. The decentralized system allows certain trusted organizations to issue credentials to users, who can then use them to prove their identity to other organizations, improving personal privacy and streamlining the verification process.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:39:07','2025-09-10 09:39:07'),(136,23,'Advertising on the Internet','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-5650b313-7fff-5e19-5b9d-ab7df9074790\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The Internet as we know it was created with ad hoc solutions for advertising. Overall, advertising consumes a lot of mobile data when web pages load, and both advertisers and consumers suffer from the lack of protocols.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">In 2017, Brave raised $35 million in 30 seconds during its Basic Attention Token (BAT) ICO to compensate advertisers and users. Instead of using a middleman like Google or Facebook\'s advertising arm, advertisers are listed directly on Brave\'s blockchain-based browser. Users who opt for this will receive fewer but more targeted advertisements without malware. And advertisers get better data on their spending.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:39:34','2025-09-10 09:39:34'),(137,23,'Human Resources','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f68db186-7fff-c94b-2ccc-1ed4e00c3430\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Conducting background checks and checking employment histories can be time-consuming, highly manual tasks for recruiters. If employment and criminal records were stored on a blockchain ledger (and thus free from the possibility of falsification), recruiters could streamline the verification process and move hiring processes faster.</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Chronobank is a blockchain project that aims to transform the HR/recruitment industry. It focuses specifically on improving short-term recruitment for on-demand jobs in cleaning, warehousing, e-commerce, and other areas. The startup aims to use blockchain to make it easier for individuals to find work on the fly and be rewarded for their work through a decentralized framework via cryptocurrency, without the involvement of traditional financial institutions.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Once a person is hired, employee engagement becomes an important part of human resource management—and blockchain could play a role in this. eXo Rewards, for example, uses cryptocurrency and a blockchain wallet to reward and motivate employees. Colleagues can send each other recognition in the form of tokens that can be used on a corporate marketplace for various goods and services.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:40:20','2025-09-10 09:40:20'),(138,23,'Economics and Corporate Governance','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-d299a8ac-7fff-8ce0-ff98-564cf78993e2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The benefits of using blockchain for smart contracts and verifiable transactions can also be used to make companies\' accounting more transparent. The Boardroom app, for example, provides a governance framework and app that allows businesses to manage smart contracts on the public and permissioned Ethereum blockchain.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The app provides a management system for organizations to ensure that smart contracts are executed according to the rules encoded on the blockchain (or to update the rules themselves). Boards can also use the app for shareholder votes by proxy and the management of joint proposals.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Aragon goes even further, using blockchain to \"disrupt the creation and maintenance of businesses and other organizational structures.\" Believing that decentralized organizations can solve the world\'s worst problems, Aragon is developing tools that allow businesses to use blockchain to manage their entire global workforce. The company sees blockchain as a tool to welcome more employees and contractors from developing countries to North American and European companies.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The transparency and immutability of blockchain records make them ideal for ESG reporting. Blockchain, in conjunction with the Internet of Things, can provide authenticated, verifiable, quantitative performance data—for example, that a factory is reducing its energy consumption or greenhouse gas emissions.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Data Gumbo\'s GumboNet ESG demonstrates this use case. At one end of the system are industrial IoT sensors that collect real-time information about the activities of buyers, suppliers, and logistics service providers. Smart contracts are then activated to measure the data against sustainability standards. The system instantly generates and updates verifiable ESG reports.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:40:51','2025-09-10 09:40:51'),(139,23,'Predictions','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-dad68e6c-7fff-3e4e-55e5-f46e031cb1cd\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As more and more industries embrace blockchain holistically, the technology could also transform the research, analysis, consulting, and forecasting industries. With an unwaveringly accurate transactional dataset to support their data analysis, forecasts will have a stronger foundation for using machine learning algorithms to generate targeted predictions and insights.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain is already creating a new \"prediction market.\" Augur, which is built on the Ethereum blockchain, allows users to predict events and be rewarded for making correct predictions. (CBINSIGHTS, 2022)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Videos</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">To deepen your knowledge, here are some more videos and links.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 36pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><