e=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Topic overview:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">1. Blockchain beyond the hype: What is the strategic business value?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;\"><a href=\"https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/mckinsey-digital/our-insights/blockchain-beyond-the-hype-what-is-the-strategic-business-value\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(5, 99, 193); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-caps: small-caps; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">LINK</span></span></span></a></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">2. Blockchain in Industries: A Survey</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;\"><a href=\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8662573\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(5, 99, 193); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-caps: small-caps; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">LINK</span></span></span></a></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">3. Blockchain technology: What it is, benefits, and its cross-industry applications</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 8pt 0pt;\"><a href=\"https://www.insiderintelligence.com/insights/blockchain-technology-applications-use-cases/:~:text=Blockchain%E2%80%99s%20potential%20use%20cases%20span,time%20transactions-beyond-the-hype-what-is-the-strategic-busines\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(5, 99, 193); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-caps: small-caps; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">LINK</span></span></span></a></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">4. Blockchain: Emerging Technology Offers Benefits for Some Applications but Faces Challenges</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><a href=\"https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-22-104625#:~:text=What%20GAO%20Found%20Blockchain%20combines,chain%20management%2C%20and%20legal%20records\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(5, 99, 193); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-caps: small-caps; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">LINK</span></span></span></a></p><div><br>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-10 09:41:54','2025-10-08 09:14:22'),(141,25,'Supply Chain Transparency: IBM and Maersk','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b5c05ad0-7fff-4641-1fae-4b5652ee4235\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This case study examines the blockchain trading platform developed by technology company IBM and container shipping company Maersk and its application, including a recent pilot project in Peru. An IBM10 executive shared insights into the TradeLens platform (platform shut down Nov 2022). An official from the Peruvian Customs Administration, SUNAT, reported on the experience of implementing the TradeLens platform for two routes: Callao - Amsterdam, Netherlands, and Callao - Algeciras, Spain. CONTEXT Traditionally, commerce generates large amounts of paperwork. Supply chains and governments rely on the physical movement of these documents to protect against illegal smuggling, counterfeit goods, and, in some cases, human trafficking. Processing the documents and information for a container shipment allegedly costs more than twice the actual cost of transportation (Consensys, n.d.). A study jointly conducted by IBM and Maersk found the following inefficiencies in their pilot projects:  - A single shipment of avocados from Mombasa, Kenya, to Rotterdam, the Netherlands, requires 30 actors/organizations, more than 100 people, and 200 information exchange operations. The interactions between these actors involve time-consuming manual, paper-based processes. The information collected across organizational boundaries was inconsistent, resulting in \"blind spots\" throughout the supply chain. These blind spots included missing or faulty paperwork throughout the supply chain with limited traceability. The exchange of messages between the individual companies was complex, cumbersome, and costly. Risk assessments were not detailed enough, and clearance procedures were vulnerable to fraud. In another trade transaction carried out through the same trade network, it took several days for the documents sent from the farm in Kenya to reach the Dutch customs authorities, as is customary for a shipment of flowers from Kenya to the Netherlands. It\'s a cumbersome process, and according to a Maersk manager, the average cross-border administrative costs of trade are 21 percent of the total cost, compared to 8 percent for transportation.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The same applies to other trade networks. Shipments from Central Europe to the United States were often delayed by four weeks due to a lack of transparency and a delayed exchange of information. The problems that caused this delay included missing customs documents preventing the gate-in at the arrival terminal and containers arriving on different modes of transport, causing complications in acceptance, and the advance notice to the terminal was not updated in time; there were delays in filing due to misunderstandings between the exporter and customs about the requirements for the documents; containers missed the ship due to delayed gate-in, visibility issues, and communication delays; and limited visibility into transport plans meant that inland logistics providers were unable to move the cargo at the expected time. CONCEPT IBM and Maersk want to address these problems through a distributed, permissioned platform called TradeLens (formerly Global Trade Digitization—GTD). The platform facilitates the exchange of data on operations and the handling of the document workflow within the supply chain ecosystem. The platform allows all stakeholders to access documents in real-time—a feature that is not unique to a blockchain-based system. The participants sign documents that they confirm in digital form. These cryptographic signatures enable documents to be authenticated in real time. These documents are entered into the blockchain (some directly by the stakeholders acting as nodes in the blockchain network, others indirectly through the stakeholders—see the implementation section below). The combination of cryptographic authentication and the fact that a blockchain transaction cannot be altered is intended to dispel the mistrust between the various actors. Because it\'s a distributed database, the different jurisdictions don\'t have to agree on a centralized authority to control the ledger.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Application of the Tradelens (GTD) platform</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/23.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 1: Interactions in the TradeLens platform</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Adaptation from IBM/Maersk CORE WP23 Presentation.)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 1 shows how a TradeLens platform works with different actors and the type of documents that are usually part of the TradeLens Paperless Blockchain Network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Privacy</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The TradeLens platform takes privacy into account by using a feature called \"Channels\" in Hyperledger Fabric. When a user (e.g., an exporter) initiates a shipment, they also list all interested parties who need to access the data. Thus, in the case of such a broadcast, only the interested parties listed can access the details of the program. In this way, for each transaction, sub-networks are created within the blockchain network for that trading network. For example, in a commercial transaction involving a shipment of flowers from Mombasa to Rotterdam, only the relevant actors have access to the information for that particular transaction. Other traders and logistics service providers in the Mombasa-Rotterdam trading network who are registered on the TradeLens platform do not have access to the information on this specific transaction. The type of data determines the level of data protection on the platform. The users who upload the data to the platform are the owners of the data. Since the vast majority of the information uploaded is data that participants already share worldwide, the data is not subject to personal data protection regulations such as the European Union\'s General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). However, commercial data, including proprietary information and invoices, is not necessarily public and requires special protection. TradeLens does not add such data to the blockchain unchanged but stores and shares this data separately. Instead, these sensitive documents are hashed, and only the hash values of such documents are publicly available via the blockchain. These hash values can be used to trace back the sensitive information, but not to retrieve it. A similar regulation was followed in Peru with SUNAT. The users who upload the data are the owners of this data. However, the information exchanged is public. SUNAT does not include any personal data or confidential business information in the TradeLens platform. IBM and Maersk also hope to use the \"channels\" feature in the long term to keep certain classes of information within a country (data localization), as many countries continue to restrict the cross-border exchange of and access to data.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Data verification</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The platform does not prevent incorrect information from being entered into the platform because there is no data verification mechanism at the nodes. So if someone enters incorrect information at the beginning of a chain, the blockchain will enter it \"faithfully\" into the system and thus not prevent the problem of \"garbage in, garbage out.\" However, the blockchain allows for an \"audit trail\" so that one can trace the origin of an incorrect data entry as soon as an error is discovered. While tracing errors is also possible via other solutions, the tamper-proof nature of the blockchain ledger makes auditing more trustworthy. This can prevent intentional data corruption and enable subsequent assessment and targeted correction. In addition, if a government participates in the blockchain network (in the future), it can be part of the consensus mechanism. Transaction validation is done automatically according to a \"chain code/smart contract\" (which is the program that runs on the blockchain to implement the business logic that applications use to interact with the ledger). This limits the erroneous information to those that cannot be detected as invalid by the automatic validation process.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Differences from other centralized technologies</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">How is the TradeLens platform different from a centralized ledger or database that stakeholders can access through different permission rules? On the one hand, a centralized database represents a single point of failure. The database is vulnerable to attack and poses a storage risk if there are no redundancies. In addition, when entries in the database are changed (either by the attacker or the system administrator), it is difficult to understand the changes that have been made. In a blockchain platform, the database is distributed among its nodes (members), so attacking all nodes at the same time is far more difficult than attacking a single node. In addition, each transaction block contains a hash of the previous transaction block, creating a chain. When an entry is changed, the corresponding hashes after the changed transaction are different from the original, so that you can immediately understand where the change was made. Therefore, a blockchain-powered platform like TradeLens is more secure than a centralized database run by a system administrator.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Participation in the dispute</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Another question related to blockchain adoption is whether a dispute arising from a transaction entered on the blockchain platform can be resolved within the framework of existing jurisdictions both within and between countries. There are very likely gaps in this area, especially in developing countries. However, these gaps are not specifically limited to blockchains. For example, for electronic windows, countries are required to have laws and regulations in place, including the recognition of electronic documents as equivalent to paper documents, the archiving and storage of electronic documents, the recognition of electronic documents in court proceedings, electronic signatures, intellectual property rights for electronic data, liability for data loss or breach, and dispute resolution, including in the case of cross-border data exchange.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Experiences from implementation</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The implementation of TradeLens varies from country to country and depends on both the country context and the specific application (e.g., customs clearance, processing, and exchange of certificates of origin). The implementation takes place in several phases (see Figure 2).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-16618128-7fff-9818-97a9-2895ab4ec712\"></span></span></p><div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/24.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-46e511b7-7fff-dbb9-5bc8-d2386979a39c\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 2: TradeLens Implementation Phases</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: BLOCKCHAIN FOR TRADE: SELECT CASE STUDIES AND LESSONS LEARNED by Nathan Associates, 2018)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Implementation costs</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The costs are made up of implementation and maintenance costs. The implementation costs, which are mainly incurred by the network\'s actors in the fourth and fifth phases mentioned above, include the costs of integrating TradeLens into existing systems using APIs. Such integration requires the involvement of IT experts in three to four organizations in a given country for a few weeks. On average, the cost of such an implementation is US$10,000 to US$100,000. In terms of running costs, the network\'s customers pay for the use of TradeLens based on the individual transactions (containers). The members of the network (e.g., governments) get access to the platform\'s data without having to pay for it, as they contribute significant amounts of data to the platform.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Technical challenges</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">IBM and Maersk have launched this solution on a pilot basis in several countries. The implementation was associated with some challenges. From a technical point of view, the solution can help developing countries to overhaul their existing trading platforms. However, a certain minimum level of IT skills is required to operate such a system. A first requirement is the ability to operate a node on the permissible blockchain. The skills required to operate such a node are relatively normal IT skills. Organizations must have a basic, pre-existing IT infrastructure (e.g., their own pool of IT staff, a functioning IT system at both the front and back end that is capable of executing consensus algorithms) to ensure that capacity building is not too difficult.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Capacity challenges</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">During the implementation, IBM and Maersk realized that not every member of the ecosystem has the technical capabilities to run a node on the permissioned blockchain (running on the Hyperledger Fabric). In addition, the individual actors in the ecosystem are used to their own systems for entering and retrieving information. Therefore, the consortium only puts certain members of the ecosystem on the nodes of the blockchain. These currently include IBM, Maersk, and usually other shipping companies (between 10 and 15 members in total). The importers, exporters, and government agencies access the platform through an API, where they can enter and retrieve information on the blockchain, but only through the nodes operated by the blockchain members. The longer-term goal is to include actors who are central to the platform, such as customs, as members of the blockchain that runs the node so that these key players can participate in the consensus process that establishes rights to the blockchain network. There were many challenges related to SUNAT, primarily due to the lack of knowledge about blockchain in the Peruvian organizations. IBM representatives from the Netherlands and the United States held several workshops in Peru to explain the benefits of the TradeLens platform and how to use it.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The challenge of interoperability</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Another challenge is the interoperability of the systems. By integrating existing IT systems in the countries (e.g., an electronic single window) into the TradeLens platform, the solution requires minimal changes to the application interface for the user. In Peru, for example, SUNAT uses an external single window—VUCE Peru—for the inspection of goods subject to restrictions and for the payment of fees from other entities and for inspections in maritime transport. In all implemented cases, including in Peru, the solution is embedded in legacy systems. Although connecting to the TradeLens platform has become easier for all agencies, such as customs, logistics companies, and carriers, collaboration between these agencies remains a challenge because the data is barely standardized even within the same country (which is also a challenge for single electronic windows). For example, customs authorities, logistics companies, and freight forwarders use different data standards, and the TradeLens platform must be adapted to the TradeLens standard by each player. TradeLens is actively working with the United Nations Rules for Electronic Data Interchange for Administration, Commerce, and Transport to align with global standards for data exchange and interoperability, in the hope that governments and trading communities will comply with these standards. Another concern of IBM developers is that there will be a proliferation of DLTs, and thus a trading community using a competing system such as IBM/Maersk\'s may not be able to interact with TradeLens, which could prevent regional connectivity and cross-border exchange of freight data, for example. As such, IBM is working with Hyperledger QUILT, a foundational blockchain tool that provides interoperability between ledger systems by implementing the Inter-Ledger Protocol (also known as ILP).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Effect</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">According to IBM, the TradeLens platform has already had an impact, albeit only in a pilot test. The impact is primarily due to the digitization of trade processes; this digitization of the entire supply chain has been made possible by the accessibility and security features of a blockchain platform. The following are some examples of the concrete improvements that have been achieved.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">TradeLens has reduced the transit time of a shipment of packaging material to a production line in the United States by 40 percent.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">TradeLens has helped reduce the steps to answering basic operational questions like \"Where\'s my container?\" from 10 steps and five people to one step and one person.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">As part of the European Union\'s nuclear research program, Dutch customs used the additional data in TradeLens to improve its targeting processes. The data allowed them to avoid unnecessary checks that they would otherwise have carried out, which benefits legitimate trade. The IBM and Maersk platform has been in a private beta phase since 2016. In mid-2018, the platform transitioned to limited availability, which is expected to transition to general availability by the end of 2018. The use of the platform is then subject to a fee. As of August 2018, 94 organizations have registered to participate. These include, but are not limited to:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Port operators: PSA Singapore, International Container Terminal Services Inc., Patrick Terminals, Modern Terminals (Hong Kong), Port of Halifax, Port of Rotterdam, Port of Bilbao, PortConnect, and PortBase.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Terminal operators APM Terminals\' Network and Holt Logistics (Port of Philadelphia).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Global container shipping companies: Maersk Line, Hamburg Süd, and Pacific International Lines (PIL).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Customs authorities: the Netherlands, Saudi Arabia, Singapore, Australia, and Peru.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Customs brokers: Ransa and Güler &amp; Dinamik.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Beneficiary Cargo Owners (BCOs): Torre Blanca/Camposol and Umit Bisiklet.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Freight forwarders and transport and logistics companies: Agility, CEVA Logistics, DAMCO, Kotahi, PLH Trucking Company, Ancotrans, and WorldWide Alliance.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In some countries, especially those without a functioning single window platform, there is a prospect of using the core TradeLens platform to implement a national single window as an extension of the platform.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Challenges of adoption in developing countries</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">There are certain prerequisites for adopting the solution in a developing country context. The system can only be introduced in countries that already have some automated IT infrastructure. The reason for this is that TradeLens connects to these electronic systems and integrates them. If automated IT systems are not in place, setting up the entire digitization infrastructure becomes a very difficult task. If an IT infrastructure is in place, then there are also special IT capacities that can support the operation of the TradeLens platform with minimal additional costs. Internet connectivity, data storage, and redundancy in the event of an outage must also be available. In the context of SUNAT, one of the most important prerequisites was the involvement of the actors who have generated the majority of the information required for the TradeLens platform in the past, such as the freight forwarders, customs authorities, and so on. The next step was to ensure that there is an adequate flow of information on the platform, that the resources for the implementation and management of the platform are in place, and that the various actors have the will to do so. So, implementing such a platform requires both resources and commitment to succeed in a development context. It is therefore worthwhile to think about blockchain-based systems as a solution for the digitization of the supply chain only if the relevant players, such as freight forwarders and customs authorities, are willing to do so.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div>\n\n</div></span></span></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:46:33','2026-01-09 12:12:17'),(142,25,'Traceability: Proof in Indonesia','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-177f18e7-7fff-4c93-fef0-61835b6d9a64\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This case study explores how a combination of mobile phones, blockchain technology, and smart tagging has traced fish sustainably caught by fishermen in Indonesia back to UK shops.</span></span></span></span></h3><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Context</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A variety of fishing practices in the fishing industry threaten the well-being of people, wildlife, and the environment around the world. These include human rights violations, overfishing, fraud, and illegal, unreported, and unregulated (IUU) fishing practices. As the Guardian reported after a six-month investigation, in some cases slaves are forced to work for years </span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve; font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">w</span></span><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">ithout pay and under threat of extreme violence in Asia to produce seafood sold by major US, British, and other European retailers. As a result, government agencies such as the U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) have increasingly introduced programs and measures for international fish brokers and importers to create more robust paper trails for fish species vulnerable to IUU fishing and seafood fraud. This traceability is required to identify the origin and social standards of seafood to demonstrate compliance with regulations (e.g., no slavery or no overfishing) and environmental standards such as the Marine Stewardship Council (MSC) fisheries standard. In addition, sustainably caught fish can also justify a price premium in some markets. For example, 72 percent of millennials in the UK are willing to pay more for products from companies that are committed to positive social and environmental impact. Even in the United States, the results of a survey showed that 80 percent of Americans who regularly eat fish think it\'s \"important\" or \"very important\" that the seafood they buy has been caught using sustainable methods. Both from a legal point of view and from a market premium point of view, it is crucial to trace the chain of custody from catch to customer. Several organizations are working to address this traceability issue, including ThisFish.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/25.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 3: ThisFish\'s approach to traceability</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: From the picture on the ThisFish website)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">However, with these systems, the effective interoperability of data along the supply chain represents a major technical challenge. In Figure 3 above: If there are other players in the supply chain, such as a factory to process the fish, the data must be transferred across multiple systems. This is achieved by creating and scanning Quick Response (QR) codes. However, the data capacity of a QR code is limited. The data can also be falsified by any of these actors; for example, some information about the fish can be added or deleted due to commercial attractiveness. Without a trusted database to track the chain of custody, it\'s difficult to determine where the data has been tampered with. A centralized system with a controlling third party is a possible solution. However, a single organization that is supposed to be responsible for ensuring transparency throughout the supply chain is both impractical and risky (unless the only organization is a large retailer/buyer that can instruct upstream partners to adopt a platform). Third parties such as non-governmental organizations (NGOs) or industry associations rarely lead such projects. In addition, a centralized system can become a single vulnerability that would be a vulnerable target for bribery, social engineering, or targeted hacking. The distribution of the costs of setting up and operating the central system is also difficult to determine and agree on.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Concept</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Provenance\'s blockchain solution is an attempt to develop an information system that is shared by all actors in the fisheries supply chain (fishermen, factories, certifiers, and consumers) without them or a third party gaining control of the database. Provenance is building a \"test layer\" on top of the existing systems, such as the open-source platform Tally-O.15. For its pilot project, Provenance tested the platform for a tuna supply chain consisting of three essential parts.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">1. From the sea to the factory:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In order to participate in the supply chain validated by Provenance, fishermen must be certified by local non-governmental organizations. The social and environmental conditions for fishermen are reviewed by NGOs, whose audit systems validate compliance with fishing practices according to an external standard. The fishermen\'s data is entered into the system as blockchain addresses, and their mobile phone numbers are noted. The NGOs certify the fishermen through digital signatures on the Provenance blockchain. The digital certification process is crucial for traceability. With traditional systems, copies of these certificates would have to be physically carried through the supply chain to prove compliance. By including these certificates in a digital platform, these records can be tracked using a reference number. These certificates can also be transferred via digital platforms without blockchain. However, a blockchain platform provides the assurance that these certificates have not been artificially inserted into the system in the later stages of the supply chain. There are several methods to track the fish to the first nautical mile (from the sea to the factory).Some methods involve attaching an RFID tag to the fish (with the information being entered into the blockchain at each stage) before converting it into a QR code during packaging. However, the process can be costly and complex if the whole fish is cut up and distributed in packages. Provenance uses other platforms, such as ThisFish\'s method, which involves attaching plastic tags to the tuna\'s loins to provide an ID to the physical product. As part of the provenance concept, the certified fishermen then send simple SMS messages to register their catch on the blockchain. Together with the unique IDs, the digital register is then transmitted to the supplier along with the catch. The supplier enters their entry into the blockchain (and adds other details such as weight and type) and passes the catch to the factory with the unique ID. Since the data is entered into the blockchain, the identity of the fisherman and the supplier is forever stored in the list of previous owners. The following illustrates the process (Figure 4) and interfaces (Figure 5):</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a37378bc-7fff-54eb-e877-10f8130ad6c8\"></span></span></p><div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/26.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-609cb3d3-7fff-8fa5-9b41-76d541d5ec3a\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 4: Case study on Provenance: From the sea to the factory</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: www.provenance.org)</span></span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/27.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-aa3093f0-7fff-c764-3bd1-390b9fd49e08\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 5: Provenance Case Study: Interface</span></span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; background-color: transparent;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: www.provenance.org)</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2. From factory to shop or restaurant:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><div style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Once the product reaches the factory, it goes through a series of processing steps (Figure 6). The employee in the factory registers the fish in the factory\'s IT system. The factory\'s IT system already uses software such as Tally-O (which does not work with blockchain). However, the Tally-O platforms are not able to collect data if the interfaces change, so there is a possibility that the newly entered data can be falsified. Provenance\'s blockchain layer via Tally-O ensures that the fish\'s history (including the journey from the certified fisherman to the factory and beyond) is tamper-proof as the product travels from one platform to another.</span></span></div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/28.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 6: From factory to shop</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: www.provenance.org)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Once the fish is processed and registered, it can be converted into either canned or packaged form. Each conversion is recorded on the blockchain. Tally-O uses mass balancing techniques to account for the number of constituents used in the conversion. So, if a single fish is used to fill multiple cans, the ID of the fish for each can is recorded, but with the exact description of how the fish was divided among the different cans. Once the conversion is complete, the identification string is encoded in a label in the form of a QR code and placed on the physical product. This product is then exported and transported through the supply chain.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-bf915133-7fff-58c2-d50b-1a685b949e63\"></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-58f75674-7fff-8ad2-5ef0-dc301e933f06\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">3. From the store/restaurant to the consumer:</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b><br></b></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b><br></b></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><b><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/29.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></b></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b><br></b></span></font></div><span style=\"\" id=\"docs-internal-guid-47ef4936-7fff-d778-9d59-0b21cc5e0c86\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 7: From factory to business</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: </span></span></span></span></span><a href=\"http://www.provenance.org\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; color: rgb(5, 99, 193); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">www.provenance.org</span></span></span></span></span></a><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">At the point of sale (supermarket, fishmonger, or restaurant), the label on the fish packaging can be read with a smartphone to inform the consumer of the entire journey of the fish. Figure 7 above shows the process, and Figure 8 below shows the user interface.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/30.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-13cc08b6-7fff-1f4c-49c9-9105f2c5c77a\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 8: In-store/Restaurant User Interface</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: www.provenance.org)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Implementation experience</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Provenance conducted a pilot project on successful fish tracking in Indonesia between January and June 2016 and reported on the following challenges:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">1. Provenance uses a public blockchain. This is to ensure that—unlike consortium blockchains—new players can be included without changing the consensus mechanism. This also prevents collusion between actors if only a few actors have access to the blockchain\'s nodes and ensures that supply chain data remains open source without being linked to a proprietary system. However, public blockchains tend to be slower, less scalable, more costly to run, and offer fewer privacy options compared to a consortium blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2. Provenance acknowledges that the QR codes and NFC (Near Field Communication) stickers used to link products to digital assets are easy to duplicate. Therefore, if at any point in the supply chain another fish is entered into the system with the duplicated QR code, the validity of the physical product connected to the blockchain will be undermined without it being shown in the register. Provenance stated that it is working on technologies (such as advanced NFC tags) that are very difficult to replicate. Provenance is not willing to publish information about who runs the nodes of their blockchain, about their consensus mechanism (which could theoretically address the aforementioned Challenge 2), or about the cost of the system, as they consider such information to be proprietary and confidential.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Resonance and outlook</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The pilot project has not led to mass adoption in the Indonesian fishing industry. However, the managing director of Provenance explains that it has paved the way for many initiatives in this area. According to Provenance, they now work in the European fishing industry, and their approach has been adopted by more than 10 companies, including Unilever, Sainsbury\'s, and Co-op, which offer many other types of food.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Challenges in adopting the state of development</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Since the platform is based on a public blockchain, scaling the solution comes at a significant financial outlay. This is due to the high costs associated with registering individual fishermen as addresses on the blockchain. In addition, it is difficult to convince the various actors in the fisheries ecosystem to use and maintain a distributed ledger. Therefore, scaling such a platform beyond high-value fishing seems far-fetched at this point. Some of these challenges can be offset when several large buyers join forces to introduce the technology into their supply chains. A similar process is being used in other food industries, where a coalition of ten founding partners of suppliers and retailers, including Walmart, Kroger, Wegmans, Tyson Foods, Driscoll\'s, Nestlé, Unilever, Danone, McCormick, and Dole, have joined forces to build a blockchain network that is compatible with each other and brings the entire ecosystem togethe</span>r.</span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div>\n\n</div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></div></span></span></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:50:07','2026-01-09 12:15:09');
INSERT INTO `subsections` VALUES (143,25,'Trade finance: Absa Group (Barclays Africa) and Wave','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f471dea-7fff-f32e-4cd6-ec4e7815ff5b\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This case study examines how Absa Group (formerly Barclays Africa) and Wave (a blockchain startup) conducted one of the first trade finance transactions using blockchain technology by facilitating a transfer between an Irish dairy cooperative and the Seychelles Trading Company. This case study is based on input from senior executives of Absa Group and the CEO of Wave.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Context</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Trade finance typically involves exchanging documents back and forth throughout the supply chain. Figure 9 below shows an example of a traditional trade finance process (simplified). The largely paper-based process takes several days and is associated with several challenges. These include:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Costs incurred by manual work (filling out the forms and routing them throughout the process)</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Risk of human error</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Risk of fraud due to verification issues</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Risk of delays in processing</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Cost and time delays caused by sending and receiving documents across multiple countries</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Environmental</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 36pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Digitizing trade finance is an attractive proposition to reduce costs and save time. However, as trade takes place across multiple national legal systems, it is difficult for countries and their stakeholders to agree on a single central platform for data processing. This is mainly because stakeholders are unable to resolve issues related to data ownership, storage, protection, and other aspects of data governance. Blockchain offers a solution that can potentially mitigate these challenges. Because blockchain solutions are decentralized and thus no central authority controls the process, they can reduce the barriers to entry to digitize commerce caused by the challenges mentioned above. Essentially, blockchain solutions could work in a similar way to paper-based transactions (where documents move through the supply chain), but with an added layer of trust made possible by digital signatures and ledger tamper-proofing. Absa, Barclays Group, and Wave recognized the opportunities of emerging blockchain technology and launched a pilot project in 2016 to test this hypothesis. The aim was to reduce costs, time, and risk of fraud and to achieve efficiency gains.</span></span></span></span></p><div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/31.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-c2d91134-7fff-2ecd-9e78-b7613e87db59\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 9: Traditional trade finance process</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Nathan Associates, Absa Bank Report, WEF Report, BCG Report)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Concept</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In the initial phase of the pilot, Wave developed a blockchain-enabled technology platform to digitize paper-based documents and allow different entities to provide a digital signature that can be verified by recipients. While digital signatures are common in many business transactions, the blockchain component allowed each transaction to be tokenized (hashed) and entered into the blockchain (the ledger is distributed among the various stakeholders), informing document holders of each step of the process flow for a given transaction. The pilot project only included the digitization of Actions 5 to 13 in Figure 9, primarily the digitization of the bill of lading and the forms for conflicts of interest. For the pilot, Absa, Barclays, and Wave used a permissionless blockchain ledger (created by a fork of the Bitcoin blockchain). However, only the participants who acted as the various nodes of the blockchain had access to the ledger. The blockchain has been kept permissionless to ensure that new participants can download the Wave app and act as a blockchain node without needing any permissions. Figure 10 illustrates the concept.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/32.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-c0eb6326-7fff-b963-c505-edba7676abb5\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 10: Absa Wave Blockchain Conceptual Flow</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Absa Group)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Steps to Execute a Trade Finance Transaction via the Wave Platform</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The process involved installing the Wave application on each party\'s computers. The Wave application is used as a standalone application that does not require integration with the stakeholders\' current systems. The application works like an email application because the documents and files are sent on a peer-to-peer basis. The general process involves the carrier issuing a bill of lading and sending it to Wave in PDF format. This PDF replaces the paper documents, and Wave makes it possible to add an electronic signature and annotations to the document as if it were a paper waybill. The carrier digitally signs the electronic waybill document (eB/L) and sends it to the exporter via Wave, as shown in Figure 10. The ownership and note chains are created in the blockchain and visible on the corresponding documents. So, Wave helps with both the transfer of digitally signed documents from one party to another (and the corresponding verification) and the tracking and notification of stakeholders via the blockchain. So, this process mimics the path of paper transactions, but in a decentralized digital format.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Privacy and security</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Data (documents such as eB/L) are like an e-mail that is held individually by each participant. Wave simply acts as an application, like Microsoft Outlook or other email platforms that provide an interface. In terms of the blockchain ledger, it only contains information about the documents—not the actual data—for each transaction, including who owns the documents or has the rights to them. Therefore, no separate data protection functions are activated in the system. Since the document transfer is done peer-to-peer and sensitive data is not accessible on the blockchain, no separate data protection measures are required.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Data verification</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">With the technology, it is not possible to prevent the incorrect entry of data. However, because each document is digitally signed and verified, and the flow of documents can be tracked on the blockchain, accountability increases. However, in such a case, ex-post audits are necessary to detect these scams in order to reduce the risk of fraud in the long term.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Need to integrate with legacy systems</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Because the version used is a standalone application, there is no need to integrate with existing IT infrastructure (reducing primary implementation costs and challenges). On the other hand, the user will have to use two applications. Integration tools are planned for future versions. If the application needs to be integrated into the legacy system, the question of data protection arises again. In terms of interoperability with other systems, the various players in the industry would need to consolidate their data structures to avoid \"technology silos\" and create a global trade finance supply chain network.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Implementation experience</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In 2016, Absa selected and successfully executed a blockchain trade finance transaction of nearly $100,000 in cheese and butter between Irish agricultural food cooperative Ornua (formerly Irish Dairy Board) and Seychelles Trading Company.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Implementation phases</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">After internal discussions, Absa and Barclays contacted the two companies and gave an overview of the pilot, after which both customers agreed to participate. The two banks also approached other participants in the process, such as the transport company Kuehne + Nagel and the customs and tax authorities in Seychelles. Originally, the entire transaction process was to be handled digitally, but as the project managers approached the start, the head of customs in Seychelles resigned, so this part of the supply chain had to be handled on paper. Implementation did not touch on many regulatory issues, except for whether the bill of lading system at the end of customs should be electronic or paper-based. All participants took part in some test runs before the actual pilot project. Once the decision was made in favor of the carrier (Kuehne + Nagel) and approval was obtained, the date and time for the transaction were determined from a legal, regulatory, and customs perspective. The first attempt was delayed, but the second attempt was successful, and much was reported about it.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Timeline for implementation</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The timeframe for setting up such a platform for a trading network can range from 2 to 8 months, depending on what the internal governance looks like and whether all parties involved are on board with data protection and cybersecurity. Absa Group and Wave executives believe it would take even longer if they were to seek specific integration with the banks\' back-office system. The current strategy of the Wave team is to work with banks so that they are familiar with the benefits of the platform before embarking on a major integration. While the platform\'s benefits are reaped by all stakeholders in the trade finance ecosystem (including importers, exporters, and their respective banks), banks are in the best position to implement this solution for the benefit of their customers.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Implementation costs</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The costs incurred by the team (Absa and Wave) in the proof-of-concept phase only concerned travel and accommodation costs in the Seychelles. The cost of the actual pilot project was around R50,000 (US$3,500).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Challenges for the administration</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The biggest challenge for most banks in implementing blockchain is that it needs to be scalable and must be accepted and adopted across the industry. The focus of this pilot project was primarily on the bill of lading, and while the carrier was happy to participate in this particular transaction, considerations need to be made to drive adoption among all key players (regulatory support is especially important in the long term) in the supply chain. This is crucial to avoid interruptions in the transaction that would turn the process into a manual process and thus reduce the benefit. Another governance challenge is the compliance requirements of banks. Banks have to comply with a number of regulations and are therefore not structured to adapt to technologies such as blockchain. For example, banks need to enter into complex legal contracts with regulators (e.g., to comply with data protection). Most startups that provide services to these banks using new technologies such as blockchain do not have the necessary legal resources to understand and comply with these contracts. Therefore, some processes need to be accelerated (by using resources to circumvent regulatory hurdles), or the startups need to be legally supported so that implementation can be done in less time.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Skills challenges</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Since the pilot project did not involve any changes to existing processes, the challenges from the end-user\'s point of view were low. Everyone involved understood the features of the Wave platform with minimal to no training (a relatively simple guide with images of the application was provided).</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Technical challenges</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">A basic internet connection is required for implementation, but this was not a major problem in this pilot project either.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Difficulties between banks</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Since the Absa Group was part of the Barclays Group at the time, the exchange of information was easy. Should the pilot be carried out with other banks, it may have been necessary to discuss the governance approach, including internal compliance agreements and other legal issues. However, in terms of technology, the Wave application is independent of the underlying IT platform. The application can be downloaded from any bank, and the trade finance transaction can be processed with different banks at the import and export locations if the appropriate consents are obtained.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Effect</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">According to Absa Group (formerly Barclays Africa) and Wave, the pilot has yielded the following benefits:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Reduce end-to-end processing costs, including issuance process, transmission, notarization, document retention (± $200 in courier fees)</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Reduced the time for continuous processing from ± 10 days to 4 hours, including issuing, notarization, verifying, modifying, sending a copy of eB/L or receiving, locating, sending additional documents</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Reduce the overall risk of end-to-end processing, including zero counterfeits and zero disputes</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Reduce operational complexity and manual intervention in the supply chain and banking segment</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Providing a streamlined customer experience for all parties (e.g., efficient transfer between counterparties and faster back-end processing)</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Provides a fallback in the event that the solution is not adopted (i.e., easy conversion to paper and XML format for SWIFT users)</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The solution received significant support and buy-in from all stakeholders who could recognize the originality of an eB/L (as proof that a live transaction can be processed via the blockchain)</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Resonance and outlook</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The trading business via the blockchain platform received a lot of press attention in 2016, with several articles in leading newspapers reporting on this transaction. In particular, Absa, Barclays, and Wave claimed that it was the first successful trade finance transaction via blockchain. However, acceptance has not gone as planned since 2016. Absa Group says this is largely due to administrative issues created by the split between Barclays and Absa Group, as well as the complexity of getting a large network of individuals and companies to adopt this solution together. Banks are generally still figuring out how to incorporate FinTech into their ecosystem, especially those that use new and emerging technologies, as the regulations involved are often not clear. Other issues, such as legal contracting (as highlighted in the governance challenges), have slowed down implementation with Wave.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Implementation challenges from a development perspective</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This solution requires a basic internet connection, similar to email usage. However, the speed of the transaction depends on the stability and speed of the internet. Developing countries that cannot provide stable internet to the various actors in the supply chain will not be able to successfully implement this solution. Other challenges include management and acceptance by the various actors in the supply chain. Stakeholders need to understand the economic, legal, and security implications as well as the benefits of blockchain. In a developing country, this can be even more difficult if political and bureaucratic institutions are wary of the impact and their procedures are not transparent. For example, government organizations that are corrupt could resist adopting a digital solution that provides greater transparency (even if the solution does not have an immediate impact on the status quo in the short term). In addition, finding support for banking compliance is a challenge for a startup or any medium-sized organization. According to Absa Group, the biggest opportunity for this platform seems to be in the area of supply chain finance if the technology can reduce the costs and risks faced by banks related to the rising costs of regulation and, in particular, financial crime, fraud, and anti-money laundering. This would have to be a joint effort by regulators, banks, and FinTech companies.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Trade Portal: Singapore &amp; Hong Kong</span></span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This case study examines the blockchain-powered data highway proposed by Singapore and Hong Kong, which connects different application areas such as the digitization of trade, trade finance, traceability, and insurance. This case study was prepared based on interviews with the Singapore Customs Authority, press releases, and limited, publicly available data about the project.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Context</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In October 2017, the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) and the Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA) signed an agreement to strengthen fintech cooperation between the two economies and promote fintech development within the region. As part of the agreement, MAS and HKMA committed to working on a cross-border, DLT-based trade finance initiative. The Global Trade Connectivity Network (GTCN) is the joint innovation project that emerged from the cooperation agreement. The main goal is to \"build a data highway using DLT between the National Trade Platform (NTP) in Singapore and the Hong Kong Trade Finance Platform that will make cross-border trade and financing cheaper, safer, and more efficient.\" A joint working committee consisting of the MAS, the HKMA, the NTP office in Singapore, and the Hong Kong Interbank Clearing Limited is leading the project. In the long term, the GTCN is intended to serve as a trading platform that connects various trading functions and ecosystems around the world. GTCN actors see the trade finance project between Singapore and Hong Kong as the first lane of the \"global data highway\" (a platform where trade-related information can be easily shared between different government agencies). A basic assumption of this project is that there will be a proliferation of blockchain platforms around the world and that the GTCN will bring these different platforms together. Therefore, interoperability between different blockchain platforms will be one of the key differentiators of GTCN.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Concept</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">GTCN is currently at a stage where the project is evaluating bids from tech companies, so the scope of the platform is confidential. However, the platform has three general goals:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">1. Build blockchain-powered end-to-end digital connectivity in the international, cross-industry trading ecosystem, collaborate with different trading platforms and participants while maintaining neutrality</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2. Enabling a common view of trustworthy cross-border trade while meeting data privacy and confidentiality requirements, benefiting all participants in the trading ecosystem</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">3. Provide a platform as a basis for the development of innovative commercial applications to facilitate cross-border trade using NTP capabilities</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/33.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9b771663-7fff-14dc-aa96-6cf0ad451dc5\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 11: 1: GTCN Network</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Singapore Customs 2018)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 11 illustrates the overall vision for the GTCN project. According to this vision, there will be direct and indirect participants in the GTCN blockchain. Direct participants include Singapore\'s NTP, Hong Kong\'s Trade Finance Platform, and, in the future, trading platforms of governments of other countries and/or regions as they implement projects. These direct participants would act as permissible nodes of the blockchain. Indirect participants would be non-state actors in the supply chain, such as banks, freight forwarders, insurers, freight companies, ports, and other trading platforms. These indirect participants will access the blockchain nodes through the direct participants. In cases where blockchain networks are already in place between different players in the ecosystem (e.g., trade finance between Barclays and Wave), these networks can be connected to the network through GTCN\'s compatible platform to comply with customs requirements (in accordance with respective state laws) and connect to other networks and entities. The GTCN will also enable the development of commercial third-party applications such as \"track and trace\" and \"validation services\" based on the GTCN network. In general, the GTCN would follow the following basic principles:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Connectivity: A cross-border infrastructure that connects different trading platforms (government or commercial) and allows platform users to exchange data and electronic trading documents with users of other connected platforms.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Open Innovation: A common API toolkit that allows interested parties to develop applications that allow users to interact with the GTCN. These commercial applications would use the connectivity and infrastructure provided by the GTCN to offer additional services, such as double funding checks and end-to-end digital trade finance flows. - Flexibility: Ability to serve multiple application areas (e.g., traceability, trade finance, etc.) within and across industries. The GTCN should be flexible enough to add new features to enable additional applications in later phases.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Scalability: Scalability to connect different trading platforms in the region. Starting from the initial connection between Hong Kong and Singapore, the GTCN should be able to establish connections with other trading platforms and process all interactions with the GTCN accordingly.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Trust: The exchange of data and documents should only be possible in a protected and approved environment to increase trust in the GTCN ecosystem so that stakeholders are ready to carry out digital transactions. The final form of the platform, including decisions on the underlying blockchain technology (e.g., Hyperledger, Ethereum, R3 Corda), will depend on the design agreed upon between the GTCN and the selected provider.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Data standardization</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Data standardization is one of the biggest challenges in realizing the interoperability of automated systems. Companies use several data models/standards to maintain their respective databases, such as Universal Business Language (UBL 2.0), ebXML, and UN/EDIFACT. The NTP platform in Singapore uses an interoperability layer that can be used to translate \"standards into standards.\" The layer allows NTP to interact with different platforms, regardless of the data standard used. The GTCN will most likely use a similar approach to data standardization.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Privacy &amp; Security</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The GTCN team attaches great importance to data protection and security. Therefore, applicants must demonstrate robust privacy and data protection methods to be approved to build the platform. However, the details of this are still confidential.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Experiences with implementation</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The heads of MAS and HKMA signed a Memorandum of Understanding during a workshop at the Singapore FinTech Festival 2017 organized by MAS. The GTCN Joint Working Committee then held intensive discussions with banks in Singapore and Hong Kong to understand the requirements for the development of the system. In early 2018, a call for proposals (RFP) was launched to select a technology provider to build and operate the GTCN. The tender was only made available to those bidders who had signed a non-disclosure agreement. The committee is currently in the evaluation phase for the selection of a provider. At the same time, the parties are working on resolving governance issues related to implementation.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Challenges</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The challenges of implementing the GTCN are similar to those of other blockchain projects, such as governance, technology, regulation, and capacity building. However, the biggest challenge for GTCN is to make the platform relevant. To do this, it is necessary to win over different parties to the idea. One of the challenges in convincing stakeholders is to make them aware of the concept of blockchain and its benefits, and GTCN takes a different approach in this regard. Rather than talking about blockchain as an esoteric concept, GTCN representatives focus on application sharing and explaining the benefits that can be generated by the platform for stakeholders in general, with less emphasis on blockchain. Trade finance was selected as the first project for the launch of the GTCN, although the GTCN has a broader goal, namely the development of a global data highway that can be used for numerous applications.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Resonance and outlook</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The GTCN is expected to be operational in the second quarter of 2019 to coincide with the planned dates for the launch of the trade finance modules on the national trading platform in Singapore and the trade finance platform in Hong Kong.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Challenges of implementation as part of development</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The GTCN provides an opportunity for several developing countries to accelerate their efforts to modernize customs, as developing countries will be able to join the proposed platform and use many of the services and networks already integrated into the platform. Modernizer, each country is at a different stage of readiness to adopt a platform like the GTCN and, in particular, to act as one of the blockchain\'s nodes. Therefore, it is necessary to analyze a country based on several criteria to understand whether it is ready to adopt the GTCN platform. Once the gaps are identified, several cross-border capacity-building projects can be used to fill these gaps and facilitate the digitization of trade.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Insights and experiences</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The case studies in the previous section show both the benefits and challenges of blockchain technology compared to other platforms (e.g., paper-based and centralized solutions). Figure 12 compares blockchain technology to both traditional/paper-based systems and its primary alternative in digitization: a centralized solution operated by a third-party provider.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve; height: auto;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter2/34.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"text-align: justify; max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></span></font><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-84e94f60-7fff-593d-42c8-e47a50635638\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Figure 12: Comparative analysis of traditional systems vs. blockchain vs. best alternative in terms of benefits and costs</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">(Source: Nathan Associates Analysis)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The advantage of blockchain technology is that it reduces transaction time and costs compared to traditional paper-based processes and is much more effective at preventing fraud. However, implementing blockchain comes at a cost and does not provide the same level of privacy as paper-based procedures. When comparing blockchain solutions to a centralized alternative, the central variant is slightly more powerful and perhaps even a bit cheaper but requires the trust of the participants in the central administrator. Participants must be able to rely on the central administrator to be honest (i.e., not tampering with the entries themselves), reliable (i.e., providing redundancies to keep the system running even if some nodes fail), secure (i.e., preventing hacking and tampering with the database), and secure (i.e., preventing hacking and tampering with the database) and that he does not use or query the data without the permission of the users). Hashing transactions ensures that the database is tamper-proof, and since the ledger is distributed, a single entity cannot single-handedly modify the entire database, which is still possible with a centralized solution, even if the database uses the technique of hashing and creating a chain. This leap of faith represents a significant obstacle to stakeholder acceptance when it comes to implementing centralized solutions. Figure 12 compares the challenges of implementing a traditional system, a blockchain solution, and a centralized database solution.</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-81b66715-7fff-f234-1501-5250249d262c\" style=\"\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Given the status quo, there are few barriers to implementation for traditional systems. However, interoperability challenges will continue to increase as trading volumes continue to increase. Digitization, either via blockchain or a centralized cloud solution, will be a difficult undertaking in terms of implementation parameters such as technology, human resources, legal frameworks, and scalability. However, if one decides to go digital, the blockchain solution will become more viable, as stakeholders from different industries and jurisdictions will most likely not agree on a central administrator to manage the entire data flow. For example, with the introduction of the electronic single window (eSW), non-customs authorities fear that a centralized customs system window will take over their tasks (i.e., all authorizations/licenses will be processed automatically in accordance with the rules set out in the ESC) and that they will lose their jobs and functions in the long term. This is a key motivating factor that has led stakeholders across the supply chain to agree on the adoption of blockchain\'s distributed ledger technology in commerce. When examining the specific applications, in addition to the general cost-benefit analysis mentioned above and the implementation challenges, the following factors must be taken into account:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Digitalization of the supply chain</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The main players who need to commit to a blockchain initiative are either the major shipping companies or the customs organizations, as they generate the most data in the system.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">IT management capabilities are required to operate the nodes of a blockchain network. In developing countries, these capacities are usually not available at the customs authorities. Therefore, carriers like Maersk and IT system implementers like IBM need to lead the early stages of implementing and managing blockchain networks.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Trade Finance</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The main players who need to commit to a blockchain initiative are banks (preferably a merger), which are backed by the respective government agencies.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Banking regulations and their impact on start-ups are additional obstacles to consider.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Traceability</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Blockchain solutions can provide confidence in the traceability of goods, which could increase food safety and risk mitigation (e.g., efficiently locating the source of a contamination outbreak in the food supply chain).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Blockchain traceability solutions can be public or private.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Provenance case study in Indonesia was an example of a public network. Public networks can be costly in the early stages due to the cost of registration, especially at the end of the supply chain for raw materials or products, and the cost of maintaining them through consensus mechanisms. The uncertainty of whether the market will bear the costs is a significant obstacle to scaling.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Anheuser-Busch In Bev uses BanQu\'s blockchain platform to monitor the origin of cassava from farmers in Zambia. This is an example of a private blockchain network. In such cases, the supply chain is well-defined and it is easier to bring the different stakeholders together on a single decentralized platform. The champion of such a project would ultimately be the brand or retailer, who would benefit from being able to determine the origin and better predict risks. (Nair, 2018)</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"\"><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Poppins, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div>\n\n\n</div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></div></span></span></div></div></span></span></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 09:56:33','2026-01-09 12:16:05'),(144,25,'Civil identity uPort on the blockchain','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e3d4d303-7fff-cb01-06e4-1bc048c9e66c\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2349999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Challenge</span></span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The United Nations predicts that by 2050, 68% of people will live in urban areas. This mass influx of citizens will put pressure on current government systems and processes. To ensure that cities are well equipped to meet the myriad challenges ahead, more and more cities are taking the step towards \"smart\" cities. Zug, also known as Crypto Valley, aims to explore blockchain-based digital identities to improve access to digital government services while increasing efficiency, data security, and election accessibility.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Rationalization of direct democracy</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In most democracies, citizens are called upon to cast their votes in a few elections, such as presidential, federal, or local elections. The representative elected by them makes political decisions on their behalf. This is called indirect democracy.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Enterprise Ethereum Solution</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Swiss have a direct democracy, where citizens are called to the ballot box about four times a year to vote on a variety of issues that are important to their respective cantons, such as smoking in restaurants, funding museums, and expanding local bus routes. While this is the most democratic government in modern times, it is also a cumbersome, expensive, and time-consuming process.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Zug used uPort, a decentralized identity platform, to create the world\'s first live implementation of a self-governing government identity project on the Ethereum blockchain, together with the City of Zug, the Institute for Financial Services Zug (IFZ) of the Lucerne University of Applied Sciences and Arts, as well as integration service provider TI&amp;M for the platform and Luxoft for the implementation of voting. In the summer of 2017, they launched a pilot program to register resident IDs on the public Ethereum blockchain. Following the pilot program, Zug officially launched the program in November 2017. uPort\'s identity model returns ownership of the identity to the individual by allowing users to register their own identity on Ethereum, send and request credentials, sign transactions, and securely manage keys and data on the open identity system.\n\n</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How it works</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The city of Zug created its own identity on the public Ethereum network, which gave it the ability to sign and verify data. Access to the identity of the city of Zug was delegated to the city clerk, who used his personal uPort identity with specific admin rights.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Experience</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A Zug resident downloaded the uPort ID app from the Apple App Store and created an account. The uPort app generated a unique private key that represented the user\'s identity on their phone, which acted as the user\'s identity agent. The resident had the option to create a backup copy of his private key so that he could regain access to his identity if he lost his phone. With this facility, the resident was given complete control over their identity and all the data associated with it. The resident visited the Zug website to register by scanning a QR code to interact with the Zug e-government platform for the first time. The resident entered his date of birth and passport number on the Zug website. The application was cryptographically signed and sent to the city as an application for a new Zug ID. The resident had to visit the residents\' registration office of the city of Zug within 14 days to verify his information in person. Once confirmed, the city official issued a verifiable ID that included the train ID signed with the city\'s identity. Other public and private organizations could offer services to use the train ID in the user\'s uPort app. Citizens gained access to various services by showing their ZUG ID in the user\'s uPort app, in this case voting on an upcoming festival.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Goals achieved: \"Secure digital interactions between citizens and authorities\"</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">350 registered citizens successfully created a digital ID, which was verified by uPort (deprecated 2021). 70 citizens took part in the vote on the presence of fireworks at an upcoming festival. Users skipped the cumbersome registration process, logged in with their uPort account, voted, and logged out without going to a polling station. It was possible to check who voted without having to rely on intermediaries or an infrastructure to count votes. The pilot has shown that user-driven identities support the modernization of e-voting initiatives, which could save the city millions in personnel and productivity costs.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-7ca94a38-7fff-8944-6c6f-afe6abbceeb7\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><br></p></span>\n\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 10:00:27','2026-01-09 12:17:44'),(145,25,'Smart Dubai','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-61c60845-7fff-fdcf-eacb-7969626f2b80\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Blockchain as a driver for the city of the future</span></span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Smart Dubai wants to make Dubai the happiest city in the world. The participation of all the city\'s stakeholders—residents, visitors, business owners, parents, and families—is the cornerstone of this strategy. To achieve this goal, a wide range of technologies will be used, including blockchain, AI, and IoT, and the focus will be on three strategic pillars: government efficiency, industry creation, and international leadership.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Working with private sector and government partners, Smart Dubai was established to create, ensure, and promote an efficient, seamless, safe, and impactful city experience for residents and visitors. To achieve its strategic pillars, Smart Dubai aims to launch initiatives and develop partnerships that contribute to the dimensions of Smart Economy, Smart Living, Smart Governance, Smart Environment, Smart People, and Smart Mobility.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The goal</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Dubai aims to be the \"first city to work entirely with blockchain\" by 2021. The Dubai Blockchain 2020 mandate, led by the Smart Dubai Office, sets out a roadmap for the adoption of blockchain technology in Dubai. The goals include achieving efficiency through the use of blockchain in 100% of applicable government services, creating and enabling a blockchain ecosystem for start-ups and enterprises, and being a global pioneer by testing cross-border blockchain cases.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Ethereum solution for businesses</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Smart Dubai Office published a call for proposals, and ConsenSys was selected as a partner from the large number of eligible candidates. In just two months of ideation, the team conducted a high-level tech analysis with government agencies, IT teams, and business process owners to define the core requirements and determine the initial use cases: energy, real estate, medical, etc. ConsenSys then conducted an analysis of the core infrastructure requirements needed to support the blockchain mandate. This analysis led to the creation of a Blockchain Platform as a Service Blueprint while also providing an argument for a blockchain-enabled digital identity. As a result, the UAE Pass was developed to integrate with blockchain networks. Finally, ConsenSys built a sandbox environment on Ethereum and hosted a series of 40-60 workshops for agencies to start prototyping and testing.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Results achieved: \"Blockchain platform as a service\"</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">To accelerate and facilitate the prototyping of blockchain solutions, the Blockchain Platform as a Service was created in partnership with Telco Du to give all government entities the freedom to build on a common framework based on their business needs. BPaaS is a fully managed, scalable, secure platform with cost-effective access via a pay-as-you-go model. BPaaS has been officially recognized by the Smart Dubai Office as one of the most important official tools to support the prototyping activities of government agencies.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The Smart City University</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Developed in collaboration with the Dubai Future Foundation, Smart City University is a blockchain-powered decentralized learning platform that supports the development of digital skills. Smart City University aims to increase the percentage of digitally skilled talent in the UAE to 10 percent by 2020 by bypassing the rigid and siloed path of traditional educational institutions. Individuals can create personalized educational pathways, including hands-on work projects, relevant reading materials, conferences, and in-person and online workshops working towards digital certifications.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Paperless strategy</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Smart Dubai goes paperless. Dubai is in the process of digitizing the 1 billion sheets of paper produced each year by digitizing all services, including visa applications, bill payments, and license renewals. These previous records are now securely processed using blockchain technology. (Consensys, N.D.)</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 10:01:13','2026-01-09 12:18:28'),(146,25,'Blockchain in agriculture','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a9781846-7fff-2fd9-97d8-887e1f4ef37d\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The use of blockchain technology in agriculture is increasing, leading to the development of a blockchain-based system in which agricultural activities can be carried out. We selected six start-up companies that have adopted a blockchain-based solution in agriculture as case studies to explore the application and benefits of using blockchain technology. There were no exact criteria for selecting the cases, except that they implemented the blockchain-based solution in agriculture. We collected additional data from internet sources such as trade journals, blogs, news sites, and company websites, as well as from scientific and practical literature on innovation management and the food industry. We focused on information on how blockchain technology has been used to solve various problems in agriculture.</span></span></span></span></h3><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Transactions: This module allows the farmer and stakeholders to easily buy and sell the goods by handling all the components of buying, selling, and logistics. Storage: All information, including payments, orders, deliveries, inventory, and confidential information, is stored digitally in this module.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Relationships: Farmers and customers can use this module to expand their business relationships.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Finance: It allows all financial transactions to be carried out and the transfer of virtual currency (tokens) between farmers and customers.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Bank transfer: Payments made to the farmer are transferred automatically. Blockchain technology has been used to eliminate counterparty risk for sellers through real-time payments, automate and simplify access to supply chain financing for buyers, and ensure that all consumers have access to the origin of their goods to make informed purchasing decisions. The platform records all important data about the cultivation, production, transport, and delivery of products in the cloud and can thus combat food fraud and security in the global supply chain. Farmers are notified of every step, such as when their crop is delivered to a buyer or when invoice payment is completed.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.6.6.1 TE-FOOD</span></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">TE-FOOD is a farm-to-table food traceability system based on a public blockchain, which allows all participants in the supply chain and customers to trace the information about the food. The FoodChain (TE-FOOD\'s blockchain) is a public blockchain that allows supply chain players and consumers to run master nodes to decentralize traceability information. TE-FOOD\'s customers have the opportunity to gain in-depth insights into the food industry\'s supply chain. TFD is the token of TE-ERC20 FOOD, which is primarily used on the Ethereum platform. Its mission is to provide transparency in the food supply chain by monitoring items through the entire supply chain (farm, processor or slaughterhouse, distributor, retailer) and providing customers, supply chain companies, and government agencies with tools to learn about the history and quality of food. TE-FOOD aims to increase consumer trust and brand awareness, gain more knowledge of the supply chain to improve operational efficiency, comply with export regulations, protect their brands from counterfeiting, and conduct product recalls faster. The TE-Food system includes:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Identification tools: These include 1D/2D barcodes/RFID ear tags, security seals, and label stickers.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Traceability tools: They consist of a B2B mobile traceability management app, a web app, a central system, external interfaces, and reporting tools. The retail and consumer tools include a mobile app for B2C fresh produce traceability and a web app, as well as digital signage tools for retail food traceability.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">National solutions for the livestock industry: These include systems for managing and enforcing animal husbandry.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Farm management tools: These tools are based on each category (vaccination, feeding, fertilizer, crop protection products, etc.).</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Food safety tools: These tools include a fraud management system, food condition sensors, and a meat quality visual analysis system. To identify the tracked physical objects (products, locations, etc.), the system uses various identification materials: plastic seals with QR codes, plastic labels with RFID, and paper labels with QR codes.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">For traceability, various client applications are provided: a mobile app used by B2B and customers to scan identification materials and request or enter data, a web app for customers who do not use the mobile app to access product history, an IoT API for food companies that allows them to combine the information obtained from the sensors, and an open interface for supply chain companies that already use software to process product information.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">TE-FOOD offers two implementation models: private or institutional. In the case of private implementation, a system is used to trace one\'s own activities, while in the case of institutional implementation, in the case of public authorities or public institutions, the system is used to trace a group of companies (geographical or sectoral). TE-FOOD includes a complete set of tools and applications required for the entire supply chain to implement food traceability through end-to-end operational visibility and process control.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">TE-FOOD specializes in food traceability and offers unique solutions for the agricultural industry:TE-FOOD is the only traceability solution that offers various services for B2B (business-to-business), B2C (business-to-consumer), and B2A (business-to-authorities) that benefit businesses, consumers, and public authorities.It increases consumer confidence as they are able to trace the origin of the food, including all the processing steps that the product has undergone.Thanks to proper traceability and IoT sensors, contaminated food can be quarantined at an early stage before it reaches the retailer, reducing the number of foodborne illnesses.Regulators have a real-time perspective of the food market, which helps improve the monitoring and enforcement of food safety regulations. One of the limitations of TE-FOOD is that the TFD token running on the Ethereum network has a low transaction rate (15 TPS) that is relatively slow. Likewise, TE-FOOD has to face direct and indirect competition from various competing companies, such as Ambrosus, WABI, MOD, and WTC. TE-FOOD, which has a large number of customers in Hungary and Vietnam, is also struggling to establish itself in the international market.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></font></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.6.6.2 Etherisc</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">It is an open-source development platform that focuses on building decentralized crop insurance applications. Etherisc develops decentralized, blockchain-centric applications for various areas of the insurance industry. Etherisc\'s blockchain solution for crop insurance was successfully tested in Sri Lanka in 2019 in collaboration with Aon and Oxfam to reduce risk and cover it effectively. In November 2020, Etherisc announced that it would partner with Chainlink to offer crop insurance in Kenya, the goal of which is to automatically trigger insurance payouts in the event of extreme weather events. Chainlink\'s crop insurance solution was developed based on Etherisc\'s Ethereum-based \"Generic Insurance Framework,\" which uses local meteorological parameters as input to the smart contract. Chainlink\'s decentralized oracle network provides a secure and reliable end-to-end connection to various external weather data sources and sends the data to the smart contracts of all parties so that they can verify the information independently. In the event of extreme weather events, insurance policies are automatically triggered by the data entered, resulting in fair, timely, and transparent payouts that an insurer cannot manipulate or change. Users can select their agricultural product and the location of their field in the crop insurance application and then apply for insurance by paying an amount in Ether to a so-called DAPP (also known as a \"smart contract\"). In the event of a drought or flood, they receive an automatic, immediate payout. Algorithms in the smart contract automatically check GPS and weather station data depending on the location of the farmer\'s fields, allowing Etherisc to cost-effectively assess risk and contract terms from the start and process claims over time. The insurer saves time and money by eliminating a labor-intensive process. Automation also reduces the risk of human error. This can curb fraud while making the payment of claims more efficient. Since crop insurance is based on blockchain technology, it has a positive impact on agriculture. Instant payments are triggered based on weather data without the need for the farmer to submit an application, eliminating a time-consuming and labor-intensive task that not only makes farming easier but also provides greater transparency. Automatic triggering of insurance policies based on weather data reduces the risk of human error and the risk of human fraud at the time of payout. Some of the challenges and problems faced by the Etherisc crop insurance solution are the basic risk of poorly designed goods, distance between the index measuring point and the actual production field, as well as the size and unpredictability of the covered region, and the risk of manipulation of weather station data used for index calculation to the benefit of the companies involved. The lack of appropriate weather stations and data is hampering the successful implementation of weather-based crop insurance solutions.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">2.6.6.3 AgriLedger</span></span></b></span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">AgriDigital has created a digital title for a physical commodity by developing the token. This token, which represents the physical commodity, remains on the blockchain, which means that anyone can access immutable information, which in turn creates \"digital trust\" between all participants in the supply chain. Agridigital is the first company in the world to perform live settlement of the physical product on the blockchain between a grower and a buyer. The company now has 300 active users and operates in 30 countries. From the successfully completed pilot project, the main benefits of Agridigital for the agricultural industry can be summarized as follows: It offers the opportunity to connect local farmers with the global supply chain. Track real-time data (location, status of assets at a given time) of a grain sale between farmer and buyer for a transparent supply chain. Executing real-time payment processing via a smart contract that helps eliminate counterparty or credit risk for the farmer, which in the Australian grain industry would ideally take two to five weeks to pay.AgriDigital offers its customers comprehensive management of trade flows, access to financing, and traceability of the origin of the goods.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">AgriLedger is a social entrepreneurship initiative for farmers that leverages distributed ledger technology and mobile applications. It is an app built on the R3 blockchain platform Corda that provides all participants in the supply chain with a comprehensive set of integrated services that increase trust among each other. In 2019, AgriLedger launched a blockchain ecosystem for Haitian farmers to increase supply chain transparency and promote fairer pricing for suppliers and retailers. AgriLedger is on a mission to support smallholder farmers by facilitating access to the global market via the mobile platform and financial services via API links with local banks and financial institutions. The application focuses mainly on traceability and payment, which allow the grower to keep ownership until the final sale. Blockchain technology is used for recording and verification, payment and money transfer, digital identity, and smart contract design. AgriLedger is a blockchain-based mobile application designed to simplify supply chain transactions that includes the following features.</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Digital identity: Every actor in the supply chain, including the farmer, receives a unique digital identification number once they create a profile by registering with key information. In this way, every farmer can be identified as an important factor in the supply chain and gain better access to financial, insurance, logistics, and other services.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Digitization of assets: Assets (such as rice or coffee) can be digitized through tokenization, which creates liquidity, facilitates peer-to-peer trading, and increases the value of agricultural commodity markets by participants from all actors in the supply chain.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Immutable data: The information stored in distributed ledger technology is immutable, creating trust, transparency, and traceability throughout the supply chain.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Record keeping and access to financial services: The digital ledger allows for better accounting and proof of income, making it easier for farmers to access financial credit and other financial services.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Digital wallet: The digital wallet makes it easier for the farmer to apply for and receive a direct deposit from the financial institution. Also, by handling financial transactions between buyer and farmer, the farmer can receive payment for their products faster and improve supply chain efficiency.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In this way, Agriledger simplifies farmers\' access to the global market. An example:A farmer from Haiti hands in 500 mangoes to a collection point, where they are counted. These 500 mangoes are registered (digitally) in the name of the farmer in the blockchain (e.g., block 1). The mangoes from the collection point are delivered to Port-au-Prince (Haiti\'s capital) and from there to the USA (let\'s say Block 2). After a week, they arrive in the U.S. (let\'s say block 3), and the next day these mangoes are sold in the supermarket (let\'s say block 4). Here, customers can find out how the mangoes were delivered by scanning the QR code sticker. On the other hand, farmers are notified by SMS when the mangoes have been sold in the target market. With AgriLedger, every farmer, supplier, and agricultural product receives a unique ID or QR code sticker that needs to be processed at every stage of the journey. The person holding the scanner is only allowed to enter data into the distributed ledger, and their ID is recorded every time they do so. In this way, digital information is recorded at every stage of the supply chain that everyone in the chain can trust. With trusted data stored in an immutable distributed ledger, farmers (in Haiti) can make informed decisions, prove their financial stability, and apply for a loan from the bank. Smallholder farmers in poor and developing countries in particular benefit from AgriLedger in several ways. Accurate and verifiable records for farmers that help ensure fair and faster post-sale pay. Reduction of production costs through the sharing of resources and collective purchasing power for products and processes.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Digital identity opens up the possibility for smallholder farmers to access financial services (banking, microfinance, and loans) that can increase farmers\' income by 50% and thus help solve the problem of unbanked farmers. AgriLedger opens the door to smallholder farmers, who find it difficult to access the global agricultural market even at the local level. AgriLedger has a huge economic impact on farmers\' lives. However, AgriLedger also struggles with some issues, such as the security of the farmer\'s private key in case someone has access to it and could make unauthorized transactions. The application is unsuitable for farmers who are illiterate, especially in developing countries. Infrastructure issues such as electricity to charge cell phones, internet access, and network coverage in remote areas.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><br></p><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2.6.6.4 Ripe.io</span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding: 5pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ripe.io, an American company founded in 2017, is engaged in the development of innovative methods for tracking food using blockchain technology through \"Blockchain of Food.\" The \"Blockchain of Food\" is a food tracking network that uses blockchain technology, IoT, AI, and machine learning to provide information about the origin of food, its growing conditions, how it is delivered, and other food data that may be of interest to consumers. Ripe.io is partnering with R3\'s Corda (blockchain platform) to develop its solution to improve transparency and trust in the agricultural food supply chain. ripe.io is currently offered as Software-as-a-Service, but in the long term it will evolve into a fully licensed API and transactional product. The goal of ripe.io is to reconnect the supply chain by telling the story of a product, by promoting transparency along the entire supply chain, and by piecing together the stories of the products along the way. The system consists of a software stack that contains a blockchain on which a hardware solution can feed and upload data as needed, resulting in a sensor-controlled Internet of Food. The system provides an architecture for collecting data in the food supply chain, recording the data on a blockchain ledger, sharing it with others in the supply chain, and validating the data while maintaining privacy and security. Blockchain technology is used to facilitate the exchange of information with all actors in the supply chain, thus validating the quality of food as it moves through the chain. With the help of blockchain and IoT, it was possible to monitor all aspects, such as temperature, humidity, and color, and store the data digitally and securely. A sensor or set of sensors collects data on a number of variables that are believed to be important to the respective actor at each step of the product lifecycle. The collected data is automatically uploaded to the blockchain without human intervention, eliminating the risk of human error. The data is available in real time and can be accessed via a mobile application or via the desktop. The data collected by various sensors over the life of the product and uploaded to the blockchain, which includes a history of the circumstances the product has encountered, can be analyzed and shared as needed to improve the entire supply chain. The primary impact of ripe.io in the agricultural industry can be summarized as follows:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Empowering customers by giving them access to information about the origin and production conditions of the harvest.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Relief for farmers, as they can record and monitor information such as temperature, humidity, light, and pH from the sensors, which are important for high-quality crop production.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The quality level of the harvest is recorded and can be accessed by all stakeholders in the supply chain to ensure food safety.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Ripe.io has set itself the goal of reconnecting the supply chain through the use of blockchain technology and IoT sensors and faces some challenges in the process, such as:</span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Performance issues, as IoT devices that continuously stream data could cause performance issues, as the throughput of the blockchain is limited due to its complex cryptographic security protocol.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Lack of trust and adoption of blockchain technology, as it is very new and not yet mature.</span></span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Problems with the interoperability of legacy systems with the new blockchain technology, which cause additional costs and expertise.</span></span></span></span></p></li></ul><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div><h4 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.235; margin-top: 2pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">2.6.6.5 AgUnity</span></span></span></span></h4><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">AgUnity is a blockchain-based smartphone app that helps smallholder farmers plan, trade, and track their daily transactions. It is built on a multichain blockchain platform that connects farmers with buyers, increasing transparency and providing them with the money they need to succeed in a global marketplace. AgUnity aims to improve the economic situation of farmers and their overall bargaining position through the use of blockchain and smartphone solutions, thus reducing food waste and farmers\' inefficiency. So far, AgUnity has launched two pilot projects in Kenya and Bougainville. The AgUnity mobile app focuses on six key features.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Planning: It helps farmers determine when crops are ready for harvest or when equipment is needed. It also makes it easier for cooperatives to exchange information and plan.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Traceability: Records every step in the supply chain and traces it back to the farmer. Buyers pay a premium for quality assurance and ethical traceability, which can increase the value of the crop by more than 50%.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Processing: Increases confidence in every stage of the process from field to market, as they gain real-time visibility into how their goods are processed or sold.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Transfer: Replace the paper records with secure phone-to-phone transactions with QR codes stored on the blockchain to avoid misunderstandings and discrepancies.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Market: Introduces farmers to the various agricultural markets where they can buy high-value products such as multi-purpose solar kits.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">Wallet: Serves as a microfinance system for farmers. The payments from the harvest sales end up in farmers\' wallets almost instantly, allowing them to withdraw money from the cooperative or make purchases via the app. Farmers are provided with mobile phones that come pre-installed with AgUnity software, ensuring that they are using program-compatible technology and secure devices when accessing the AgUnity blockchain.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">In remote regions, the app can also work without an internet connection until one is established. The app, with a customizable pictographic interface, allows the integration of different crop species and cultural features into the platform. Using a blockchain makes it easier to convey to farmers that if both parties agree to a transaction, no one, including the farmer, the cooperative, or even AgUnity, can change the records.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">This property of the blockchain also provides an additional layer of protection to ensure that these transactions are not hacked by third parties who want to transfer receipts from farmers to themselves. Farmers receive a free smartphone that loads the AgUnity application, which helps farmers become more effective through planning and collaboration, among other basic applications such as Google Maps, YouTube, and Facebook. Designed specifically for farmers with low literacy skills, these phones have a simple interface that does not allow farmers to download any other applications to the phone. The farmer retains ownership of all the data he collects with the application. The farmer logs in to the application to track the processing and sale of the crop. All members can view the transactions and thus ensure that all parties adhere to the agreements. Each farmer is assigned a digital wallet where the receipts are stored, which are then converted into cash at the cooperative. Farmers can also communicate about crop planning and device sharing through AgUnity\'s encrypted messaging services. It was observed that farmers in Kenya were able to increase their income by three times in one season with the AgUnity application, which enables collaboration and trust.</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The key benefits of AgUnity implementation can be highlighted as follows:</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-montserrat), Montserrat, sans-serif;\">The smartphones provided to farmers with built-in applications play an important role in storing and maintaining immutable records that enable trust between all stakeholders.The instant debit of payments to farmers\' wallets, which can be used for purchases, allows easy access to larger agricultural markets.Paperless transactions based on the blockchain reduce the risk of fraud and discrepancies. (Bhusal, 2021)</span></span></span></span></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n\n</div></div></div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-10 10:02:54','2026-01-09 12:19:20'),(147,26,'What is a crypto wallet?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-396a8094-7fff-8663-915f-aa7d602786ea\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Contrary to popular belief, crypto wallets do not contain physical coins; they store cryptographic keys (private/public keys) that control blockchain balances.</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Instead, they store the public and private keys needed to buy cryptocurrencies and provide digital signatures that authorize each transaction. There are different types of crypto wallets, including physical devices, software, and even paper. Which crypto wallet is best for you depends entirely on your individual trading needs.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cryptocurrency wallets store users\' public and private keys and provide a user-friendly interface for managing cryptocurrency balances. They also support cryptocurrency transfers via the blockchain. Some wallets even allow users to perform certain actions with their cryptocurrencies, such as buying and selling or interacting with decentralized applications (dapps). It is important to remember that cryptocurrency transactions are not \"sending\" crypto tokens from one person\'s mobile phone to someone else\'s mobile phone. When sending tokens, a user\'s private key signs the transaction and sends it to the blockchain network. The network then takes the transaction into account to reflect the updated balance in both the sender\'s and recipient\'s addresses. So, the term \"wallet\" is a bit misleading, as crypto wallets don\'t store cryptocurrencies in the same way that physical wallets store cash. Instead, they read the public ledger to show the balance of a user\'s addresses and contain the private keys that allow the user to make transactions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Not sure what a public or private key is?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A key is a long string of random, unpredictable characters. While a public key is like an account number and can be widely shared, the private key is like a password or PIN for a bank account and should be kept secret. In public-key cryptography, each public key is paired with a corresponding private key. Together, they are used to encrypt and decrypt data.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter3/1.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\">\n</span></span><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-39aaec00-7fff-317a-09d8-869d775ca6e0\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 1: Public and Private Key</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: crypto.com)</span>\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Why is a crypto wallet needed?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A user\'s cryptocurrency is only as secure as the method they use to store it. Although cryptocurrencies can technically be stored directly on an exchange, it is not advisable to do so unless they are small amounts or with the intention of trading frequently. For larger amounts, it is recommended to transfer the majority to a crypto wallet, whether it is a hot wallet or a cold wallet. This way, they retain ownership of their private keys and have full power and control over their own finances.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How do cryptocurrency wallets work?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As mentioned earlier, a wallet doesn\'t technically contain a user\'s coins. Instead, it contains the key to the coins stored on public blockchain networks. In order to carry out various transactions, a user must verify their address with a private key consisting of a series of specific codes. The speed and security often depend on the type of wallet a user owns.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h3><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span>\n</span></span></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:12:36','2025-10-09 07:00:11'),(148,26,'Different Types of Crypto Wallets','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a61664c7-7fff-fc64-2d36-0b0c3d64f131\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">There are two main types of crypto wallets: software-based hot wallets and physical cold wallets. Read on to learn more about the different types of cryptocurrency wallets and to find out which ones might be the most suitable.</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Hot and Cold Wallets—What\'s the Difference?\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter3/2.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 2: Hot and Cold Wallet Comparison</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: crypto.com)</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Hot Wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The main difference between hot wallets and cold wallets is whether they are connected to the internet. Hot wallets are connected to the internet, while cold wallets are kept offline. This means that the funds stored in hot wallets are more accessible, and therefore hackers can get to them more easily.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Examples of hot wallets include:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 59.349999999999994pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Web-based wallets</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 59.349999999999994pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Mobile wallets</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 59.349999999999994pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Desktop Wallets</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">With hot wallets, the private keys are stored and encrypted in the app itself, which is kept online. Using a hot wallet can be risky because computer networks have hidden vulnerabilities that can be exploited by hackers or malware programs to enter the system. Storing large amounts of cryptocurrencies in a hot wallet is a fundamentally poor security practice, but the risks can be mitigated by using a hot wallet with stronger encryption or by using devices that store private keys in a secure environment.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">There are various reasons why a market participant might want their cryptocurrency holdings to be either connected to the internet or disconnected from the internet. For this reason, it is not uncommon for cryptocurrency holders to own multiple cryptocurrency wallets, including both hot and cold wallets.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Cold Wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">As explained at the beginning of this section, a cold wallet is completely offline. Cold wallets are not as convenient as hot wallets, but they are much more secure. An example of a physical medium used for \"cold\" storage is a piece of paper or an engraved piece of metal.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Examples of cold wallets include:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 59.349999999999994pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Paper wallets</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 59.349999999999994pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Hardware wallets</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">What is a paper wallet?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">A paper wallet is a physical place where the private and public keys are written down or printed. In many ways, this is more secure than storing funds in a hot wallet because hackers have no way to remotely access these keys, which are protected from phishing attacks. On the other hand, there is a risk that the piece of paper will be destroyed or lost, which can lead to the funds being irretrievably lost.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">What is a hardware wallet?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">A hardware wallet is an external accessory (usually a USB or Bluetooth device) that stores a user\'s keys, who can sign a transaction only by pressing a physical button on the device, which malicious actors cannot control. Cryptocurrencies that do not need to be accessed immediately are best stored offline in a cold wallet. However, users should note that securing their assets is entirely their own responsibility—they must ensure that they do not lose them or get them stolen.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Tip: To increase security, you should separate the public and private keys, store them offline, and store the physical wallet in a safe deposit box.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Hot Wallets vs. Cold Wallets: Which Is Better?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Both storage methods have advantages and disadvantages, and the decision depends on the user\'s preferences. For example:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">For day-to-day trading, accessibility is paramount, which means that a hot wallet may be worth considering. However, if you want to store a large amount of crypto assets and value security over convenience, you should consider a cold wallet.\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Custodial and non-custodial wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">In addition to the wallets mentioned above, wallets can be further divided into custodial and non-custodial wallet types.\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter3/3.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-c20242cc-7fff-1dbd-9898-7deaaa1ad66c\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\" id=\"docs-internal-guid-3b394774-7fff-8c32-d31f-cd7cf8641203\"></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\" id=\"docs-internal-guid-271b5044-7fff-86b2-d8a9-1017561f1120\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 3: Comparison of custodial and non-custodial wallet</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: crypto.com)</span>\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Custodial Wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Most web-based crypto wallets are custodial wallets. These wallets are usually offered on cryptocurrency exchanges and are known for their convenience and ease of use, and they are especially popular with beginners and experienced day traders. The main difference between custodial wallets and the above types is that users no longer have full control over their tokens, and the private keys needed to sign transactions are only held by the exchange. This means that users must trust that the service provider will keep their tokens safe and take strict security measures to prevent unauthorized access. These measures include two-factor authentication (2FA), email verification, and biometric authentication, for example, through facial recognition or fingerprint verification. Many exchanges will not let a user transact until these security measures are properly set up.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Crypto exchanges and custodial wallet providers also usually take other measures to ensure the security of users\' tokens. For example, some of the funds are usually transferred to the company\'s cold wallet, which is safe from online attackers.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Crypto.com has taken numerous measures to ensure the protection of client funds. After rigorous security audits by a team of cybersecurity and compliance experts, Crypto.com is the first crypto company in the world to achieve ISO/IEC 27701:2019, ISO22301:2019, ISO27001:2013, and PCI:DSS 3.2.1, Level 1 compliance and has been independently assessed on Tier 4, the highest level for NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy Frameworks, as well as Service Organization Control (SOC) 2 compliance. In addition, the company has insurance coverage for customer funds totaling $360 million.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Non-Custodial Wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">With non-custodial wallets, on the other hand, the user retains full control over their money, as the private key is stored locally with the user. When launching a non-custodial wallet, the user is asked to write down and securely store a list of 12 randomly generated words, which are referred to as a \"recovery,\" \"seed,\" or \"mnemonic\" phrase. The user\'s public and private keys can be generated from this phrase. This serves as a backup or restore mechanism in case the user loses access to their device. Anyone who has the seed phrase can gain full control over the funds in the wallet. If the seed phrase is lost, the user also loses access to their funds. It is therefore imperative to keep the mnemonic phrase in a safe place and not store a digital copy of it anywhere. Do not print them on a public printer or take a photo of them. Note that hardware wallets are non-custodial in nature, as the private keys are stored on the device itself. There are also software-based non-custodial wallets, such as the Crypto.com DeFi Wallet. The common denominator is that the private keys and the funds are completely under the control of the user. As a popular saying in the crypto community goes, \"Not your keys, not your coins!\" Conversely, this means that users themselves must be responsible for their own security in terms of storing passwords and seed phrases. If these are lost, recovery can be difficult or impossible because they are usually not stored on a third-party server.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-760dc4bd-7fff-0689-048b-9f97f866f476\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Custodial Wallets vs. Non-Custodial Wallets: Which Are Better?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Custodial wallets and non-custodial wallets have various advantages and disadvantages that make them suitable for different types of users: For those who tend to lose passwords and devices, it makes sense to use a custodial wallet, as an exchange or custodian is likely to have better security practices and backup options. For this reason, it is a popular option for beginners who have little to no experience in crypto trading. In addition, the transaction fees at a custodian bank are usually cheaper or even free. However, if you prefer to keep full control of your own money, you should consider a non-custodial wallet. Ultimately, it\'s all a matter of personal choice.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">For added security: multi-signature wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Multi-signature wallets—or </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">multisig </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">wallets—require two or more private key signatures to authorize transactions. This solution is useful for a number of use cases: a person using a multisig wallet can prevent them from losing access to the entire wallet if a key is lost. For example, if a user loses a key, there are still two other keys that can sign transactions. Multisig wallets can prevent the misuse of funds and fraud, making them a good option for hedge funds, exchanges, and corporations. Since every authorized person has a key and a majority of keys are required for a signature, it becomes impossible for any person to unilaterally carry out unauthorized transactions. For all wallet types described above, there are multisig versions—multisig hot wallets, cold wallets, hardware wallets, etc.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">NFT wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">An NFT wallet is a secure place where non-fungible tokens (NFTs) are stored. There are two main options for NFT wallets: hardware wallets or software-based wallets.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">A look at an NFT wallet: What to consider?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Which NFT wallet is right for you depends on a number of factors, including the user\'s experience and security requirements, as well as the type of tokens they want to store. Here are some things to consider when choosing an NFT wallet:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: -3.8pt; padding-left: 3.25pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Compatibility with NFT marketplaces—The user needs a wallet that integrates with the NFT marketplaces they want to buy from.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: -3.8pt; padding-left: 3.25pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Strong security features—may include two-factor authentication (2FA), email verification, or biometric authentication.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: -3.8pt; padding-left: 3.25pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">User-friendly interface—A good NFT wallet should have a streamlined user interface and be easy to set up.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: -3.8pt; padding-left: 3.25pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Accessibility on multiple devices—Most NFT wallets are available through web extensions or as mobile/desktop applications. For more convenience, take a look at a wallet that is available on multiple devices and can synchronize transactions in real time.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: -3.8pt; padding-left: 3.25pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Cross-chain compatibility—Most wallets support Ethereum-based tokens; however, those who want to mint, buy, and sell tokens on other networks need a wallet with cross-chain compatibility. Popular hardware wallets include devices from Ledger and Trezor. However, since NFTs are not natively supported by any of these wallets, users will need to connect their hardware wallet to a hot wallet that can store and manage NFTs. For a complete solution, we recommend the Crypto.com DeFi Wallet, which is widely regarded as one of the most trusted and secure wallets for storing NFTs and was voted the best NFT wallet of 2022 by TradingPlatforms.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">More about Crypto.com DeFi Wallet</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The Crypto.com DeFi wallet is non-custodial, which means that users retain full control over their private keys and assets. Available on Android and iOS, the DeFi wallet allows users to manage more than 700 tokens on more than 20 blockchains and send cryptocurrencies to anyone with their preferred confirmation speed and network fee. In addition, the dedicated wallet supports NFTs on Ethereum, Cronos, and Crypto.org Chain and allows users to easily view the top collections with the NFT Spotlight feature. Users can also use the wallet to earn passive income by locking up cryptocurrencies such as CRO, USDC, and DOT. Crypto.com users can now manage their NFTs through the Crypto.com app.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Conclusion</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Result</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">When it comes to crypto wallets, there is no perfect solution. Each type of wallet has different strengths, purposes, and trade-offs. It\'s up to the user to weigh up what works best for them: for those with a high risk tolerance who want to make online payments regularly and quickly, the convenience of a hot wallet, such as the Crypto.com app, might be the most suitable. But for those who are a little more risk-averse and want to hold their coins for the long term, a secure offline device, such as a hardware wallet, might make the most sense. The final decision is in the hands of the user, with Crypto.com DeFi\'s non-custodial wallets being one of many secure options. Since storing large amounts of coins in a single wallet is quite risky, a combination of cold and hot wallets is usually ideal and can help find the right balance between convenience and security.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">(What Is a Crypto Wallet?, 2022)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span>\n</div></span></span></div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:15:54','2025-10-08 09:30:09'),(150,26,'Why do you need to protect your crypto wallet?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-18175009-7fff-0589-ceb6-d7772412ef5c\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Now that we know the different types of crypto wallets, let\'s understand why it\'s so important to protect them:</span></span></span></h3><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The LastPass incident:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> In October 2023, hackers stole about $4.4 million from 25 LastPass vault app users. They exploited vulnerabilities affecting 80–85 different wallets. Even well-known wallet providers can fall victim to security breaches, highlighting the need for robust security measures.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br><br></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">BitForge vulnerabilities:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Crucial wallet providers, including Coinbase, Binance, and ZenGo, were vulnerable to a series of cryptographic protocol flaws, collectively referred to as \"BitForge.\" These flaws allowed attackers to gain access to complete private keys, putting users\' funds at risk. Continuous security updates and patches are critical.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br><br></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The MetaMask incident:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> On April 19, 2023, MetaMask users suffered a major hack resulting in the loss of millions of dollars. No wallet is completely immune to threats; security is ultimately in the user’s hands.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br><br></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Phishing attacks:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Cybercriminals trick crypto owners into revealing private information. For example, Dominic Lacovone lost $650,000 when scammers accessed his iCloud account, where his MetaMask recovery phrase was stored.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br><br></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:12pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Vulnerable key management systems:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Wallets storing mnemonics insecurely can be exploited. In the 2022 Slope wallet hack, stored mnemonic keys were stolen, resulting in over $4 million in customer losses.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br><br></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Updated and Precise Examples:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Slope Wallet Hack (Aug 2, 2022):</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Mnemonics stored in logs allowed attackers to drain ≈$4.1M from thousands of Solana addresses. Postmortems are available from CertiK and HackMD.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br><br></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">LastPass Breach (Oct 25, 2023):</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Attackers used prior breach data to steal ≈$4.4M from ~25 users in a single day. Sources: CoinDesk, BleepingComputer, Merkle Science.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br><br></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:12pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">BitForge Disclosures (2023):</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Research exposed vulnerabilities in some MPC implementations across multiple providers, emphasizing the importance of continuous cryptographic auditing. Sources: Fireblocks, Bitdefender.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><br><br></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">When it comes to protecting your digital assets, knowing wallet security is paramount. Implementing robust measures can be the difference between keeping your assets safe and falling victim to threats.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:-7pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How to protect crypto wallets? Let\'s understand how to ensure the security of your crypto wallet.\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter3/4.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Table 1: Security measures for the crypto wallet at a glance</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: Sharma, Types Of Crypto Wallets Explained [UPDATED], 2023)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Hardware wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Hardware wallets are the gold standard for cryptocurrency security. These are physical devices designed to keep your private keys offline, making them virtually immune to online threats. Brands like Ledger and Trezor offer top-notch security with a user-friendly interface.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:-3pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Two-factor authentication (2FA)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Enabling 2FA further protects your crypto wallet. Not only will you need to enter your password, but you will also need to enter a unique code from your mobile device to log in. This double-check system helps prevent unauthorized access.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Multi-signature wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Multi-signature wallets (multi-sig) require multiple private keys to authorize a transaction. They are ideal for shared or business accounts because they ensure that there is no single point of failure.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Secure passwords</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Using strong, unique passwords for each wallet is fundamental. Password managers like LastPass can generate and store complex passwords, reducing the risk of unauthorized access.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Securing the Seed Phrase</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Never underestimate the importance of your seed phrase. Store it safely offline because it\'s your recovery key. The division into two secure storage locations provides additional protection.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cold Storage</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">When you store your assets in a \"cold wallet,\" they are not connected to the internet and thus protected from online attacks. A classic example is paper wallets, which offer offline security.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">VPN for additional shielding</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Using a VPN (Virtual Private Network) when accessing your crypto wallet provides encryption for your online activities. It disguises your location and protects you from possible prying eyes on public networks.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Multiple wallets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">If you spread your assets across multiple wallets, you spread your risk. If a wallet has problems, your other assets will remain safe, which reduces potential losses.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trusted Sources</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Only obtain hardware wallets from reputable vendors or official sources. Avoid third-party vendors to minimize the risk of compromised devices.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Safe environment</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Using a secure, malware-free device and avoiding risky actions such as installing unknown applications or clicking on suspicious links will keep your wallet environment safe. You can choose the type of crypto wallets according to your needs, but remember to back them up regularly and use the latest software. (Sharma, 2023)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-95a59f5a-7fff-0ce7-8a21-a7707901d448\"></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:19:16','2025-10-08 09:31:03'),(151,26,'Are cryptocurrency wallets safe?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b92b163f-7fff-d12e-377e-195ecd15c27e\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Wallets are secure to varying degrees. The level of security depends on the type of wallet you use (desktop, mobile, online, paper, or hardware) and the service provider. Hardware wallets combined with secure seed backups are generally the safest option for retail users, while custodial exchanges carry counterparty risk. A web server is inherently a riskier environment for storing your currency compared to an offline environment. Online wallets expose users to possible vulnerabilities in the wallet platform that can be exploited by hackers to steal your money. Offline wallets, on the other hand, cannot be hacked because they are not connected to an online network and do not rely on a third party for security. Although online wallets have proven to be the most vulnerable to hacking, careful security precautions must be taken and followed when using each wallet. Keep in mind that if you lose your private keys, no matter what wallet you use, you\'ll lose your money. If your wallet is hacked or you send money to a scammer, there is no way to reclaim lost money or reverse the transaction. You need to take precautions and be very attentive! Secure your wallet. Keep only small amounts of currency for everyday use online, on your computer or mobile phone, and keep the majority of your money in a highly secure environment. Cold or offline storage options for backups, such as Ledger Nano X, paper, or USB, protect you from computer failures and allow you to recover your wallet in the event of loss or theft. However, it does not protect you from eager hackers. Indeed, when you choose an online wallet, there are inherent risks that you can\'t always protect yourself against. Update your software. Keep your software up to date so you have the latest security improvements. Not only should you update your wallet software regularly, but you should also update the software on your computer or phone. Add additional layers of security. The more layers of security, the better. Setting long and complex passwords and ensuring that every withdrawal of funds requires a password is a good place to start. Use wallets that have a good reputation and offer additional layers of security, such as two-factor authentication and additional PIN code requirements every time you open a wallet application. You should also consider a wallet that offers multisig transactions, such as Armory or Copay. A multisig, or multisignature, wallet requires the consent of one or more other users before a transaction can be made.</span></span></span></h3><div><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Multi-currency or single use?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Although Bitcoin is by far the most well-known and popular digital currency, hundreds of new cryptocurrencies (so-called altcoins) have emerged, each with its own ecosystem and infrastructure. If you want to use a variety of cryptocurrencies, the good news is that you don\'t have to set up a separate wallet for each currency. Instead of using a cryptocurrency wallet that only supports a single currency, it can be more convenient to set up a multi-currency wallet that allows you to use multiple currencies through the same wallet.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Are there any transaction fees?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">In general, transaction fees are only a tiny fraction of traditional bank fees. Sometimes, certain types of transactions require fees to be paid to the network\'s miners, while some transactions do not incur any fees at all. It is also possible to set your own fee. As a guideline, an average transaction size of 226 bytes will incur a fee of 18,080 satoshis, or $0.12. If you set a low fee, there may be times when your transaction gets a low priority and you have to wait hours or even days for the transaction to be confirmed. If you want to complete your transaction and have it confirmed immediately, you may need to increase the amount you are willing to pay. Regardless of which wallet you end up using, you shouldn\'t worry about transaction fees. You either pay very low transaction fees, choose your own fees, or pay no fees at all. A clear improvement compared to the past!</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Are cryptocurrency wallets anonymous?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Somehow, yes, but not really. Wallets have a pseudonymity. While wallets are not tied to a user\'s actual identity, all transactions are publicly and permanently stored on the blockchain. Your name or personal address won\'t be there, but data like your wallet address can be linked to your identity in a variety of ways. While there are efforts to simplify anonymity and privacy, complete anonymity also has its obvious drawbacks. Check out the DarkWallet project, which aims to improve privacy and anonymity through stealth addresses and coin mixing.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Which cryptocurrency wallet is the best?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">There is an ever-growing list of options. However, before you choose a wallet, you should consider how you want to use it. Do you need a wallet for everyday purchases or just to buy and hold the digital currency for an investment? Are you planning to use multiple currencies or a single currency? Do you want to access your digital wallet from anywhere or just from home? Take some time to determine your needs, then choose the wallet that works best for you.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:20:20','2025-10-08 09:31:50'),(152,26,'Pros and Cons of Individual Wallets','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-7a28dae0-7fff-c960-e8cb-fe0a5fc6fc9e\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Atomic Wallet</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Atomic Wallet is a new non-custodial multi-asset solution for the secure storage and management of BTC, ETH, XLM, XRP, LTC, and over 300 other coins and tokens. The crypto assets and features are updated regularly. The private keys are securely encrypted on the user\'s device, giving you full control over your funds. The desktop app is available for Windows, macOS, Ubuntu, Debian, and Fedora. Private alpha versions of the mobile apps for Android and iOS will be released in October 2018. An Atomic wallet is a secure, all-in-one cryptocurrency storage without custody with a smooth and comprehensive interface. The wallet supports Atomic Swaps, a state-of-the-art feature that helps users save significantly on fees. Atomic Wallet also allows users to buy cryptocurrencies with USD and EUR and exchange their assets at the best rates via Changelly or ShapeShift.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros: Convenient interface, optimal privacy and security, decentralized, multi-currency, custody-free, built-in exchange, accepted bank cards, 24/7 support.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons: Not all coins support Atomic Swaps yet</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Bread Wallet</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A Bread Wallet is a simple mobile digital Bitcoin wallet that makes sending Bitcoins as easy as sending an email. The wallet can be downloaded from the App Store or Google Play. Bread wallets offer a standalone client, so there is no need to use a server when sending or receiving bitcoins. This means that users can access their money at any time and have full control. All in all, the clean interface, sleek design, and drive to constantly improve security make Bread Wallet a safe and fast application that is a pleasure for both beginners and experienced users.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros: Good privacy and security, beginner-friendly, simple and clean, open-source software (freeware), free.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons: No web or desktop interface, lack of features, hot wallet.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Mycelium</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Advanced users looking for a mobile digital Bitcoin wallet should look no further than Mycelium. Mycelium\'s mobile wallet allows iPhone and Android users to send and receive bitcoins and maintain complete control over the bitcoins. No third party can freeze or lose your funds! With enterprise-grade security that is superior to most other apps and features like cold storage and encrypted PDF backups, a built-in QR code scanner, a local commerce marketplace, and secure chat, among others, you can understand why Mycelium has long been considered one of the best wallets on the market.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Good data protection, advanced security, feature-rich, open-source software, free</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> No web or desktop interface, hot wallet, not suitable for beginners</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt