e for those who need a multi-currency wallet.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Good privacy and security, multiple currencies, multi-platform wallet linking, great user support, feature-rich, user-friendly, free.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The code is not open source; loading can be slow.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Armory</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Armory is an open-source Bitcoin desktop wallet that\'s perfect for experienced users who value security. Armory\'s features include cold storage, multi-signature transactions, one-time printable backups, a multi-wallet interface, GPU-resistant wallet encryption, key import, key sweeping, and more. Although it takes a while to understand Armory and reach its full potential, it\'s a great option for tech-savvy users who want to keep their funds safe.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Good privacy, great security features, multi-signature options, solid cold storage options, free.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Only accessible via the desktop client, not suitable for beginners.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trezor</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trezor is a hardware Bitcoin wallet that is ideal for storing large amounts of Bitcoins. Trezor cannot be infected with malware and never reveals your private keys, making it as secure as traditional fiat money. Trezor is open source and transparent, with all technical decisions benefiting from wider community consultation. It\'s easy to use, has an intuitive interface, and is Windows, OS X, and Linux compatible. One of the few drawbacks of the Trezor wallet is that you have to carry it with you to send bitcoins. Therefore, Trezor is best suited for inactive savers, investors, or people who want to keep large amounts of Bitcoin very safe.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Good security and privacy, cold storage, simple web interface, built-in screen, open-source software, beginner-friendly.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cost $99; it is a must to send bitcoins</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Ledger Nano</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Ledger Wallet Nano X is a new hierarchical deterministic multisig hardware wallet for Bitcoin users that aims to eliminate a range of attack vectors by using a second layer of security. However, this tech-heavy description doesn\'t mean much to the average consumer, which is why I\'m going to explain it in plain language by describing what makes the Ledger Wallet Nano tick. In terms of hardware, the Ledger Wallet Nano is a compact USB device based on a smart card. It\'s about the size of a small flash drive, measuring 39 x 13 x 4 mm (1.53 x 0.51 x 0.16 inches) and weighing just 5.9 g.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Screen/device protected by swivel metal cover, multi-currency support, third-party apps can run on the device, U2F support, when restoring a wallet from seed, the whole process can be done from the device without having to connect it to a computer, pretty inexpensive (~$65 USD)</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Not-so-advanced wallet software (no transaction labeling, no ability to create hidden accounts, no password manager)</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Green Address</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Green Address is an easy-to-use Bitcoin wallet that is an excellent choice for beginners. Green Address can be used via desktop, online, or mobile, with apps available for Chrome, iOS, and Android. Features include multi-signature addresses and two-factor authentications for greater security, securing the wallet on paper, and instant confirmation of transactions. One downside is that Green Address has to approve all payments, so you don\'t have full control over your spending.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">High security, multiple platforms and devices, multi-sig, beginner-friendly, open-source software, free.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Hot wallet, average data protection, the third party has to approve payments.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain.info/Blockchain.com</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Blockchain.com (formerly Blockchain.info) is one of the most popular Bitcoin wallets. This wallet can be accessed from any browser or smartphone. Blockchain.info offers two different additional levels. For the browser version, users can enable two-factor authentication, while mobile users can enable a PIN code request every time they open the wallet application. Although your wallet is stored online and all transactions must go through the company\'s servers, Blockchain.info does not have access to your private keys. Overall, it is an established company that is trusted in the Bitcoin community and is a solid wallet for storing your currency.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pros: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Good security, easy-to-use web and mobile interface, well-known and trustworthy company, beginner-friendly, free.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cons:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Hot wallet, weak privacy, third-party trust required, outages (Rosic, 2020)</span></span></span></p></li></ul></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:21:14','2025-10-08 09:32:40'),(153,26,'How do crypto exchanges work?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-ed3f4d9d-7fff-79b6-927f-e36e4d13eccd\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Crypto exchanges are marketplaces where you can buy, sell, and trade cryptocurrencies. They act as digital platforms connecting buyers and sellers, enabling trading of a wide range of digital assets. If you want to dive into the world of cryptocurrencies, a crypto exchange is key.</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Custody Considerations: Centralized exchanges act as custodians for user funds. Note: misuse or misplacement of a customer’s assets often results in the complete loss of user funds. A major example is the FTX collapse in November 2022, which involved misused customer funds and led to high-profile legal proceedings (Investopedia, ABC News).</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Good practice when using exchanges includes checking custody arrangements, account segregation, and proof-of-reserves before depositing large sums. Choosing exchanges with segregated accounts can help mitigate bankruptcy risk.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What is a crypto exchange?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A crypto exchange is an online platform where you can buy and sell cryptocurrencies. The platform acts as an intermediary in transactions, allowing users to exchange various fiat currencies (e.g., U.S. dollars), Bitcoin, or altcoins (such as Cardano and Dogecoin). For example, you can use a crypto exchange to exchange one type of cryptocurrency for another or fiat currencies for cryptocurrencies. Another option is to exchange your cryptocurrency for fiat currency.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How do crypto exchanges work?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Crypto exchanges work similarly to exchanges for other types of assets, such as a securities exchange. In other words, the exchange matches buyers with sellers. Before you can start trading cryptocurrencies, you will need to register and fund your account. From there, you can create different order types to buy or sell cryptocurrencies, or even speculate on them. These orders are then compiled in what is known as an order book, which lists the amounts of cryptocurrencies that users want to buy and sell, as well as the desired price. Based on this information, the buyer and seller pairs are matched by the exchange.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Decentralized vs. centralized crypto exchanges</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">There are two main types of cryptocurrency exchanges, and it is important to understand the differences when choosing a crypto exchange. The most common type is a centralized crypto exchange that is supervised by a third party that is responsible for overseeing the platform and ensuring that transactions run smoothly. While these exchange operators can facilitate the buying and selling of cryptocurrencies, they also come at a price—usually, centralized crypto exchanges charge an additional fee to the exchange operator. Examples of popular centralized crypto exchanges include Binance, Coinbase, Kraken, Gemini, and Crypto.com.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A decentralized crypto exchange (DEX), on the other hand, does not have a central figure to oversee transactions on the platform. Instead, the platform relies on blockchain technology or distributed ledgers, and transactions are processed by</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Peer-to-peer trading is handled directly between users. These exchanges, which are generally less common than their centralized counterparts, tend to be a bit more difficult to use and require more technological know-how and knowledge of cryptocurrencies. Also, there is no central authority to turn to if a problem arises. Examples of popular decentralized exchanges include KLAYswap, Uniswap, dYdX, and PancakeSwap.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:21:59','2025-10-08 09:33:14'),(155,26,'Companies invest in cryptocurrencies','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-ea98b1ee-7fff-7ac5-14c2-b92d6186b714\"><h1 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></h1><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Guidance and considerations for companies on the allocation of digital assets</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">More and more companies have started investing cash in digital assets and cryptocurrencies. This is a new dynamic and a departure from the conventional investments of funds or similar in this area. How would Strategy (formerly his guide) help? You will find the relevant questions, processes, and procedures for making such a decision. Some companies actively provide cash for digital assets. We saw the first meaningful examples of this dynamic in 2020, which continues despite the volatility and turbulence in the markets. An early example was Strategy (formerly MicroStrategy Inc.). In 2020, the company announced that it had bought more than $1 billion worth of Bitcoin and acquired even more in the years that followed. The strategy described this as an investment that \"offers the opportunity to achieve better returns and preserve the value of our capital compared to holding cash for a longer period of time.\" Some companies have followed suit, and others may now be wondering how to invest in Bitcoin and other digital assets. There are a variety of reasons for adding digital assets to a company\'s balance sheet, whether it is the pursuit of asymmetric risk return, as seen in recent years, or as a natural hedge against fluctuating fiat currencies, whether as part of a corporate strategy that relies on modern, open technologies, or as a complement to an operating strategy, which provides for the acceptance of digital assets as a means of payment. This document largely focuses on Bitcoin investing, as companies have recently invested more in Bitcoin and it is widely used as a store of value. It should be noted that there are numerous types of digital assets, each with its own unique characteristics. Ether (ETH) is also considered a store of value, with the added benefit of enabling transactions in Ethereum-based decentralized applications. These are in contrast to central bank digital currencies (CBDCs) and stablecoins, which are digital representations of fiat currencies. Their value is derived from the actual currency in circulation, and in the case of CBDCs, they are issued by a central bank. Stock and derivative tokens are digital assets whose value may represent actual company shares or a legal claim to another asset or financial instrument. Some digital assets have additional attributes, such as voting rights in a protocol, or they can provide an access layer for participating in a decentralized application. These can bring some commercial or economic benefit to the holder. Before investing in a digital asset, it is important to understand the specific terms and characteristics of the investment, as these affect accounting, taxes, risks, controls, and legal considerations, among others. Therefore, below are some pointers on the basics of a company\'s decision to invest in digital assets such as Bitcoin. In addition, we outline the ongoing actions that teams in an organization should take to monitor and drive a long-term investment. In other words, our goal is to answer the question \"How would you do this?\" and not \"Why do you do this?\" Before we continue, we want to make one thing clear: there is no manual or infallible approach to this kind of courageous action. There is only conscientious effort, disciplined analysis, new thinking and rethinking, dedicated collaboration between the individual departments, and, above all, rigorous implementation. So what follows is not a step-by-step recipe but rather a guided tour of the vast terrain that companies can traverse when considering investing in Bitcoin. Given the many variables and different characteristics of digital assets, the provisions set out in this guide are not necessarily relevant or applicable to all digital assets. Nonetheless, the general methods and considerations outlined here can be applied to several investment scenarios of companies in selected digital assets.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The high-level view of a company\'s finance department</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In general, the main purpose of the treasury function is to manage risk and preserve capital. When deciding on and executing digital assets for investment and operational purposes, digital asset governance risk can be key to all activities. Governance involves not only creating a policy but also understanding the types of investments the company makes and placing this alternative investment vehicle—digital assets like Bitcoin—in the broader investment strategy. Executives should also be familiar with the specifics and nature of the investment vehicle (more on this below in the discussion on controls). Since this is a financial investment, it is important that the Chief Financial Officer, CRO, CEO, CTO, CFO, and Board of Directors have a clear assessment and understanding of the risk profile of the investment and the company\'s risk tolerance, and how these two factors may match or diverge from each other. Ultimately, governance is about monitoring and ensuring that the frameworks and requirements set by the organization are met. Risk tolerance may need to be adjusted regularly depending on the stake and type of digital asset. Risk tolerance can take different forms and requires decisions on questions such as, \"What percentage of cash on hand is used for alternative investments in digital assets after accounting for operating costs?\" What risk margin is acceptable for the company? Managing risk is rarely a matter of \"setting and forgetting.\" Risk is an ever-moving target, and adjustments within an agreed range of risk tolerance may need to be made frequently. When it comes to digital assets, finance should consider not only the investment side but also how these assets can be incorporated into day-to-day operations such as payments, debt management, fundraising, IPOs, etc. There are other important considerations that a finance leader should make when incorporating digital assets into the company\'s business operations. Understanding the underlying functions associated with certain digital assets is important to effectively use and deploy the asset\'s full potential while establishing a robust control structure to ensure proper use. Control and storage are often essential elements for an organization, whether it wants to self-manage assets (self-custody), hire a third-party provider, or take a hybrid approach. With the decision on retention, a company can determine its risk to the counterparty, as each option affects control and ownership of the assets. The collapses of some digital asset banks and exchanges have highlighted the importance of understanding the risks held on external platforms and in institutions. The importance of risk management also applies to the management of digital assets spread across multiple wallets, exchanges, and custodians.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">With the emerging technologies, a holistic view is likely needed to help an organization verify its positions and liquidity across its wallets and exchanges, as the asset is volatile compared to traditional fiat money. New technologies and vendors have emerged that focus on reporting, management, transaction activity, and digital asset usage within a single platform. Several vendors have developed integrations with leading treasury management systems to enable real-time visibility into liquidity and reporting to support the treasury function. Finance departments using digital assets should have a risk assessment framework in place to identify where risks exist, how the assets are managed, and whether the system has adequate controls in place. The following points highlight the key factors that companies should consider when managing their finances:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Overall purpose, function and type of use of digital assets (payments, investments, stakes, etc.)</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Establishing internal and external controls that comply with specific digital asset policies to properly manage digital assets across all lines of business</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Ability to integrate digital assets into key treasury operations to meet the company\'s goals and strategy</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How can finance use these assets more strategically to increase efficiency in payroll, paying suppliers, trading, interacting with customers, and cross-border transactions with subsidiaries and others?</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A first and final principle for finance should be that digital asset management is a vibrant and adaptable process. It can and should constantly adapt to market, regulatory, and risk reality.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Custody raises a number of important questions. Will the company hold the asset on its own, or will it rely on third-party providers? While self-custody provides easy access to assets, it also comes with additional risks related to accidental loss, transaction authorization, and transaction monitoring and recording. Given the complexity and risk associated with self-custody, more and more companies are turning to external custodians. Then it is a matter of evaluating the strengths and weaknesses of the various custody processes and procedures. If a company chooses to store its digital assets with an exchange or custodian, it is appropriate to carefully consider numerous potential risk issues and questions. These include, but are not limited to:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How does the external exchange or custodian secure the material of the private keys?</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Can the company trust the accuracy of the third-party account statements?</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What plans are in place in the event that custody services are discontinued?</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How does the stock market deal with market anomalies, such as flash crashes?</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What is the provider\'s hard fork policy in supporting new digital assets?</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What happens if private keys and passwords are lost or stolen?</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A good way to address these potential issues is to obtain and review SOC 1 and/or SOC 2 reports from potential exchanges or custodians.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Conclusion:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Monitoring regulatory and normative changes while refocusing for success</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As the market events and ongoing discussions on regulation and standard-setting enliven the digital asset ecosystem, it is imperative that companies investing in these digital assets dedicate the resources, time, and attention to monitoring the evolving situation. At the same time, they should continue to address the necessary transformation of their organization so that when new regulations and standards are announced, they are able to understand their implications and implement their rules. Any major investment in digital assets raises more than just technical or regulatory issues related to finance, accounting, reporting, taxes, and controls. It is also about a significant cultural realignment—internal and external—between the many different groups and departments, including but not limited to the Board of Directors, the Audit Committee, Risk, Corporate Reporting, Finance, Taxation, Internal Audit, Operations, Controls, Technology, and Investor Relations. Since many of these departments interact with external parties, such as the external auditor, tax and legal advisors, etc., it is essential to realign the mindset accordingly when dealing with these external groups. What does this realignment look like? Usually, the various functions and departments of a company establish procedures and assumptions for collaboration inside and outside the company, based on normal, well-functioning transactions. The terrain of digital assets is still a new frontier of possibilities, so it is necessary for each corporate department and its external partners to rethink the application of the rules and guidelines of their core competency and to be guided by current and expected rules and standards when they are announced. Only a few of the norms associated with old investments in securities, fiat currencies, or treasuries can be applied. Once each group has gained a certain level of familiarity with the application of the evolving rules and standards to digital assets, they should actively listen to each other, gain an understanding of the sensitivities, assess any operational or technical dependencies, and finally reconsider how they work together and address the challenges together. Many more companies are starting to evaluate the potential benefits of investing in digital assets like Bitcoin. The more experience they gain and the more interest they generate, the more likely it becomes that strategic investments in digital assets will become routine. However, companies should have the right risk measures and tolerance in place to make these types of investments worthwhile. The circumstances faced by companies that want to invest in such investments are complex and constantly changing. However, with the right commitment from all departments and external parties, they can be mastered. And with proper attention to rules and standards, as well as processes, procedures, and risks across the decision-making spectrum, digital investments can offer innovative, bold, and dynamic alternatives to traditional investments. (Deloitte, n.d.)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-10 12:23:36','2025-10-08 09:33:43'),(156,27,'Overview of the Swiss Financial Market','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-113a3856-7fff-5209-c12f-0b87227ef445\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Switzerland is world-famous not only for its banking but also for property insurance and reinsurance, commodity trading, and trade finance. The Swiss financial market plays an important role in supporting the national economy and includes the following financial market segments:</span></span></span></h3><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Swiss market for fixed-income securities (bonds)</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Swiss derivatives market</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Swiss options and futures market</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Swiss market for foreign investments</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Swiss foreign exchange market</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Swiss investment fund market</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Each segment can be assigned to either a trading or exchange system, a clearing and settlement system, or a payment system that deals with the payment of trades. The SIX Swiss Exchange is an important securities settlement organization that organizes, oversees, operates, and regulates key components of the Swiss capital market. The shares traded on the SIX Swiss Exchange are mainly held in the accounts of domestic and international investors in Switzerland. Bonds, exchange-traded funds (ETFs), exchange-traded structured funds (ETSFs), and other investment funds are also traded on the SIX Swiss Exchange platform. The SMI, or Swiss Market Index, is the main index of the SIX Swiss Exchange.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:25:30','2025-10-08 09:34:17'),(157,27,'Business Environment','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-51b850d4-7fff-cd97-b110-4c1c1bd1610c\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 12.5pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Securities Dealers</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Securities dealers are those who fall under the criteria defined in the Stock Exchange Act and deal with securities and other directly related transactions. All domestic and foreign securities dealers must obtain a license from FINMA in accordance with the Stock Exchange Act. If the securities dealers are banks, they must also comply with the Banking Act. Only after receiving the license can the legal entity be entered in the commercial register and start working as a securities trader. In order to obtain a license, the applicant must provide FINMA with proof that the following points have been met. Compliance with the conditions regarding corporate documentation, structure and organization of the company, management, and the required information on certain shareholders and persons in key positions. The detailed criteria for granting a license and the provisions governing business conduct are set out in the Stock Exchange Act.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Asset managers and financial intermediaries</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Asset managers </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">This type of financial sector enjoys a very liberal regulatory and market framework, as it does not fall under either the Banking Act or the Stock Exchange Act. The portfolio manager can be represented by any type of legal entity that manages its clients\' funds. Asset managers are subject to the Anti-Money Laundering Act (AMLA). This provision is intended to ensure the quality of the capital invested in the transaction. In addition, the Swiss Bankers Association provides banks with the \"Due Diligence Agreement\" and has introduced the \"Guidelines for Asset Management\" for the exercise of asset management mandates.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Financial intermediaries </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Financial intermediaries are legal and natural persons who receive funds on a professional basis. Both can either be self-regulated and a member of a recognized Swiss self-regulatory organization or report directly to FINMA. Organizations that are neither regulated nor self-regulated must obtain a license from the Federal Anti-Money Laundering Control Authority for their activities.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Legislation on collective investment schemes</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Swiss investment law defines an investment fund as a pool of assets raised by investors through a public offering for the purpose of joint investment. The fund is managed by a fund management company that looks after the interests of investors according to the principle of risk distribution. Open-ended collective investment schemes are funds established on a contractual basis or an investment company with variable capital (SICAV). A closed-ended collective investment scheme is a limited partnership for collective investment schemes or an investment company with fixed capital (SICAF). The investment funds are supervised by FINMA and must comply with the legal framework of the Collective Investment Schemes Act (CISA), the Collective Investment Schemes Ordinance (CISO), and the Ordinance of the Federal Banking Commission on Collective Investment Schemes (CISO-SFBC). The CISA has been brought into line with the new EU funds directive UCITS (Undertakings for Collective Investments in Transferable Securities) and contains basic regulations aimed at protecting investors by ensuring the transparency and functioning of the market. However, the CISO and the CISO-SFBC were created to issue more detailed investment regulations.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:26:07','2025-10-08 09:34:46'),(158,27,'Corporate structures in Switzerland','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-bb810fce-7fff-7e1b-dc92-5bb8a877baf6\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Switzerland offers a highly competitive and innovative business environment, making it an excellent testing market for all types of businesses. The economic freedom guaranteed in the Swiss constitution allows anyone, including foreigners, to run, set up, or participate in a business. However, foreign nationals must have both a work and residence permit to run a business personally or permanently. Swiss law distinguishes between two types of companies, which are clearly defined:</span></span></span></h3><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Corporations:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Public limited companies and limited liability companies</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Partnerships: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">limited partnership, general partnership and sole proprietorship</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Legal entities are regulated by the Civil Code or the Swiss Code of Obligations. At the federal level, legal entities have their registered office in a specific canton where the commercial register is kept. Anyone who operates a trade, manufacturing, or other trade must be registered in the relevant commercial register. The register is a public document. Before you decide on a type of company, you should carefully consider the following factors:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Amount and source of required capital</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Risk and liability issues</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Management and Legal Restrictions</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Tax treatment</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Social Security Expectations and Insurance Requirements</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Public limited company</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A public limited company, hereinafter referred to as an SA/AG, is a legal entity that functions as a corporation similar to the US corporation and the British public limited company. It is founded by at least one natural or legal person with a registered share capital and its own company name. Shareholders\' liability is limited to the amount of the subscribed share capital. The SA/AG is often chosen by foreign companies as the legal form for Swiss subsidiaries because it is suitable for large companies and small to medium-sized businesses. This legal form can be considered the most widespread among Swiss companies. The shareholders of the SA/AG enjoy the right of anonymity. Requirements for incorporation:The SA/AG must be entered in the commercial register. A minimum share capital of CHF 100,000 is required. Of this, at least 50% of the share capital should be paid in at the time of incorporation. The share capital can be divided into bearer or registered shares with a minimum nominal value of CHF 0.01. Bearer shares must be fully paid up and transferred by assignment or, if certificates are issued, by physical delivery. Registered shares must be endorsed, and the transfer of registered shares must be entered in the company\'s share register. A contribution in kind is subject to a special report by the founders, which must be confirmed by the auditors. There are no requirements for the nationality or residence of the directors, but at least one person with individual signing authority must be legally resident in Switzerland. Alternatively, it is possible to have two Swiss residents with a double signature. The incorporation is completed with the entry of the company in the commercial register.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Taxation: The SA/AG is subject to certain taxes. Corporate income tax is levied at both the federal and cantonal levels, while capital tax is levied only at the cantonal level. Total income tax is based on worldwide income and can vary from 12% to 26% on pre-tax profits, depending on the canton and municipality of residence. The capital tax is about 0.3% to 0.6% of net assets. Withholding tax is levied on dividends and interest. Stamp duties are usually levied on capital at incorporation if equity exceeds CHF 1 million. Depending on the activities carried out and the turnover achieved, VAT is due. Double taxation treaties and tax exemptions are possible.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Accounting &amp; Audit: Swiss law requires that annual financial statements, including balance sheets and profit and loss accounts with annexes, be prepared annually in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles in Switzerland. The company\'s accounting can be done according to any internationally recognized standard (Swiss GAAP/FER, IFRS, or US GAAP) and in any currency. For tax purposes, the annual financial statements must be prepared in accordance with Swiss law (CO) and in Swiss francs. In the case of unlisted companies, the financial statements are only submitted to the tax authorities and are not disclosed. Consolidation of subsidiaries\' financial statements is required if two of the following criteria are met in two consecutive financial years:</span></span></span></p></li><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Total assets: CHF 10 million</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Total sales: CHF 20 million</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">An average headcount of 200 employees over the year</span></span></span></p></li></ul></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The requirements for the audit depend on the activities, the accounting, and the number of employees. The complete audit requirements apply to companies if they are obliged to prepare consolidated financial statements, are listed on the stock exchange, or if two of the following three figures are exceeded in two consecutive financial years:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Total assets: CHF 10 million</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Total sales: CHF 20 million</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">An average headcount of 50 or more employees during the year</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In the case of a full audit, the auditor must also confirm the existence of an internal control system established in accordance with the specifications of the Board of Directors in relation to the preparation of the annual report. Companies that are not subject to ordinary auditing in accordance with the criteria of Art. 727 CO are generally subject to a limited audit. In the case of a limited audit, the auditor gains less certainty than in the case of an ordinary audit. The auditor\'s certificate is therefore less binding than for an ordinary audit. Small companies that are not subject to full scrutiny can opt out with the consent of all shareholders, implying that no scrutiny is required. This is possible if fewer than 10 full-time employees are employed in the company on an annual average.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Limited Liability Company</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The limited liability company, hereinafter referred to as a limited liability company, is a corporation with its own legal personality. This form of company is an alternative to the SA/AG, as it has similar costs and founding modalities. Both forms require the signing of a public deed of incorporation by all founders. The liability of the shareholders is limited to the share capital. Recently, the share of the Sàrl/GmbH companies has increased thanks to the lower structural and capital costs compared to the SA/AG, and thus its profitability for small and medium-sized enterprises. In contrast to a stock corporation, however, it is subject to stricter disclosure requirements.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Requirements for incorporation: The limited liability company must be registered in the Commercial Register. The share capital of the company must be at least CHF 20,000 and must not exceed CHF 2 million. At least 50% of the share capital must be paid in cash or in kind by each of the partners when the company is founded. Each shareholder participates in the share capital in the form of one or more par value quotas with a nominal value of at least CHF 100. All members and all capital contributions or changes must be reported to the Commercial Registry annually. Bearer shares are not permitted. Residents of Switzerland must be able to represent the company in a legally binding manner. Taxation, Accounting, and Audit: The tax, bookkeeping, and audit procedures are identical to the AG/SA.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">General partnership</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The general partnership is a personal association of at least two natural persons, which usually pursues an economic purpose and operates as a commercial business. Legal entities cannot join a general partnership because it does not have legal personality. It is founded and managed on the basis of a partnership agreement that stipulates a strict non-competition clause for all partners. The partners are liable for all debts of the company, which means that all partners are subsidiarily, personally, and jointly and severally liable. A minimum capital is not required. The general partnership is subject to entry in the Commercial Register, even if it is considered to have been established before registration. The anonymity of each partner is preserved, unless the tax authorities require it for a specific shareholder.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Limited partnership</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A limited partnership is an association of at least two natural or legal persons, at least one of whom is fully liable for all liabilities of the partnership. In contrast to the general partnership, limited partnerships can also have legal entities as members. In addition, the partnership must consist of at least one fully liable general partner, unlike the limited partners, whose liability is limited to the amount of their contributions. According to the Swiss Code of Obligations, the general partner must be a natural person and not a company. Recently, Switzerland introduced a new law regulating collective investment schemes. According to this law, the LPP can be used as a suitable form of investment for private equity investments. Thanks to the LLP, Switzerland has strengthened its status as a financial center, as this type of partnership is no longer forced to move to Luxembourg, Ireland, or the Channel Islands.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Taxation: General partnerships and limited partnerships are not considered tax subjects. The profits generated are taxed as personal income of the partners. The same applies to the assets of partnerships, which are subject to the personal wealth tax of the partners.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Accounting: The rules of commercial accounting according to the Swiss Code of Obligations apply, which provide for double-entry bookkeeping with balance sheet, inventory, and income statement. An appeal is not necessary.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Independent individual activity Sole proprietorship</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The individual independent activity (sole proprietorship) is similar to the general partnership but is founded by only one person. This means that a single person runs the company and does not form a company. The entrepreneur provides the capital and is therefore fully liable for the company\'s debts. If the company is successful, it can easily be converted into a corporation such as an SA/AG or Sàrl/GmbH.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Requirements for incorporation: There are no binding legal regulations and formal deeds of incorporation, which means that no minimum capital is required. The obligation to register in the commercial register is only required from a turnover of CHF 100,000.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Taxation: The sole proprietorship is not subject to cantonal or federal taxation. However, the sole proprietor is subject to income tax and wealth tax on the profit generated and the assets of the company.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Accounting: The rules of Swiss commercial accounting according to the Swiss Code of Obligations, which requires double-entry bookkeeping with balance sheet, inventory, and income statement, apply. An appeal is not necessary.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Branches inventory,</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In terms of licensing, registration, taxation, and accounting, a branch office is treated like any other Swiss company. The branch is legally dependent on the main company and must therefore have the same company name and business activities.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Requirements for incorporation: A branch office must be entered in the commercial register. In the case of a branch of a foreign company, it must have a legal representative residing in Switzerland.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Taxation: The branch is treated as a legal entity. Upon incorporation, no tax is levied on share issuance. In addition, no withholding tax is levied on profits from the Swiss branch to the foreign headquarters.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Accounting: The rules of commercial accounting apply in accordance with the Swiss Code of Obligations, which requires double-entry bookkeeping with a balance sheet, inventory, and profit and loss account. An appeal is not necessary.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Establishment procedures: Local banks, consulting firms, trust companies, corporate lawyers, and the economic development department of the chosen canton can help to accompany the project until the start of business activities on site. The usual procedure for setting up a company takes between two and four weeks on average and depends on the chosen legal form and the canton where it is located. Highly specialized Swiss financial advisors are available to assist with the successful establishment and management of the company. (SME Portal, n.d.)</span></span></span></p></li></ul></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:27:07','2025-10-08 09:35:08'),(159,27,'Swiss Corporate Taxation','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-09d1b68a-7fff-4a00-ef75-1c1c8a2bc19a\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Swiss corporate tax rates are among the lowest in Europe. Total corporate taxes amount to about 17-28% of profit before taxes (PBT) and are levied at the federal, cantonal, and municipal levels. This approach leads to intercantonal and intermunicipal tax competition and to a steadily decreasing tax burden. Swiss corporate taxation is explained in detail below.</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Types of taxes</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Income tax: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Companies resident in Switzerland are taxed on their worldwide income. In principle, all expenses incurred in order to make a profit and recorded in the statutory accounts are tax-deductible. Expenses that are not economically justified, on the other hand, are not tax-deductible. The taxable profit is therefore based on the profit and loss account adjusted for tax purposes for the period.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Capital tax:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Only the cantons levy an annual capital tax at the cantonal level, which varies from canton to canton and depends on the tax status of the company. Capital tax is imposed/levied on the following basis:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Share capital, paid-up surplus, legal reserves, other reserves, retained earnings</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Provisions that are not deductible for tax purposes</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Debt capital that has the economic character of equity under Swiss law</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Withholding tax: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In Switzerland, withholding tax is used to prevent tax evasion and is levied at a rate of 35 percent on the payment of dividends and interest on bank deposits, bonds, and bond-like loans. Switzerland has concluded double taxation treaties with around 90 countries that allow for full or partial tax relief, usually in the form of a refund. Especially with EU countries, withholding tax is no longer due if certain criteria are met. Switzerland recently agreed with the governments of Germany and the United Kingdom that withholding tax will be deducted from future income and gains from these assets if residents of these two countries have liquid assets in Switzerland. There will also be a one-time tax charge in relation to unreported income from the past. The fees are not charged if the owners of the assets can prove that there are no taxes in their home country. The rules are complex, and further advice should be obtained from the PKF specialist office in Switzerland.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Stamp duty:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> A stamp duty of 1% is levied on the subscribed capital of the SA/AG and Sàrl/GmbH that exceeds CHF 1 million. In addition, a stamp duty of between 0.15% and 0.3% applies to certain securities transfers.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Property taxes: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The amount of taxes on capital gains from real estate depends on the canton in which the property is located. The right to tax such profits is reserved to the cantons. The taxation systems applied by the cantons vary between the special cantonal real estate gains tax and the ordinary corporate profit tax.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">VAT: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Swiss VAT model is similar to the EU model. The standard VAT rate is 8.1%. Lower rates apply to accommodation services (3.8%), food, water, agricultural products, medical products, books, newspapers, and cultural services (2.5%). Certain sectors of the economy are exempt from VAT, such as healthcare, education, culture, sports, social welfare, most banking and insurance, the real estate sector, and gambling. The exemption applies to the export of goods and some international business models. VAT registration is mandatory for companies with a turnover of more than CHF 100,000.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Double taxation treaties: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Switzerland has concluded around 90 tax treaties to minimize the double taxation of dividends, royalties, and interest payments.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Special tax regimes: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">There are various tax privileges at the cantonal level, in particular for holding and domiciliary companies, provided that certain conditions are met.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Federal</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">For corporations and cooperatives domiciled in Switzerland with their registered office or place of effective management in Switzerland, the Confederation levies a flat-rate tax of 8.5% on profit after tax, corresponding to 7.8% on profit before tax.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cantonal level</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Depending on the canton and municipality, the effective tax rate of the canton and the municipality is between approx. 10% and 20%.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Holding</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Holding companies are legal entities whose primary business purpose, according to the articles of association, is to hold and manage long-term investments. Profits from qualifying investments are generally tax-exempt. In order to benefit from the holding tax privilege, which generally reduces the taxation of profits that do not originate from qualifying holdings to 7.8%, two-thirds of the total assets must consist of participations, or two-thirds of the total income must come from participations.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Domicile company</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The tax privilege of the domiciliary company is granted to companies that carry out a purely administrative activity in Switzerland. The effective tax rate depends on the importance of the activity carried out in Switzerland.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Mixed society</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">This tax regime, which is granted to companies with predominantly foreign business, is generally used by international trading companies and can reduce the overall effective tax rate to around 10%.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Other</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Other tax benefits can be claimed for main companies and financial branches.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:27:42','2025-10-08 09:35:36'),(160,27,'Incentives and subsidies','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f67ad722-7fff-0476-e537-a8c1d7e556e1\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 12.5pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Properties</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Companies based abroad and Swiss companies controlled by persons abroad are considered foreigners for the acquisition of real estate. Legal entities have the choice of buying or renting the property in Switzerland. The legal restrictions should be taken into account when making the decision. These restrictions may vary depending on the type of property, its use, and its location.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Real estate</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Foreigners can purchase commercial real estate and land without any special restrictions. Commercial real estate can also be purchased as an investment and rented to third parties. In principle, no permit is required for the acquisition of real estate used for a commercial activity, i.e., for a professional or industrial activity.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Rental of real estate</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">There are no special restrictions for properties rented out for commercial purposes. If you want to rent commercial real estate in Switzerland, there are commercial zones of high cantonal value available to you. Such peri-urban business parks allow for easy B2B collaboration and easy access to transportation and highways. (PKF Certifica SA, n.d.)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:28:32','2025-10-08 09:36:03'),(161,27,'Cryptocurrencies & Blockchain in Switzerland','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a6b690f8-7fff-9ebb-bf6d-08054e858262\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cryptoassets &amp; Blockchain Consulting editors Richard B. Levin, Kevin Tran, and Megan Kilissanly Nelson Mullins Riley &amp; Scarborough LLP have authored a handbook that allows for a direct comparison of local conditions, including the legal and regulatory framework, the use of crypto assets for investment, financing, trading, and payments, cryptocurrency mining, blockchain and other distributed ledger technologies, and recent trends.</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">General legal and regulatory framework</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:12pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What is the legal framework for crypto assets? Is there specific legislation for crypto assets and companies doing business with crypto assets?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Switzerland has not created an entirely separate legal regime for crypto. Instead, FINMA and the revised Anti-Money Laundering (AML) framework have extended existing AML/CFT supervision to virtual assets and virtual asset service providers (VASPs). FINMA published guidance and introduced a virtual-asset audit module in 2021, and the revised Anti-Money Laundering Act (AMLA) entered into force on 1 January 2023. FINMA continues to categorize crypto-assets based on their economic function and applies existing financial market rules to their issuance and transfer (FINMA, finma.ch; Lecocq Associate, lecocqassociate.com).</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:-7pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">From a regulatory point of view, FINMA distinguishes between three different types of crypto assets and refers to these investments as tokens. We speak of an asset (security) token, the payment token, and the utility token, as well as mixed forms of them. Depending on the type of cryptoasset, different laws must be observed, namely the Banking Act (BankG), the Financial Market Infrastructure Act (FMIA), the Collective Investment Schemes Act, the Insurance Supervision Act, the Anti-Money Laundering Act (AMLA), the Financial Services Act, and the Financial Institutions Act. In particular, non-fungible tokens (NFTs), protocol tokens, or stablecoins must also be assessed according to the above-mentioned regulations, even if FINMA\'s typical three token categories do not really fit such token types in some cases. From a civil law perspective, two types of tokens can be distinguished. Tokens that primarily represent value in the blockchain context, such as Bitcoins. According to conventional wisdom, these \"payment tokens\" are purely factual, intangible assets. The second type of token embodies a legal position with similar functions to securities (also known as an \"I-owe-you token\"). With the passage of the DLT Act on September 25, 2020, the Swiss Parliament passed a bill amending the current laws to include crypto assets and digital ledger technologies (DLT) in Swiss law, making the Swiss crypto legal framework one of the most advanced in the world. The Swiss Code of Obligations (CO) came into force on 1 February 2021. Ledger-based securities are treated as a new form of securities alongside securities, securitized securities, and book securities when created and transferred in a ledger such as DLT. The following significant changes came into force on 1 August 2021. The Federal Act on Debt Enforcement and Bankruptcy is to explicitly regulate the segregation of crypto-based assets in the event of insolvency, insofar as it is no longer required at the technical level but only on the basis of records. On the other hand, the relaxed segregation rules stipulate that such pooled wallet providers with off-balance sheet crypto assets must apply for a fintech license, even if the value of the crypto assets exceeds the limit of 100 million Swiss francs. The FMIA introduced a new licensing category for \"DLT trading facilities.\" It works similarly to the existing multilateral trading facilities (MTFs), but allows direct access for retail investors. In addition, it enables other services in the trade value chain within the same legal entity, such as clearing, settlement, and custody services.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How would you describe the government\'s general approach to regulating crypto assets in your country?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The government\'s general approach is to create the best possible framework conditions for Switzerland to establish and develop as a leading, innovative, and sustainable location for fintech and DLT companies. In addition, it aims to consistently combat abuses, especially in the areas of money laundering and terrorist financing, and to safeguard the integrity and good reputation of Switzerland as a financial and business location. With its principle-based and technology-neutral laws and regulations, Switzerland is very flexible with regard to new technologies and business models. In addition, the legislative and government bodies of the Confederation and the cantons are prepared to comply with these innovative approaches.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Supervisory authorities</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Which state authorities regulate crypto assets and transactions made with crypto assets?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As Switzerland\'s supervisory authority, FINMA is also responsible for market supervision of crypto assets. For pure anti-money laundering supervision, financial intermediaries must join and be subject to a private self-regulatory organization that is recognized and supervised by FINMA. In addition, portfolio managers are licensed by FINMA but supervised by a private supervisory organization authorized by FINMA. On 16 February 2018, FINMA published the ICO guidelines, which divide the different types of crypto assets into three categories and were supplemented on 11 September 2019 with regard to stablecoins.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Regulatory sanctions</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What sanctions can regulators impose for breaches related to crypto assets?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">If the regulatory requirements are not complied with, FINMA can impose the sanctions specified in the Federal Act on the Swiss Financial Market Supervisory Authority; for example, enforcement proceedings are initiated. Possible measures include the obligation to restore order, the issuance of a declaratory order, a ban on practicing a profession, the publication of the supervisory order, the confiscation of an unlawful profit, the appointment of investigators, the withdrawal of a license or permit, and the liquidation of a company. As a rule, the exercise of an activity that actually requires a permit; without a permit, it is also a criminal offense that is punished by the law enforcement authorities. The non-publication or publication of an incomplete, misleading, or false prospectus for a public security token offering will not be prosecuted by FINMA but is subject to criminal law and triggers civil liability of the offeror towards investors.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Jurisdiction</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Which courts have jurisdiction over disputes related to crypto assets?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">There is no specialized court that has jurisdiction over crypto assets. Depending on the law violated, the existing civil, criminal, or administrative courts at the federal or cantonal level, or both, have jurisdiction. In purely civil cases, the parties can also agree on arbitration proceedings, provided that there are no mandatory rules on jurisdiction.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Legal Status of Cryptocurrencies</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Is owning cryptocurrencies, using cryptocurrencies in business transactions, and exchanging cryptocurrencies for local currency legal in your country?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cryptocurrencies are not considered legal tender in Switzerland. However, there are no restrictions on the legal ownership, transaction, and exchange of cryptocurrencies. In some cases, anti-money laundering regulations or licensing requirements may apply.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Fiat currencies</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What fiat currencies are commonly used in your country?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In Switzerland, the official fiat currency is the Swiss franc, which is issued by the Swiss National Bank and is considered legal tender.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trade associations</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Which are the leading industry associations that deal with legal and political issues related to crypto assets?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Swiss Blockchain Federation (SBF), the Crypto Valley Association (CVA), and the Capital Markets and Technology Association (CMTA) are leaders in the (CVA).</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Crypto assets for investment and financing</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Regulatory threshold: What attributes do regulators consider when deciding whether a crypto asset is subject to regulation in your country? According to the Financial Market Supervisory Authority (FINMA), the applicable regulation depends on the type of crypto assets. In its ICO guidelines, FINMA distinguishes between </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">three different types of tokens:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Payment tokens:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> They are tokens that are intended to be used now or in the future as a means of payment for the purchase of goods or services, or as a means of money, store of value, or transfer. Cryptocurrencies do not create any claims against their issuer. Payment coins are not considered securities. However, collecting or transferring these cryptocurrencies or even assisting in the transfer of cryptocurrencies in an ongoing business relationship is usually subject to the Anti-Money Laundering Act (AMLA).</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Utility tokens: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">They are intended to provide digital access to applications or services via a blockchain-based infrastructure. If a utility token functions exclusively or partly as an investment in economic terms, FINMA treats it as securities, i.e., in the same way as asset tokens.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Asset tokens:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> These represent assets, such as a debt or equity claim against or to the issuer. For example, asset tokens promise a share of future earnings or future capital flows of the issuing company or platform. In terms of their economic function, these tokens are treated in the same way as stocks, bonds, or derivatives. In general, tokens that enable the trading of physical assets on the blockchain also fall into this category. FINMA considers asset tokens to be securities, which means that the offering or trading of them is subject to securities regulations (Financial Services Act (FinSA), Financial Market Infrastructure Act (FMIA), and FINMA) as well as civil law provisions of the Swiss Code of Obligations.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The individual token classifications are not mutually exclusive; both asset and utility tokens can be classified as payment tokens (hybrid tokens). Depending on the type of crypto asset, different laws may apply. In particular, the Banking Act (BWG) introduced the term \"crypto-asset\" and defined in which cases a fintech license or even a banking license is required. According to the report, crypto assets are crypto-based assets that are collected and can no longer be individually assigned to an individual customer. These crypto assets must serve as a means of payment for the acquisition of goods or services, or for the transfer of money or value. Crypto-assets are not considered crypto-assets within the meaning of the BA if they are booked as balances in the customer accounts of securities or precious metal dealers, asset managers, a DLT trading facility, or similar companies and are used exclusively for the settlement of customer transactions. In addition, no interest may be paid for this, and for accounts other than those of securities dealers, settlement must be made within 60 days.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:29:21','2025-10-08 09:36:39'),(162,27,'Investor Classification','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-2434d9cb-7fff-2df5-f3e7-10ba6c1df856\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How are investors who invest in crypto assets classified and treated differently?</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">According to FinSA, there are three main types of investors associated with financial services. Institutional clients such as banks and securities firms, professional clients such as financial professionals, and retail investors, who essentially do not fall into the two categories mentioned above and are considered consumers. High-net-worth individuals can declare that they want to be treated as professional clients for investment purposes. The Collective Investment Schemes Act (CISA) distinguishes between qualified and non-qualified investors. The definition of a qualified investor refers to the professional client according to FinSA. Clients with an ongoing wealth management or investment advisory relationship with a supervised and licensed financial institution are also classified as qualified investors.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Initial Coin Offerings</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What are the rules and restrictions for conducting and investing in Initial Coin Offerings (ICOs)?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">There is no uniform law for ICOs in Switzerland. Depending on the qualification of the crypto asset, different regulations may apply. There is no licensing requirement by FINMA for the implementation of an ICO, unless a crypto asset is considered a derivative or there is a repayment obligation on the part of the issuer. In these cases, a license as a securities firm or a banking license may be required. The banking license is the highest regulated category of financial market participants. An ICO of a payment token triggers obligations under the AMLA. However, payment tokens are considered securities as long as they do not function on a blockchain. An ICO of a utility token is not subject to the AMLA if the functionality of the token relates to access to the blockchain for mainly non-financial purposes. If a utility token functions exclusively or partly as an investment in economic terms, FINMA treats it as a security. According to FinSA, an ICO of an asset token can lead to the publication of a prospectus or information sheet. The issuance of NFTs is generally not subject to financial market regulation, as long as it does not circumvent regulations. A circumvention would be given, for example, if each out of 100 NFTs generally represents 1/100 of a painting, as in this case each NFT would be exactly the same except for its unique number and thus would have the same value and would be interchangeable. This would trigger the securities regulations under Swiss law. In contrast, an NFT that refers to a specific piece of the 100 pieces of the painting (e.g., piece B3 or H5) would be unique not only in terms of its number but also its contents and therefore not interchangeable with another NFT. In general, four phases of an ICO can be distinguished in Switzerland.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pre-financing phase</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Investors are only given the prospect that they will receive tokens at some point in the future. The tokens, the underlying blockchain, or both, have yet to be developed. At this stage, there are no transferable tokens on a blockchain.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pre-sale phase (voucher)</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Investors receive tokens that entitle them to purchase or receive other tokens at a later date. A conversion or exchange is required.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pre-operative phase</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The main functionality of the tokens is ready but cannot be used at the time of issuance because the application, platform, or underlying blockchain has yet to be developed or is not yet finalized. Once the development of the platform or underlying blockchain is complete, there is no need to convert a token.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Bullet</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Operational phase</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The key features of the tokens are ready and can be used in the intended way at the time of issuance on a working blockchain, application, or platform.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Security Token Offerings</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What are the rules and restrictions for conducting and investing in Security Token Offerings (STOs)?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The offering of crypto-assets that qualify as securities only leads to a licensing requirement if the crypto-assets are derivatives or collective investment schemes or if an intermediary places the securities on the primary market on behalf of the issuer (admission as a securities dealer required). In addition, there are strict regulatory requirements for the issuance and offering of structured products to retail customers and retail investors.In the case of a public offer, issuers of securities must publish a sales prospectus under FinSA, which must be reviewed and approved by a supervisory body approved by FINMA. Exceptions to this rule are set out in FinSA and include offers to professional investors, offers to fewer than 500 investors, offers to investors investing more than 100,000 Swiss francs, offers of securities with a minimum denomination of 100,000 Swiss francs, and offers limited to a total amount of 8 million Swiss francs. When securities are offered to retail investors, the issuer is usually required to prepare a key information document.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Stablecoins</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What are the rules and restrictions for issuing and investing in stablecoins?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">For stablecoins, FINMA follows the rules based on the stablecoin supplement to the ICO guidelines. This follows the same approach as blockchain-based tokens, mainly targeting the economic function and purpose of a token. Depending on the case, FINMA will follow the principle of \"same risks, same rules\" and the relevant characteristics of each case. Since stablecoins can be variable, regulatory requirements differ depending on the assets (e.g., currencies, commodities, securities, and real estate) backed or pegged to the stablecoin and the legal rights of its holders. Regulations for banking, fund administration, financial infrastructure, money laundering, and securities trading can all become relevant.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Are crypto assets distributed via airdrop treated differently than other types of supply mechanisms?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Generally not, but in certain cases, anti-money laundering regulations may apply. If the airdrop takes place without the required activity of the receiving party (in particular no purchase price and no other consideration, including (personal) data), the receiving party has not made an investment decision; therefore, there is generally no prospectus requirement.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Advertising and marketing</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What laws and regulations govern the advertising and marketing of crypto assets used for investment and financing?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Crypto-assets used for investment or financing are generally to be regarded as securities and trigger the prospectus and key information document requirements of the FinSA for the issuer and the obligations of conduct at the point of sale for the financial service provider. In particular, the advertising of financial instruments must be clearly recognizable as such. The advertising must refer to the prospectus and the key information document of the respective financial instrument. Advertising for the acceptance of cryptocurrencies as public deposits under the Banking Act to residents of Switzerland is only permitted with a banking license. In all other cases, there are no strict regulations for advertising. However, the laws on unfair competition and the criminal law provisions on fraud must be observed.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trade restrictions</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Are investors in an ICO/STO/stablecoin subject to any trading restrictions after the initial offering?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Generally not, except for any transmission restrictions imposed by the issuer as a result of securities laws or derivatives trading obligations. In addition, Swiss or other sanctions regulations may prohibit transfers to crypto assets.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Crowdfunding</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What are the differences between crowdfunding and crypto offerings?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">According to Swiss regulations, four crowdfunding categories must be distinguished, which apply regardless of whether it is fiat or crypto. Crowddonating, crowdsupporting, crowdlending, and crowdinvesting. In general, only crowdfunding and crowdinvesting platforms with debt capital are currently subject to the Anti-Money Laundering Act (AMLA). According to the BA, crowdlending can lead to the requirement of a banking license. However, depending on the amount of funds raised, certain exceptions and facilitations may apply. The Fintech license is available in particular for innovative projects that collect no more than 100 million francs from the public or unlimited bundled crypto-based assets and neither invest nor earn interest on these funds. This authorization provides for numerous relaxations in terms of capital and organizational requirements. Depending on its structure, crowdinvesting can trigger the regulations for collective investment schemes.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Transfer agents and share registrars</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What laws and regulations apply to transfer agents and share registrars of crypto assets?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">No specific laws apply to these services. In general, the AMLA must be observed when transferring any kind of cryptocurrency that qualifies as a financial instrument or means of payment, and also when supporting the transfer of cryptocurrencies in a long-term business relationship. In particular, the exchange of cryptocurrencies for another cryptocurrency or fiat currency is considered a currency exchange or money transfer and is therefore subject to the AMLA. The provision of crypto-asset transfer services also triggers anti-money laundering obligations if the service provider shares or retains the private key of its customers.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Anti-Money Laundering and KYC Compliance</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What requirements and guidelines for anti-money laundering (AMLA) and customer knowledge (KYC) apply to the offering of crypto assets?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The AMLA and the corresponding ordinance define the obligations that must be fulfilled by the financial intermediaries subject to these laws. In general, only an ICO that deals with payment tokens or a hybrid token with payment functions is subject to the AMLA. However, the AMLA and KYC requirements are often triggered when a financial intermediary is involved in a transaction involving payment tokens. Natural or legal persons providing services related to crypto-assets within the scope of the AMLA must join a self-regulatory organization. The private companies recognized by FINMA are required to comply with the AMLA. The following typical obligations apply within the scope of the AMLA.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Identification of customers</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The verification of ownership, the verification of politically exposed persons and sanctions checks, and the determination of the origin of funds and assets, as well as increased due diligence in the event of high risks, must be carried out accordingly. As part of additional investigations, further background information on the business relationship must be obtained. Depending on the circumstances, the origin, purpose,, or background of the assets brought or withdrawn, the origin of the assets, or the business activities of the customer or the beneficial owner must be clarified. There are documentation obligations, reporting obligations, and the freezing of assets is possible. In addition, the Travel Rule applies to cryptocurrency transactions in a similar way to fiat currency transfers. The scope of the said obligation may vary depending on the service or activity and the number of Swiss francs collected or transferred. Currently, there are no specific rules, guidelines, or established practices for crypto asset identification or proof of ownership. However, these controls must be carried out in order to comply with the AMLA.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Financial Action Task Force Sanctions and Compliance</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What laws and regulations apply to crypto assets to enforce government sanctions, counter-terrorist financing principles, and Financial Action Task Force (FATF) standards?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Sanctions are implemented in Switzerland through the Embargo Act (EMBA) and the corresponding ordinances on specific sanctions against certain countries, persons, or entities in order to restrict the provision of certain services and the sale of goods that these persons finance. The international UN sanctions are directly applicable in Switzerland and must be observed on a regular basis, especially in the provision of financial services. In addition, Switzerland usually also implements EU sanctions. However, the Swiss government is not allowed to impose its own sanctions or sanctions that are stricter than those of the EU. Business relationships with sanctioned persons may not be established or must be broken off. In Switzerland, sanction regulations are completely separate from AML regulations. The main authority responsible for implementing and monitoring the sanctions regulations is the State Secretariat for Economic Affairs (SECO). The principles of the UN and the FATF on combating the financing of terrorism are implemented by the sanctions legislation of the EMBA and the AMLA, in particular through the increased due diligence and reporting obligations. As part of the AMLA framework, the Travel Rule is implemented in particular by Article 10 of the Anti-Money Laundering Ordinance FINMA (AMLO-FINMA) and the regulations of self-regulatory organizations (SROs). Finally, there is no specific regulation in Switzerland for virtual asset service providers (VASP) within the meaning of the FATF, but the VASP requirements are mainly implemented by the AMLA and also by the licensing requirements of other financial market laws, such as the OAG or FinIA.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:34:16','2025-10-08 09:37:22'),(163,27,'Crypto Asset Trading','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-7358a536-7fff-1209-520a-0d5dac0c57fb\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 12.5pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Transactions in fiat currency</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What are the rules and restrictions for exchanging fiat currency and cryptocurrencies?</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The commercial purchase and sale of cryptocurrencies against fiat currencies (e.g., Swiss francs), but also between different cryptocurrencies, constitutes an exchange (two-party transaction) or money transfer (three-party business) subject to the Anti-Money Laundering Act (AMLA), provided that they are not qualified as securities or utility tokens. In the case of currency exchange transactions, for example, the contracting party must be identified if the minimum amount is 5,000 francs. For transactions with virtual currencies, the value is 1,000 francs. For a minimum amount of 15,000 francs, the beneficial beneficiary must be identified. The money changer must take appropriate measures to ensure that it is the customer\'s wallet (two-party transaction) and not that of a third party. Otherwise, it would be a transfer of funds, and the identification requirement would apply to zero Swiss francs for outgoing transactions and 1,000 Swiss francs for incoming transactions. For transactions with payment tokens, financial intermediaries must apply the Travel Rule based on the Anti-Money Laundering Ordinance of the Financial Market Supervisory Authority (FINMA) to every transaction, including transactions on wallets held with unregulated wallet providers. That is, the name, address, and wallet address of the sending party and the name and wallet address of the receiving party are required. Trading cryptocurrencies, which are securities, either on behalf of clients or for your own account, usually requires a securities trading license. This only applies if certain turnover thresholds are exceeded. The authorization requirement also applies to the public issuance of derivatives or the placement of securities for issuers by the company. The bilateral systematic address of crypto-assets and related derivatives are financial instruments that are subject to additional regulatory requirements under the Financial Market Infrastructure Act (FMIA). A banking license is usually required to accept customer deposits. Cryptocurrencies and the associated private keys can be deposits within the meaning of the Banking Act. Professional forex traders are not allowed to accept public deposits unless they have a banking license. The same applies to crypto-asset traders who share or store their customers\' private keys. However, depending on the number of funds received, a fintech license can be purchased.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Bilateral trading (brokerage or dealership)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Licensing requirements and obligations for professional trading in securities generally require a license under the Financial Institutions Act as a securities firm, issued by FINMA. The exact requirements and the licensing procedure depend heavily on the registered office of the securities firm and the business activity carried out. A securities firm domiciled in Switzerland is any legal entity or partnership that sells or buys securities on a commercial basis on the secondary market for its own account with the intention of selling them again within a short period of time (e.g., proprietary traders and market makers). This also applies on behalf of third parties (e.g., customer dealers) as well as through the public offering of securities on the primary market (e.g., issuing houses) or through the commercial creation of derivatives and their public offering on the primary market (e.g., derivatives houses).Companies that acquire or sell payment or asset tokens in secondary trading on behalf of customers are considered financial service providers within the meaning of the Financial Services Act (FinSA) and are subject to the obligations of conduct at the point of sale.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Derivatives Trading Obligations</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Depending on the status of the counterparties involved, trading in crypto-assets that are derivatives may be subject to several derivatives trading obligations under the FMIA, such as reporting, clearing, and risk mitigation obligations.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trading platforms</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Order matching: Centralized or decentralized trading platforms where crypto assets are traded as securities usually require approval as a financial market infrastructure (FMI) of the category of an exchange or multilateral trading facility (MTF). Only regulated participants are allowed to trade on such an FMI, i.e., not retail investors. A licensed bank or securities firm may operate an organized trading facility through which financial instruments other than securities may also be traded. Organized trading systems are also directly accessible to retail investors. Payment token trading platforms do not require an FMI license if they only offer spot transactions. Trading in pure utility tokens does not trigger an FMI licensing requirement, as utility tokens do not qualify as financial instruments.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Clearing and settlement: The provision of clearing and settlement services associated with the power to dispose of private keys usually triggers banking regulations related to payment tokens, fiat currencies, or securities firm regulations related to asset tokens. In addition, an entity that settles and settles payment obligations based on uniform rules and procedures could even require an FMI license, similar to a payment system. If an organized trading facility offers transaction processing related to payment tokens or fiat currencies, it must hold customer funds in settlement accounts for no more than 60 calendar days in order to limit regulatory requirements to anti-money laundering. Insofar as such platforms also offer their customers account management, for example, the settlement of margins, and keep the crypto assets in collective accounts on the blockchain, a subordination to the Banking Act must also be examined. For these companies, the fintech license can be an attractive option. As many infrastructures based on distributed ledger technology (DLT) take an integrated approach to exchange and post-trade services, Switzerland introduced a new category of financial market infrastructures as of 1 August 2021, tailored to the specificities of a DLT-based multilateral exchange for ledger-based securities with direct access for retail investors, which will enable matching, execution, clearing, settlement, and custody within the same legal entity. In addition, cryptocurrencies are allowed to be traded via a DLT trading system.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Custody</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How are cryptocurrency custodians regulated?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Custody services related to pure utility tokens are not regulated.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Normal custody of payment and asset tokens: The simple custody of asset tokens with the power to have private keys is subject only to the AMLA. The activities of a central securities depository, on the other hand, are subject to a license from FINMA. In contrast, the custody of a payment token may also be subject to a banking or fintech authorization if the custody provider holds the private keys and does not completely separate the tokens per customer at a technical or accounting level and is not contractually obligated to keep the payment tokens available to the customer at all times. The custody of assets, whether crypto-assets or assets from the analogue world, does not in itself constitute a financial service within the meaning of Article 3 (c) FinSA. This custody activity lacks at least the characteristic of the activity carried out for clients, such as the acquisition or disposal of financial instruments, the acceptance and transmission of orders in relation to financial instruments, or the asset management activity, in order to be identified as a financial service. In particular, there is no asset management if the sole purpose of the transfer of the assets is custody and there is no power of attorney to invest the assets. Accordingly, a custody service provider is not covered by FinSA as long as its service is limited to custody as such. However, if a sale of tokens that are considered financial instruments is only possible via an account with the provider of custody services, e.g., because the private key is located there, it is likely to be a financial service under FinSA. Central securities depository of asset tokens: A central securities depository is a category of financial market institutions that is subject to a license from FINMA. It is the operator of a central custodian or securities settlement system. This is referred to as an institution for the central custody of securities and other financial instruments according to uniform rules and procedures. In our view, the mere issuance of security tokens or payment tokens does not qualify as a securities settlement system or payment system, provided that the respective blockchain or DLT is actually operated in a decentralized manner. Since a full-fledged crypto-asset securities exchange usually intends to provide after-hours services that require a CSD license, care must be taken to ensure that a legal entity does not hold two different FMI licenses. Therefore, two legal entities would be required for these projects. All custody service providers who have the ability to transfer their customers\' crypto assets are subject to AML regulations. This means that they not only have the authority to dispose of the private keys but also any means of influencing or controlling the smart contract. The smart contract makes it possible to carry out the transfer, which is subject to a long-term business relationship with the customer.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Stock market traders</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">How are exchange traders for crypto assets regulated?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The licensing requirements and obligations for commercial trading in securities generally require a license under the Financial Institutions Act as a securities firm, which is granted by FINMA. The exact requirements and the licensing procedure depend heavily on the registered office of the securities firm and the business activity carried out. A securities firm domiciled in Switzerland is any legal entity or partnership that sells or buys securities on a commercial basis. This can be done on the secondary market for its own account with the intention of selling them again within a short periolicenseehalf of third parties, by offering securities to the public on the primary market or by creating derivatives on a commercial basis and offering them to the public on the primary market. Companies that acquire or sell payment or asset tokens in secondary trading on behalf of clients are considered financial service providers under FinSA and are subject to the obligations of conduct at the point of sale.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Derivatives Trading Obligations</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trading in cryptocurrencies, which are derivatives, may be subject to several FINMA derivatives trading obligations, such as reporting, settlement, and risk mitigation obligations, depending on the status of the counterparties involved.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Decentralized Trading Venues</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What is the legal status of decentralized trading venues for cryptocurrencies?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The scope of the rules depends on the degree of decentralization of the different value chains involved.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trading and Order Matching</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Typically, the mechanisms for order matching are organized centrally, which often triggers an FMI license requirement as an exchange, multilateral trading facility, or organized trading facility. In the case of fully decentralized solutions, no FMI license would be required. Since 1 August 2021, there has been a new category of FMI, the DLT trading system for trading ledger-based securities, which qualify as asset tokens according to FINMA. It enables multilateral trade with direct access for retail clients.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Clearing and settlement</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Often, decentralization refers to decentralized clearing and settlement processes, which means peer-to-peer clearing or settlement of transactions without the involvement of the trading platform. So, if the trading platform does not operate a smart contract involved in the transaction, nor does it have the authority to dispose of the private keys during those transactions, it usually does not trigger AML regulations or licensing requirements for banks or securities firms. However, if the smart contract is operated by the corresponding trading platform and offers technical control and influence options, these decentralized trading platforms are usually at least subject to the AMLA according to FINMA\'s practice, as they have control over third-party assets by confirming, releasing, or blocking orders. DeFi structures in particular often fall within the scope of the AMLA because it also covers support for transactions with cryptocurrencies in the context of long-term business relationships.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Peer-to-peer exchanges</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What is the legal status of peer-to-peer (person-to-person) transfers of cryptocurrencies?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Peer-to-peer transactions usually do not fall within the scope of the AMLA if the wallet service provider has neither the power of disposal over the private keys nor any other influence over the transaction or the smart contract. However, if a wallet service provider can exercise control over the participants\' assets or influence the smart contract, the AMLA applies. Providers of wallets without a custodial function can also fall within the scope of the AMLA if they are considered supporters of transactions with cryptocurrencies in the context of long-term business relationships. The AMLA\'s obligations to trade derivatives apply to all (counter)parties to transactions with asset tokens that are considered derivatives.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trading with anonymous parties</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Does the law allow cryptocurrency trading with anonymous parties?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In principle, the law does not prohibit trading with anonymous parties. However, the FINMA guideline \"Payments on the blockchain\" of February 2019 clarifies that financial intermediaries executing orders with payment tokens must fully comply with the Travel Rule under FINMA\'s Anti-Money Laundering Ordinance. Contrary to the recommendations of the Financial Action Task Force, there is no exception in Swiss AML regulations for payments with unregulated wallet providers. Finally, the sanction provisions of the Embargo Act (EmbA) must also be taken into account.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Foreign trading venues</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Are foreign cryptocurrency exchanges subject to their country\'s laws and regulations for cryptocurrency trading?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">If a foreign exchange or multilateral trading facility enables trading in cryptocurrencies that are to be classified as securities, it needs recognition by the FMIA before it can grant access to Swiss-regulated participants. Depending on their business model and structure, foreign trading platforms that address unregulated Swiss clients directly must check whether they are providing a financial service and are therefore subject to FINMA\'s rules of conduct, whether they offer financial instruments to the public and are therefore subject to FINMA\'s prospectus and key information document requirements, or whether the obligations of the FMIA apply to derivative transactions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Under what circumstances can a citizen in your country legally exchange cryptocurrencies on a foreign exchange?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">There are no restrictions in Swiss law in this regard, except that the Swiss client must check whether the FMIA derivatives trading obligation applies in connection with derivative transactions. In FINMA\'s official practice in connection with decentralised exchanges (DEX) for payment tokens, every user is considered a currency exchange service provider within the meaning of the AMLA if he or she acts commercially. Once crypto assets are exchanged, taxes are incurred.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Tax liabilities</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In principle, all types of crypto assets and the corresponding transactions are subject to federal, cantonal, and municipal taxes, such as income, wealth, and profit tax, stamp duty, and withholding tax or VAT. The Federal Tax Administration has introduced the following. On 27 August 2019, it published a working paper on cryptocurrencies and initial coin offerings and initial token offerings in connection with wealth, income, and profit tax, withholding tax, and stamp duty, in which it points out in particular that it is guided by the token classification of the FINMA ICO guidelines. The brochure \"VAT Information 04\" was supplemented on 1 January 2018 with a section on services related to blockchain and distributed ledger technology. All federal, cantonal, and municipal tax authorities allow the filing of tax rulings and have gained extensive experience over many years.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:35:09','2025-10-08 09:38:19'),(164,27,'Legal Status of Cryptocurrencies','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-54330760-7fff-48f0-0e78-b7f5609b3cca\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 12.5pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">State-recognized asset</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Has the state recognized cryptocurrencies as legal tender or issued its own cryptocurrencies?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Swiss government has not (yet) recognized cryptocurrency as legal tender or issued its own cryptocurrency. However, every person is free to accept cryptocurrencies as a means of payment, and it can also be contractually agreed to pay with cryptocurrencies. The canton of Zug calls itself \"Crypto Valley,\" like the Silicon Valley of cryptocurrencies, and has accepted the cryptocurrencies Bitcoin and Ether as a means of payment since 2017 for defined fees and since 2020 also for tax payments. At the Commercial Registry Office of the Canton of Zug, the fees can be paid with the cryptocurrencies Bitcoin and Ether. In a project with SIX Group, the Swiss National Bank has examined whether SIX Group\'s digital exchange can use a digital currency issued by the Swiss National Bank for internal transaction processing.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Bitcoin</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Does Bitcoin have a special status among cryptocurrencies?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">No, it is not recognized as legal tender and falls into the \"normal\" token category of payment tokens.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Banks and other financial institutions</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Do banks or other financial institutions allow cryptocurrency accounts?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In general, Swiss banks or other financial institutions are allowed to offer cryptocurrency accounts. On the one hand, many banks and other financial institutions are still refusing to do so, primarily because they consider the regulatory risks to be too high and because they often do not yet have the necessary know-how. However, this is slowly changing. On the other hand, the Swiss Financial Market Supervisory Authority (FINMA) has already granted two full banking and securities house licenses to Swiss institutions that focus primarily on crypto-based financial services and offer, among other things, cryptocurrency accounts. Several applications for banking licenses, securities dealer licenses, and fintech licenses are still being processed by FINMA. In addition, there are other crypto storage service providers in the market that are structured in such a way that they do not require a banking and securities trading license.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Mining</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Legal status: What is the legal status of cryptocurrency mining activities?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The mining of tokens in itself does not constitute a financial service within the meaning of Article 3 (c) of the Financial Services Act (FinSA). It does not meet the criterion of an activity for clients that has as its object the acquisition or sale of financial instruments or the acceptance and brokerage of orders for financial instruments, at least not if the mined tokens do not constitute financial instruments within the meaning of FinSA. If, for example, cryptocurrencies are mined with the sole function of a cryptocurrency, the miner is not a financial service provider according to Article 3 (d) FinSA. If, on the other hand, cryptocurrencies are mined that constitute financial instruments within the meaning of FinSA, the classification of a miner as a financial service provider depends primarily on how close the customer relationship is in the sense of a contractual relationship. The order must relate to the specific design of the purchase or sale of financial instruments or the acceptance and brokerage of orders relating to financial instruments. The revenue from token mining in the form of tokens or transaction fees is usually not subject to anti-money laundering regulations, provided that it is used for private purposes.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Government Statement: What Views Have Government Officials Expressed on Cryptocurrency Mining?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In its report on digital ledger technologies published on 14 December 2018 and in its report on virtual currencies published on 25 June 2014, the Federal Council explicitly addressed mining with regard to the provisions of the AMLA and the provision of financial services under FinSA. Apart from that, no other official statements have been made so far. Regarding staking in proof-of-stake-based blockchains through the provision of validation services, the Swiss regulator FINMA has not yet officially commented on the regulatory implications. Therefore, there is some uncertainty about the use. However, it is always possible to apply for a non-action letter from FINMA in order to obtain complete legal certainty.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Licenses for cryptocurrency mining: Are licenses required for cryptocurrency mining?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In principle, the mining of cryptocurrencies in Switzerland does not require a license within the meaning of financial market legislation. In terms of staking for third parties on proof-of-stake-based blockchains by providing verification services, AML regulations apply, and depending on the wallet structure, a fintech or banking license may be required.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Taxes: How is the acquisition of cryptocurrencies by mining cryptocurrencies taxed?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">If the mining activity qualifies as a commercial activity in a specific case, the income from mining is subject to income or profit tax so that the income or profits generated by mining are taxable at the federal, cantonal, and municipal levels. In addition, the ownership of cryptocurrencies is subject to wealth tax.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Staking</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">(Proof-of-Stake blockchains)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">If someone runs a staking node with their own assets, it does not constitute a financial service, nor is it subject to AML or banking regulations. However, if a person acts as a staking service provider for \"staking customers,\" they are subject to AML regulations. Depending on the type of wallet structure, which can be fully segregated per customer or bundled, banking regulations with fintech or even banking license requirements must be met. In addition, the payouts of staking rewards are not considered interest payments within the meaning of the Swiss Banking Ordinance, as they are paid by the protocol and not by the staking service provider.These general explanations relate solely to staking services related to proof-of-stake-based blockchains and the provision of validation services. All other forms of staking, in particular the usual or non-technical use of the term \"staking\" for blocking assets to obtain a return without any further requirements, usually qualify as securities under Swiss law and are therefore subject to securities regulations.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Node Licenses</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Are licenses required to operate a blockchain/DLT node?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The operation of a node within a decentralized, distributed blockchain or ledger is generally not subject to approval. However, in certain cases, approval as a central securities depository or as a DLT trading system may be required when operating a central node within an approved DLT-based platform. If nodes are operated within central networks, a careful examination of the requirements of Swiss financial market regulation is also necessary.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Restrictions on the operation of nodes: Are there any restrictions on the operation of a blockchain/DLT node?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">There are no known specific restrictions on the operation of nodes within distributed, decentralized blockchains or distributed ledgers. However, the operation of a node within the new DLT trading facility is regulated. The approach of the Financial Market Authority is still unknown. Finally, the Swiss sanctions regulations, in particular the Embargo Act, also apply to Swiss-based operators of blockchain/DLT nodes.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">DAO Liability: What is the legal liability of participants in a decentralized autonomous organization (DAO)?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A DAO is an example of a smart contract where the smart contract can independently dispose of an organization\'s resources. The governance of the organization is described in the smart contract, which ensures that the organization behaves as described. However, the DAO is neither a fixed term in Swiss law nor does it have a defined structure. It must therefore be analyzed in detail on a case-by-case basis on the basis of specific characteristics. In many cases, especially when assets are raised by multiple users to fund the DAO and its activities, and if those users have voting rights, a DAO often qualifies as a collective investment scheme. In many other cases, a DAO would at least be considered a simple company within the meaning of the Commercial Code, as it is a catch-all provision.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">DAO Assets: Who Owns a DAO\'s Assets? Since a DAO is neither explicitly defined in Swiss law nor has a specific structure, the question of ownership of the assets must be assessed on a case-by-case basis, taking into account the applicable laws.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Open Source: Are DLTs based on open-source protocols or software legally treated differently from private DLTs? In terms of financial market regulations, there is no difference between these two scenarios.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Smart Contracts</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Are smart contracts legally enforceable?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The application of classical private law to smart contracts raises questions due to the automated and immutable nature of contract fulfillment technology. First, the exchange of mutual expressions of intent between the parties does not take place in the traditional way. Each party expresses its will, and the system serves as a mediator. The computer system therefore plays an important role in the process of contracting, but it is not a party to the contract. According to the current doctrine, neither party can conclude a contract with the computer system alone, as it has no legal personality within the meaning of the Swiss Civil Code. The application of the current provisions on contract performance to a smart contract that directly affects this area also raises questions. In the event of defective performance of the contract, the question of liability arises, for example, for programming errors or machine errors despite correct programming. The question also arises as to whether the application of Articles 197 of the Code of Obligations (CO) (warranty for defects in the purchased item) and 367 of the CO (liability for defects in connection with work performed) is possible in certain cases of technical program errors. Finally, the anonymity of the parties inherent in blockchain technology is a key obstacle to the implementation of existing contract provisions. If a contracting party wants to assert its rights, it must necessarily know its counterparty. From today\'s perspective, legal doctrine recommends that the parties enter into a smart contract with appropriate mechanisms for any changing circumstances or for dispute resolution. There will certainly be more developments in the smart contract space, but these have only just begun. If a smart contract is deployed as part of the new DLT trading facility, the enforceability of this contract must be ensured by the platform in accordance with the provisions of the Financial Market Infrastructure Act.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Trends</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Recent developments—Are there any new trends, notable rulings, or \"hot\" topics related to cryptocurrencies or blockchain in case law?</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Since the entry into force of the DLT Act on 1 February and 1 August 2021, Switzerland is still waiting for FINMA to issue the first license for a DLT trading facility. It will be interesting to see if this will usher in a larger trend towards tokenization and asset tokens. Since the Swiss population rejected the partial abolition of the Swiss withholding tax on banknotes in a referendum in September 2022, Switzerland will continue to not be a favorable place to issue products. However, interesting share-based certificate structures are still possible. The introduction of ledger-based rights will certainly give a boost to this industry. NFTs are still popular and, in most cases are not subject to Swiss financial market regulations, making Switzerland an interesting place to issue.Finally, linking decentralized autonomous organizations (DAOs) with Swiss associations has become very popular, as Swiss associations do not have controllable shares or shares, and associations are very flexible legal instruments. (Levin et al., 2022)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cryptocurrencies: Beyond the hype</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Since the world of cryptocurrencies is very much changing, fundamental questions are still open. Markets and technology are evolving, and the legal and regulatory framework is still in its infancy. Before jumping into crypto investing, we believe investment professionals should take a cautious, considered approach. Rather than taking definitive black-and-white positions, we believe that it is more valuable for our audience, which includes investors, policymakers, the media, and other people interested in crypto, to explain the main themes that emerged from the interviews we conducted. In this way, we can also convey the mix of insightful, but sometimes contradictory, ideas that have been conveyed to us. To make this diversity more manageable for the interested reader, let\'s start with two concise recommendations, one for policymakers and the other for investors. For the former, we suggest that the policy should be technology-neutral. Laws and regulations should not favor incumbents but rather allow startups with innovative technologies to challenge and compete with incumbents and infrastructure providers in traditional finance. However, politics should not jeopardize investor and consumer protection in the name of innovation or technological novelty. We emphasize the importance for investors to base investments on sound analysis. Mere novelty, not to mention hype and speculation, must not justify an investment, either in crypto assets or in more traditional assets.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As an introduction to the expert\'s view of the crypto market, we\'ll provide an overview of the crucial types of crypto assets and trading platforms, as well as a sense of size and scope. Despite their rapid rise, crypto assets remain relatively small compared to traditional assets.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Three main topics resonated with many of our interlocutors. First, there is the question of how to value crypto assets, which often elude traditional discounted cash flow analysis. Valuation questions, in turn, lead to an examination of crypto use cases, which may indicate emerging demand and potential scale. The second fundamental issue is whether crypto investments are compatible with fiduciary duty, a question that is of particular concern to pension fund investment professionals and regulators. We track the specific characteristics of crypto assets in relation to certain elements of fiduciary duty to illustrate the challenges that arise in fulfilling a fiduciary audit of a prudent investment process. Our third topic revolves around the challenge of securely storing crypto assets given their novel underlying technology. In the following, we reproduce some of the most important remarks made by our interviewees. The picture that emerges from this may seem like a hodgepodge to some. Still, we believe that it is best for our readers to present a mosaic of ideas rather than a logical or linear narrative that takes a point of view and neglects or discards others. We would like to conclude with a short series of key messages about some of the most fundamental issues that have emerged from our research and interviews, including the need for crypto investors to base their decisions on a solid investment argument. Examining cryptocurrency use cases, especially in the absence of cash flows, the need to look beyond the hype and distinguish the disruptive potential of crypto technology from the value of individual cryptocurrencies, as well as the need to assess the value of cryptocurrencies, and creating a strong regulatory framework that benefits both crypto providers and users. These questions, challenges, and puzzles will continue to occupy crypto industry professionals, investors, and policymakers, but they also make the topic of crypto investing so fascinating. (Deane &amp; Fines, 2023)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:37:35','2025-10-08 09:39:02'),(165,27,'Portfolio Management','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f5f68b83-7fff-d7e3-f597-8f5f83cb1087\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Portfolio management is the art and science of selecting and monitoring a group of investments that meet the long-term financial goals and risk tolerance of a client, company, or institution. Some individuals carry out their own portfolio management. This requires a fundamental understanding of the key elements of portfolio construction and maintenance that drive success, including asset allocation, diversification, and rebalancing.</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Managing an investment portfolio involves building and monitoring a selection of assets, such as stocks, bonds, and cash, that meet an investor\'s long-term financial goals and risk tolerance. Active portfolio management requires the strategic buying and selling of stocks and other assets in an attempt to outperform the broad market. Passive portfolio management attempts to achieve the market\'s returns by mimicking the composition of one or more indices. Investors can use strategies that aggressively seek profits, are conservatively focused on preserving capital, or are a mixture of both. Portfolio management requires clear long-term goals, clarity about the changes in tax legislation by the tax office, understanding of the investor\'s risk tolerance, and a willingness to deal with the investment opportunities. Professional, licensed asset managers work on behalf of their clients, while individuals can choose to build and manage their own portfolios. The ultimate goal of the asset manager is to maximize the expected return on investments at an appropriate level of risk. Portfolio management requires the ability to balance strengths and weaknesses, opportunities and risks across the investment spectrum. Trade-offs must be made in decisions, from debt to equities to domestic versus international investments, and growth versus security. Practice trading with virtual money. Find out what a theoretical investment would be worth today.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Passive versus active</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Portfolio management can be either passive or active. Passive management is a long-term strategy where you commit to one thing and forget about it. It can involve investing in one or more exchange-traded index funds (ETFs). This is commonly referred to as indexing or index investing. Those who build indexed portfolios can use modern portfolio theory (MPT) to optimize the mix. Active management seeks to outperform an index by actively buying and selling individual stocks and other assets. Closed-end funds are generally actively managed. Active managers can use a variety of quantitative or qualitative models to support their valuations of potential investments.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Active: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Investors who take an active management approach use fund managers or brokers to buy and sell stocks, trying to outperform a particular benchmark index, such as the Standard &amp; Poor\'s 500 Index or the Russell 1000 Index. In an actively managed mutual fund, a single portfolio manager, co-manager, or team of managers actively makes the investment decisions for the fund. The success of an actively managed fund depends on a combination of thorough research, market forecasts, and the expertise of the portfolio manager or management team. Portfolio managers who actively invest pay close attention to market trends, changes in the economy, changes in the political situation, and news that affects companies. This data is used to choose the time of purchase or sale of equipment in such a way that irregularities can be exploited. Active managers claim that these practices increase the potential for higher returns than simply replicating the holdings of a particular index. Trying to beat the market inevitably comes with additional market risk. Indexation eliminates this risk because human error is not possible when selecting stocks. Index funds are also traded less frequently, which means they have lower expense rates and are more tax-efficient than actively managed funds.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Passive: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Passive portfolio management, also known as index fund management, aims to track the return of a specific market index or benchmark. Managers buy the same stocks listed in the index with the same weighting that they represent in the index. A passive strategy portfolio can be built in the form of an exchange-traded fund (ETF), mutual fund, or mutual fund. Index funds are called passive because they have a portfolio manager whose job is to track the index instead of picking the assets bought or sold. Management fees for passive portfolios or funds tend to be much lower than for active management strategies.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Discretionary versus non-discretionary</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Another important element of portfolio management is the concept of discretionary and non-discretionary management. This approach to portfolio management determines what a third party is allowed to do in relation to your portfolio. Discretionary or non-discretionary management is only relevant if you have your portfolio managed by an independent broker. If you want the broker to only execute trades that you have specifically approved, you will need to opt for a non-discretionary investment account. The broker can advise you on the strategy and suggest investment decisions. However, without your consent, the broker is merely an advisor who must behave as you see fit. On the other hand, some investors prefer to put all decision-making in the hands of their broker or financial manager. In these cases, the financial advisor may buy or sell securities without the investor\'s consent. However, the investment adviser has a fiduciary duty to act in the best interests of the client when managing the portfolio.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Responsibilities of Asset Manager</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">An asset manager meets with a client for a face-to-face meeting to get a detailed picture of the client\'s current financial situation, long-term goals, and risk tolerance. Based on this, the portfolio manager can come up with a proposal on how the client can achieve their goals. If the client accepts the plan, the portfolio can be created by purchasing the selected assets. The client can deposit a lump sum at the beginning or increase the portfolio regularly, or both. The portfolio manager is responsible for monitoring the assets and making changes to the portfolio as necessary with the client\'s consent. Portfolio managers typically charge a fee for their service, which is based on the client\'s assets under management.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Asset allocation</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Asset allocation is the process of spreading the investor\'s money across different asset classes to reduce risks and maximize opportunities. The key to effective portfolio management is the long-term mix of assets. Generally, these are stocks, bonds, and cash equivalents such as certificates of deposit. However, there are also other investments that are often referred to as alternative investments, such as real estate, commodities, derivatives, and cryptocurrencies. Asset allocation is based on the recognition that the different types of assets do not move in unison with each other, and some are more volatile than others. A mix of assets provides balance and protects against risk. Investors with a more aggressive profile are weighting their portfolios toward more volatile investments such as growth stocks. Investors with a conservative profile weight their portfolios in more stable investments such as bonds and blue-chip stocks. The rebalancing capitalizes on recent gains and opens up new opportunities while keeping the portfolio in line with its original risk/reward profile.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Diversification</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Diversification involves owning assets and asset classes that have been shown to move in opposite directions over time. The only certainty about investing is that it is impossible to consistently predict winners and losers. A smart approach is to put together an asset basket that covers a broad spectrum within an asset class. Diversification is about spreading the risk and return of individual securities within an asset class or between asset classes. Because it\'s difficult to know which subset of one asset class or sector is likely to outperform another, diversification aims to capture the returns of all sectors over time while reducing volatility at any given time. True diversification takes place across different categories of securities, economic sectors, and geographical regions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Rebalancing</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Rebalancing is used to return a portfolio to its original target allocation at regular intervals, usually annually. This is done to restore the original mix of assets when the movements of the markets throw them out of balance. For example, a portfolio that starts out with 70% equities and 30% fixed income could transition to an 80/20 split after a prolonged market rally. The investor has made a good profit, but the portfolio now has a higher risk than the investor can accept. A rebalancing usually involves selling high-priced securities and putting that money into lower-valued and unpopular securities. The annual rebalancing allows the investor to take profits and increase growth opportunities in high-potential sectors while adjusting the portfolio to the original risk/reward profile.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Tax efficiency</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A potentially important aspect of portfolio management concerns how your portfolio is designed to minimize taxes in the long run. This concerns the way different retirement accounts are used, how long securities are held, and which securities are held. For example, keep in mind that certain bonds may be tax-free. This means that the dividends earned do not have to be taxed. On the other hand, the tax authority has different rules for taxing short-term or long-term capital gains. For people who earn less than $41,675 in 2023, the tax rate on capital gains may be $0. On the other hand, a short-term capital gains tax of 15% may apply if your income is above this IRS limit. Portfolio management includes investments in all forms of investment.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Typical strategies</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The specific situation of each investor is individual. While some investors are risk-averse, others tend to earn the highest returns and also take the most risk in the process. Broadly speaking, there are several common portfolio management strategies that an investor can consider.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Aggressive:</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">An aggressive portfolio focuses on maximizing potential returns. The investor often invests in riskier industries or untested alternative investments and does not worry about losses. Instead, the investor is looking for the \"home run\" investment, where he hits the bull\'s eye with a single investment.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Conservative:</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A conservative portfolio, on the other hand, is about capital preservation. Very risk-averse investors can pursue a portfolio management strategy that minimizes growth but also the risk of loss.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Moderate:</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;A moderate portfolio management strategy is a mix of an aggressive and a conservative approach. In an attempt to achieve the best of both worlds, a moderate portfolio will still invest heavily in stocks, but it will also diversify and may be more selective in its selection of these stocks.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Income-oriented:</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">This is often a consideration for older investors, because some people who have no income depend on their portfolio to generate income that they can live on. Remember that a retiree no longer has a stable income. However, this retiree may no longer be interested in creating wealth, but in using his existing wealth to live. This strategy favors fixed-income securities or stocks that pay dividends.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Tax-efficient:</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">As mentioned earlier, investors can tend to focus primarily on minimizing taxes, even if it comes at the expense of higher returns. This can be especially important for high earners who are in the highest capital gains tax bracket. This can also be a priority for young investors who still have a very long way to go before retirement. By entering a Roth IRA, these investors can grow their portfolio over their entire lives and do not have to pay federal taxes when they withdraw in retirement.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Challenges</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Regardless of the strategy chosen, portfolio management is always associated with some hurdles that often cannot be completely eliminated. Even if an investor has a completely safe portfolio management strategy, investment portfolios are subject to market fluctuations and volatility that can be unpredictable. Even the best management approach can lead to significant losses. While diversification is an important aspect of portfolio management, it can also be difficult to achieve. Finding the right mix of asset classes and investment products to achieve a balance between risk and return requires a deep understanding of the market and the risk tolerance of the individual investor. It can also be costly to buy a wide range of securities to achieve the desired diversification. To develop the best portfolio management strategy, an investor must first know their risk tolerance, investment horizon, and expected returns. This requires a clear short- and long-term goal. Because life circumstances can change quickly, investors need to be aware that some strategies limit the liquidity or flexibility of their investments. Also, the tax office can make changes to the tax legislation that may force a change in the final strategy. Finally, if an investor hires a portfolio manager to manage their investments, a management fee will be charged. The portfolio manager often has to comply with certain regulatory reporting requirements and may not have the same views or concerns about the market as you do.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Goals</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The goal of portfolio management is to create and maintain an individualized plan for long-term investments to achieve a person\'s key financial goals. This means selecting a mix of investments that match the person\'s tasks, goals, and risk tolerance. It also needs to reassess the actual performance of the portfolio over time to ensure it\'s on track and revise it if necessary.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Quintessence Conclusion</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Anyone who wants to increase their money is spoilt for choice. You can manage your own investment portfolio, or you can hire a professional manager to do it. You can choose a passive management strategy by investing your money in index funds. Or you can try to beat the markets by shifting your money from one investment to another more often.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:39:31','2025-10-08 09:40:33'),(166,27,'Risk Management for Cryptocurrencies','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-de0551dc-7fff-a55e-1d20-895921df8a37\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Guide to effective risk management</span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cryptocurrency risk management requires a systematic approach to identify, analyze, evaluate, and develop strategies to address risks associated with investing in digital assets. To effectively manage these risks, a structured risk management process must be followed. This chapter looks at the four basic steps of cryptocurrency risk management: risk identification, risk analysis, risk assessment, and treatment planning.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cryptocurrency Risk Management Steps</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Step: Risk identification</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The first phase of cryptocurrency risk management is about identifying the risks associated with investing in cryptocurrencies. This requires a comprehensive assessment of potential risks, which include factors such as market volatility, liquidity risk, cybersecurity risk, regulatory risk, and operational risk. Financial institutions can use various tools such as risk checklists, risk registers, and risk workshops to ensure thorough identification of risks and leave no stone unturned.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Step: Risk analysis of cryptocurrency risks</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Once the risks have been identified, the next step is to analyze each risk in detail. This analysis involves assessing the likelihood of the risk occurring and the potential impact it could have on the financial institution\'s portfolio. Quantitative and qualitative techniques such as scenario analyses, stress tests, and sensitivity analyses can be used for risk analysis. These techniques help identify the potential impact of different risk scenarios and evaluate the effectiveness of different risk mitigation strategies.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Step: Conduct a cryptocurrency risk assessment</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">After risk identification and analysis, a risk assessment is carried out in the next phase. It involves assigning a risk score to each identified risk based on its likelihood of occurrence and its potential impact on the financial institution\'s portfolio.&nbsp;Financial institutions can use a number of risk assessment scales to conduct risk assessments, such as the Probability-Impact Matrix or the Risk Heatmap. These tools help prioritize risks and identify risks that require immediate attention due to their importance.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Step: Develop a strategy to manage cryptocurrency risks</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The final step in the cryptocurrency risk management process is to develop a treatment plan for the identified risks. This includes formulating a comprehensive risk mitigation strategy that aims to minimize the likelihood and impact of each risk. Financial institutions can use various risk mitigation techniques, including risk avoidance, risk mitigation, risk transfer, and risk acceptance, to create an effective treatment plan. These techniques help ensure proper portfolio diversification and effective management of the risks associated with cryptocurrency investments.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">ResultConclusion</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">By following these four key steps—risk identification, risk analysis, risk assessment, and treatment planning—financial institutions can overcome the challenges associated with cryptocurrency investing and proactively manage potential risks. Implementing a solid risk management framework allows for informed decision-making and increases the overall stability and resilience of cryptocurrency portfolios. (Financial Crime Academy, 2023)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:56:25','2025-10-08 09:40:51'),(167,27,'Management of Crypto Investment Risks','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-1ed7614e-7fff-3238-1d54-9bfd7b2a36d1\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Key Points:</span></span></span></h3><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Like any investment, cryptocurrency comes with a number of risks, such as volatility, liquidity, operational, and cybersecurity risks.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Investors can take steps to mitigate these risks, such as by trading through reputable exchanges.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Investors are encouraged to do the necessary research and maintain a balanced portfolio to avoid over-focusing on one asset class.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Those who have been following last year\'s crypto news will have heard of FTX, which went bankrupt from being one of the largest cryptocurrency exchanges in the world. This was just one of many examples of a number of problems that service providers and exchanges have had to deal with recently. The losses were immense as individuals\' savings were at risk due to issues with these platforms. In addition, large amounts of cryptocurrencies have been lost due to simple mismanagement – for example, $181 million worth of Bitcoin, which was lost when its owner accidentally threw away the wrong hard drive. Although cryptocurrencies as an asset class offer diversification of the investment portfolio and access to emerging technologies that have the potential to revolutionize various industries, investors need to be aware of the risks associated with trading cryptocurrencies.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">1. Risk: Strong price fluctuations and volatility</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Cryptocurrencies are highly volatile, and their prices can fluctuate dramatically within short periods of time. This volatility can lead to significant gains but also significant losses; there is even a risk of losing all the capital. While price fluctuations are common with any investment, they are even more pronounced with cryptocurrencies due to the still young nature of the asset class and investor sentiment swings resulting from the evolution of regulations, industry news, and media hype. To illustrate this volatility, the cryptocurrency market peaked at around $3 trillion in 2021 but fell drastically to below $1 trillion in 2022. Risk management options:One way to mitigate the risk of investing in cryptocurrencies is to diversify the portfolio and avoid concentrating your investments on a single investment vehicle. In addition, as with any investment, it is important that you do your own research. At the very least, this means that you should know (a) how long the token has existed, (b) what the market cap is, and (c) how it could be used in the real world—for example, for online payments or as a store of value.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">2. Risk: Liquidity risk</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">An investment classified as illiquid means that investors may run into problems when trying to buy, sell, or convert it into cash. This problem is particularly evident in lesser-known cryptocurrencies. Due to their limited trading activity, these currencies could have higher price volatility, creating difficulties for investors trying to liquidate their holdings without paying unfavorable prices. Investors may also temporarily lose access to their crypto investments if there is unexplained or prolonged downtime of trading platforms or if exchanges temporarily suspend crypto deposits or withdrawals, such as if they want to perform maintenance on the platform. This poses a risk to investors who want to buy/sell/access their crypto assets during this period. Risk management options:One way to reduce liquidity risk is to trade higher-cap crypto assets. These are likely to be more popular and therefore more liquid. You can also use multiple exchanges to access liquidity through different platforms, avoiding being locked out of trading by the downtime of a single exchange.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">3. Risk: Operational risk from the custody of cryptocurrencies</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A unique feature of cryptocurrencies compared to other asset classes is that they allow any person to self-custody the asset. This eliminates the need to entrust custody to an external custodian. However, greater control over the asset comes with a greater risk of mismanagement of private keys (private keys are used to access self-custody cryptocurrencies). For example, self-custody requires a person to have the expertise and willingness to manage the private key through adequate backups and secured physical storage locations. With self-custodial keys, any cryptocurrencies secured by the key set will be lost if access to the private keys is lost. While private keys managed by third parties typically have recourse to lost credentials (e.g., when users forget their credentials for these crypto platforms), users must trust that the third-party provider has proper controls and security measures in place to protect their assets. Therefore, it is important for cryptocurrency investors to be aware of the various risks that depend on the type of custody they choose. Risk management options:Investors must ensure that they keep their private keys safe or strive to store them properly with a trusted custodian. Unlike non-custodial wallets, where the loss of keys means the total loss of funds, a custodial wallet allows you to recover lost credentials. You can also diversify your retention options by using different custodians and approaches (non-custodial and custodial).</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">4. Risk: Fraud, theft and cybersecurity risks</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A crypto hack occurs when hackers gain unauthorized access to your wallets and steal your cryptocurrencies. This risk is higher with hot wallets because they are connected to the internet. Cryptocurrency exchanges are popular targets for cybercriminals—the lack of a regulatory framework and the anonymity of crypto transactions make them vulnerable to cybercrime. An example of a cybersecurity incident is the Binance security breach in May 2019, where hackers stole more than $40 million worth of Bitcoin. The hackers used a variety of techniques, including phishing and viruses, to obtain a large amount of user data that gave them access to move Bitcoin off the network. Fortunately, the exchange had set aside funds for such incidents and was able to minimize the impact on customers. In addition to direct hacks, fraudulent use of cryptocurrencies that you have stored with an exchange is also a potential risk. For example, the founders of FTX were accused of fraudulently using customer funds to fund other business and political activities. Risk management options:Similar to losing access to your wallet, it\'s important that the storage of your digital assets is as secure as possible. To protect yourself from the bankruptcy of an exchange, choose an exchange that has a credible reputation and provides segregated accounts to its investors. When you use a custodial wallet, choose a trusted company to run the platform because they manage the private keys for your cryptocurrencies (they hold the keys to your funds).</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A trusted custodian has:</span></span></span></p><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Sufficient security measures.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Proven good risk management.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A good financial situation that minimizes the risk of bankruptcy.</span></span></span></p></li></ol><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Like all investments, cryptocurrency trading comes with risks. Investors need to be aware of these risks and take the necessary steps to mitigate them. Due to the uncertainty facing the cryptocurrency industry, investors should do their own research and maintain a balanced portfolio without putting all their eggs in one basket. (DBS, 2023)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-10 12:57:16','2025-10-08 09:41:19'),(168,27,'Successfully Using Volatile Crypto Markets','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-bac588a4-7fff-7b48-8c9f-1a244e9e0744\"><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Mastering risk management is key to success in crypto trading.</span></span></span></span></span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In the fast-paced world of crypto trading, understanding and mastering the art of risk management is not only a prudent decision but the be-all and end-all of survival. Risk management in crypto trading is more than a mere concept; the compass guides traders through the volatility of the crypto market. This comprehensive article looks at risk management in crypto trading, from the basic principles to advanced techniques used by experienced traders. Discover how to navigate crypto risk management and participate in the crypto market safely and profitably. From identifying and understanding the various risks in the crypto market to executing tactical decisions that manage risk in crypto trading, this guide will equip you with the insights and tools you need to succeed in the dynamic world of crypto trading.</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:-3pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">What is crypto risk management?</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;padding:5pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Crypto risk management is the foundation on which successful trading strategies in the volatile crypto markets are built. It is the systematic approach that traders use to identify, assess, and mitigate the risks associated with their investment decisions in the crypto market. Essentially, it is a fundamental concept of risk management in crypto trading that aims to preserve capital and increase profitability. The crypto trading risk management area includes a set of crypto trading risk management strategies, each tailored to the preferences of different traders, a range of disciplines, and risk tolerance levels. These strategies include:</span></span></span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: norm