llets</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Marketplaces—SuperRare: Marketplace for Digital Art</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">SuperRare - Digital Art Marketplace Rarible: Digital Collectibles Marketplace. Trade on Rarible to farm RARI tokens</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">OpenSea—P2P marketplace for all NFTs</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">DeFi—Aavegotchi: Owning and trading avatars backed by interest-bearing tokens that represent loans on the DeFi lending platform Aave</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">NFTfi: Using NFTs as collateral for a loan</span></span></span></p></li></ul></span>\n\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-12 07:42:36','2025-10-08 11:39:21'),(238,38,'Tokenization at a glance','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-24585c9d-7fff-e13c-45cf-31305533b8af\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In the financial markets, distributed ledger and blockchain technologies are often associated with the idea of cryptocurrencies. However, these digital means of payment represent only a small part of the universe of financial instruments that are now commonly referred to as \"digital assets\" and have in common that they are based on \"distributed ledger technology\" or \"DLT.\" However, one of the most attractive features of this technology is that it opens the door to a welcome modernization of the way securities and financial products are issued, held, and transferred, as well as the way companies interact with investors. The procedure for issuing and transferring securities (e.g., shares of private companies) today is little different from what was common two centuries ago: shares and other transferable securities are issued in the form of physical certificates and transferred by manually handing over documents with assignments and ink-on-paper signatures. Not issuing certificates (as some companies do) is hardly an adequate alternative, as it exposes the acquirer to the risk of multiple assignments and causes them to lose sight of the rightful owner of a particular security. Publicly traded securities are typically held in custody by custodians and transferred by debiting and crediting custodial accounts, but the cost of holding such \"intermediary\" securities with custodians and CSDs is significant. DLT represents a quantum leap in this context, as it allows securities (and other financial instruments) to be linked to digital tokens recorded on a distributed ledger (typically a blockchain) instead of physical certificates. The transfer of such \"tokenized\" securities is timestamped, publicly available on the ledger, and cannot be forged, with the personal data of the respective holders protected by cryptographic means. Since DLT makes it technically impossible to transfer the same digital token twice to a distributed ledger, the transfer of a particular tokenized security can always be traced. Digital tokens can be held either by their owners themselves (through the control of so-called \"private keys\") or by professional custodians, just like traditional intermediary securities. It is to the credit of the Swiss federal authorities that they recognized the potential of DLT for the financial sector at an early stage and adopted legislation that provides a clear and reliable legal framework for the digitization of financial instruments. According to Swiss legislation, often referred to as \"Lex DLT,\" financial instruments of Swiss or foreign issuers can be linked to digital tokens created using a digital code called a \"smart contract\" and recorded on a distributed ledger (public or private) such as the Ethereum or Tezos blockchain. Industry associations such as the Capital Markets and Technology Association have also adopted standards to facilitate the issuance, trading and custody of such digitized financial instruments.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The consequences of advancing digitization are profound. Tokenization simplifies the way securities can be issued, transferred, held, or admitted to trading, as well as the way companies can raise capital to fund their activities. But the digitization of securities also opens up opportunities that go beyond simply replicating existing capital market infrastructures. The digital code that governs tokenized securities may be equipped with features unknown to traditional securities, such as automating certain corporate actions (e.g., dividend or interest payments) or managing stock plans (e.g., vesting, exercising, or forfeiting stock grants to directors or employees). Digitalization can also facilitate the implementation of mechanisms used in private equity transactions (e.g., the \"drag along\" or \"call\" functions regularly encountered in shareholder agreements) or the implementation of certain compliance processes such as the identification of security holders or beneficial owners. Tokenization opens the door to a wide universe of new opportunities that the financial industry is only just beginning to grasp and exploit. With well-thought-out and flexible legislation that creates an explicit legal basis for the digitization process, Switzerland is well positioned to take advantage of the opportunities offered by the new technology. Its flexible and DLT-friendly legal framework also allows it to become the location of financial intermediaries and trading platforms that are organized to take full advantage of DLT in the financial sector.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:44:31','2025-10-08 11:40:20'),(239,38,'What is tokenization?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-91e0305f-7fff-6d13-6b04-100d609ae3cc\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Tokenization is simply the process of digitizing securities and registering them on a distributed ledger such as a blockchain. It involves creating digital tokens that are linked to or represent a security, for example:</span></span></span></p><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Shares,</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Profit participation certificates,</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Debt securities</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Units in collective investment schemes (i.e., funds) Structured products</span></span></span></p></li></ol><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Tokenization can be seen as the representation of traditional securities as digital assets, also known as ledger-based securities. Importantly, in Switzerland (CMTA, n.d.): Tokenization does not lead to the creation of new types of assets. Tokenized shares are—and will remain—shares of the company that issued them. A company can only tokenize shares that already exist, i.e., shares must be issued in accordance with Swiss corporate law before they can be tokenized;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Tokenized shares do not constitute a new category of shares under Swiss law.\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter5/9.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"><br></span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0ea0ecdf-7fff-a354-3b0a-d5c3c679c32f\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 1: Digitization of private assets—an opportunity for several trillions</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/NY.GDP.MKTP.CD, https://focus.world-exchanges.org/articles/market-capitalisation, https://www.icmagroup.org/market-practice-and-regulatory-policy/secondar-markets/bond-market-size/)</span>\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Put simply, there are two main value chains in the world of securities:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Listed Markets | Listed capital markets: Consisting of listed securities. These include, for example, large companies that are listed on the stock exchange or are seeking an IPO; Private markets: Consisting of the rest of the securities. These include, for example, Taurus, QoQqa, Bank Cité Gestion, or any small and medium-sized enterprises (\"SMEs\") you can find in your area.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">It is interesting to note that there are 27 million companies in the European Union and the United Kingdom, of which only about 8,500 are listed on the stock exchange. This means that there are 3,000 times more private companies than publicly traded companies. All companies in the world must have share capital. Many are very small (2-3 person operations) with a stable shareholder base (think of your bakery next door) and do not need to carry out large financial activities or have their shares digitized. However, many others need to grow and attract talent: they need to finance themselves through capital increases or bonds. They may also need to implement employee stock ownership plans (stocks, stock options, etc.). According to Eurostat, a significant number of 177,000 companies are considered to be fast-growing. We believe that tokenization can be helpful for a large portion of these companies. Tokenization has great potential in the private markets value chain, unlike the listed capital markets. The former is largely paper-based; it can take weeks or months to transfer shares of a private company, while the latter, contrary to what some think, is fairly well standardized and works relatively well. Tokenization could open up previously unimagined worlds for private assets, similar to how the internet and e-commerce have transformed many industries over the past two decades. In the next few years, buying or selling shares in a private company should be as easy as buying a book on Amazon, because (i) the technology exists and (ii) there is regulation, as the next section shows.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span>\n</div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:45:29','2025-10-08 11:41:06'),(240,38,'Overview of the regulatory framework','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-4f70cb19-7fff-c069-4ca6-8a6421f107e8\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Asset tokenization is not yet possible everywhere in the world. However, most financial centers are increasingly adopting a clearer legal framework for digital assets. Issuers must ensure that the country or jurisdiction in which they are based recognizes ledger-based securities in their law. Figure 2 below provides an overview of the major financial centers and their respective regulatory frameworks regarding digital assets in general.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Germany:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The Electronic Securities Act, which came into force in June 2021, reforms German securities law. Among other things, it enables the launch of a new form of electronic securities that can be booked in a crypto securities registry, which is another name for distributed ledgers. Also, the services of the crypto securities registry are a financial service that is subject to licensing.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Luxembourg:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The law of 1 March 2019 had recognized the possibility of holding and registering non-denominated securities in securities custody accounts via DLT. The law of 22 January 2021 allowed the issuance of Luxdematerialized securities (listed or unlisted) on distributed ledgers. On 20 February 2023, the Luxembourg Chamber voted on draft law 8055, which transposed the EU pilot regulation into local law and further clarified the above points.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Switzerland:</span></span></b></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Switzerland was the first Tier 1 financial center in the world to create a clear regulatory framework for digital assets and tokenized securities (see below).\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter5/10.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 2: Overview of the main financial centres and their respective regulatory frameworks</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Source: BCG Analysis)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><b style=\"font-weight:normal;\" id=\"docs-internal-guid-81c6b87e-7fff-2116-b9a5-6a8661d33380\"><br></b></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Why Tokenize—Advantages</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The tokenization of securities offers a variety of advantages, depending on your point of view. Electronic, programmable, and non-intermediary format: the transfer of securities is instantaneous, and functions can be programmed directly into the security (whitelisting, freezing, unfreezing, destroying, restoring, etc.). Instant posting and settlement: This means that issuers can book their securities with banks (if they wish) and settlement.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Simplified trading: Thanks to electronic trading, issuers can easily provide liquidity to their shareholders or employees, possibly around the clock.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Price discovery mechanisms are significantly improved when issuers admit their securities to trading on a regulated market.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Costs: The financial and operational costs remain manageable. In addition, there are the costs of the annual reports required for the admission of securities to trading on a regulated market.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">For the avoidance of doubt, companies that are admitted to trading on a regulated market such as an organized trading facility (as defined in Swiss law) remain private companies. These costs are therefore a fraction of what listed companies have to raise.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Public transparency: The price to pay for trading on a regulated market is to accept that the financial statements will be published.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Legal aspects: The tokenization of shares increases the level of security that the acquirer of such instruments can put in the fact that they are actually recognized as their legal owner. The holder of a tokenized security cannot transfer this instrument twice. The buyer of such instruments can therefore trust that the seller was actually the owner of the transferred securities. This is a key difference from traditional unsecuritized securities (such as the shares of a company for which no physical share certificates have been issued). In the case of a traditional non-securitized security, the acquirer acquires a title to the instrument transferred only if the transferor himself had such a title. This is generally difficult to prove. This requires proof of an uninterrupted chain of assignments between all persons who have owned the security since the date of initial issue. Evidence of such an uninterrupted chain of transmissions is often lacking. The buyer can then only hope that the seller owned the transferred securities. In the case of a tokenized security, the buyer has certainty about this, and Swiss law recognizes the legal claim of the purchaser of the token to the associated security.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Funding models: As mentioned earlier, tokenization allows unlisted private companies to take advantage of new funding and investment models. Tokenization allows them to open their capital to investors in various ways and through different channels, such as regulated digital platforms. Until now, investors had few opportunities to invest in these companies and could only access publicly traded companies. Tokenization could thus contribute to the modernization and democratization of finance by making investments easier and more accessible to the average investor. In the last section, you will find a use case where Qoqa Services Limited has absorbed CHF 1.2 million from its customer base within 19 minutes. Also note that a company with a bad business model and poor business results will remain a bad company even if it is tokenized.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Cost savings: Tokenization can also reduce operational and financial costs, both for businesses and investors. The acquisition and transfer of tokenized shares is direct and immediate, while the transfer of an uncertificated security can take weeks or even months:</span></span></span></p></li><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Faster execution of transactions that may only be a matter of seconds.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Fewer intermediaries and therefore lower costs. Tokenization also allows companies to automate certain contractual tasks and corporate actions through smart contracts.</span></span></span></p></li></ul></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Asset universe eligible for tokenization:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">This tokenization process is not limited to stocks. It can work for assets such as commodities, real estate, debt, structured products, and funds, as well as certain forms of intangible assets such as property rights or content licenses. Regardless of the asset class, tokenization increases the level of security with which a holder is actually recognized as the rightful owner. Potential buyers can rest assured that the seller actually owns the securities offered for sale. This is a significant change compared to traditional uncertificated securities, as the acquirer only acquires title to the transferred instrument if the transferor itself owns such a title, which may be difficult to prove. You may need to prove an unbroken chain of assignments. (Taurus Report, 2023)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">\n</span></span><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:47:20','2025-10-08 11:42:12'),(241,38,'Understanding the Tokenization Landscape','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-5f1e931f-7fff-2546-83ec-450d1f3f670a\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">On-chain asset tokenization offers the opportunity to remove many of these obstacles to asset illiquidity, as well as the current modality of traditional fractionation. On-chain asset tokenization helps reshape the entire process of finding and matching investors with investment opportunities, as well as the subsequent opportunities of the secondary market after an investment. This is a process in which an issuer mints digital tokens (each representing a fraction of an underlying digital/physical asset) on a distributed ledger (i.e., a blockchain), thereby guaranteeing transparent and immutable ownership. There are essentially two types of tokenized assets:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">a) Fungible tokenized assets are interchangeable and divisible, meaning each unit of the tokenized asset has the same market value and validity and can be divided into as many parts as were configured at issue (e.g., fiat, tokenized securities, cryptocurrency, gold). and</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;b) Non-fungible tokenized assets are unique and non-exchangeable, i.e., tokens cannot be replaced by other tokens of the same type, as each token represents a unique value and attribute (e.g., old paintings or records, residential property, or collector cards). Figure 6 shows the existing and emerging tokenization landscape. However, a shift from traditional fractionalization to on-chain tokenization is imminent, broadening the range of asset classes, stakeholders, and regulatory opportunities for tokenization. Therefore, it is important to understand and appreciate the added value of fractionalizing assets on blockchain-based platforms.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">There are clear differences between the landscapes of traditional fractionation and on-chain tokenization today:</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter5/11.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\">\n</span></span><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-c40ae949-7fff-8bdb-31e8-0a43f623c51e\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 3: Comparison of traditional fractionation and on-chain tokenization</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: BCG Analysis)</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The mechanics of on-chain asset tokenization and its advantages over traditional fractionation. The end-to-end process of on-chain tokenization of assets involves five key steps:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Ecosystem Assembly: Service providers ensure that the integration of the technology is done smoothly with a large ecosystem of providers, allowing issuers to create a customized end-to-end solution (e.g., custody, KYC/AML providers, legal, marketing, consulting, tax, etc.)</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Register Underlying &amp; Configure Token: The asset is registered and made available for tokenization on the blockchain network. Once the fundraising is structured and the ecosystem is mapped, issuers can configure their tokens in a simple and intuitive way, regardless of the type of asset. The number of assets to be registered on the platform is a decision made in coordination between the issuer and the platform provider. The assets are usually publicly visible, but some are also traded in an invite-only auction or through a select group of approved brokerage dealers.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Set compliance rules: These compliance rules are coded into the smart contract and allow for faster processing and lower protocol fees that can scale as demand and complexity of regulation grow. Issuers have the flexibility to determine who is allowed to hold the token, how many investors are allowed to hold the token, and how it can be transferred.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Store, manage, and distribute tokens: Tokens are stored in a software vault and supported by a custodial service to manage digital twins (i.e., to maintain the connection between an existing asset and its digital representation token). Tokenization service providers provide issuers with an automated and reportable way to manage initial token distribution as well as future distribution events. Issuers assign a broker-dealer to all clients on the platform. Customers can trade with each other. If the issuer wants to make the platform accessible to as many investors as possible, a large marketing campaign followed by an auction is required.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: nowrap; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Execute Corporate Actions: Allows the issuer to enter some details and create a corporate action for which the engine determines permissions, schedules communication, distributes capital (if necessary), and updates records. Tokenization significantly reduces the cost of these corporate actions.\n<img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter5/12.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\">\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 4: Mechanisms of on-chain tokenization of assets</span></span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: BCG Analysis)</span></span>\n<img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter5/13.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\">\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 5: Schematic mechanisms Tokenization through the lifecycle of assets across all stakeholders</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(Source: Global Legal Insights, Clifford Chance Report, Charlton Quantum Report, BCG Analysis)</span>\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">On-chain asset tokenization offers six distinct advantages over traditional fractionalization:</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -13.5pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Improves affordability by enabling investments in divisible, fractional assets of high-priced instruments (e.g., hedge funds, alternatives)</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -13.5pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Enables cross-border accessibility by enabling the listing of previously illiquid assets (e.g., natural resources, land, old paintings) subject to local regulations in each jurisdiction and seamless trading on the secondary market</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -13.5pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Creates liquidity and increases flexibility by enabling the trading of assets before maturity (e.g., future yields from agricultural land). Network nodes (e.g., tokenization of government infrastructure projects as public property rights, improved tax refund)</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -13.5pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Streamline transaction efficiency by</span></span></span></p></li><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -27pt;padding-left: 86.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">(a) enabling higher transaction speeds at lower prices due to improved cost-effectiveness in the transfer of assets with smart contracts to enable the automation of exchanges;</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -27pt;padding-left: 86.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">b) Reducing friction by ensuring that a single KYC is sufficient for all investments/platforms by linking users\' wallets to the blockchain,</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -27pt;padding-left: 86.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">c) Profit from asset servicing, i.e., the ability to distribute token holders without having to go through transfer agents/3rd party custodians and custodians during the life of the asset, and</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -27pt;padding-left: 86.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">d) Reducing settlement times with blockchain to overcome DvP inefficiencies.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:9pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;margin-left: -13.5pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Ensures better pricing of illiquid assets as</span></span></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-left: 95.35pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Immutable transparency and a blockchain-powered platform is relieved of accountability by providing a clear historical and current transaction record and an immutable assignment/record of property rights governed by smart contracts on a shared ledger on a distributed P2P process by helping to reduce rent-seeking by intermediaries (e.g., auction houses, asset management companies) (Suresh et al., 2022).</span></span></span></p></li></ul></span></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:49:10','2025-10-08 11:44:31'),(242,38,'Types of Tokenized Assets','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0bb911fd-7fff-99a8-ac45-cec7fb4e9cc6\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">There are a variety of options when it comes to tokenized assets. Most of them have yet to be researched. We\'ve seen bonds, gold, and certain types of agricultural products converted into tokens, but that\'s just the tip of the iceberg. The different types of assets and products that can and will be converted into tokens would require a separate treatise, but to give you an idea of what can be achieved through this innovation, we will give some examples from the real estate sector to give you a better idea.</span></span></span></p><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Real Estate Crowdfunding Tokens:</span></span></span></p></li><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Community-driven investments: Enable local communities to invest in neighborhood projects, fostering a sense of ownership and commitment.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Micro-investments: Allow investors to participate in real estate projects with very small amounts.</span></span></span></p></li></ol><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Income-generating tokens:</span></span></span></p></li><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Rent-sharing tokens: Investors receive a share of the rental income proportional to their token ownership.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Dividend-paying tokens: Similar to stocks, these tokens pay dividends from the profits generated by the underlying assets.</span></span></span></p></li></ol><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Asset-Backed Stablecoins:</span></span></span></p></li><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 