sition: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Mineral Rights Tokens: Own a share in the mineral rights of a property.</span></span></span></p></li></ol><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Sustainability and ESG tokens:</span></span></span></p></li><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Green building tokens: Invest in real estate that meets high environmental standards.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Community Impact Tokens: Support projects with a positive social impact and earn returns.</span></span></span></p></li></ol><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Tokenized real estate funds:</span></span></span></p></li><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Diversified real estate fund tokens: Invest in a diversified portfolio of real estate through a single token.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"2\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Thematic real estate fund tokens: Participate in funds that focus on specific themes such as smart cities, co-working spaces, or sustainable living.</span></span></span></p></li></ol></ol><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Conclusion:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">By leveraging blockchain and tokenization, the industry can create a wide range of financial products that provide greater accessibility, liquidity, and innovation, ultimately democratizing access to investment and unlocking value for investors worldwide. Tokenization will revolutionize all aspects of financial life as we know it in the near future, creating secure, trustless, and transparent environments for investors and consumers alike. Your data will be tokenized; your concert ticket and rental agreement will be NFTs. Tokenization is the rapidly approaching future, and those who understand and accept these facts will be better positioned to survive and thrive in the new, fully digital economy that is emerging and being implemented before our eyes. (Sleep et al., 2023)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,1,70,'2025-09-12 07:50:57','2025-10-08 11:45:04'),(243,39,'AI (Artificial Intelligence) Definition','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-734a07ec-7fff-99dd-ba31-8c687785e0b9\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Artificial intelligence can be defined as a field of study that deals with the development of systems that act and think like humans. This definition covers every definition of artificial intelligence that can be found in the literature. It offers four different faces of artificial intelligence, which will be explained in the next section. This means that artificial intelligence programs/systems are programs/systems that act like a human, think like a human, act rationally, and think rationally. Each of the four faces of artificial intelligence, as stated in the definition, is explained using a suitable model. Each model is used to explain each of the following facets of artificial intelligence: acting like a human, thinking like a human, acting rationally, and thinking rationally.</span></span></span></p><br></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:51:46','2025-10-08 11:45:33'),(244,39,'Turing Test Model—Act Like a Human','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-7fa219c9-7fff-f6a8-01ec-e0209d0ceaba\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The Turing test model explains what it means to act like a human. In 1958, Alan Turing proposed a test model that would help people understand what it means to act like a human. The test that Alan Turing proposed consisted of a computer being interrogated by a human being by teletype. The computer passed the test without knowing whether the questioner was a machine or a human answering the questions. However, the full Turing test also includes a video signal that tests the subject\'s perceptual ability, as well as the exchange of physical objects between the questioner and the subject. Alan Turing therefore defined a person\'s behavior as intelligent behavior. A machine/human that behaves intelligently is a machine that achieves a performance at the level of a human when it comes to cognitive questions. In order for a computer to achieve the intelligence of a human, it must have the following skills or requirements. The ability to communicate in a natural language, such as English, French, etc. The ability to store information before or during interrogation. The ability to use the stored information to answer questions and draw a new conclusion. In artificial intelligence, this is called automatic closing. The ability to adapt to new circumstances based on new data, it discovers the pattern in the data and makes an appropriate decision. Also, passing the entire Turing test requires additional skills, namely:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The ability to perceive hearing, taste, sight, touch, and smell with the sensory organs. The ability to move objects. In artificial intelligence, this is called robotics.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Intelligence</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Based on the above requirements or capabilities of an intelligent system, we can use any requirement of an intelligent system to understand the various aspects or tasks that an artificial intelligence system can perform. Below are the tasks that an artificial intelligence system can perform. Natural Language Processing: This task allows an artificial intelligence system to communicate in natural language, e.g. English.</span></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Knowledge Representation: This task allows an artificial intelligence system to use a specific method/formalism to store knowledge about a specific area. This is known as the knowledge base of an expert system.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Automated reasoning: This task allows an artificial intelligence system to query the stored knowledge in order to find an answer to the user\'s query.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Machine Learning: This task allows an artificial intelligence system to solve a problem with the help of a series of data. A number of training data are stored.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Sensory perception: This task enables artificial intelligence to solve a problem by using the sensory perceptions for seeing, touching, hearing, tasting, and smelling.</span></span></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 77.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Robotics: This aspect allows artificial intelligence to solve a problem by moving itself or objects from one place to another.</span></span></span></p></li></ul><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Cognitive Model—Thinking Like a Human</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">If we want to say that a certain program thinks like a human, we have to be able to determine in some way how people think. We need to penetrate into the actual workings of the human brain. There are two ways to do this: through introspection—by trying to grasp our own thoughts—or through psychological experiments. Once we have a sufficiently precise theory of mind, it is possible to express this theory in the form of a computer program. Cognitive science combines computer models from artificial intelligence with experimental techniques from psychology to create precise and testable theories about the functioning of the human mind.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Rational Agent Model - Rational Action</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">An agent is someone who perceives and acts to achieve their goal. Rational action therefore means acting like an agent. Artificial intelligence is therefore considered the study and construction of rational agents. One of the ways to act rationally is to draw a correct conclusion by applying the law of thought.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Law of Thought - Rational Thinking</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The law of thought helps to explain what rational thinking means. It means right thinking, i.e., if the right prerequisites (facts) are given, it always leads to the right conclusion. The law of thought was developed by the Greek philosopher Aristotle. It marked the beginning of logic, which is very important for artificial intelligence.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Basic discipline of artificial intelligence</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Artificial intelligence is a young field of research, but it uses many ideas, viewpoints, and techniques from various ancient disciplines. This section looks at the different ideas, viewpoints, and techniques that artificial intelligence takes up from the various ancient disciplines. They form the foundation on which artificial intelligence stands.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Philosophy</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The theories of thinking and learning that artificial intelligence uses have emerged from philosophy. It began with the writings of Plato, his teacher Socrates, and his pupil Aristotle. Socrates wanted to know the characteristics of piety in order to find out about the standards by which he could judge his actions and the actions of other people. In other words, he asked about the algorithm that can be used to distinguish between piety and non-piety. In response to this, Aristotle formulated the law that regulates the rational part of the mind. He developed the informal system of the syllogism for correct reasoning, which can be used to draw conclusions from the original premises. Aristotle, however, did not believe that all parts of the mind are controlled by logical processes; he also had an idea of intuitive thinking. Philosophy had thus established the tradition that the mind was conceived as a physical device that functions primarily through thought and the knowledge it contains. In the theory of knowledge, which uses artificial intelligence, philosophy identified the source of knowledge using the following principles. The principle of induction, which states that general rules are acquired through repeated associations between their elements. This principle has been refined by the principle of logical positivism, which states that all knowledge can be characterized by logical theories, which are ultimately linked to observational sentences that arise from sensory impressions. Philosophy, which still adheres to the philosophical image of the mind, has also established a connection between knowledge and action. Artificial intelligence is interested in what this connection looks like and how certain actions can be justified. Because if you understand how actions are justified, it will be possible to develop an agent of artificial intelligence with justified actions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Mathematics</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Artificial intelligence uses mathematical tools as formal tools in the following three main areas of mathematics: computation, logic, and probability. In artificial intelligence, calculations can be expressed as formal algorithms, while logic has remained a formal language for representing knowledge in artificial intelligence. Probability allows us to draw logical conclusions and measure the degree of certainty/uncertainty in our conclusions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Psychology</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The principle of cognitive psychology states that the brain possesses and processes information. The theory of human behavior in psychology states that its valid components are beliefs, goals, and reasoning steps. In the early days of artificial intelligence and cognitive science, however, no significant distinction was usually made between the two areas. It was common practice to refer to artificial intelligence programs as psychological outcomes without claiming that they accurately model human behavior. In the last ten years, however, the methodological distinctions have become clearer, and most of the work can now be assigned to one or the other area.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Computer engineering</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">In reality, artificial intelligence belongs to the field of computer science or computer technology. If artificial intelligence is a discipline in its own right, ideas, viewpoints and techniques from computer science or computer engineering must be used for artificial intelligence to be successful.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Linguistics</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Much of the early work on knowledge representation (the study of how knowledge can be put into a form that a computer can handle) was related to language and was influenced by research in linguistics. Modern linguistics and artificial intelligence were \"born\" around the same time, so linguistics does not play a major role in the development of artificial intelligence. Instead, the two grew up together and overlapped in a hybrid field called computational linguistics or natural language processing, which focuses on the problem of language use.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Inference</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Artificial intelligence has been defined and explained in this lesson. Based on this definition and explanation, we can easily identify artificial intelligence systems. Artificial intelligence is an interdisciplinary subject that has something in common with other fields such as mathematics, psychology, philosophy, linguistics, computer engineering, etc.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:53:15','2025-10-08 11:46:38'),(245,39,'History of Artificial Intelligence and Projection for the Future','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-b34d1b29-7fff-a90f-e9ef-732a3ec5e7c7\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The history of artificial intelligence focuses on people, their important contributions, and the date of their contribution to the development of artificial intelligence. This is very useful because it helps us to identify those who have made an important contribution to the development of artificial intelligence. On the other hand, the future projections examine the new and future research directions of artificial intelligence.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The birth of artificial intelligence</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">John McCarthy was the first to coin the term \"artificial intelligence\" in 1956 at a conference of the same name held at Dartmouth College in Hanover, New Hampshire. One of the participants in the conference who was very optimistic about the future of artificial intelligence was Marvin Minsky from MIT. However, even before this time, there were already several research projects that contributed to the emergence of artificial intelligence. One of these researches was conducted by Vannevar Bush in 1945. Another research was conducted in 1950 by Alan Turing, which helped to understand what an intelligence system means. Alan Turing\'s research in 1950 led to the popular Turing test model, which was used to explain what it means to act like a human. The birth of artificial intelligence cannot therefore be complete without taking into account the life of Alan Turing, who made an important contribution to the birth of artificial intelligence.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Alan Turing (1912 - 1954)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">He was a British mathematician who, although he lived for a short time, made a significant contribution to the development of computer technology in general and artificial intelligence in particular. In 1936, he developed a universal calculating machine, the so-called Turing machine. He proved that the calculating machine is capable of solving any problem, as long as it can be represented and solved as an algorithm. A few decades later, the first digital computer was built. Turing\'s electromechanical computer was used to decipher the code used by the German U-boats in the Atlantic, contributing to British victory in World War II. In 1950, Alan Turing developed a test to determine whether a machine was intelligent. This test has been called the Turing test model and is used by the artificial intelligence community to explain what it means to behave like a human.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Other important contributions before the birth of AI</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Below are other significant systems of artificial intelligence that emerged before the birth of artificial intelligence in 1956: Ebruİz Bin Rezzaz Al Jezeri, one of the pioneers of cybernetic science, built water-powered, automatically controlled machines in 1206. Karel Capek first introduced the concept of the robot in 1923 in the play Rossum\'s Universal Robots (RUR). The first artificial intelligence programs for the Mark 1 device were written in 1951.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Historical development of other artificial intelligence systems</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Since the birth of artificial intelligence in 1956, various systems of artificial intelligence have been developed, which can be divided into the following epochs:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Expert system (1950s - 1970s)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Expert systems as a subfield of AI emerged in the early 1950s, when the Rand-Carnegie team developed the general problem solver to tackle theorem proofs, geometric problems, and the game of chess. Around the same time, LISP, which later became the dominant programming language for artificial intelligence and expert systems, was invented by John McCarthy at MIT. In the 1960s and 1970s, expert systems were increasingly used in industrial applications. Some of the most well-known applications from this period were DENDRAL (a chemical structure analyzer), XCON (a computer hardware configuration system), MYCIN (a medical diagnostic system), and ACE (AT&amp;T\'s cable maintenance system). PROLOG, an alternative to LISP in logic programming, was developed in 1972 and was used in computational linguistics, in particular the processing of natural language processing.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">First Winter of Artificial Intelligence (1974 - 1980)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Due to a lack of financial resources, there was no significant development in research on artificial intelligence between 1974 and 1980. This period is referred to as the first AI winter in the history of artificial intelligence. It ended with the introduction of expert systems.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Second Winter of Artificial Intelligence (1987 - 1993)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Between 1987 and 1993, funding for artificial intelligence was significantly reduced so that there were no significant contributions to research in the field of artificial intelligence. This period is known as the second winter of artificial intelligence. In the literature, the first and second winters of artificial intelligence are summarized as the winter of artificial intelligence, which took place between 1974 and 1993.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Intelligent Agents (1993 - present)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">At the end of the second AI winter, the focus of research in the field of artificial intelligence shifted to what are called intelligent agents. An agent can be thought of as something that perceives and acts. He acts to achieve his goal. So, an agent can be a software application that retrieves and presents information from the internet, makes online purchases, etc. Intelligent agents can be referred to as agents or bots and have evolved into personal digital assistants with the advent of big data programs.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.26;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Projections into the future of artificial intelligence</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Below you will find future projections that show the direction of research in the field of artificial intelligence.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Virtual personal assistants</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Research in the field of artificial intelligence is currently aimed at the development of virtual personal assistants such as Facebook M, Microsoft Cortana, or Apple Siri. Today and in the future, artificial intelligence research is about developing virtual personal assistants. In the field of natural language processing, assistants should be able to communicate with the user in natural language. In robotics, it is able to move from place to place and provide a physical personal assistant. In the field of big data, he will be able to make informed business decisions based on extensive data. In the field of machine learning, he will be able to perform complex tasks.</span></span></span></p><br></span>\n\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:54:17','2025-10-08 11:47:07'),(246,39,'New Applications of Artificial Intelligence','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-39f35d3d-7fff-f5cf-efa7-1da25a026162\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Blockchain network. The data block is shared by all computers on the blockchain network. This means that all computers have access to the data block, and it is updated every ten minutes on the network. The block of data is stored in a shared database, which in turn is stored on each of the computers on the blockchain network. Blockchain is an easy way to share information between computers in a secure and automated way. The process is initiated by a party that creates a block of data for sharing. The data is checked by thousands or millions of other computers on the Internet. The verified data is added to a chain that cannot be easily faked.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin: The first application of artificial intelligence on blockchain.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin remains the first application of blockchain technology. It is a digital currency that was created in 2009. It is a payment system that offers lower processing fees than the traditional online payment systems. Bitcoin does not appear as a physical coin but only as a balance that appears in a public ledger in the cloud along with all Bitcoin transactions. Bitcoin balances are managed with public and private keys. The public and private keys are long strings of numbers and letters that are linked to the mathematical encryption algorithm used to create them. The public key can be compared to a bank account number. It is the address that is published in the world where others send Bitcoins. The private key, on the other hand, can be compared to the PIN of an ATM, which is known only to the owner of the public key. It is used to authorize Bitcoin transactions. The following terms will help you understand Bitcoin:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Bitcoin Wallet</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">It is a physical electronic device or software used for Bitcoin trading. It allows users to record the ownership of coins.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Peer-to-Peer</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">This is the technology used to enable instant payments. It involves the exchange of data and information between parties without the involvement of a central authority.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Miners</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">They are the people or companies who own the significant computing power and participate in the Bitcoin network. Rewards and transaction fees are used to motivate them. They can be considered decentralized authorities that ensure the credibility of the Bitcoin network. They also ensure that Bitcoin is not duplicated. So, mining is the process of verifying every single Bitcoin transaction or adding a block of Bitcoin transactions to the blockchain.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Transaction</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">This is the process of making a purchase or payment with Bitcoin. Each transaction forms a piece of data/record. Transactions are collected and managed in blocks. The transactions in a block are secured in a network of computers (chain) with the help of advanced cryptography. Bitcoin miners add a new block of transactions to the blockchain, and miners make sure that the transactions are correct.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Earning Rewards</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">This is the process of Bitcoin earning by Bitcoin miners, either by verifying Bitcoin transactions or by adding a block of transactions to the blockchain. The former is quite simple; it involves the verification of 1 MB of transactions. In the second case, a complex mathematical problem has to be solved, the so-called proof of work. Bitcoin, the first application of blockchain technology, therefore allows individuals to protect their personal data while generating economic value on a smaller scale. The data generated when Bitcoin is used on blockchain technology relies on artificial intelligence for its analysis.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Applications of Artificial Intelligence to Blockchain Technology</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The following are various areas in which artificial intelligence can be applied to blockchain technology, especially Bitcoin technology.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Intelligent computing power</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The operation of a blockchain requires the generation of encrypted data (blocks), the analysis of which requires a large amount of computing power. For example, hashing algorithms are used to mine the Bitcoin blocks (data). In such an algorithm, all possible candidates for the solution are systematically enumerated and then checked whether each candidate meets the problem statement before the transaction is verified. However, with artificial intelligence, the above task can be done in a smart and efficient way by using a machine learning-based algorithm with appropriate training data.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Analysis of diverse data</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Although Bitcoin is the first application of blockchain technology, it is currently being used in a number of industries to create decentralization of data and networks. SingularityNET, for example, makes targeted use of blockchain technology to promote a wider distribution of data and algorithms. With the diverse applications of blockchain technology, this means that artificial intelligence can be used to analyze the various data that blockchain technology generates.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Analysis of protected data</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The success of the artificial intelligence machine learning tool used to analyze blockchain data depends on the amount of training data. The training data of blockchain technology is protected or secured because the blockchain allows encrypted data to be stored on a distributed ledger.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.26;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Monetization of data</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Data monetization is the process where others can decide how to sell data to generate profits for businesses. Blockchain itself monetizes data by first cryptographically protecting our data and using it as we see fit. In the same way, artificial intelligence uses the cryptographically protected data by first buying it through data marketplaces.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Decision-making</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Blockchain technology provides the processes for generating secured data, while artificial intelligence uses its machine learning tool to analyze the data to make informed decisions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Internet of Things (IoT)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">This is another technology that relies on the application of artificial intelligence. The Internet of Things is the collection of billions of devices around the world that are connected to each other to collect and share data. This technology is made possible by the availability of cheap and powerful microprocessor computers and wireless networks. Any object can therefore be connected to each other. When these objects are connected to sensors that allow them to collect and communicate/share real-time data without human intervention, they become smart devices. So, any object can become a smart IoT device as soon as it can be connected to the internet with sensors to collect and share information. Internet of Things devices are devices that do not normally have an internet connection. Therefore, personal computers and mobile devices are not considered Internet of Things devices. Cars and household electrical appliances (refrigerators, vending machines, etc.) can be considered IoT devices.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">History of the Internet of Things</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">In the 1980s and 1990s, the idea of equipping objects in our environment with sensors and intelligence was first discussed. However, some of the first projects before that time were internet-enabled vending machines. This project was prevented for the following reasons: the technology that the machine was supposed to use was not yet mature, the chips were too large and bulky, and communication between objects was not possible at the time.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Data Science, Big Data, and Data Analytics</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The amount of digital data that is generated is growing at a rapid pace every day. According to estimates, about 1.7 Mbytes of data will be generated per second for each person by 2020. Some of this data is structured, while other parts are unstructured. Data science is therefore concerned with the cleansing, processing, and analysis of this enormous data. Data science combines the following disciplines: statistics, mathematics, programming, problem-solving, data collection, and artificial intelligence with the aim of gaining insight into the large amounts of data. It\'s a hodgepodge of techniques used when trying to gain insights from the vast amount of digital data. Big data refers to the enormous amount of data that cannot be processed with the traditional applications. However, IBM\'s Gartner Mitchell-Jones defines big data as \"high-volume, fast, or multi-variant information assets that require cost-effective, innovative forms of information processing that enable insights, decision-making, and process automation.\" It is high volume, high speed because the data is generated at a high speed, and high variety because different types of digital data can be generated. Data analysis, on the other hand, is the process of examining datasets using specialized systems and software to draw conclusions about the information they contain. It is used in commercial industry to enable companies to make informed business decisions and by scientists and researchers to verify or disprove scientific models, theories, and hypotheses. All of these terms—data science, big data, and data analytics—are related to machine learning, an aspect of artificial intelligence that uses training data to make informed decisions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Artificial Intelligence Products</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">There are many artificial intelligence products/systems that use different technologies. These emerging artificial intelligence products/systems are described in this section.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">IBM Watson</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">This is a cognitive platform and artificial intelligence product developed by IBM, named after the founder of IBM, Thomas Watson. It follows the same cognitive elements as humans and thinks just like them. It is a question-answering system that uses advanced natural language processing, information gathering, knowledge representation, automatic reasoning, and machine learning technologies to develop a system for answering questions. IBM Watson\'s capabilities have evolved from a system for answering questions to a system that combines the different aspects of an intelligent system, i.e., it can now see, hear, read, speak, taste, understand, reason, interpret, learn, and make recommendations.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Self-driving/autonomous cars</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">\"Self-driving cars,\" \"driverless cars,\" or \"autonomous vehicles\" are terms used to describe cars that don\'t need a human driver. It drives itself. It is an emerging artificial intelligence system that incorporates various aspects of artificial intelligence. It can understand natural language if you talk to it through the appropriate interface to tell it your goal. It demonstrates all the skills of a professional driver and drives you through the road network. It uses computer vision by seeing and identifying objects on the road and knowing when to brake and when to accelerate. It demonstrates all the skills of a professional driver with a zero tolerance for accidents. It also integrates other systems provided by the vehicle network, such as an automatic routing system, cruise control, etc. This artificial intelligence product is powered by the 5th generation (5G) network.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Face recognition system</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Facial recognition is the process of identifying or verifying a person\'s identity based on their face. This method uses an artificial intelligence system/product called a facial recognition system. The system can identify and verify a person\'s identity in images, videos, or in real time. It can be used by law enforcement agencies to track vaccinated individuals. It uses a computer algorithm to detect certain characteristic details in a person\'s face, such as the distance between the eyes or the shape of the chin. These are then converted into a mathematical representation and compared with data about other faces collected in a facial recognition database. Some facial recognition systems are designed to calculate the probability of a match between the unknown person and the person stored in the facial recognition database.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">The future of business: artificial intelligence, machine learning and deep learning</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">In recent years, scientists and pioneers have begun to devote themselves to artificial intelligence. Faster and more powerful GPUs enabled the advancement of technology. Industry observers reported this boost in 2015, when fast and powerful parallel processing became accessible. Academic research for \"big data\" and \"analytics\" has also increased the potential when infinite amounts of data could be stored and analyzed. Today we are experiencing the era of deep learning. Deep learning involves the use of artificial neural networks (A.N.N.) to perform multi-level learning. It is part of the machine learning processes based on how the data is presented using sophisticated algorithms. Deep learning is leading to a revolution in analytics and enabling practical applications of artificial intelligence (AI). We see it as necessary as automatically tagging photos on Facebook, a process developed by Yann LeCun in 2015. On the other hand, in 2015, Blippar developed an augmented reality app that uses deep learning to identify objects in real time. At the same time, we can assume that artificial intelligence will also be used in companies in the future, especially in decision-making schemes and processes. Artificial intelligence refers to machine intelligence and describes the ability of a machine to replicate the cognitive functions of a human. It is the ability to learn and solve problems. In computer science, these machines are aptly referred to as \"intelligent agents\" or bots. But not all terms of AI are created equal. Artificial intelligence has improved the way we deal with various aspects of decision-making processes. Today, there are three recognized levels in the spectrum of AI, all of which we can experience today (see Figure 1)</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter5/14.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\">\n</span></span><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-17461266-7fff-3a06-9702-3332bbffa2b5\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 1: Contemporary Recognized Levels in the Artificial Intelligence Spectrum</span>\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">More specifically, we have the following:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Assisted Intelligence—This is about automating basic tasks; this includes machine sets in production lines (i.e., industry-oriented). Advanced Intelligence—AI learns from human input; we, in turn, can make more accurate decisions based on the information we receive from the AI. Autonomous intelligence—This is AI without humans; think of driverless cars and autonomous robots. Artificial intelligence is not the end but the beginning of a new world that increases efficiency and effectiveness while improving innovation opportunities. According to a 2018 study by UNESCO-Netexplo (UNESCO-Netexplo, 2018), up to 24% of companies are using or planning to use artificial intelligence. The best examples can be found in healthcare, financial services, and the automotive industry. In the financial services industry, many accounting firms collect vast amounts of data to create a large-scale economic decision-making model for 320 million U.S. consumers. The model is designed to help financial service providers map consumer behavior, simulate \"their future selves,\" and predict their performance (Ajay et al., 2018). On the other hand, the automotive industry has developed many AI applications, from vehicle design to supporting marketing and sales decisions (McKinsey et al., 2016). For example, artificial intelligence has led to more innovative cars (even without a driver) that are equipped with multiple sensors that learn and recognize patterns. This can be implemented by adding safe driving features that warn the driver of potential collisions and lane departure. As in the financial services industry, AI is used to develop a model of the automotive ecosystem. Here, some bots map the decisions of actors such as buyers, car manufacturers, and transport service providers. It has helped companies anticipate the adoption of electric and autonomous vehicles and introduce non-restrictive pricing systems in their market. It has also empowered them to make better advertising decisions. The main feature is that artificial intelligence systems can run through more than 200,000 go-to-market (G.T.M.) scenarios, not just a handful. This gives you optimized scenarios that maximize business revenue. Something similar is happening in retail, marketing, and sales. For vendors who want to be competitive and stand out from the competition, retail is an arena of analytics and machine learning (Deloitte Insights, 2018).\n\n</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter5/15.png\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"><br></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Figure 2: Applications of AI and decision-making processes</span></span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-7e4df96f-7fff-91c0-7636-adb9318c2805\"><br></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span>\n</div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:56:07','2025-10-08 11:48:29'),(247,39,'A.I. and Business Decisions - Thematic Segments','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-20199d11-7fff-54ef-a396-c6b04b84fc18\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Before the revival of artificial intelligence and its final commercial application, executives had to rely on inconsistent and incomplete data. With artificial intelligence, they can move to data-based models and simulations. Today\'s AI systems start from scratch and flow into a regular big data regime (Knapp, 2018). The increased intelligence in action eventually provides leaders with complex models as a basis for decision-making. Many AI applications improve decision-making skills, as shown in Figure 2. In marketing, for example, automating market sharing and campaign management allows for more effective decision-making and faster response to customer feedback. You\'ll get valuable information about your customers\' preferences that will help you improve interactions with them (MarketMuse, 2019). Marketing automation is one of the most important features of a practical CRM application. Sales automation with the help of AI is also a great advantage for many retailers. Through AI-powered monitoring and control, retailers can accurately predict and respond to product demand. One example is the online retail giant Amazon. In 2012, he acquired Kiva Systems, which develops warehouse robots. Since their introduction, the Kiva robots have been tasked with monitoring and replenishing products and fulfilling orders. They can even do the lifting. That\'s a huge leap in performance for Amazon compared to when humans had to do the heavy lifting. Also, social computing helps marketers understand the social dynamics and behavior of a market. With the help of AI, they can simulate, analyze, and ultimately predict consumer behavior. These A.I. apps can also be used to understand social media and extract data. In this context, opinion mining is a type of data mining that searches for opinions and prospects online. It\'s a way for retailers to learn more about how their target audience is embracing their products. Manual evaluation and analysis take many hours. AI helps reduce manual work by providing reliable search and analysis capabilities. This form of AI is often used by search engines, which regularly list people\'s interests in specific websites, web pages, and products. These bots use various algorithms to determine a target\'s HITS and PageRank, among other things. They use hyperlink-based AI traits where bots look for rows of linked pages and view them as groups that share a common interest.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:56:59','2025-10-08 11:49:03'),(248,39,'The future of decision-making in AI','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-148c9e81-7fff-99a8-6666-47a0c4aeb2bf\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Many experts believe that AI can improve people\'s work and make it more efficient. And indeed, this is especially true when it comes to decision-making. When decision-makers and executives have reliable data analysis, suggestions, and follow-up through artificial intelligence systems, they can make better decisions for companies and their employees. It is not only the work of individual team members that is improved. AI also improves the company\'s competitive position. The gap lies in the development of artificial intelligence systems that can handle the vast amounts of data that are currently available. According to the 2020 Gartner Marketing Organization Survey, a market research firm, the data available today is expected to increase by up to 800% by 2021. About 80% of this will be unstructured data consisting of images, emails, audio clips, and the like. At this point, there is no human or artificial intelligence that can sift through this amount of data to make it usable for businesses. Slowly but surely, machine learning is beginning to influence our daily lives, from using a digital assistant on your smartphone to help you predict the weather on your daily commute to using chatbots and personalizing purchases (Accenture Interactive, 2016). But while machine learning seems to have arrived in everyday life, understanding and realizing its potential in the professional field is still a challenge. The desire is there, but so is the difficulty of bringing about real change on a productive level. Many organizations are reluctant to make the transformative changes they need for their future digital transformation. The following four key trends show, among other things, how machine learning is starting to deliver real value.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In everyday work:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">(1) the rise of digital services,</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">(2) Transforming data into value-added processes,</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">(3) digitization and exploitation of unstructured documents, and</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">(4) Unstructured data conversion and compliance (see Figure 3).</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><img src=\"https://ptgr-bucket.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/chapter5/16.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg my-4 cursor-move hover:ring-2 hover:ring-primary/50 transition-all\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\">\n</span></span><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-9c7c4e19-7fff-d483-8cbe-201a7e8c5bcc\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">F<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">igure 3: Trends in machine learning in the workplace</span></span></span></span></p><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">It is estimated that 80% of communication between companies and customers is handled by software robots (Lynch, 2019). At the same time, they will take on internal company tasks based on communication with the customer to provide better service. This can lead to a significant change in both operations and future staffing needs. Companies should have a clear vision and a solid corporate culture to effectively plan and manage such change. Effectively monitoring large amounts of data for better value, understanding specific trends and patterns, and even detecting anomalies and behaviors are currently mature enough in practice to implement machine learning. In addition, machine learning provides organizations with the ability to gain deep knowledge of large amounts of unstructured data and automate and accelerate its analysis. Examples include the lifecycle of managing contracts or invoices. The use of technologies such as machine learning (M.L.), natural language processing (N.L.P.), and optical character recognition (O.C.R.) to extract, compare, and analyze data contained in unstructured documents provides tremendous value (Iriondo, 2018). However, this use should be based on both technological solutions and business processes. In addition, increased compliance is an area where machine learning and natural language processing/understanding are starting to radically change the data landscape, especially in the financial services sector (Baldwin, 2018). Their implementation helps increase speed and efficiency, improve risk management, and reduce workloads. Each of these four areas adds value to a company looking to combine new technologies with its digital transformation.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><br></span>\n</div></span></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 07:59:53','2025-10-08 11:49:46'),(249,39,'Current Trends and Perspectives in Commerce and Banking','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-2ea3d351-7fff-6309-4f99-2fc65988c062\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">We have entered the 4th generation of trading, and we will have to adapt to it. Today we have personalized orders and the introduction of robotics in retail. The retail of the future will offer a personalized and targeted experience that participates in and socializes our lives. In any case, the retail sector is and will be one of the largest employers in the labor market. Retail is changing, moving online, and being influenced by the development of artificial intelligence through processes such as recommendation engines, targeted advertising, supply chain optimization, and payment services. With the momentum of technological development, there is the potential for a massive upheaval, subject to changes on two levels:</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">(a) in mentality and culture and</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">(b) in the legal framework.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Throughout human history, all phases of change have led, among other things, to a reform of the trading landscape, where a clear comparative advantage for innovation is also having access to as much data as possible. Today, a new consumer is at the forefront. It is enough to observe children and see how they deal with new technologies. By giving the entrepreneur \"promptly\" access to \"critical\" information about customer preferences, such as forecasts or optimization scenarios, a real revolution in business planning itself is created. The determinants of the 4th Industrial Revolution are not exclusively technological. Rather, the 4th Industrial Revolution is a complex social and economic process and must be treated as such. A typical example of such polarization would be the emergence of a small number of electronics or, better, digital stores in the retail and service sectors. Second, it would change the structure of employment by transforming white-collar workers into a new type of self-employed. Thirdly, there would be greater pressure on wages and working conditions. Artificial intelligence and robotics mean new jobs for technical disciplines and the rest of the chain. In addition, the development of new business models means that less effort and time are required to complete a leadership task, giving individuals the freedom to think and create. Data through artificial intelligence creates a suitable environment for simple and fast electronic ordering for consumers. It is possible to receive a supermarket order in just a few hours, regardless of what time it was placed during the day. It creates a solution to a critical weekly need of an average household, allowing them to invest their time in activities that interest them. In the highly competitive banking environment, artificial intelligence solutions are overshadowed by blockchain solutions. There are already consortia of major banks worldwide that are trying to create a common blockchain platform to monitor logistics and employee data in the banking sector. Another important innovation is the technological infrastructure for virtual currencies, which makes the processing of international payments faster and cheaper. There is no doubt that the FinTech sector is on the rise, and numerous AI applications have already been successfully implemented. It remains to be seen how quickly financial institutions will adopt these technologies in all countries. Trends in applications and, more broadly, computing, such as deep learning, personalized applications, and integration, are paramount. If the customer is involved, the entire process in the trade is differentiated.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 08:00:53','2025-10-08 11:50:03'),(250,39,'Deep Learning and Current Applications','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-944fc671-7fff-67c3-4a92-457e270a163a\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\">Both machine learning and deep learning are subfields of artificial intelligence, with the latter merely being the further development of the former. In machine learning, the algorithms are created by humans. Developers are responsible for analyzing and learning from the data they receive (Chen, 2018). So, they make their decisions based on what they know from the data. Deep learning, on the other hand, learns via an artificial neural network that mimics the human brain and allows the machine to analyze data based on a specific process, just like humans do to a greater or lesser extent. In other words, deep learning machines don\'t need a human programmer to tell them what to do with the data in order to learn from it. This happens through the extraordinary amount of data they collect—that is, the data is the source for running deep learning models. If all this seems theoretical enough to you, you can see where this deep learning, as the experts call it, is used. Many companies are already using machine learning to improve the customer experience, for example, in online self-service solutions. But there are also examples of deep learning solutions used to serve customers, such as chatbots in individual stores that answer questions about products and purchases at any time. As deep learning becomes more sophisticated, the retail sector is expected to be one of the most important areas of application. While the automatic translation model is not new, deep learning helps improve automatic text translation by using crosswise neural networks and enabling translations from images. Deep learning begins with the recognition of spoken dialects. A machine detects that the speaker speaks English, and then the artificial intelligence learns to recognize the differences between the dialects. Once the dialect is selected, another artificial intelligence algorithm specializes in this trait. And all this happens without the participation of a human. A well-known example of the use of artificial intelligence is autonomous driving. You may not know that there is not just one artificial intelligence system that \"works\" when a self-driving vehicle is on the road. Some deep learning systems are trained to recognize street signs, while others are trained to recognize pedestrians. As a car moves through the streets, it can use millions of artificial intelligence algorithms to help it drive and interact with the environment. Other deep learning applications have achieved such precision in sorting images, recognizing objects, and even disassembling or restoring images that goes beyond human intervention. Even handwritten digits can be identified. Deep learning with neural networks teaches machines to automate tasks performed by humans. Just as importantly, machines can also learn punctuation, grammar, and style within a text and use the model they develop to automatically create a new text with correct spelling, grammar, and style similar to the example. In the experiments so far, they have managed to reproduce almost everything, from Shakespeare to Wikipedia texts. In addition, deep learning can also help with indexing when a company needs to filter out the negative news from the market analysis. In other words, the system can be trained to collect information by filtering it based on emotions so that you only get streams of excellent or bad news and avoid unnecessary information. After all, there are numerous deep learning applications for robots that are so powerful that the mechanical friends learn to imitate humans simply by observing them. Deep learning works in the same way that the human brain processes the experiences of its environment, its senses, and any additional data it receives.</span></span></span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span>\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-09-12 08:01:27','2025-10-08 11:50:32'),(259,39,'Case Studies','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n\n\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6b324e47-7fff-19cf-9a33-7cf4c0e417bf\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Safe on the road as a human-machine team</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In the future, more and more vehicles will participate in road traffic in a highly automated manner, at least in part. In the process, they also get into difficult traffic situations that they cannot manage on their own—but in which humans can provide support. The intelligent assistance system KoFFI helps to detect such situations at an early stage and solve them through trustworthy driver-vehicle cooperation. In order to optimize this, technology, ethics, and legal experts worked closely together from the outset during development. Dense fog lies over the country road; the driver can only see a few meters away. A tractor slows down the traffic. Should the driver overtake now? \"In this situation, the machine has a clear advantage,\" explains Marcel Woide from the University of Ulm and member of the KoFFI (Cooperative Driver-Vehicle Interaction) research project funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF). \"With state-of-the-art technology such as LIDAR or radar systems, the intelligent car can see through the fog—and safely overtake the tractor,\" says Woide. The situation is different without fog. Here, people usually have the better view, as the technology only covers a few hundred meters. The automotive industry envisages five development stages until a vehicle drives fully automatically. It still takes time until the last stage is reached, and so the human remains responsible. In practice, this means that there will be many traffic situations that neither automation nor the driver alone can ideally solve. This is where KoFFI comes in: through smooth cooperation between vehicle and driver, tricky situations are to be mastered quickly and safely.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Humans and cars cooperate</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Under the leadership of the project coordinator Robert Bosch GmbH, the project partners (Daimler AG, EML European Media Laboratory GmbH, Heilbronn University of Applied Sciences, Stuttgart Media University, and Ulm University) researched how a partially automated vehicle can become a cooperative partner in road traffic. The goal: Driver and vehicle should recognize critical traffic situations as early as possible in order to be able to react appropriately. In the driving simulator they developed themselves, the KoFFI researchers played through situations such as the fog ride described at the beginning with test drivers. Astonishing finding: \"Eight out of ten drivers abandon the overtaking maneuver in the fog despite state-of-the-art technology if the car does not explain its actions,\" reports Woide. The KoFFI driving assistant was therefore equipped with a voice dialog system and a multimodal user interface. This means that the vehicle can explain itself both visually and via audio. A software framework ensures that the artificial intelligence recognizes the driver\'s mood based on the style of speech and reacts accordingly. Situations were simulated in which humans on the one hand and automation on the other are overwhelmed. It was important to find joint solutions.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The system suggests; the driver decides</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">But who decides in the event of disagreement? Mainly humans, explains Marcel Woide. As a rule, the vehicle only makes suggestions that the driver can reject at any time. The only exception is that there is a risk of an accident—for example, because the driver overlooked another road user when turning. \"Then our guardian angel function takes over and stops the vehicle in a controlled manner,\" explains Woide. When the guardian angel should intervene was optimized by means of simulations in cooperation with ethics researchers and legal scholars from the HdM Stuttgart. The KoFFI developers tested not only in the driving simulator but also on public roads how the interaction between man and machine can best succeed. Together, the team has developed ethical recommendations and guidelines for automated driving. The project results form the basis for the continuous development of cooperative driver-vehicle interactions. (Robert Bosch GmbH, 2019)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Digital twin for personalized medicine</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Efficient healthcare requires intuitively usable and semantically linked data from various sources in the clinical environment. However, clinical data is often only loosely structured and stored in the form of continuous text or raw data, so that only a fraction of the data\'s potential can be used. To overcome these problems, digital medical twins of patients are being researched and developed at the Innovation Center Computer Assisted Surgery (ICCAS) at Leipzig University. A digital twin in medicine is the virtual representation of the patient that contains all the necessary data (e.g., on medication, diseases, and treatment processes, but also genetic data). In the digital twin, however, not only can data be stored in a structured way and linked with each other, but also... It can also be used to test and optimize therapies, minimize risks, and predict the individual course of a disease with a computer model. Such digital models form the basis of any future-proof technology to support medical staff in therapy decision-making, implementation, and success monitoring. With GAIA-X, a secure and trustworthy data infrastructure for Europe is currently being developed, which allows the secure exchange of models, data, and services. The aim is to develop concepts for the integration of digital twins into the GAIA-X ecosystem so that health data, trained models, and analysis modules can be shared between different healthcare facilities (e.g., clinics, practices, and outpatient facilities) in Germany but also in countries within the EU at any time.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Scenario: Personalized diagnostics, therapy and care</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">A look into the future of location-independent, personalized medicine:In 2030, it is expected that every patient will receive a digital twin, personalized diagnostics and therapy, and regular telemedical care from their family doctor. The health data is linked from various sources (e.g., electronic patient record, medication plan, and documentation from the family doctor and hospital, as well as image data) in the personal digital twin. The remote support is supplemented by various sensors, whose data is integrated into the digital twin. These include mobile apps, fitness wristbands (wearables), and scales, as well as blood pressure, heart rate, and oximetry monitors for electrocardiological monitoring. The digital twin accompanies the patient throughout the entire treatment. GAIA-X also provides a Europe-wide ecosystem so that such models, health data, and developed analysis modules can be exchanged securely and across sectors and countries. Smart services, such as AI-based sensor and image data evaluation and comprehensive simulations and treatment predictions, can provide new software tools for medical treatment. The recorded raw data is evaluated by AI algorithms within a computing cluster of the GAIA-X ecosystem and made available to the doctor either in the practice or during home visits in a processed form to support diagnostics. In addition, data from past examinations is available at any time and in any place so that it can be used for intelligent progress assessment.</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Secure encryption of patient-related data</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"font-family: var(--font-inter), Inter, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Back to the present: If chronically ill patients want to travel, this is now associated with a great deal of effort. For possible medical treatment abroad, the patient file must be carried with a current medical report, the last surgical report if applicable, radiological images and findings, and information on the medication translated into the respective national language. In 2030, this information can be available at any time throughout Europe via the digital twin and GAIA-X. Secure communication between medical applications and the digital twin is fully end-to-end encrypted due to the sensitivity of the patient-related data. Overarching tasks such as authentication, rights management, and user administration are provided by the GAIA-X infrastructure. The necessary interfaces to clinical primary systems for the digital twin\'s access to patient-related data are carried out in accordance with medical communication standards, in particular HL7 FHIR and DICOM. This means that data can not only be viewed from any location but also stored in the digital twin. Patients receive location-independent treatment at the highest level and greater patient safety through cross-facility care processes, interdisciplinary expert decisions, and the availability of structured data at the point of care. Medical users benefit from new, innovative assistance functions and software tools for the preparation, presentation, and analysis of clinical, imaging, and sensory data, based on a patient-specific digital twin. In addition to improved patient care, this also leads to seamless data integration without media discontinuities between different institutions throughout Europe. (Innovation Center Computer Assisted Surgery ICCAS, n.d.)</span></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Further reading:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">News from the Gartner Hype Cycle on AI: </span><a href=\"https://www.gartner.de/de/artikel/gartner-hype-cycle-2022-zum-thema-ki\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#0563c1;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:small-caps;text-decoration:underline;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">LINK</span></a></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-45fda92b-7fff-a838-cfaf-928442a4e5ae\"></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Working with Artificial Intelligence | Case studies from production, work and services: </span><a href=\"https://publica-rest.fraunhofer.de/server/api/core/bitstreams/e1da9d02-54a2-443c-bff1-46872ccd043e/content\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#0563c1;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:small-caps;text-decoration:underline;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">LINK</span></a></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><div><br>\n\n</div></span>\n</div>',1,1,0,'2025-09-17 06:11:01','2025-10-17 11:23:44'),(260,26,'How do crypto exchanges make money?','<div class=\"prose prose-lg max-w-none space-y-4\">\n<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-d7f7d1af-7fff-938f-4a1b-3fb50bd871b5\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Crypto exchanges that are centralized (i.e., operated by exchange operators) make their money primarily through fees. Specifically, they can earn from the following types of fees:</span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Withdrawal fees: </span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">As you may have guessed, this fee is charged by the platform for withdrawing cryptocurrencies or other currencies. It is usually charged as a flat fee to cover the cost of transferring your cryptocurrencies from the platform.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2449999999999999;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><span style=\"width:100px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"></span></span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Deposit Fees: </span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Deposit fees can apply to both crypto and cash deposits, with sometimes no cost to this promotion.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Trading fees:</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"> These fees apply when an order is executed on the platform. The fee is usually a percentage of the trade value, with the rate depending on whether you are the maker or the taker. Fees for trading on margin:Some platforms offer margin trading, in which case additional fees will apply. The fees are based on the amount borrowed and the interest. An additional fee may apply if your position is liquidated. In addition to fees, crypto exchanges can also earn from the growth of the cryptosphere, for example, by charging a fee for listing a new cryptocurrency or offering unique crypto pairings on their exchange.</span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Which are the largest crypto exchanges?</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">According to the editors of CoinMarketCap, a cryptocurrency price tracking website, the top three crypto exchanges that allow U.S. residents to trade on the platform are Binance, Coinbase, and Kraken (as of December 2021). The ranking is based on trading volume, liquidity, trading volume, and confidence that the reported trading volumes are legitimate.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Binance</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Binance is the world\'s largest crypto exchange by trading volume. In the version available to users in the US, Binance.US, you can trade over 50 cryptocurrencies. The platform, which features competitive transaction fees, is best suited for more experienced investors and offers advanced charting features. However, it is not currently available in all 50 states.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Coinbase</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Coinbase is one of the largest crypto exchanges based in the U.S. and is known for its user-friendly platform. On Coinbase, you can buy, sell, and store \"hundreds\" of cryptocurrencies. For the more advanced, there\'s also Coinbase Pro, which builds on top of Coinbase and offers more options when it comes to charts and indicators. However, the fees at Coinbase can be higher compared to other exchanges.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Octopuses (Kraken)</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Kraken was founded in 2011 and bills itself as one of the \"largest and oldest Bitcoin exchanges in the world.\" The crypto exchange allows the purchase of over 50 cryptocurrencies and attaches great importance to high security. Although the platform has some advanced trading features that might be interesting for experienced investors; it may be a bit complicated for beginner crypto investors.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">There are a few things to consider when choosing the right crypto exchange, including:</span></p><ul style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Accessibility: </span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">An important factor in determining whether you can start trading on a particular crypto exchange is whether the platform is available in your country and state. Not all platforms are accessible everywhere due to regulations and restrictions, so it\'s important to check. This information can usually be found on the platform\'s website or in the terms and conditions.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Fees:</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\"> A crypto exchange is an example of how the lowest fees are not always the best choice. Platforms that offer higher security or easier trading often charge higher fees. So, if you\'re still learning how to trade crypto, it might be worth putting up with the cost (keep in mind, though, that this could eat into your returns). Those who expect to trade frequently should keep an eye on trading costs above all else. Whichever route you choose, make sure you know what fees may apply and how much they are.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Security: </span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Since cryptocurrencies are not backed by a central institution and are usually not covered by SIPC insurance, you need to pay attention to security when choosing a crypto exchange. Pay attention to whether the exchange has its own insurance policy and how much of its assets are generally held offline. Also, look at more general security factors such as two-factor authentication, and consider a platform\'s reputation and prominence.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Coins Offered: </span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">You should also take a look at what coins are available on the platform, especially if you\'re interested in less popular or newer coins. Think about which coins you want to invest in before choosing a platform, and then look around to see if those coins are included in the platform\'s offering or not.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans Symbols&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre; margin-left: 59.35pt;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">Liquidity</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;\">: Another thing to keep in mind is whether you can sell your cryptocurrency if you want to. In general, larger, more popular platforms tend to have a higher trading volume, which allows for better liquidity. This can give you a better chance of buying and selling at the best price if you are able to trade faster.</span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">How to start trading on a crypto exchange</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;background-color:#ffffff;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">To start trading, you must first open an account with a crypto exchange of your choice. This usually requires you to provide some basic information, such as your name, birthday, mailing address, and Social Security number. You may also be required to submit a photo or scan of a government-issued ID to verify your account. Once your identity is verified, you\'ll need to fund your account, which is usually done by connecting your bank account or a debit or credit card (note that cards may incur an additional fee). After the account is set up, you can start buying cryptocurrencies. After purchase, it is recommended to store your cryptocurrency in a safe place, such as a cryptocurrency wallet (some exchanges offer this to their users). You can also store your cryptocurrency in the crypto exchange compared to a wallet if you plan to trade actively. If you really want to invest in cryptocurrencies, it\'s also worth buying one of the best crypto tracking apps. It allows you to keep track of all your investments and manage your cryptocurrencies in one place. (Stanek, 2021).</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><br></span></div></span>\n</div>',1,0,70,'2025-10-09 07:16:17','2025-10-09 07:16:17');
